msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic|rdfs:label"
msgid "GMEOW Logic"
msgstr "GMEOW Logic"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic|skos:definition"
msgid "The GMEOW Logic module — home of the `logic:` reasoning vocabulary. It declares the canonical UFO⁺ foundation (the foundational sorts and relations authored in `logic:`, of which gUFO is a generated down-projection), the semantic profiles every rule set must declare, the world/modal terms, the four distinct quantitative axes (probability, confidence, weight, evidence), and the preservation-polarity vocabulary of the loss ledger. The `logic:` namespace is the canonical foundation; OWL, Datalog, SHACL, Prolog, N3, and the gUFO/BFO/DOLCE upper ontologies are its generated lossy projections (Principle 17). `logic:` terms are STANDALONE: they carry no gUFO parentage, because gUFO is a projection of `logic:`, not its ground. The normative semantics are in `design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md`; the preservation contract is in `design/LOGIC-CONFORMANCE.md`."
msgstr "Le GMEOW Logic module — home de the `logic:` raisonnement vocabulary."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AbstractIndividual|rdfs:label"
msgid "Abstract Individual"
msgstr "abstrait individu"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AbstractIndividual|skos:definition"
msgid "An individual that exists outside spacetime and bears no qualities — a number, a set, a value structure — neither enduring nor perduring nor inhering. The counterpart of gufo:AbstractIndividual; the abstract sibling of the concrete (endurant/perdurant) individuals. Quality values live here (stated in prose, not as a subclass edge)."
msgstr "Un individu qui exists outside spacetime et bears no qualities — a number, a set, a valeur structure — neither enduring nor perduring nor inhering."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AbstractIndividualType|rdfs:label"
msgid "Abstract Individual Type"
msgstr "abstrait individu type"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AbstractIndividualType|skos:definition"
msgid "A logic:Type whose instances are logic:AbstractIndividuals — the type whose extension (via logic:instanceOf) is drawn from individuals outside spacetime (numbers, sets, logic:QualityValues). The counterpart of gufo:AbstractIndividualType. Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. Contrast logic:ConcreteIndividualType, whose instances are located in spacetime."
msgstr "Un logic:type dont instances sont logic:AbstractIndividuals — the type dont extension (via logic:instanceOf) est drawn de individuals outside spacetime (numbers, sets, logic:QualityValues)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AchievementGoal|rdfs:label"
msgid "Achievement Goal"
msgstr "accomplissement objectif"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AchievementGoal|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:GoalExpressionKind for a goal satisfied once its logic:boundSituationType FIRST obtains at any state along the logic:Path — a one-shot attainment. Contrast logic:MaintenanceGoal (must hold at every state)."
msgstr "Le logic:GoalExpressionKind pour a objectif satisfied once its logic:boundSituationType FIRST obtains at tout état along the logic:chemin — a one-shot attainment."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ActionSchema|rdfs:label"
msgid "Action Schema"
msgstr "action schéma"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ActionSchema|skos:definition"
msgid "A named precondition / effect / invariant template that a transaction program may invoke: the reusable unit of state change. Distinct from the concrete transaction program that instantiates it, so a reusable schema is never conflated with a single state-changing run. Punned (OWL 2 DL metamodelling): it is simultaneously the IR node kind AND the class whose instances are specific reusable action schemas — an action occurrence is a gmeow:Event that instantiates one such schema through logic:instantiatesSchema. The structure means–end reasoning reads is declared on a schema by the eight action-theory facets: logic:precondition, logic:effect, logic:invariant, logic:capability, logic:nondeterministicOutcome, logic:observation, logic:compensation, and logic:actionResource."
msgstr "Un named précondition / effet / invariant template qui a transaction program peut invoke: the reusable unit de état change."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AdmissibleValuationPolicy|rdfs:label"
msgid "Admissible Valuation Policy"
msgstr "admissible évaluation politique"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AdmissibleValuationPolicy|skos:definition"
msgid "The facet value class of the admissible-valuation (gap/glut) policy: which of the four Belnap values a valuation is ALLOWED to assign. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract. Forbidding the gap, the glut, or both carves the classic sub-logics out of the same logic:BelnapBilattice algebra — it is a FORMAL ERROR to reduce the FDE↔LP difference to the designated-value set, because the two differ precisely in this admissible-valuation set, not in their designated values."
msgstr "Le facet valeur class de the admissible-évaluation (gap/glut) politique: qui de the quatre Belnap values a évaluation est ALLOWED à assign."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AdmitAllFour|rdfs:label"
msgid "Admit All Four"
msgstr "Admit tous quatre"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AdmitAllFour|skos:definition"
msgid "The admissible-valuation policy that permits all four Belnap values — true, false, both (glut), and neither (gap). It carves out First-Degree Entailment (FDE): a valuation may leave an atom under-determined (gap) or over-determined (glut). Reducing the FDE↔LP difference to the designated-value set is a formal error — FDE differs from LP by admitting the gap, not by its designated values."
msgstr "Le admissible-évaluation politique qui permet tous quatre Belnap values — true, false, both (glut), et neither (gap)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AffineCorrespondence|rdfs:label"
msgid "Affine Correspondence"
msgstr "affine correspondance"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AffineCorrespondence|skos:definition"
msgid "A co-projection onto a shared component: the 'similar but not quite' alignment, where source and view agree on a common part but neither embeds in the other. The companion of logic:Prism in the partial-alignment band — a Prism focuses an optional variant, an affine correspondence focuses a shared sub-structure. The correct rung for a logic:Vague logic:Determinacy target, NOT a low-confidence logic:Equiv. Caps: laws on the shared component only."
msgstr "Un co-projection sur a shared component: the 'similar mais not quite' alignment, où source et view agree sur a commun part mais neither embeds dans the other."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AgencyAssessment|rdfs:label"
msgid "Agency Assessment"
msgstr "agentivité évaluation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AgencyAssessment|skos:definition"
msgid "The canonical relational construct of holonic agency: a four-valued assessment of whether a holon exhibits Koestler's two co-equal Janus tendencies — self-assertive (autonomy, as a whole) and integrative (subordination, as a part) — always made relative to a declared logic:HolonicAgencyProfile. Holon integrity is assessed, never asserted — the assessment is reified with the role properties logic:agencyHolon and logic:agencyProfile, and the engine derives its logic:agencyVerdict (logic:HolonIntegral, logic:AutonomyDeficient, logic:IntegrationDeficient, or logic:AgencyUnknown). The two pathologies are the collapse of one tendency: a 'part' with no autonomy (logic:AutonomyDeficient) and a 'whole' that refuses to integrate (logic:IntegrationDeficient); integrity is both present, and neither face is privileged over the other (Principle 9). The convenient unary reading 'this holon is integral' is the lossy projection of this assessment, exactly as logic:Holon projects logic:HolonicPosition and logic:EmergenceAssessment carries emergence (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Le canonique relational construct de holonic agentivité: a quatre-valued évaluation de whether a holon exhibits Koestler's two co-equal Janus tendencies — self-assertive (autonomie, as a whole) et integrative (subordination, as a part) — toujours made relative à a declared logic:HolonicAgencyProfile."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AgencyUnknown|rdfs:label"
msgid "Agency Unknown"
msgstr "agentivité inconnu"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AgencyUnknown|skos:definition"
msgid "The agency-verdict value when neither Janus tendency is evidenced: under the declared logic:HolonicAgencyProfile, the assessed holon bears neither an logic:selfAssertiveBasis value nor an logic:integrativeBasis value, so neither the self-assertive nor the integrative marker can fire and the integrity question has no positive footing. This subsumes the 'cannot pose the question' case: it fires both when the holon bears no basis value and when the profile declares no basis at all (no marker can derive). The first-class fourth value, kept distinct from the two pathologies so that a holon evidencing neither tendency is never silently read as a deficiency of one — failure-to-evidence is not integrity, and a basis-free profile is unknown, not deficient. Mirrors logic:EmergenceUnknown and logic:ConstraintUnknown (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Le agentivité-verdict valeur lorsque neither Janus tendency est evidenced: sous the declared logic:HolonicAgencyProfile, the assessed holon bears neither an logic:selfAssertiveBasis valeur nor an logic:integrativeBasis valeur, so neither the self-assertive nor the integrative marker peut fire et the intégrité question possède no positif footing."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AgencyVerdict|rdfs:label"
msgid "Agency Verdict"
msgstr "agentivité verdict"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AgencyVerdict|skos:definition"
msgid "The closed class of holonic-agency outcomes: the four-valued result an logic:AgencyAssessment receives via logic:agencyVerdict. Its four named individuals are logic:HolonIntegral (both Janus tendencies present), logic:AutonomyDeficient (a 'part' with no autonomy), logic:IntegrationDeficient (a 'whole' refusing to integrate), and logic:AgencyUnknown (neither tendency evidenced, so the integrity question has no positive footing). The set is closed, so a misspelt verdict names no declared value and is rejected rather than silently accepted, mirroring logic:EmergenceVerdict and logic:ConstraintVerdict (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Le closed class de holonic-agentivité outcomes: the quatre-valued résultat an logic:AgencyAssessment receives via logic:agencyVerdict."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Aggregate|rdfs:label"
msgid "Aggregate"
msgstr "agrégat"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Aggregate|skos:definition"
msgid "The emergence-verdict value for a part-reducible whole property: under the declared logic:ReductionTheory of an logic:EmergenceAssessment, the whole's property is reconstructible from its proper parts — the theory carries the property in its logic:reductionBasis and a proper part also bears it (logic:bearsProperty) — so the property is a mere aggregate, a sum or closure over parts, not an emergent one. The positive, derivation-grounded verdict, reached by an actual part-reconstruction rather than by negation; contrast logic:Emergent (not part-reducible under the theory) and logic:EmergenceUnknown (the reducibility question cannot be posed) (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Le emergence-verdict valeur pour a part-reducible whole propriété: sous the declared logic:ReductionTheory de an logic:EmergenceAssessment, the whole's propriété est reconstructible de its proper parts — the theory porte the propriété dans its logic:reductionBasis et a proper part also bears it (logic:bearsProperty) — so the propriété est a mere agrégat, a sum ou fermeture sur parts, not an emergent one."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AggregateConstraint|rdfs:label"
msgid "Aggregate Constraint"
msgstr "agrégat contrainte"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AggregateConstraint|skos:definition"
msgid "Compact sugar for an aggregate-comparison constraint (P6): a logic:onClass target, an aggregate over a path (logic:aggFunction, optional logic:aggDistinct, logic:aggPath), a logic:aggComparator, and a logic:aggCompareTo right-hand side (a compared property IRI, or a literal). Expands to a canonical logic:Constraint carrying both the honest reified FOL integrity and a structured aggregate satellite, lowered to a SELECT $this … GROUP BY $this HAVING(…) sh:SPARQLConstraint. Frontend-only authoring shortcut. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:AggregateConstraint only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Compact sugar pour an agrégat-comparison contrainte (P6): a logic:onClass target, an agrégat sur a chemin (logic:aggFunction, facultatif logic:aggDistinct, logic:aggPath), a logic:aggComparator, et a logic:aggCompareTo right-hand side (a compared propriété IRI, ou a literal)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AndDecomposition|rdfs:label"
msgid "And-Decomposition"
msgstr "And-décomposition"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AndDecomposition|skos:definition"
msgid "The decomposition of a gmeow:Goal under which all of its necessary sub-goals must hold together for the parent to be satisfied — a conjunctive node of the and-or goal graph means–end search runs over. It groups the logic:necessaryFor sub-goals of the parent: every grouped sub-goal must be satisfied. The co-equal counterpart of logic:OrDecomposition (any one sufficient sub-goal settles the parent); the two compose into the and-or goal graph. Decomposition carries satisfaction dependency and is typed apart from the generic mereology spine — a sub-goal may be both a gmeow:properPartOf and logic:necessaryFor its parent, yet part-hood alone does not express the satisfaction dependency planning needs."
msgstr "Le décomposition de a gmeow:objectif sous qui tous de its necessary sub-goals doit hold together pour the parent à be satisfied — a conjonctif nœud de the and-or objectif graphe means–end search runs over."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AntiRigidType|rdfs:label"
msgid "Anti-Rigid Type"
msgstr "Anti-Rigid type"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AntiRigidType|skos:definition"
msgid "A logic:Type that applies contingently to EVERY one of its instances — for each instance there is a world of existence in which it lacks the type (the anti-rigidity witness; logic:rigidlyAppliesTo holds for none of its instances). The counterpart of gufo:AntiRigidType; the meta-type whose instances are the anti-rigid sorts: logic:Phase and logic:Role (each a logic:AntiRigidType and a logic:Sortal), logic:RoleMixin and logic:PhaseMixin (each a logic:AntiRigidType and a logic:NonSortal). Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. The discipline that anti-rigid instantiation owes a witness is logic:dischargeObligation. Contrast logic:RigidType."
msgstr "Un logic:type qui applies contingently à EVERY one de its instances — pour each instance there est a monde de existence dans qui it lacks the type (the anti-rigidity témoin; logic:rigidlyAppliesTo holds pour none de its instances)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ArgumentationSemantics|rdfs:label"
msgid "Argumentation Semantics"
msgstr "argumentation sémantique"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ArgumentationSemantics|skos:definition"
msgid "The facet value class of the argumentation facet: how conflicts among defeasible arguments are resolved. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract. Its individuals range from no argumentation through the grounded and preferred Dung semantics to a policy-specific resolution. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:ArgumentationSemantics only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le facet valeur class de the argumentation facet: how conflicts parmi defeasible arguments sont resolved."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Aspect|rdfs:label"
msgid "Aspect"
msgstr "aspect"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Aspect|skos:definition"
msgid "A moment (trope): an endurant that exists only by inhering in a bearer on which it existentially depends — a colour, a belief, a marriage's commitment. The counterpart of gufo:Aspect, covering its intrinsic/extrinsic split (gufo:IntrinsicAspect inheres in a single bearer, gufo:ExtrinsicAspect depends on several): logic: carries that distinction on the inherence/dependence relation rather than as separate classes. The dependent counterpart of logic:Substantial. Qualities and modes are aspects (stated in prose, not as a subclass edge)."
msgstr "Un moment (trope): an endurant qui exists uniquement par inhering dans a bearer sur qui it existentially depends — a colour, a belief, a marriage's engagement."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AssessmentDimension|rdfs:label"
msgid "Assessment Dimension"
msgstr "évaluation dimension"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AssessmentDimension|skos:definition"
msgid "The value-vocabulary class of the factored axis a logic:CognitiveAssessment judges, named via logic:assessmentDimension. An OPEN value vocabulary (individuals, never subclasses): a new dimension is a new individual rather than a reshaping of the construct, the same orthogonal-factorization discipline the foundation applies to claim modality and contextual scope. The dimensions vary independently — an assessment on one says nothing about another — and an assessment names exactly one."
msgstr "Le valeur-vocabulary class de the factored axis a logic:CognitiveAssessment judges, named via logic:assessmentDimension."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AssessmentLevel|rdfs:label"
msgid "Assessment Level"
msgstr "évaluation niveau"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AssessmentLevel|skos:definition"
msgid "The value-vocabulary class of an ordinal level on an assessment's scale, the object of logic:assessmentLevel and logic:thresholdLevel when the scale is ordinal. An OPEN, ordered value vocabulary (logic:levelNone ≺ logic:levelEmerging ≺ logic:levelCompetent ≺ logic:levelStrong), ordered by logic:levelAtOrAbove so that 'a level at or above a threshold' is well-defined for the coarse-ladder projection without a numeric comparison (which would force a procedural profile). An assessment whose scale is continuous carries a literal logic:assessmentLevel instead; the ordinal levels are the projection scale. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:AssessmentLevel only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le valeur-vocabulary class de an ordinal niveau sur an évaluation's scale, the object de logic:assessmentLevel et logic:thresholdLevel lorsque the scale est ordinal."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AtomicGoal|rdfs:label"
msgid "Atomic Goal"
msgstr "atomique objectif"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AtomicGoal|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:GoalExpressionKind for a leaf goal satisfied exactly when its logic:boundSituationType obtains at the relevant state. The base of the compositional algebra; contrast the conjunctive/disjunctive combinators and the temporal kinds."
msgstr "Le logic:GoalExpressionKind pour a leaf objectif satisfied exactly lorsque its logic:boundSituationType obtains at the relevant état."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AutonomyDeficient|rdfs:label"
msgid "Autonomy Deficient"
msgstr "autonomie déficient"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AutonomyDeficient|skos:definition"
msgid "The agency-verdict value for the first Koestlerian pathology — a 'part' with no autonomy: under the declared logic:HolonicAgencyProfile, the holon bears an logic:integrativeBasis value (it subordinates as a part) but bears no logic:selfAssertiveBasis value, so its self-assertive (autonomy-as-a-whole) face has collapsed. Reached by negation-as-failure over the self-assertive marker while the integrative marker holds, so the verdict is profile-relative, never a bare default. The co-equal counterpart of logic:IntegrationDeficient (the opposite collapse); contrast logic:HolonIntegral (both faces) and logic:AgencyUnknown (neither evidenced) (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Le agentivité-verdict valeur pour the first Koestlerian pathology — a 'part' avec no autonomie: sous the declared logic:HolonicAgencyProfile, the holon bears an logic:integrativeBasis valeur (it subordinates as a part) mais bears no logic:selfAssertiveBasis valeur, so its self-assertive (autonomie-as-a-whole) face possède collapsed."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AvoidanceGoal|rdfs:label"
msgid "Avoidance Goal"
msgstr "évitement objectif"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/AvoidanceGoal|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:GoalExpressionKind for a goal satisfied only while its proscribed logic:boundSituationType NEVER obtains across the interval, violated at the first state it obtains — the dual of logic:MaintenanceGoal. While the window is still open the evaluation is logic:GoalEvaluationUndetermined."
msgstr "Le logic:GoalExpressionKind pour a objectif satisfied uniquement while its proscribed logic:boundSituationType NEVER obtains across the interval, violated at the first état it obtains — the dual de logic:MaintenanceGoal."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/BelnapBilattice|rdfs:label"
msgid "Belnap Bilattice"
msgstr "Belnap bilattice"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/BelnapBilattice|skos:definition"
msgid "The four-valued Belnap truth algebra with the values true, false, both (over-determined / glut) and neither (under-determined / gap). The richest truth algebra a ReasoningContract may select; the classic sub-logics (FDE, LP, K3, classical) are carved out of this same algebra by the admissible-valuation policy and the designated-value set, which vary independently of the algebra."
msgstr "Le quatre-valued Belnap vérité algebra avec the values true, false, both (over-determined / glut) et neither (under-determined / gap)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/BindingOptional|rdfs:label"
msgid "Binding Optional"
msgstr "liaison facultatif"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/BindingOptional|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:ColumnBinding value for a column that may be unbound in some rows (e.g. projected from a SPARQL OPTIONAL). Wire value `optional`."
msgstr "Le logic:ColumnBinding valeur pour a colonne qui peut be unbound dans some rows (e.g."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/BindingRequired|rdfs:label"
msgid "Binding Required"
msgstr "liaison obligatoire"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/BindingRequired|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:ColumnBinding value for a column bound in every result row. An unbound required column is a hard contract violation. Wire value `required`."
msgstr "Le logic:ColumnBinding valeur pour a colonne bound dans chaque résultat row."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Blocked|rdfs:label"
msgid "Blocked"
msgstr "bloqué"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Blocked|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:FeasibilityStatus value for a goal with no path from the current situation, where the obstruction may yet lift — temporarily unreachable rather than permanently so. Contrast logic:Infeasible (unreachable in every reachable situation) and logic:Feasible (a path exists)."
msgstr "Le logic:FeasibilityStatus valeur pour a objectif avec no chemin de the current situation, où the obstruction peut yet lift — temporarily unreachable plutôt que permanently so."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/BridgeView|rdfs:label"
msgid "Bridge View"
msgstr "pont View"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/BridgeView|skos:definition"
msgid "The floor rung: a commitment-shifting comorphism with NO satisfaction-preservation claim — the alignment to BFO, DOLCE, SUMO or YAMATO. A bridge view carries logic:morphismKind logic:CommitmentShiftingBridge, and the loss ledger refuses to emit owl:equivalentClass for it. Caps: no preservation law; the alignment is a by-reference bridge, never an identity."
msgstr "Le floor rung: a engagement-shifting comorphism avec NO satisfaction-preservation claim — the alignment à BFO, DOLCE, SUMO ou YAMATO."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/BudgetBoundedResource|rdfs:label"
msgid "Budget-Bounded Resource"
msgstr "budget-Bounded ressource"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/BudgetBoundedResource|skos:definition"
msgid "The resource execution policy that runs under a declared resource budget or bound: on exhaustion the engine returns a budget-exhausted, incomplete result — sound but incomplete — and never a false answer. The bounded counterpart of logic:CertifiedFragmentResource; a contract may carry both, since resource is an execution policy holding several independent properties together rather than a single complete-vs-bounded toggle."
msgstr "Le ressource exécution politique qui runs sous a declared ressource budget ou bound: sur exhaustion the engine returns a budget-épuisé, incomplet résultat — sound mais incomplet — et jamais a false answer."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/BudgetExhausted|rdfs:label"
msgid "Budget Exhausted"
msgstr "budget épuisé"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/BudgetExhausted|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:EvaluationStatus value for a run that hit a declared resource budget or bound before finishing. Wire value `budget-exhausted`. The specific budget that tripped (answers/inference/depth) is carried alongside as consumed-budget detail so the historical answer-status strings remain a lossless projection."
msgstr "Le logic:EvaluationStatus valeur pour a run qui hit a declared ressource budget ou bound avant finishing."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Builtin|rdfs:label"
msgid "Builtin"
msgstr "primitive"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Builtin|skos:definition"
msgid "A native computational primitive usable in rule bodies under logic:ProceduralPrologProfile: the registry entry for a derivational builtin such as string concatenation, date arithmetic, or basic math (criticism 8, LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md §OWL 2 criticisms). Builtins are the lightweight derivations a foundation genuinely needs (Principle 12, in-logic); heavy domain computation — geo/datum transforms, relation-algebra composition, vector operations — stays external by reference. The registry is declared here; builtin execution is seamed to the compiler/engine. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:Builtin only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Un native computational primitive usable dans règle bodies sous logic:ProceduralPrologProfile: the registry entrée pour a derivational primitive such as string concatenation, date arithmetic, ou basic math (criticism 8, LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md §OWL 2 criticisms)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CandidateAccepted|rdfs:label"
msgid "Accepted"
msgstr "accepté"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CandidateAccepted|skos:definition"
msgid "The canonical, axiom-bearing lifecycle state: a candidate a reviewer has promoted, reachable only through logic:CandidateUnderReview with a recorded logic:reviewedBy decision. A candidate asserted as accepted without that review is a checked governance violation, not a soft warning. Wire value `accepted`."
msgstr "Le canonique, axiom-bearing cycle de vie état: a candidat a reviewer possède promoted, reachable uniquement par logic:CandidateUnderReview avec a recorded logic:reviewedBy decision."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CandidateLifecycleState|rdfs:label"
msgid "Candidate Lifecycle State"
msgstr "candidat cycle de vie état"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CandidateLifecycleState|skos:definition"
msgid "The closed value class of the logic:candidateLifecycle facet: the four-state machine a logic:FormalizationCandidate moves through. Its individuals are logic:CandidateProposed (entry; every extraction lands here), logic:CandidateUnderReview, logic:CandidateAccepted (canonical, axiom-bearing) and logic:CandidateRejected. logic:CandidateAccepted is reachable only through logic:CandidateUnderReview with a recorded logic:reviewedBy decision, never directly. The set is closed, so a misspelt state names no declared value and is rejected (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, §Typed formalization governance)."
msgstr "Le classe de valeurs fermée de the logic:candidateLifecycle facet: the quatre-état machine a logic:FormalizationCandidate moves through."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CandidateProposed|rdfs:label"
msgid "Proposed"
msgstr "proposé"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CandidateProposed|skos:definition"
msgid "The lifecycle entry state: a candidate freshly extracted and not yet reviewed. An LLM extraction ALWAYS enters here; it carries no canonical force. Wire value `proposed`."
msgstr "Le cycle de vie entrée état: a candidat freshly extracted et not yet reviewed."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CandidateRejected|rdfs:label"
msgid "Rejected"
msgstr "rejeté"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CandidateRejected|skos:definition"
msgid "The terminal lifecycle state for a candidate review declined to formalize — recorded rather than deleted, so the decision (and its negative case) is auditable. Wire value `rejected`."
msgstr "Le terminal cycle de vie état pour a candidat révision declined à formalize — recorded plutôt que deleted, so the decision (and its négatif case) est auditable."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CandidateUnderReview|rdfs:label"
msgid "Under Review"
msgstr "Under révision"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CandidateUnderReview|skos:definition"
msgid "The lifecycle state of a candidate a reviewer is actively adjudicating — the mandatory waypoint between logic:CandidateProposed and logic:CandidateAccepted. Wire value `under-review`."
msgstr "Le cycle de vie état de a candidat a reviewer est actively adjudicating — the mandatory waypoint entre logic:CandidateProposed et logic:CandidateAccepted."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CanonicalProjection|rdfs:label"
msgid "Canonical Projection"
msgstr "canonique projection"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CanonicalProjection|skos:definition"
msgid "The projection-target value requesting the answer be rendered in the canonical logic: surface — the orthogonal, lossless form GMEOW reasons over, before any down-projection. The default output request; it never alters which entailments hold."
msgstr "Le projection-target valeur requesting the answer be rendered dans the logique canonique: surface — the orthogonal, lossless form GMEOW reasons over, avant tout down-projection."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Category|rdfs:label"
msgid "Category"
msgstr "catégorie"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Category|skos:definition"
msgid "A rigid non-sortal that classifies instances of several different Kinds by shared essential properties without itself supplying a principle of identity: it dispersively spans Kinds rather than carrying its own identity criterion. Rigid but identity-dispersive; the rigid counterpart of the anti-rigid RoleMixin and PhaseMixin."
msgstr "Un rigid non-sortal qui classifies instances de several different Kinds par shared essential properties sans itself supplying a principle de identité: it dispersively spans Kinds plutôt que carrying its own identité criterion."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CategoryDefeasibleDefault|rdfs:label"
msgid "Defeasible Default"
msgstr "Defeasible Default"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CategoryDefeasibleDefault|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:FormalizationCategory for defeasible content a more specific fact may override — default-logic force, distinct from plain typicality. Wire value `defeasible-default`."
msgstr "Le logic:FormalizationCategory pour defeasible content a more specific fact peut override — default-logic force, distinct de plain typicality."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CategoryDeliberateOverlap|rdfs:label"
msgid "Deliberate Overlap"
msgstr "Deliberate Overlap"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CategoryDeliberateOverlap|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:FormalizationCategory for a mereological sharing fact deliberately admitted — an intended overlap rather than an accidental one. Wire value `deliberate-overlap`."
msgstr "Le logic:FormalizationCategory pour a mereological sharing fact deliberately admitted — an intended overlap plutôt que an accidental one."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CategoryDerivationRule|rdfs:label"
msgid "Derivation Rule"
msgstr "dérivation règle"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CategoryDerivationRule|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:FormalizationCategory for a productive rule whose head is entailed — content that adds to the reasoned closure. Wire value `derivation-rule`."
msgstr "Le logic:FormalizationCategory pour a productive règle dont head est entailed — content qui adds à the reasoned fermeture."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CategoryDocumentationOnly|rdfs:label"
msgid "Documentation Only"
msgstr "Documentation Only"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CategoryDocumentationOnly|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:FormalizationCategory for explanatory prose that is NOT to be formalized at all — the category that records a deliberate decision to leave content unaxiomatized. Wire value `documentation-only`."
msgstr "Le logic:FormalizationCategory pour explanatory prose qui est NOT à be formalized at tous — the catégorie qui enregistre a deliberate decision à leave content unaxiomatized."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CategoryEquivalenceDefinition|rdfs:label"
msgid "Equivalence Definition"
msgstr "Equivalence définition"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CategoryEquivalenceDefinition|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:FormalizationCategory for prose stating the necessary-and-sufficient identity of a term — a definitional equivalence. Wire value `equivalence-definition`."
msgstr "Le logic:FormalizationCategory pour prose stating the necessary-and-sufficient identité de a terme — a definitional equivalence."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CategoryIntegrityConstraint|rdfs:label"
msgid "Integrity Constraint"
msgstr "intégrité contrainte"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CategoryIntegrityConstraint|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:FormalizationCategory for an integrity condition whose violation is a finding, not a derivation — a CBox constraint rather than a productive rule. Wire value `integrity-constraint`."
msgstr "Le logic:FormalizationCategory pour an intégrité condition dont violation est a finding, not a dérivation — a CBox contrainte plutôt que a productive règle."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CategoryNecessaryCondition|rdfs:label"
msgid "Necessary Condition"
msgstr "Necessary Condition"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CategoryNecessaryCondition|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:FormalizationCategory for prose stating a one-directional necessary condition (the term implies the condition). Wire value `necessary-condition`."
msgstr "Le logic:FormalizationCategory pour prose stating a one-directional necessary condition (the terme implies the condition)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CategoryNonEntailmentObligation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Non-Entailment Obligation"
msgstr "Non-implication obligation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CategoryNonEntailmentObligation|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:FormalizationCategory for a deliberate non-assertion — prose recording a conclusion the foundation must never draw, realized as a logic:NonEntailmentObligation. Wire value `non-entailment-obligation`."
msgstr "Le logic:FormalizationCategory pour a deliberate non-assertion — prose recording a conclusion the foundation doit jamais draw, realized as a logic:NonEntailmentObligation."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CategoryRecommendation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Recommendation"
msgstr "Recommendation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CategoryRecommendation|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:FormalizationCategory for advisory content that is never enforced — guidance carried but not reasoned over. Wire value `recommendation`."
msgstr "Le logic:FormalizationCategory pour advisory content qui est jamais enforced — guidance carried mais not reasoned over."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CategorySufficientCondition|rdfs:label"
msgid "Sufficient Condition"
msgstr "Sufficient Condition"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CategorySufficientCondition|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:FormalizationCategory for prose stating a one-directional sufficient condition (the condition implies the term). Wire value `sufficient-condition`."
msgstr "Le logic:FormalizationCategory pour prose stating a one-directional sufficient condition (the condition implies the terme)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CategoryTypicality|rdfs:label"
msgid "Typicality"
msgstr "Typicality"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CategoryTypicality|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:FormalizationCategory for generic, what-normally-holds content — kept distinct from logic:CategoryDefeasibleDefault, whose force is override rather than genericity. Wire value `typicality`."
msgstr "Le logic:FormalizationCategory pour generic, what-normally-holds content — kept distinct de logic:CategoryDefeasibleDefault, dont force est override plutôt que genericity."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CertifiedFragmentResource|rdfs:label"
msgid "Certified-Fragment Resource"
msgstr "Certified-Fragment ressource"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CertifiedFragmentResource|skos:definition"
msgid "The resource execution policy that requires the rule set to lie within a certified-complete, terminating fragment: it guarantees hard termination and a complexity bound, and the result reports complete-for-fragment. The certified counterpart of logic:BudgetBoundedResource; because resource is an execution policy holding independent properties together, a contract may require both a certified fragment and a budget at once."
msgstr "Le ressource exécution politique qui exige the règle set à lie within a certified-complet, terminating fragment: it guarantees hard terminaison et a complexity bound, et the résultat reports complet-for-fragment."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ChaseAcceptanceWitness|rdfs:label"
msgid "Chase Acceptance Witness"
msgstr "Chase Acceptance témoin"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ChaseAcceptanceWitness|skos:definition"
msgid "The acceptance record that an existential-rule chase materialization terminated under a weak-acyclicity certificate, executed natively by gmeow_logic::materialize::materialize_routed, which surfaces the ChaseAdmission termination certificate as a first-class gmeow:Finding. It carries, through logic:carriesTerminationCertificate, the certificate evidence. The flagship producer runs the native chase and pins that the surfaced Finding is non-empty and that the derivation carries an explain trace passing gmeow_logic::explain::assert_faithful; this witness is the ontological twin the thin logic:ChaseAcceptanceWitnessShape gates. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:ChaseAcceptanceWitness only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le acceptance record qui an existential-règle chase matérialisation terminated sous a weak-acyclicity certificat, executed natively par gmeow_logic::materialize::materialize_routed, qui surfaces the ChaseAdmission terminaison certificat as a first-class gmeow:Finding."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Choice|rdfs:label"
msgid "Choice"
msgstr "Choice"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Choice|skos:definition"
msgid "The guarded-choice program combinator: selects one of two sub-programs based on whether a guard situation holds at the current state. The left operand (logic:leftOperand) is executed when the guard holds; the right operand (logic:rightOperand) is executed when it does not. The guard is declared through logic:guardSituation, reusing the same property the conditional goal expression reads — a choice combinator is a PROGRAM operator that dispatches on a guard, typed APART from a conditional formula connective that holds at a single state. The two operands are binary, carried by logic:leftOperand and logic:rightOperand (the same properties logic:SerialConjunction uses). A plan whose branches are conditioned on what an earlier observation revealed is a POLICY — a reading of a plan, not a separate class — and its branches are resolved through logic:planBranch, logic:branchGuard, and logic:nextActionSchema; logic:Choice is the structural combinator that expresses the branching operator in the program body. Distinct from goal-level logic:DisjunctiveGoal, which evaluates a truth-at-a-state condition over sub-expressions, not a program that dispatches control to one of two sub-programs."
msgstr "Le guarded-choice program combinator: selects one de two sub-programs based sur whether a guard situation holds at the current état."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ChoiceGroupConstraint|rdfs:label"
msgid "Choice Group Constraint"
msgstr "Choice Group contrainte"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ChoiceGroupConstraint|skos:definition"
msgid "Compact sugar for a choice-group cardinality constraint (P1): a logic:onClass target, a set of logic:choicePredicate predicates, and a logic:choiceMode ('exactly-one', 'at-most-one', or the 'exactly-one-of-N' alias of 'exactly-one'). The compiler expands it into a canonical logic:Constraint whose integrity is the XOR / at-most formula over the ∃-requiredness of each predicate. Frontend-only: it is not a new node kind, only an authoring shortcut."
msgstr "Compact sugar pour a choice-group cardinality contrainte (P1): a logic:onClass target, a set de logic:choicePredicate predicates, et a logic:choiceMode ('exactly-one', 'at-most-one', ou the 'exactly-one-of-N' alias de 'exactly-one')."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ClassicalModelSemantics|rdfs:label"
msgid "Classical Model Semantics"
msgstr "Classical modèle sémantique"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ClassicalModelSemantics|skos:definition"
msgid "The model-semantics facet value selecting classical first-order entailment: truth in every model. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract; contrast the least-model, well-founded, and stable-model values that select a distinguished model or model set for rule programs."
msgstr "Le modèle-sémantique facet valeur selecting classical premier ordre implication: vérité dans chaque modèle."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ClassicalTwoValued|rdfs:label"
msgid "Classical Two-Valued"
msgstr "Classical Two-Valued"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ClassicalTwoValued|skos:definition"
msgid "The two-valued truth algebra with only true and false. The degenerate truth algebra a ReasoningContract selects when neither gluts nor gaps are needed; equivalent to selecting the Belnap algebra with logic:ForbidGapAndGlut, offered as a direct value for the common classical case."
msgstr "Le two-valued vérité algebra avec uniquement true et false."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Closed|rdfs:label"
msgid "Closed"
msgstr "Closed"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Closed|skos:definition"
msgid "The occurrent-boundary value for a completed unitary event: a perdurant whole over a closed temporal interval, finished and no longer able to change — the arrival, the run completed, the executed record. The event half of the YAMATO/Galton action(open)/event(closed) distinction; a Closed occurrent that bears a time-varying logic:Fluent is the logic:OccurrentChangeAsymmetry violation, since a completed whole cannot vary. Contrast logic:Open."
msgstr "Le occurrent-boundary valeur pour a completed unitary event: a perdurant whole sur a closed temporal interval, finished et no longer able à change — the arrival, the run completed, the executed record."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ClosedWorldClosure|rdfs:label"
msgid "Closed-World Closure"
msgstr "Closed-monde fermeture"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ClosedWorldClosure|skos:definition"
msgid "The closed-world value of the closure map: for the predicate or context key it is bound to, the materialized extension is complete and absence may be read as falsity. Realized within a logic:WorldBoundary by the built-in SHACL (the CWA lane); it is the per-key value of the closure map, never a global flag — open-world is the default for unlisted keys."
msgstr "Le monde fermé valeur de the fermeture map: pour the prédicat ou contexte key it est bound to, the materialized extension est complet et absence peut be read as falsity."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ClosureAcceptanceWitness|rdfs:label"
msgid "Closure Acceptance Witness"
msgstr "fermeture Acceptance témoin"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ClosureAcceptanceWitness|skos:definition"
msgid "The acceptance record that an EL→RL→DL reasoning closure (gmeow_logic::reason::reason_all) genuinely entailed new atoms: it names, through logic:closureEntailedAtom, at least one atom the closure derived beyond its asserted EDB. The flagship producer runs the native closure and pins that a designated entailed atom is present and absent from the EDB; this witness is the ontological twin the thin logic:ClosureAcceptanceWitnessShape gates. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:ClosureAcceptanceWitness only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le acceptance record qui an EL→RL→DL raisonnement fermeture (gmeow_logic::reason::reason_all) genuinely entailed new atoms: it names, par logic:closureEntailedAtom, au moins one atom the fermeture dérivé beyond its asserted EDB."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ClosureEntry|rdfs:label"
msgid "Closure Entry"
msgstr "fermeture entrée"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ClosureEntry|skos:definition"
msgid "A reified entry of the Closure facet map: it binds a predicate or context key (logic:closureKey) to an open- or closed-world value (logic:closureValue). The Closure facet is a map, not a global flag; WorldBoundary-scoped closed-world is the per-key value, open-world the default for unlisted keys."
msgstr "Un reified entrée de the fermeture facet map: it binds a prédicat ou contexte key (logic:closureKey) à an ouvert- ou monde fermé valeur (logic:closureValue)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ClosureValue|rdfs:label"
msgid "Closure Value"
msgstr "fermeture valeur"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ClosureValue|skos:definition"
msgid "The facet value class of a single closure setting — open-world or closed-world. It is the per-key value of the closure map (carried as the map default via logic:defaultClosure or as the value of a logic:ClosureEntry), not the closure facet itself, which is a map keyed by predicate or context."
msgstr "Le facet valeur class de a single fermeture setting — monde ouvert ou monde fermé."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CognitiveAssessment|rdfs:label"
msgid "Cognitive Assessment"
msgstr "cognitif évaluation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CognitiveAssessment|skos:definition"
msgid "The canonical record of how good some reasoning is, or how capable a reasoner is: a reified, vantage-indexed node naming exactly one logic:AssessmentDimension and carrying its assessed agent (logic:assessedAgent), subject and granularity (logic:assessmentSubject with logic:subjectGranularity), task or context (logic:assessmentContext), scale and level (logic:assessmentScale with logic:assessmentLevel), evaluator and standpoint (logic:assessmentEvaluator, attributed via gmeow:accordingTo), evidence (logic:assessmentEvidence), method (logic:assessmentMethod), valid interval (carried by gmeow:duringInterval) and the strength with which the judgment itself is held (carried by logic:confidence). The dimensions vary independently, so a single ordinal familiarity-to-mastery scale collapses exactly the distinctions an assessment exists to draw; the construct keeps them factored. A self-assessment and an observer's assessment of the same agent are two coexisting records, never reconciled into one verdict, and because the node is reified an assessment is itself a subject another assessment can range over — an evaluation of the evaluator — with no new machinery. The convenient ordinal reading is the lossy coarse-ladder projection of this assessment, exactly as logic:AgencyAssessment projects the unary 'this holon is integral'; a reliability assessment is a logic:CognitiveAssessment on the reliability dimension over a series of runs, distinct from the single-run logic:ResultAssurance. Normative in design/LOGIC-COGNITION.md."
msgstr "Le canonique record de how good some raisonnement is, ou how capable a raisonneur is: a reified, vantage-indexed nœud naming exactement un logic:AssessmentDimension et carrying its assessed agent (logic:assessedAgent), subject et granularity (logic:assessmentSubject avec logic:subjectGranularity), task ou contexte (logic:assessmentContext), scale et niveau (logic:assessmentScale avec logic:assessmentLevel), evaluator et point de vue (logic:assessmentEvaluator, attributed via gmeow:accordingTo), preuve (logic:assessmentEvidence), method (logic:assessmentMethod), valid interval (carried par gmeow:duringInterval) et the strength avec qui the judgment itself est held (carried par logic:confidence)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CoherenceCertificate|rdfs:label"
msgid "Coherence Certificate"
msgstr "cohérence certificat"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CoherenceCertificate|skos:definition"
msgid "The contract-scoped assertion, issued ONLY from a CONCLUSIVE check (the summarized logic:ReasoningResult has logic:EvaluationCompleted, or logic:CompleteForFragment), that over the certified fragment the inspection was COMPLETE and found no forbidden integrity violation and no undisclosed contradiction. Scoped by contract (logic:contractHash on the linked result), fragment (logic:certifiedFragment), budget (logic:consumedBudget) and bundle (logic:bundleHash, logic:axiomHash). Coherence means 'every contradiction present is permitted under the contract and disclosed, or has been reported as a violation' — NEVER 'this bundle contains no contradiction'. A complete check is the only thing entitled to the word certify; a bounded check yields a logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation instead. Carries logic:permittedConflictWitness for disclosed gluts and logic:forbiddenViolationWitness (necessarily empty for an issued certificate). Authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust); a lossy documentation projection (Principle 17). Normative in design/LOGIC-CONFORMANCE.md, §The coherence certificate."
msgstr "Le contract-scoped assertion, issued ONLY de a CONCLUSIVE vérification (the summarized logic:ReasoningResult possède logic:EvaluationCompleted, ou logic:CompleteForFragment), qui sur the certified fragment the inspection was complet et found no forbidden intégrité violation et no undisclosed contradiction."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CoherenceCheckAttestation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Coherence Check Attestation"
msgstr "cohérence vérification attestation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CoherenceCheckAttestation|skos:definition"
msgid "The strictly weaker outcome a BOUNDED or INCOMPLETE coherence check issues (the summarized logic:ReasoningResult has logic:BudgetExhausted, or logic:Incomplete / logic:CompletenessUnknown): it records only that no forbidden integrity violation and no undisclosed contradiction was found WITHIN the completed search. A budget-exhausted run produces an attestation, NEVER a logic:CoherenceCertificate, because it cannot rule out a contradiction it never reached. Honest evidence, not a certification of coherence. Carries the same scoped payload (logic:summarizesResult, logic:bundleHash, logic:contradictionPolicy, logic:checkIssuedAt). Authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust); a lossy documentation projection (Principle 17). Normative in design/LOGIC-CONFORMANCE.md, §The coherence certificate."
msgstr "Le strictly weaker résultat a BOUNDED ou incomplet cohérence vérification issues (the summarized logic:ReasoningResult possède logic:BudgetExhausted, ou logic:incomplet / logic:CompletenessUnknown): it enregistre uniquement qui no forbidden intégrité violation et no undisclosed contradiction was found WITHIN the completed search."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Collection|rdfs:label"
msgid "Collection"
msgstr "collection"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Collection|skos:definition"
msgid "A plurality individuated by its members, where the members are themselves the relevant units of the whole — a deck of cards, a committee, a playlist. The counterpart of gufo:Collection; members relate to it via logic:memberOf rather than logic:properPartOf. Contrast logic:Quantity, which is individuated by constitution rather than by member count."
msgstr "Un plurality individuated par its members, où the members sont themselves the relevant units de the whole — a deck de cards, a committee, a playlist."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ColumnBinding|rdfs:label"
msgid "Column Binding"
msgstr "colonne liaison"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ColumnBinding|skos:definition"
msgid "The closed value class of the logic:columnBinding facet: whether a column's variable is bound in every row. Its individuals are logic:BindingRequired and logic:BindingOptional. The set is closed, so a misspelt value names no declared binding and is rejected. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:ColumnBinding only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le classe de valeurs fermée de the logic:columnBinding facet: whether a colonne's variable est bound dans chaque row."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CommitmentShiftingBridge|rdfs:label"
msgid "Commitment-Shifting Bridge"
msgstr "engagement-Shifting pont"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CommitmentShiftingBridge|skos:definition"
msgid "A bridge that shifts ontological commitment rather than preserving satisfaction: the kind borne by a logic:BridgeView alignment to a top-level ontology (BFO, DOLCE, SUMO, YAMATO). The loss ledger refuses to emit owl:equivalentClass for it; the bridge is adopted by reference (Principle 5), never as an identity collapse."
msgstr "Un pont qui shifts ontological engagement plutôt que preserving satisfaction: the kind borne par a logic:BridgeView alignment à a top-niveau ontology (BFO, DOLCE, SUMO, YAMATO)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CommittedExecution|rdfs:label"
msgid "Committed Execution"
msgstr "Committed exécution"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CommittedExecution|skos:definition"
msgid "The execution-mode value under which a transaction program's elementary updates are committed — the effects advance the path and persist. The default execution mode; contrast logic:HypotheticalExecution, which discards effects."
msgstr "Le exécution-mode valeur sous qui a transaction program's elementary updates sont committed — the effects advance the chemin et persist."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CommonLogicProjection|rdfs:label"
msgid "Common Logic Projection"
msgstr "commun Logic projection"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CommonLogicProjection|skos:definition"
msgid "The projection-target value requesting the answer be rendered to the ISO Common Logic surface. One of several output targets a single contract may name at once; like every projection target it is a rendering request and never alters which entailments hold."
msgstr "Le projection-target valeur requesting the answer be rendered à the ISO commun Logic surface."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ComparativeRelationshipType|rdfs:label"
msgid "Comparative Relationship Type"
msgstr "comparatif relation type"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ComparativeRelationshipType|skos:definition"
msgid "A logic:RelationshipType whose instances are comparative relations grounded directly in the qualities of their relata, with NO mediating relator (heavier-than, older-than, the same colour as). The counterpart of gufo:ComparativeRelationshipType; the relation holds in virtue of the relata's logic:Quality values standing in an ordering within a logic:QualitySpace, not in virtue of any logic:Relator. Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. Contrast logic:MaterialRelationshipType, which is relator-founded."
msgstr "Un logic:RelationshipType dont instances sont comparatif relations ancré directly dans the qualities de their relata, avec NO mediating relator (heavier-than, older-than, the same colour as)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CompatibilityRule|rdfs:label"
msgid "Compatibility Rule"
msgstr "compatibilité règle"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CompatibilityRule|skos:definition"
msgid "A single local rule of the reasoning-contract feature model (constraint graph): it states that two facet values require each other, exclude each other, or together demand a particular resource value or decidability class. The supported-contract set is computed from these rules — a contract is supported iff it violates none. Authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust) and projected here as documentation; the projection is lossy (Principle 17). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:CompatibilityRule only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Un single local règle de the raisonnement-contract feature modèle (contrainte graphe): it states qui two facet values require each other, exclude each other, ou together demand a particular ressource valeur ou decidability class."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CompleteForFragment|rdfs:label"
msgid "Complete For Fragment"
msgstr "complet For Fragment"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CompleteForFragment|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:CompletenessStatus value for an answer complete for the certified fragment the contract pins — a conclusive evaluation even when the whole run did not otherwise complete. Wire value `complete-for-fragment`."
msgstr "Le logic:CompletenessStatus valeur pour an answer complet pour the certified fragment the contract pins — a conclusive evaluation even lorsque the whole run did not otherwise complet."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CompleteOverApproximation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Complete Over-Approximation"
msgstr "complet Over-Approximation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CompleteOverApproximation|skos:definition"
msgid "The projection may overgenerate but does not miss canonical answers: complete but possibly unsound. Every canonical answer appears, alongside possible spurious ones; the dual of logic:SoundUnderApproximation."
msgstr "Le projection peut overgenerate mais ne fait pas miss canonique answers: complet mais possibly unsound."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CompletenessStatus|rdfs:label"
msgid "Completeness Status"
msgstr "complétude Status"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CompletenessStatus|skos:definition"
msgid "The closed value class of the logic:resultCompleteness field: relative to what is the answer complete? Its individuals are logic:CompleteForFragment, logic:Incomplete, and logic:CompletenessUnknown. The set is closed; a misspelt value is rejected (design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md, §The reasoning result). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:CompletenessStatus only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le classe de valeurs fermée de the logic:resultCompleteness field: relative à what est the answer complet?"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CompletenessUnknown|rdfs:label"
msgid "Completeness Unknown"
msgstr "complétude inconnu"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CompletenessUnknown|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:CompletenessStatus value when completeness is not a defined question for the request — e.g. a genuine incomparable-entrenchment revision tie. Wire value `unknown`."
msgstr "Le logic:CompletenessStatus valeur lorsque complétude n'est pas a defined question pour the request — e.g."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConcreteIndividual|rdfs:label"
msgid "Concrete Individual"
msgstr "concret individu"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConcreteIndividual|skos:definition"
msgid "A logic:Individual located in spacetime — an endurant or a perdurant, something that bears qualities and stands in causal relations. The counterpart of gufo:ConcreteIndividual; the concrete sibling that complements logic:AbstractIndividual within logic:Individual. Every logic:Endurant and every logic:Perdurant is a logic:ConcreteIndividual (stated in prose, not as a subclass edge); it is the instance-level counterpart of logic:ConcreteIndividualType."
msgstr "Un logic:individu located dans spacetime — an endurant ou a perdurant, something qui bears qualities et stands dans causal relations."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConcreteIndividualType|rdfs:label"
msgid "Concrete Individual Type"
msgstr "concret individu type"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConcreteIndividualType|skos:definition"
msgid "A logic:Type whose instances are logic:ConcreteIndividuals — the type whose extension (via logic:instanceOf) is drawn from individuals located in spacetime (endurants and perdurants). The counterpart of gufo:ConcreteIndividualType; the umbrella over logic:EndurantType together with the type-of-perdurants. Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. Contrast logic:AbstractIndividualType."
msgstr "Un logic:type dont instances sont logic:ConcreteIndividuals — the type dont extension (via logic:instanceOf) est drawn de individuals located dans spacetime (endurants et perdurants)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConcurrencyControlProtocol|rdfs:label"
msgid "Concurrency Control Protocol"
msgstr "concurrence contrôle Protocol"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConcurrencyControlProtocol|skos:definition"
msgid "The IMPLEMENTATION MECHANISM that enforces a chosen isolation level — HOW a guarantee is achieved, never the guarantee itself. The closed value class of concurrency-control protocols. Its individuals are logic:StrictTwoPhaseLocking, logic:StrongStrictTwoPhaseLocking, logic:TimestampOrdering, logic:OptimisticValidation, and logic:MultiversionConcurrencyControl. The set is closed; a misspelt value is rejected. This is one of three distinct, separately-declared concurrency concerns that must NOT be conflated: a logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol is a mechanism, a logic:SerializabilityCriterion is a property of a history, and a logic:IsolationLevel is a guarantee strength — a protocol is how a guarantee is achieved, it is never the guarantee itself."
msgstr "Le IMPLEMENTATION MECHANISM qui enforces a chosen isolation niveau — HOW a guarantee est achieved, jamais the guarantee itself."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConcurrentComposition|rdfs:label"
msgid "Concurrent Composition"
msgstr "concurrent composition"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConcurrentComposition|skos:definition"
msgid "The concurrent-composition program combinator: two sub-programs advance together with their elementary steps interleaved over a shared path. The left sub-program is carried by logic:leftOperand and the right by logic:rightOperand. This is the COMPOSITION OPERATOR that states two programs run concurrently — it is DISTINCT from the three separately-declared concurrency correctness concerns the transaction layer keeps apart: (a) logic:SerializabilityCriterion is a correctness PROPERTY OF A HISTORY (conflict-serializability or view-serializability), (b) logic:IsolationLevel is the declared GUARANTEE STRENGTH a schedule must meet, and (c) logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol is the IMPLEMENTATION MECHANISM enforcing that strength. ConcurrentComposition names the structural operator; whether the resulting history is serializable, what isolation is declared, and which protocol enforces it are separately-declared facets. A logic:ConcurrentHistory carries the conflict edges whose cycle structure logic:SerializationAnomaly detects; logic:ConcurrentComposition names the program that gives rise to such a history. Typed APART from ordinary (at-a-state) conjunction — concurrent programs advance over a shared path segment, while a conjunctive formula holds at a single state."
msgstr "Le concurrent-composition program combinator: two sub-programs advance together avec their elementary steps interleaved sur a shared chemin."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConcurrentHistory|rdfs:label"
msgid "Concurrent History"
msgstr "concurrent historique"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConcurrentHistory|skos:definition"
msgid "The transaction history of a concurrent composition: the node that carries the logic:precedes conflict edges whose cycle structure logic:SerializationAnomaly classifies. The native concurrent evaluator DERIVES it from the interleaved execution of a logic:ConcurrentComposition's two legs (it may also be authored directly as a conflict graph). It is a HISTORY-LEVEL property bearer, kept DISTINCT from the logic:ConcurrentComposition PROGRAM that gives rise to it and from the logic:TransactionOutcome VERDICT of running that program — a history records which conflicting operations were ordered against which, not whether a path exists. Its serializability is judged against the logic:serializabilityCriterion it carries (default logic:ConflictSerializability); a cyclic conflict graph is surfaced as a logic:SerializationAnomaly finding, never silently linearized and never a logical contradiction within a state."
msgstr "Le transaction historique de a concurrent composition: the nœud qui porte the logic:precedes conflit edges dont cycle structure logic:SerializationAnomaly classifies."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConditionalGoal|rdfs:label"
msgid "Conditional Goal"
msgstr "conditionnel objectif"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConditionalGoal|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:GoalExpressionKind for a goal whose target applies only when its logic:guardSituation holds; when the guard is false the goal prescribes nothing and its evaluation reflects does-not-apply rather than satisfied or violated. The single operand carries the guarded target sub-expression."
msgstr "Le logic:GoalExpressionKind pour a objectif dont target applies uniquement lorsque its logic:guardSituation holds; lorsque the guard est false the objectif prescribes nothing et its evaluation reflects does-not-apply plutôt que satisfied ou violated."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConditionalRangeAssertion|rdfs:label"
msgid "conditional range assertion"
msgstr "conditionnel plage assertion"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConditionalRangeAssertion|skos:definition"
msgid "A central record asserting that, on a target class, a focus node whose gmeow:-selector property carries a NAMED value must bind — through a second value property — an instance of a required type. It names the class with logic:conditionalRangeTarget, the discriminant property with logic:conditionalRangeSelector and its triggering value with logic:conditionalRangeSelectorValue, the constrained property with logic:conditionalRangeValue, and the demanded type with logic:conditionalRangeRequiredType; the native coherence gate joins them to raise a violation when the selector matches yet the value is not of the required type. Carries a logic:formalizes back-reference to the domain property whose prose it encodes."
msgstr "Un central record asserting that, sur a target class, a focus nœud dont gmeow:-selector propriété porte a NAMED valeur doit bind — par a second valeur propriété — an instance de a obligatoire type."


msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConfConsistent|rdfs:label"
msgid "Conformance Consistent"
msgstr "conformité cohérent"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConfConsistent|skos:definition"
msgid "The conformance-verdict value when a model exists and the conjecture is NOT entailed: the reduction premises ∧ ¬conclusion is satisfiable, so the axiom set is consistent and the entailment fails. The decided-negative outcome the coarse three-bucket view assigns to the TPTP SZS logic:SzsSatisfiable and logic:SzsCounterSatisfiable statuses and to the W3C mf:NegativeEntailment test kind. One of the two informative meet-elements of the logic:ConformanceVerdict lattice (with logic:ConfInconsistent), below the least-informative join logic:ConfIncomplete; the RDF image of the native runner verdict `consistent`."
msgstr "Le conformité-verdict valeur lorsque a modèle exists et the conjecture est NOT entailed: the reduction premises ∧ ¬conclusion est satisfiable, so the axiom set est cohérent et the implication fails."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConfIncomplete|rdfs:label"
msgid "Conformance Incomplete"
msgstr "conformité incomplet"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConfIncomplete|skos:definition"
msgid "The conformance-verdict value when the reasoner did not decide the problem — it gave up, exhausted its resource budget, or returned an explicit unknown. The decided-nothing outcome the coarse three-bucket view assigns to the TPTP SZS logic:SzsUnknown, logic:SzsGaveUp, logic:SzsTimeout, and logic:SzsResourceOut statuses. The least-informative join (⊤) of the logic:ConformanceVerdict lattice, above both logic:ConfInconsistent and logic:ConfConsistent, so a genuinely-undecided result is never silently read as a decided one; the RDF image of the native runner verdict `incomplete`. Kept strictly distinct from a native capability gap (an out-of-fragment construct is a hard-fail ledger row, not an incomplete swallowed into agreement)."
msgstr "Le conformité-verdict valeur lorsque the raisonneur did not decide the problem — it gave up, épuisé its ressource budget, ou returned an explicit inconnu."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConfInconsistent|rdfs:label"
msgid "Conformance Inconsistent"
msgstr "conformité incohérent"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConfInconsistent|skos:definition"
msgid "The conformance-verdict value when the conjecture is entailed / the axiom set has no model: the reduction premises ∧ ¬conclusion is UNSATISFIABLE. The decided-positive outcome the coarse three-bucket view assigns to the TPTP SZS logic:SzsTheorem, logic:SzsUnsatisfiable, and logic:SzsContradictoryAxioms statuses and to the W3C mf:PositiveEntailment test kind. One of the two informative meet-elements of the logic:ConformanceVerdict lattice (with logic:ConfConsistent), below the least-informative join logic:ConfIncomplete; the RDF image of the native runner verdict `inconsistent`. The coarse bucket is a lossy projection: it does not distinguish logic:SzsContradictoryAxioms from logic:SzsUnsatisfiable, so the verbatim token is preserved as provenance via logic:rawStatusToken (design/LOGIC-CONFORMANCE.md, the external FOL soundness oracle)."
msgstr "Le conformité-verdict valeur lorsque the conjecture est entailed / the axiom set possède no modèle: the reduction premises ∧ ¬conclusion est UNSATISFIABLE."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConflictSerializability|rdfs:label"
msgid "Conflict Serializability"
msgstr "conflit Serializability"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConflictSerializability|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:SerializabilityCriterion value satisfied when an equivalent serial order exists that is reachable from the history by swapping only non-conflicting operations — no swap of a pair of conflicting operations is required. A history property, not a protocol. Contrast logic:ViewSerializability."
msgstr "Le logic:SerializabilityCriterion valeur satisfied lorsque an equivalent sériel order exists qui est reachable de the historique par swapping uniquement non-conflicting operations — no swap de a pair de conflicting operations est obligatoire."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConformanceVerdict|rdfs:label"
msgid "Conformance Verdict"
msgstr "conformité verdict"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConformanceVerdict|skos:definition"
msgid "The closed, three-valued lattice of external-corpus conformance outcomes: the result a conformance comparison receives when a native verdict is graded against a community-decided ground truth. Its three named individuals are logic:ConfInconsistent (entailment holds / no model), logic:ConfConsistent (a model exists / entailment fails), and logic:ConfIncomplete (the reasoner did not decide) — the last being the least-informative join (⊤) so an undecided result never masquerades as a decided one. The RDF image of the native runner's verdict-status value, and the target of the SZS-status and W3C manifest-kind alignment; the SZS→verdict collapse is a declared lossy projection (logic:SoundUnderApproximation) that this closed lattice makes machine-checkable. The set is closed, so a misspelt verdict names no declared value and is rejected rather than silently accepted, mirroring logic:EmergenceVerdict and logic:ConstraintVerdict (design/LOGIC-CONFORMANCE.md, the two orthogonal correctness axes)."
msgstr "Le closed, three-valued lattice de external-corpus conformité outcomes: the résultat a conformité comparison receives lorsque a native verdict est graded contre a community-decided ground vérité."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Conjecture|rdfs:label"
msgid "Conjecture"
msgstr "conjecture"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Conjecture|skos:definition"
msgid "A named, standpoint-scoped candidate formula under active epistemic test: the dynamic, testable specialization of the logic:FormalizationCandidate spine (rdfs:subClassOf logic:FormalizationCandidate). Because it subclasses the candidate, a conjecture carries all eight universal candidate carriers (logic:candidateSourceHash, logic:candidateExtractionProvenance, logic:candidateScope, logic:candidateContract, logic:candidateCategory, logic:candidateLifecycle, logic:candidateProjectionBehavior, logic:candidateSemanticRisk); what specializes it is that its positive/negative cases are ENGINE-PRODUCED (via a scoped reasoning run recorded through logic:verdictProvenance) rather than reviewer-asserted. Its verdict is always scoped to a single reified standpoint (logic:conjectureStandpoint, REQUIRED — Principle 9 refuses a global-false verdict), and it carries an EPISTEMIC lifecycle (logic:conjectureLifecycleState: open / corroborated / refuted-in-standpoint / withdrawn) ORTHOGONAL to the GOVERNANCE lifecycle it inherits from the candidate (logic:candidateLifecycle). Conclusiveness reuses the existing logic:DischargeVerdict value class (logic:conjectureDischargeVerdict), never a freshly minted notion: a conclusive independence carries logic:ObligationDischarged, a budget-exhausted or fragment-gap run carries logic:ObligationUnknown. The conjectured formula is tested symmetrically against its constructed strong negation as two INDEPENDENT legs — support for the formula (the standpoint's KB entails it) and support for its negation (the KB refutes it, decided by the inconsistency of asserting the formula) — so a KB that entails BOTH the formula AND its negation from one standpoint yields the Belnap glut logic:InfoBoth, a within-standpoint contradiction LOCALIZED to the candidate proposition (a genuine refutation still carrying a concrete logic:ContradictionWitness), whereas a KB contradictory for reasons UNRELATED to the candidate cannot host a meaningful test at all. A refutation names a concrete logic:ContradictionWitness, and the two symmetric promotion legs feed a corroborated formula back as a canonical-axiom candidate (logic:conjecturePromotionCandidate) and a robustly-refuted formula forward as a logic:NonEntailmentObligation candidate (logic:antiConjectureObligationCandidate) (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the conjecture-and-refutation section)."
msgstr "Un named, point de vue-scoped candidat formule sous active épistémique test: the dynamic, testable specialization de the logic:FormalizationCandidate spine (rdfs:subClassOf logic:FormalizationCandidate)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConjectureCorroborated|rdfs:label"
msgid "Corroborated"
msgstr "Corroborated"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConjectureCorroborated|skos:definition"
msgid "The epistemic state of a conjecture whose formula was Supported (Belnap true) from its standpoint: the symmetric test found for the formula and no counterexample. Corroboration is provisional support, never proof — a corroborated formula becomes eligible for the positive promotion leg (logic:conjecturePromotionCandidate to a canonical-axiom candidate), still gated through review. Wire value `corroborated`."
msgstr "Le épistémique état de a conjecture dont formule was Supported (Belnap true) de its point de vue: the symmetric test found pour the formule et no contre-exemple."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConjectureLifecycleState|rdfs:label"
msgid "Conjecture Lifecycle State"
msgstr "conjecture cycle de vie état"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConjectureLifecycleState|skos:definition"
msgid "The closed four-member value class of the logic:conjectureLifecycleState facet: the EPISTEMIC state a logic:Conjecture occupies, ORTHOGONAL to the GOVERNANCE lifecycle (logic:CandidateLifecycleState) it inherits from the candidate spine — Principle 9 refuses to collapse two distinct axes into one. Its individuals are logic:ConjectureOpen, logic:ConjectureCorroborated, logic:ConjectureRefutedInStandpoint and logic:ConjectureWithdrawn, each projected from a Belnap truth-value origin (Supported becomes Corroborated; Opposed or Both becomes RefutedInStandpoint; Neither-conclusive becomes Open carrying logic:ObligationDischarged; Undetermined or BudgetExhausted becomes Open carrying logic:ObligationUnknown; Withdrawn is an author action, never engine-produced). The set is closed, so a misspelt state names no declared value and is rejected (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the conjecture-and-refutation section)."
msgstr "Le closed quatre-member valeur class de the logic:conjectureLifecycleState facet: the épistémique état a logic:conjecture occupies, ORTHOGONAL à the GOVERNANCE cycle de vie (logic:CandidateLifecycleState) it inherits de the candidat spine — Principle 9 refuses à collapse two distinct axes dans one."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConjectureOpen|rdfs:label"
msgid "Open"
msgstr "ouvert"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConjectureOpen|skos:definition"
msgid "The epistemic state of a conjecture whose symmetric formula / negation test was NOT conclusive in either direction: neither corroborated nor refuted. Two Belnap origins land here and are told apart by the carried logic:conjectureDischargeVerdict — a Neither-conclusive run (formula and negation both genuinely undecided within a complete fragment) carries logic:ObligationDischarged (conclusive independence), while an Undetermined or budget-exhausted run carries logic:ObligationUnknown (not proved absent, carried forward). A timeout NEVER reads as refuted. Wire value `open`."
msgstr "Le épistémique état de a conjecture dont symmetric formule / negation test was NOT conclusive dans either direction: neither corroborated nor refuted."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConjectureRefutationWitnessConstraint|rdfs:label"
msgid "Conjecture refutation-witness constraint"
msgstr "conjecture réfutation-témoin contrainte"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConjectureRefutationWitnessConstraint|skos:definition"
msgid "A closed-world integrity constraint: a logic:Conjecture in logic:ConjectureRefutedInStandpoint names at least one logic:conjectureRefutationWitness — the concrete logic:ContradictionWitness backing the refutation."
msgstr "Un monde fermé intégrité contrainte: a logic:conjecture dans logic:ConjectureRefutedInStandpoint nomme au moins one logic:conjectureRefutationWitness — the concret logic:ContradictionWitness backing the réfutation."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConjectureRefutedInStandpoint|rdfs:label"
msgid "Refuted In Standpoint"
msgstr "Refuted In point de vue"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConjectureRefutedInStandpoint|skos:definition"
msgid "The epistemic state of a conjecture whose formula was Opposed or Both (Belnap false or contradictory) from its standpoint: a concrete counterexample was found, forcing some individual to owl:Nothing. The refutation is scoped to the standpoint (Principle 9), never global-false, and MUST name a concrete logic:ContradictionWitness (logic:conjectureRefutationWitness, enforced by logic:ConjectureShape and verify.conjecture-refutation-witness-required). A robustly-refuted formula becomes eligible for the anti-conjecture promotion leg (logic:antiConjectureObligationCandidate to a logic:NonEntailmentObligation candidate forbidding the formula). Wire value `refuted-in-standpoint`."
msgstr "Le épistémique état de a conjecture dont formule was Opposed ou Both (Belnap false ou contradictory) de its point de vue: a concret contre-exemple was found, forcing some individu à owl:Nothing."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConjectureWithdrawn|rdfs:label"
msgid "Withdrawn"
msgstr "retiré"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConjectureWithdrawn|skos:definition"
msgid "The terminal epistemic state of a conjecture its author retired — a deliberate authoring action, NEVER an engine-produced verdict (a withdrawn conjecture carries logic:verdictProvenance logic:VerdictReviewerAsserted). Recorded rather than deleted, so the retirement and any partial evidence stay auditable. Distinct from refuted: withdrawal is a human decision to stop testing, not a found counterexample. Wire value `withdrawn`."
msgstr "Le terminal épistémique état de a conjecture its author retired — a deliberate authoring action, NEVER an engine-produced verdict (a retiré conjecture porte logic:verdictProvenance logic:VerdictReviewerAsserted)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConjunctiveGoal|rdfs:label"
msgid "Conjunctive Goal"
msgstr "conjonctif objectif"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConjunctiveGoal|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:GoalExpressionKind for a goal satisfied only when ALL of its logic:operand sub-expressions are satisfied. The conjunctive combinator of the goal algebra; co-equal counterpart of logic:DisjunctiveGoal."
msgstr "Le logic:GoalExpressionKind pour a objectif satisfied uniquement lorsque tous de its logic:operand sub-expressions sont satisfied."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Constraint|rdfs:label"
msgid "Constraint"
msgstr "contrainte"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Constraint|skos:definition"
msgid "An integrity condition whose violation is a finding, not a derivation: the node kind for a condition that detects bad data rather than producing new facts. Kept distinct from logic:DerivationRule so a check is never mistaken for a productive rule."
msgstr "Un intégrité condition dont violation est a finding, not a dérivation: the nœud kind pour a condition qui detects bad données plutôt que producing new facts."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConstraintBinding|rdfs:label"
msgid "Constraint Binding"
msgstr "contrainte liaison"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConstraintBinding|skos:definition"
msgid "The constraint-verdict value for a downward constraint that holds upon its target: under the declared logic:GovernanceRegime of a logic:DownwardConstraint, the named target is a proper part of the governing whole and the regime activates the constrained state (logic:activationBasis), and no declared override is borne by the target — so the whole's constraint binds the part. The verdict is strictly regime-relative: it is reached by negation-as-failure over the override derivation while the assessment still binds a declared regime, never as a bare 'unconstrained' default, and a different or stronger logic:GovernanceRegime may activate or quiet the same state under another constraint without contradiction. This is downward constraint, not material causation — the whole limits the part's permissible role/state, it does not produce the part. Contrast logic:ConstraintOverridden and logic:ConstraintUnknown (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Le contrainte-verdict valeur pour a downward contrainte qui holds upon its target: sous the declared logic:GovernanceRegime de a logic:DownwardConstraint, the named target est a proper part de the governing whole et the regime activates the constrained état (logic:activationBasis), et no declared override est borne par the target — so the whole's contrainte binds the part."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConstraintOverridden|rdfs:label"
msgid "Constraint Overridden"
msgstr "contrainte Overridden"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConstraintOverridden|skos:definition"
msgid "The constraint-verdict value for a downward constraint defeated by a declared exception: the logic:DownwardConstraint names an override (logic:constraintOverride) and the constrained target bears that override token (logic:bearsProperty), so the whole's constraint does not bind the part. The positive, derivation-grounded verdict, reached by an actual override-match rather than by negation; it settles before logic:ConstraintBinding so that an overridden constraint is never read as binding. Constraint, not causation: the override quiets a governing limit, it does not unmake a part. Contrast logic:ConstraintBinding (active and not overridden) and logic:ConstraintUnknown (no regime activates the state) (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Le contrainte-verdict valeur pour a downward contrainte defeated par a declared exception: the logic:DownwardConstraint nomme an override (logic:constraintOverride) et the constrained target bears qui override token (logic:bearsProperty), so the whole's contrainte ne fait pas bind the part."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConstraintUnknown|rdfs:label"
msgid "Constraint Unknown"
msgstr "contrainte inconnu"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConstraintUnknown|skos:definition"
msgid "The constraint-verdict value when the binding question cannot be posed: the logic:DownwardConstraint names a target that is a proper part of the governing whole, but no declared logic:GovernanceRegime activates the constrained state (no logic:constraintRegime, or the regime's logic:activationBasis does not carry the state), and no override is borne — so neither a binding (logic:ConstraintBinding) nor an override-defeat (logic:ConstraintOverridden) can be derived. The first-class third value, kept distinct from the other two so that an un-activated constraint is never silently read as binding — failure-to-activate is not constraint, and a regime-free constraint is unknown, not binding (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Le contrainte-verdict valeur lorsque the liaison question ne peut pas be posed: the logic:DownwardConstraint nomme a target qui est a proper part de the governing whole, mais no declared logic:GovernanceRegime activates the constrained état (no logic:constraintRegime, ou the regime's logic:activationBasis ne fait pas carry the état), et no override est borne — so neither a liaison (logic:ConstraintBinding) nor an override-defeat (logic:ConstraintOverridden) peut be dérivé."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConstraintVerdict|rdfs:label"
msgid "Constraint Verdict"
msgstr "contrainte verdict"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ConstraintVerdict|skos:definition"
msgid "The closed class of downward-constraint outcomes: the tri-valued result a logic:DownwardConstraint receives via logic:constraintVerdict. Its three named individuals are logic:ConstraintBinding (the whole's constraint holds upon the part under the declared regime), logic:ConstraintOverridden (a declared exception defeats it), and logic:ConstraintUnknown (no regime activates the constrained state). The set is closed, so a misspelt verdict names no declared value and is rejected rather than silently accepted, mirroring logic:EmergenceVerdict and logic:MereologyConstraint (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Le closed class de downward-contrainte outcomes: the tri-valued résultat a logic:DownwardConstraint receives via logic:constraintVerdict."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ContextAxis|rdfs:label"
msgid "Context Axis"
msgstr "contexte Axis"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ContextAxis|skos:definition"
msgid "The facet value class of one index axis of the multi-dimensional context facet. Context is multi-dimensional: a single result may be indexed simultaneously by world, standpoint, time, and path. Each logic:ContextAxis individual names one such axis; they coexist on one result rather than being alternative values of one slot."
msgstr "Le facet valeur class de one index axis de the multi-dimensional contexte facet."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ContradictionWitness|rdfs:label"
msgid "Contradiction Witness"
msgstr "contradiction témoin"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ContradictionWitness|skos:definition"
msgid "The RDF shape of the runtime refutation witness a conjecture test emits when it refutes the formula: the concrete counterexample that forced an individual to owl:Nothing. It names the offending individual (logic:witnessIndividual), the world IRI the contradiction was found in (logic:witnessWorld), and the set of premises that jointly entailed the contradiction (logic:witnessPremise, one serialized triple each, multi-valued). It is an ABox artifact — a produced fact about a specific reasoning run, not a constraint — and is present exactly when its conjecture is logic:ConjectureRefutedInStandpoint (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the conjecture-and-refutation section)."
msgstr "Le RDF forme de the runtime réfutation témoin a conjecture test emits lorsque it refutes the formule: the concret contre-exemple qui forced an individu à owl:Nothing."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ControlFlowEdge|rdfs:label"
msgid "Control-Flow Edge"
msgstr "contrôle-flux Edge"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ControlFlowEdge|skos:definition"
msgid "A reified control-flow edge between two process nodes — the canonical FLOW-GRAPH form of control flow, mediating a source node (logic:flowFrom) and a target node (logic:flowTo). Complementary to, NOT a duplicate of, the structured-program combinators (logic:Choice, logic:Iteration, logic:ConcurrentComposition, logic:Fallback): the combinators are the program-TREE form an interpreter walks, while a logic:ControlFlowEdge is the binary-edge form the DAG-workflow acyclicity certifier runs Tarjan SCC over. A graph carrying a logic:Iteration loop edge (or any back-edge) is outside the DAG fragment. Downstream reified control-flow relators such as gmeow:ControlFlow specialize this class. A Relator mediating two distinct relata (its flowFrom and flowTo nodes), satisfying the relator-mediation discipline."
msgstr "Un reified contrôle-flux edge entre two process nodes — the canonique flux-graphe form de contrôle flux, mediating a source nœud (logic:flowFrom) et a target nœud (logic:flowTo)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Correspondence|rdfs:label"
msgid "Correspondence"
msgstr "correspondance"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Correspondence|skos:definition"
msgid "A law-bearing, possibly-lossy, possibly-bidirectional alignment between a source pattern and a target pattern: the ninth node kind. It carries its morphism class on an ordered law-spine, its claimed laws with discharge status, the separated quantitative axes, FOL/SOL caveats, and standpoint indexing; its get and put legs are transaction programs while its caveat-and-relation envelope is meta-level and stays meta. It is the single kind cross-ontology alignment compiles into, and from which the SSSOM, EDOAL, FnO, SPARQL, and up-lift surfaces are generated lowerings. Fully specified in design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md."
msgstr "Un loi-bearing, possibly-lossy, possibly-bidirectional alignment entre a source pattern et a target pattern: the ninth nœud kind."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CorrespondenceLaw|rdfs:label"
msgid "Correspondence Law"
msgstr "correspondance loi"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CorrespondenceLaw|skos:definition"
msgid "The closed value class of the lens laws a logic:Correspondence can claim through a logic:LawClaim: logic:GetPut, logic:PutGet, logic:PutPut and logic:SectionLaw. Which laws are claimable is capped by the correspondence's logic:MorphismClass rung, and each claim carries a logic:DischargeVerdict. The set is closed, so a misspelt law names no declared value and is rejected (design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md, the ninth-node-kind section). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:CorrespondenceLaw only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le classe de valeurs fermée de the lens laws a logic:correspondance peut claim par a logic:LawClaim: logic:GetPut, logic:PutGet, logic:PutPut et logic:SectionLaw."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CorrespondenceRelation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Correspondence Relation"
msgstr "correspondance relation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CorrespondenceRelation|skos:definition"
msgid "The typed, closed value class of a logic:Correspondence's relation, on an ordered lattice rather than a free string: logic:Equiv ⊐ { logic:Subsumes, logic:SubsumedBy } ⊐ logic:Overlaps ⊐ logic:RelatedMatch, with logic:Disjoint the negative pole. From one authored relation the compiler derives the SSSOM predicate, the EDOAL relation symbol and the OWL-alignment-axiom strength, so the generated alignment artifacts cannot drift apart. The set is closed, so a misspelt relation names no declared value and is rejected (design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md, the relation-lattice section)."
msgstr "Le typed, classe de valeurs fermée de a logic:correspondance's relation, sur an ordered lattice plutôt que a free string: logic:Equiv ⊐ { logic:Subsumes, logic:SubsumedBy } ⊐ logic:Overlaps ⊐ logic:RelatedMatch, avec logic:disjoint the négatif pole."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CounterfactualAcceptanceWitness|rdfs:label"
msgid "Counterfactual Acceptance Witness"
msgstr "contrefactuel Acceptance témoin"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CounterfactualAcceptanceWitness|skos:definition"
msgid "The acceptance record that a Stratum-C counterfactual world was constructed and resolved to a deterministic outcome, executed natively by gmeow_logic::counterfactual::construct_and_resolve over the entrenchment ordering. It names, through logic:selectedByEntrenchment, the outcome the entrenchment ranking selected. The flagship producer runs the native resolution and pins the deterministic selected binding; this witness is the ontological twin the thin logic:CounterfactualAcceptanceWitnessShape gates. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:CounterfactualAcceptanceWitness only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le acceptance record qui a Stratum-C contrefactuel monde was constructed et resolved à a deterministic résultat, executed natively par gmeow_logic::contrefactuel::construct_and_resolve sur the entrenchment ordering."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CounterpartNonTransitivityObligation|rdfs:label"
msgid "counterpart must not become transitive"
msgstr "counterpart must not become transitive"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CounterpartNonTransitivityObligation|skos:definition"
msgid "The standing non-entailment obligation that cross-realm counterpart identity (gmeow:counterpartOf) stays non-transitive: it is symmetric but deliberately not transitive, so the foundation must never derive it (any derivation, transitive or otherwise, is forbidden — it is assertion-only). Discharged by syntactic reachability over the counterpart rule heads (no rule head produces the predicate). Guards the coreference slice (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, §Typed formalization governance)."
msgstr "Le standing non-implication obligation qui cross-realm counterpart identité (gmeow:counterpartOf) stays non-transitive: it est symmetric mais deliberately not transitive, so the foundation doit jamais derive it (any dérivation, transitive ou otherwise, est forbidden — it est assertion-only)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Crisp|rdfs:label"
msgid "crisp"
msgstr "crisp"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Crisp|skos:definition"
msgid "The target relationship is ontically sharp: the alignment either holds or does not, with no borderline cases. The determinacy of an equivalence or a clean subsumption."
msgstr "Le target relation est ontically sharp: the alignment either holds ou ne fait pas, avec no borderline cases."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CrossNodeConstraint|rdfs:label"
msgid "Cross Node Constraint"
msgstr "Cross nœud contrainte"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/CrossNodeConstraint|skos:definition"
msgid "Compact sugar for a cross-node co-occurrence / inequality constraint (P5): a logic:onClass target and two roles (logic:roleA, logic:roleB) that must, per logic:crossMode, either 'co-occur' (be present together) or 'differ' (never bind the same value). Expands to a canonical logic:Constraint whose integrity is the bi-implication (co-occur) or the join + inequality (differ, via the logic:termEqual filter relation). Frontend-only authoring shortcut."
msgstr "Compact sugar pour a cross-nœud co-occurrence / inequality contrainte (P5): a logic:onClass target et two roles (logic:roleA, logic:roleB) qui must, per logic:crossMode, either 'co-occur' (be present together) ou 'differ' (never bind the same valeur)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DagWorkflowContract|rdfs:label"
msgid "DAG-Workflow Contract"
msgstr "DAG-Workflow Contract"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DagWorkflowContract|skos:definition"
msgid "The named ReasoningContract that requests the DAG-workflow resource policy (logic:resourcePolicy logic:DagWorkflowResource), under which a loop-free logic:Plan is topologically schedulable and complete-for-fragment. It is a CONTRACT (a standing request on the Resource facet), NOT a logic:ReasoningPreset: a preset bundles a model-semantics selection, whereas this fixes only the execution-discipline (Resource) facet — the contract-not-profile doctrine, applied so the resource discipline is a facet a contract requests, not a semantic profile. The dogfooded build pipeline runs logic:executedUnderContract this contract; a cyclic plan resolves to `unsupported` with its offending edge named rather than being approximated to a nearby supported semantics."
msgstr "Le named ReasoningContract qui requests the DAG-workflow ressource politique (logic:resourcePolicy logic:DagWorkflowResource), sous qui a loop-free logic:plan est topologically schedulable et complet-for-fragment."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DagWorkflowResource|rdfs:label"
msgid "DAG-Workflow Resource"
msgstr "DAG-Workflow ressource"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DagWorkflowResource|skos:definition"
msgid "The resource execution policy of the DAG-workflow profile: it requires the plan's control/dataflow graph to be a loop-free (acyclic) DAG — no logic:Iteration and an acyclic logic:dataflowConsumes / flow-edge closure — so the schedule is a topological order with a hard termination guarantee, and the result reports logic:CompleteForFragment. Acyclicity is the universal structural guarantee certified here; a typed terminal discipline such as the build pipeline's single gmeow:kindSink is an additional per-surface constraint, not part of this graph-level certification. A specialization of the certified-fragment discipline of logic:CertifiedFragmentResource applied to process control flow rather than rule recursion; because resource is an execution policy holding independent properties together, a contract may carry both a DAG-workflow requirement and a budget at once. A plan outside the acyclic fragment is still valid canonically but resolves to `unsupported` under this policy, the offending edge disclosed by logic:dagCycleWitness — never silently truncated."
msgstr "Le ressource exécution politique de the DAG-workflow profil: it exige the plan's contrôle/dataflow graphe à be a loop-free (acyclic) DAG — no logic:itération et an acyclic logic:dataflowConsumes / flux-edge fermeture — so the schedule est a topological order avec a hard terminaison guarantee, et the résultat reports logic:CompleteForFragment."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DataFlowEdge|rdfs:label"
msgid "Data-Flow Edge"
msgstr "données-flux Edge"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DataFlowEdge|skos:definition"
msgid "A reified dataflow edge between two process nodes — the FLOW-GRAPH counterpart of the logic:dataflowConsumes property, mediating a source (producer) node via logic:flowFrom and a target (consumer) node via logic:flowTo. Use the property form (logic:dataflowConsumes) for a bare binary dependency and this reified form when an edge must carry its own attributes (the flowing entity, a guard, an order). Downstream reified dataflow relators such as gmeow:DataFlow specialize this class. A Relator mediating two distinct relata, satisfying the relator-mediation discipline. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:DataFlowEdge only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Un reified dataflow edge entre two process nodes — the flux-graphe counterpart de the logic:dataflowConsumes propriété, mediating a source (producer) nœud via logic:flowFrom et a target (consumer) nœud via logic:flowTo."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DatalogFragment|rdfs:label"
msgid "Datalog Fragment"
msgstr "Datalog Fragment"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DatalogFragment|skos:definition"
msgid "The formula-fragment facet value selecting the function-free, range-restricted Datalog class of formulae. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract; the decidable, terminating fragment more restrictive than logic:HornFragment (no function symbols) and the projection target for which least-model semantics is PTIME-data."
msgstr "Le formule-fragment facet valeur selecting the fonction-free, plage-restricted Datalog class de formulae."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DatalogProjection|rdfs:label"
msgid "Datalog Projection"
msgstr "Datalog projection"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DatalogProjection|skos:definition"
msgid "The projection-target value requesting the answer be rendered to a Datalog surface. One of several output targets a single contract may name at once; like every projection target it is a rendering request and never alters which entailments hold."
msgstr "Le projection-target valeur requesting the answer be rendered à a Datalog surface."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DeadlineWindowGoal|rdfs:label"
msgid "Deadline-Window Goal"
msgstr "Deadline-Window objectif"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DeadlineWindowGoal|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:GoalExpressionKind for an achievement or maintenance target indexed to a bounding logic:deadlineWindow interval; the evaluation stays logic:GoalEvaluationUndetermined while the window is open and becomes conclusive once it closes. The single operand carries the windowed target sub-expression."
msgstr "Le logic:GoalExpressionKind pour an accomplissement ou maintien target indexed à a bounding logic:deadlineWindow interval; the evaluation stays logic:GoalEvaluationUndetermined while the window est ouvert et becomes conclusive once it closes."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DefaultNegation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Default Negation"
msgstr "Default Negation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DefaultNegation|skos:definition"
msgid "The negation-as-failure operator: a body literal that holds when its atom is not derivable. One member of the negation-operator set facet (which may also include logic:ExplicitNegation); a program using it requires at least the stratified-negation reading of the model-semantics facet rather than positive-Horn least-model semantics."
msgstr "Le negation-as-échec opérateur: a body literal qui holds lorsque its atom n'est pas derivable."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DefeasibleEvidence|rdfs:label"
msgid "Defeasible Evidence"
msgstr "Defeasible preuve"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DefeasibleEvidence|skos:definition"
msgid "A reified declaration that one relation or fact (logic:evidenceProperty) is DEFEASIBLE — defeater-blockable — evidence for another (logic:evidenceFor), carrying its logic:defeasibleStrength, and explicitly NOT a strict entailment. The support can come apart: the evidence may hold while the supported claim fails (and conversely), so the engine never materializes the supported edge from the evidence under the default reasoning — only a consumer opting into defeasible reasoning under a declared contract draws it, defeated when a declared defeater holds. The central recast of any 'X is evidence for Y, not X entails Y' relationship; its first instance is gmeow:hasSkill as defeasible evidence for gmeow:knowsAbout."
msgstr "Un reified declaration qui one relation ou fact (logic:evidenceProperty) est DEFEASIBLE — defeater-blockable — preuve pour another (logic:evidenceFor), carrying its logic:defeasibleStrength, et explicitly NOT a strict implication."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DeleteUpdate|rdfs:label"
msgid "Delete Update"
msgstr "Delete Update"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DeleteUpdate|skos:definition"
msgid "An elementary Transaction-Logic update of the `del(F)` kind: it retires one active support from the successor state while retaining the historical support in the path record. `del` is supersession, not physical erasure; state validity changes by moving to a successor snapshot, while displayability remains a separate disclosure decision."
msgstr "Un elementary transaction-Logic update de the `del(F)` kind: it retires one active support de the successor état while retaining the historical support dans the chemin record."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DeonticFramework|rdfs:label"
msgid "Deontic Framework"
msgstr "Deontic cadre"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DeonticFramework|skos:definition"
msgid "The normative framework: obligation, prohibition, permission, and recommendation evaluated against the deontic-ideal worlds of the typed context algebra, with issuer-indexed force (an ought is always according-to an authority, never bare) and serial deontic accessibility so the universal obligation condition is never vacuously satisfied (design/LOGIC-TELEOLOGY.md, the norms-and-deontic-force-over-goals section)."
msgstr "Le normative cadre: obligation, prohibition, permission, et recommendation evaluated contre the deontic-ideal worlds de the typed contexte algebra, avec issuer-indexed force (an ought est toujours according-to an authority, jamais bare) et sériel deontic accessibility so the universel obligation condition est jamais vacuously satisfied (design/LOGIC-TELEOLOGY.md, the norms-and-deontic-force-over-goals section)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DependencyModel|rdfs:label"
msgid "Dependency Model"
msgstr "Dependency modèle"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DependencyModel|skos:definition"
msgid "A probability model carrying an EXPLICIT joint distribution over a correlated set of logic:probability facts: where logic:FullIndependence factorizes as a product, a dependency model substitutes a declared joint table (logic:correlates names the correlated facts; logic:jointOutcome enumerates the joint outcomes with their logic:jointProbability). Facts outside the correlated set remain independent and factorize as usual. The declared joint outcomes must be exhaustive and sum to one. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:DependencyModel only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Un probability modèle carrying an EXPLICIT joint distribution sur a correlated set de logic:probability facts: où logic:FullIndependence factorizes as a product, a dependency modèle substitutes a declared joint table (logic:correlates nomme the correlated facts; logic:jointOutcome enumerates the joint outcomes avec their logic:jointProbability)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DerivationRule|rdfs:label"
msgid "Derivation Rule"
msgstr "dérivation règle"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DerivationRule|skos:definition"
msgid "A head entailed from a body: the productive subset of the IR, where satisfying the antecedents derives the consequent. Distinct from logic:Constraint, whose violation is reported as a finding rather than producing new assertions."
msgstr "Un head entailed de a body: the productive subset de the IR, où satisfying the antecedents derives the consequent."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DesignateTrueAndBoth|rdfs:label"
msgid "Designate True And Both"
msgstr "Designate True And Both"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DesignateTrueAndBoth|skos:definition"
msgid "The designated-value set that counts both true and both (the glut) as designated — i.e. as holding for the purpose of consequence. The designated set shared by FDE and LP in their standard presentations; what distinguishes FDE from LP is the admissible-valuation policy, not this designated set, so it is a formal error to attribute the FDE↔LP difference to the designated values."
msgstr "Le designated-valeur set qui counts both true et both (the glut) as designated — i.e."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DesignateTrueOnly|rdfs:label"
msgid "Designate True Only"
msgstr "Designate True Only"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DesignateTrueOnly|skos:definition"
msgid "The designated-value set that counts only true as designated. The designated set of K3 and classical logic; combined with the admissible-valuation policy and truth algebra it fixes which logic a contract selects, the three components varying independently."
msgstr "Le designated-valeur set qui counts uniquement true as designated."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DesignatedValueSet|rdfs:label"
msgid "Designated Value Set"
msgstr "Designated valeur Set"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DesignatedValueSet|skos:definition"
msgid "The facet value class of the designated-value set: which truth values count as designated (as holding) for the purpose of consequence. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract. It is one of the three independent components — truth algebra, admissible-valuation policy, designated values — that together separate FDE, LP, K3 and classical logic; collapsing any two of them erases exactly the choices that distinguish those logics. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:DesignatedValueSet only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le facet valeur class de the designated-valeur set: qui vérité values count as designated (as holding) pour the purpose de consequence."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Determinacy|rdfs:label"
msgid "Determinacy"
msgstr "détermination"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Determinacy|skos:definition"
msgid "The closed two-value axis recording whether the TARGET RELATIONSHIP a logic:Correspondence asserts is ontically crisp (logic:Crisp) or vague (logic:Vague). It is separate from logic:confidence: 'similar but not quite' is logic:Vague determinacy with a logic:AffineCorrespondence class, NOT a low-confidence logic:Equiv. Conflating the two destroys the distinction between an uncertain sharp claim and a confident fuzzy one. The set is closed, so a misspelt value names no declared determinacy and is rejected (design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md, the quantitative-and-contextual-axes section)."
msgstr "Le closed two-valeur axis recording whether the TARGET relation a logic:correspondance asserts est ontically crisp (logic:Crisp) ou vague (logic:Vague)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Dialect|rdfs:label"
msgid "Dialect"
msgstr "Dialect"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Dialect|skos:definition"
msgid "A named sub-language of the canonical logic: IR, in the MLIR sense of a dialect with its own node verifiers and progressive lowering (not an LLVM-style substrate). The one F1 dialect is logic:RelationalCore, the logical-to-physical lowering waist between the full IR and the native execution engine."
msgstr "Un named sub-language de the logique canonique: IR, dans the MLIR sense de a dialect avec its own nœud verifiers et progressive lowering (not an LLVM-style substrate)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DimensionThreshold|rdfs:label"
msgid "Dimension Threshold"
msgstr "dimension Threshold"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DimensionThreshold|skos:definition"
msgid "One row of a logic:LadderProjectionProfile: a logic:projectsLadderEdge ladder property paired with the logic:sourceDimension it reads and the minimum logic:thresholdLevel an assessment on that dimension must clear (by the logic:levelAtOrAbove order) for the edge to be emitted. The gmeow:hasMastered rung is the only one with two rows — procedural competence and transfer — both of which must clear, so mastery of one narrow task no longer implies broad command of a subject. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:DimensionThreshold only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "One row de a logic:LadderProjectionProfile: a logic:projectsLadderEdge ladder propriété paired avec the logic:sourceDimension it reads et the minimum logic:thresholdLevel an évaluation sur qui dimension doit clear (by the logic:levelAtOrAbove order) pour the edge à be emitted."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DischargeBoundedCorpus|rdfs:label"
msgid "Bounded Corpus"
msgstr "Bounded Corpus"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DischargeBoundedCorpus|skos:definition"
msgid "The discharge condition holding when the obligation is explicitly bounded to a declared corpus or mutation-test space and exhaustive checking within that bound is complete. Named in the closed set but not yet engine-backed. Wire value `bounded-corpus`."
msgstr "Le acquittement condition holding lorsque the obligation est explicitly bounded à a declared corpus ou mutation-test space et exhaustive checking within qui bound est complet."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DischargeCertifiedFragment|rdfs:label"
msgid "Certified Fragment"
msgstr "Certified Fragment"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DischargeCertifiedFragment|skos:definition"
msgid "The discharge condition holding when the check runs within a certified complete fragment (e.g. a Datalog stratum or EL profile over which the chase terminates and is complete). Named in the closed set but not yet engine-backed. Wire value `certified-fragment`."
msgstr "Le acquittement condition holding lorsque the vérification runs within a certified complet fragment (e.g."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DischargeCondition|rdfs:label"
msgid "Discharge Condition"
msgstr "acquittement Condition"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DischargeCondition|skos:definition"
msgid "The closed five-member value class of the logic:obligationDischargeCondition facet: the condition under which a logic:NonEntailmentObligation's absence-of-proof is conclusively checkable. Its individuals are logic:DischargeCertifiedFragment, logic:DischargeFiniteClosure, logic:DischargeSyntacticReachability, logic:DischargeConservativeExtension and logic:DischargeBoundedCorpus. The foundation engine wires logic:DischargeSyntacticReachability and logic:DischargeFiniteClosure; the other three are named but not yet engine-backed, so an obligation declaring one of them is a hard error rather than a silent pass. The set is closed, so a misspelt condition names no declared value and is rejected (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, §Typed formalization governance)."
msgstr "Le closed five-member valeur class de the logic:obligationDischargeCondition facet: the condition sous qui a logic:NonEntailmentObligation's absence-of-preuve est conclusively checkable."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DischargeConservativeExtension|rdfs:label"
msgid "Conservative Extension"
msgstr "Conservative Extension"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DischargeConservativeExtension|skos:definition"
msgid "The discharge condition holding when a conservative-extension proof establishes the added axioms cannot introduce the forbidden conclusion. Named in the closed set but not yet engine-backed. Wire value `conservative-extension`."
msgstr "Le acquittement condition holding lorsque a conservative-extension preuve establishes the added axioms ne peut pas introduce the forbidden conclusion."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DischargeFiniteClosure|rdfs:label"
msgid "Finite Closure"
msgstr "Finite fermeture"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DischargeFiniteClosure|skos:definition"
msgid "The discharge condition holding when a finite materialized derivation graph is available and complete: the obligation is discharged by checking the forbidden predicate is absent from that closure. Engine-backed (the foundation chase over an adversarial fixture). Wire value `finite-closure`."
msgstr "Le acquittement condition holding lorsque a finite materialized dérivation graphe est available et complet: the obligation est discharged par checking the forbidden prédicat est absent de qui fermeture."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DischargeSyntacticReachability|rdfs:label"
msgid "Syntactic Reachability"
msgstr "Syntactic Reachability"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DischargeSyntacticReachability|skos:definition"
msgid "The discharge condition holding when a syntactic dependency/reachability analysis over the rule heads shows the forbidden predicate is unreachable — no rule head unifies with it, directly or through any chain of rule applications. Engine-backed (reachability over the foundation rule strata). Wire value `syntactic-reachability`."
msgstr "Le acquittement condition holding lorsque a syntactic dependency/reachability analysis sur the règle heads shows the forbidden prédicat est unreachable — no règle head unifies avec it, directly ou par tout chain de règle applications."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DischargeVerdict|rdfs:label"
msgid "Discharge Verdict"
msgstr "acquittement verdict"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DischargeVerdict|skos:definition"
msgid "The closed three-value class of the logic:obligationDischargeVerdict facet: the result an obligation check returns. Its individuals are logic:ObligationDischarged, logic:ObligationUnknown (carried forward, never 'proved absent') and logic:ObligationViolated. The set is closed, so a misspelt verdict names no declared value and is rejected (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, §Typed formalization governance)."
msgstr "Le closed three-valeur class de the logic:obligationDischargeVerdict facet: the résultat an obligation vérification returns."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Discipline|rdfs:label"
msgid "Discipline"
msgstr "Discipline"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Discipline|skos:definition"
msgid "A named OntoUML structural discipline a class can violate: the closed vocabulary of anti-patterns the foundation lowering checks (stereotype cardinality, identity overlap, free role, mixed rigidity, relator completeness). Its named individuals are the labels a logic:violation fact points at; the set is closed so a misspelt label names no declared discipline and is rejected rather than silently accepted."
msgstr "Un named OntoUML structurel discipline a class peut violate: the closed vocabulary de anti-patterns the foundation lowering checks (stereotype cardinality, identité overlap, free role, mixed rigidity, relator complétude)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Disjoint|rdfs:label"
msgid "disjoint match"
msgstr "disjoint match"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Disjoint|skos:definition"
msgid "The negative pole of the correspondence-relation lattice: source and view share no instances, an asserted non-alignment. Lowers to owl:disjointWith. Distinct from the mereological relation logic:disjoint (two entities sharing no part); this records that two aligned patterns are deliberately kept apart."
msgstr "Le négatif pole de the correspondance-relation lattice: source et view share no instances, an asserted non-alignment."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Disjunctive|rdfs:label"
msgid "Disjunctive"
msgstr "Disjunctive"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Disjunctive|skos:definition"
msgid "The residue shape tag for a formula in which a disjunction (logic:or) appears — a choice the single determinate body of a Horn rule cannot express. Disclosed when a Horn-fragment target carries such a formula as flagged unsupported residue."
msgstr "Le residue forme tag pour a formule dans qui a disjunction (logic:or) appears — a choice the single determinate body de a Horn règle ne peut pas express."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DisjunctiveGoal|rdfs:label"
msgid "Disjunctive Goal"
msgstr "Disjunctive objectif"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DisjunctiveGoal|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:GoalExpressionKind for a goal satisfied when ANY of its logic:operand sub-expressions is satisfied. The disjunctive combinator of the goal algebra; co-equal counterpart of logic:ConjunctiveGoal."
msgstr "Le logic:GoalExpressionKind pour a objectif satisfied lorsque ANY de its logic:operand sub-expressions est satisfied."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DisjunctiveRequirednessConstraint|rdfs:label"
msgid "Disjunctive Requiredness Constraint"
msgstr "Disjunctive Requiredness contrainte"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DisjunctiveRequirednessConstraint|skos:definition"
msgid "Compact sugar for a disjunctive-requiredness constraint (P3): a logic:onClass target and a set of logic:anyOf predicates, at least one of which is required. Expands to a canonical logic:Constraint ∀this. C(this) → (∃p1 ∨ … ∨ ∃pn). Frontend-only authoring shortcut. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:DisjunctiveRequirednessConstraint only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Compact sugar pour a disjunctive-requiredness contrainte (P3): a logic:onClass target et a set de logic:anyOf predicates, au moins one de qui est obligatoire."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Disposition|rdfs:label"
msgid "Disposition"
msgstr "Disposition"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Disposition|skos:definition"
msgid "A bearer-held tendency, power, or liability to manifest events of a characteristic type when triggered — a fragility, a solubility, a hazard's potential to harm — which remains fully real even while it never manifests. gUFO has no Disposition class and models such tendencies as a gufo:IntrinsicMode; logic: subsumes that by carrying the disposition as first-class, so an unmanifested tendency needs no counterfactual reification. A logic:Mode whose manifestations are logic:Events of the characteristic type (stated in prose, not as a subclass edge); the bearer relation is asserted with a domain property (Principle 5), never gufo:inheresIn."
msgstr "Un bearer-held tendency, power, ou liability à manifest events de a characteristic type lorsque triggered — a fragility, a solubility, a hazard's potential à harm — qui remains fully real even while it jamais manifests."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DownwardConstraint|rdfs:label"
msgid "Downward Constraint"
msgstr "Downward contrainte"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/DownwardConstraint|skos:definition"
msgid "The canonical relational construct of holonic governance: the downward (governing) face of a holon, a typed directed constraint a whole imposes on a named proper part — the whole limits which roles or states the part may take. This is downward CONSTRAINT, never material causation: the governing whole bounds the part's permissible state, it does not produce or compose the part. Reified with the role properties logic:constraintWhole, logic:constraintTarget, logic:constraintState, logic:constraintRegime, and logic:constraintOverride, and the engine derives its logic:constraintVerdict (logic:ConstraintBinding, logic:ConstraintOverridden, or logic:ConstraintUnknown). The constraint is structured and NON-TRANSITIVE by default (ME9): it applies to the explicitly named target and says nothing automatic about the target's own proper parts — there is no rule cascading the constraint down logic:properPartOf, exactly as no rule propagates logic:bearsProperty down it (mirroring logic:EmergenceAssessment / logic:HolonicPosition; design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Le canonique relational construct de holonic governance: the downward (governing) face de a holon, a typed directed contrainte a whole imposes sur a named proper part — the whole limits qui roles ou states the part peut take."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ElementaryUpdate|rdfs:label"
msgid "Elementary Update"
msgstr "Elementary Update"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ElementaryUpdate|skos:definition"
msgid "A single Transaction-Logic state-transition primitive over a path of WorldStore snapshots. Its two concrete forms are `ins(F)`, which makes a support hold in the successor state, and `del(F)`, which retires one active support in the successor state without deleting the historical assertion. Conflicting same-fact updates are resolved by the declared entrenchment ordering. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:ElementaryUpdate only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Un single transaction-Logic état-transition primitive sur a chemin de WorldStore snapshots."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EmergenceAssessment|rdfs:label"
msgid "Emergence Assessment"
msgstr "Emergence évaluation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EmergenceAssessment|skos:definition"
msgid "The canonical relational construct of emergence: a tri-valued assessment of whether a whole's property is reducible to its proper parts, always made relative to a declared logic:ReductionTheory. Emergence is assessed, never asserted — the assessment is reified with the role properties logic:assessmentWhole, logic:assessmentProperty, and logic:assessmentReductionTheory, and the engine derives its logic:assessmentVerdict (logic:Aggregate, logic:Emergent, or logic:EmergenceUnknown). Failure to derive a property from the parts under one theory is not proof of irreducibility: because the assessment records the theory it is relative to, a later, stronger theory can overturn an logic:Emergent verdict without contradiction. The convenient unary reading 'P is emergent' is the lossy projection of this assessment, exactly as logic:Holon projects logic:HolonicPosition (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Le canonique relational construct de emergence: a tri-valued évaluation de whether a whole's propriété est reducible à its proper parts, toujours made relative à a declared logic:ReductionTheory."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EmergenceUnknown|rdfs:label"
msgid "Emergence Unknown"
msgstr "Emergence inconnu"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EmergenceUnknown|skos:definition"
msgid "The emergence-verdict value when the reducibility question cannot be posed: the whole bears the property under assessment, but the logic:EmergenceAssessment declares no logic:ReductionTheory (no logic:assessmentReductionTheory), so neither a part-reconstruction (logic:Aggregate) nor a theory-relative non-reduction (logic:Emergent) can be derived. ME9's first-class third value, kept distinct from logic:Aggregate and logic:Emergent so that a genuinely unclassifiable assessment is never silently read as emergence — failure-to-derive is not irreducibility, and a theory-free assessment is unknown, not emergent (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Le emergence-verdict valeur lorsque the reducibility question ne peut pas be posed: the whole bears the propriété sous évaluation, mais the logic:EmergenceAssessment déclare no logic:ReductionTheory (no logic:assessmentReductionTheory), so neither a part-reconstruction (logic:agrégat) nor a theory-relative non-reduction (logic:Emergent) peut be dérivé."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EmergenceVerdict|rdfs:label"
msgid "Emergence Verdict"
msgstr "Emergence verdict"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EmergenceVerdict|skos:definition"
msgid "The closed class of emergence-assessment outcomes: the tri-valued result an logic:EmergenceAssessment receives via logic:assessmentVerdict. Its three named individuals are logic:Aggregate (part-reducible under the declared theory), logic:Emergent (borne by the whole but not part-reducible under that theory), and logic:EmergenceUnknown (the reducibility question cannot be posed). The set is closed, so a misspelt verdict names no declared value and is rejected rather than silently accepted, mirroring logic:MereologyConstraint (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Le closed class de emergence-évaluation outcomes: the tri-valued résultat an logic:EmergenceAssessment receives via logic:assessmentVerdict."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Emergent|rdfs:label"
msgid "Emergent"
msgstr "Emergent"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Emergent|skos:definition"
msgid "The emergence-verdict value for a genuinely emergent whole property: under the declared logic:ReductionTheory of an logic:EmergenceAssessment, the whole bears the property but it is not reconstructible from the parts — the theory does not carry it in its logic:reductionBasis, or no proper part bears it — so the property does not propagate down logic:properPartOf and is not entailed by the parts' properties. The verdict is strictly theory-relative: it is reached by negation-as-failure over the aggregate derivation, never as a bare 'unflagged' default, and failure to derive under this theory is not proof of irreducibility — a stronger logic:ReductionTheory may reduce the same property under a different assessment without contradiction. Contrast logic:Aggregate and logic:EmergenceUnknown (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Le emergence-verdict valeur pour a genuinely emergent whole propriété: sous the declared logic:ReductionTheory de an logic:EmergenceAssessment, the whole bears the propriété mais it n'est pas reconstructible de the parts — the theory ne fait pas carry it dans its logic:reductionBasis, ou no proper part bears it — so the propriété ne fait pas propagate down logic:properPartOf et n'est pas entailed par the parts' properties."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Endurant|rdfs:label"
msgid "Endurant"
msgstr "Endurant"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Endurant|skos:definition"
msgid "A continuant: an individual that persists through time and is wholly present at each moment of its existence, enduring through change rather than unfolding through it. The counterpart of gufo:Endurant and the bearer side of the endurant/perdurant divide; contrast logic:Perdurant, which has temporal parts. Substantials and aspects are both endurants."
msgstr "Un continuant: an individu qui persists par time et est wholly present at each moment de its existence, enduring par change plutôt que unfolding par it."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EndurantType|rdfs:label"
msgid "Endurant Type"
msgstr "Endurant type"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EndurantType|skos:definition"
msgid "A logic:Type whose instances are logic:Endurants — the type whose extension (via logic:instanceOf) is drawn from continuants. The counterpart of gufo:EndurantType; the type-of-endurants branch under which the sortal and non-sortal foundation meta-types (logic:Kind, logic:Phase, logic:Role, logic:Category, …) ultimately fall. Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. Contrast logic:Event and logic:Situation, which carry gUFO's EventType/SituationType roles per the down-projection."
msgstr "Un logic:type dont instances sont logic:Endurants — the type dont extension (via logic:instanceOf) est drawn de continuants."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EngineCapability|rdfs:label"
msgid "Engine Capability"
msgstr "Engine Capability"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EngineCapability|skos:definition"
msgid "A declared capability of a reasoning engine — the executional ability an actor must hold to execute a logic:ActionSchema, named as the object of logic:capability. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:EngineCapability only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Un declared capability de a reasoning engine — the executional ability an actor doit hold à execute a logic:ActionSchema, named as the object de logic:capability."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EngineCapability|skos:example"
msgid "logic:EngineCapability rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ."
msgstr "logic:EngineCapability rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EntrenchmentRevision|rdfs:label"
msgid "Entrenchment Revision"
msgstr "Entrenchment Revision"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EntrenchmentRevision|skos:definition"
msgid "The revision-policy value under which conflicting information is absorbed by an AGM-style belief revision driven by a declared epistemic-entrenchment ordering: the least entrenched beliefs are surrendered to restore consistency. Contrast logic:MonotonicRevision (nothing retracted) and logic:TruthMaintenanceRevision (justification-tracked retraction)."
msgstr "Le revision-politique valeur sous qui conflicting information est absorbed par an AGM-style belief revision driven par a declared épistémique-entrenchment ordering: the least entrenched beliefs sont surrendered à restore consistency."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EpistemicFramework|rdfs:label"
msgid "Epistemic Framework"
msgstr "épistémique cadre"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EpistemicFramework|skos:definition"
msgid "The knowledge, justification, and argumentation framework: doxastic accessibility (logic:doxasticallyAccessible), knowing-that that is factive only relative to a world and an epistemic standard, evidential warrant (logic:evidenceStrength), and defeasible argumentation resolved under a declared logic:ArgumentationSemantics with typed attacks. Factivity stays honest in a paraconsistent, world-indexed setting — knowing P in a world entails P in that world, never globally (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the argumentation-and-epistemic-standards section)."
msgstr "Le connaissance, justification, et argumentation cadre: doxastic accessibility (logic:doxasticallyAccessible), knowing-that qui est factive uniquement relative à a monde et an épistémique standard, evidential warrant (logic:evidenceStrength), et defeasible argumentation resolved sous a declared logic:ArgumentationSemantics avec typed attacks."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EqualityPolicy|rdfs:label"
msgid "Equality Policy"
msgstr "Equality politique"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EqualityPolicy|skos:definition"
msgid "The facet value class of the equality facet: when two terms are taken to denote one entity. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract. Its individuals range from RDF equality through explicit (asserted) equality to an optional unique-name assumption. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:EqualityPolicy only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le facet valeur class de the equality facet: lorsque two terms sont taken à denote one entity."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Equiv|rdfs:label"
msgid "equivalent"
msgstr "equivalent"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Equiv|skos:definition"
msgid "The top of the correspondence-relation lattice: the source pattern and the view pattern denote one and the same extension. Lowers to sssom:exactMatch and (when the logic:MorphismClass and logic:LawClaim set support it) owl:equivalentClass; the strongest claim, never licensed for a commitment-shifting bridge."
msgstr "Le top de the correspondance-relation lattice: the source pattern et the view pattern denote one et the same extension."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EvaluationCompleted|rdfs:label"
msgid "Evaluation Completed"
msgstr "Evaluation Completed"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EvaluationCompleted|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:EvaluationStatus value for a run that reached its natural end on the request — a conclusive evaluation. Wire value `completed`."
msgstr "Le logic:EvaluationStatus valeur pour a run qui reached its natural end sur the request — a conclusive evaluation."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EvaluationStatus|rdfs:label"
msgid "Evaluation Status"
msgstr "Evaluation Status"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EvaluationStatus|skos:definition"
msgid "The closed value class of the logic:resultEvaluation field (the computation axis): what the engine was ABLE to do. Its individuals are logic:EvaluationCompleted, logic:BudgetExhausted, and logic:EvaluationUnsupported. The set is closed; a misspelt value is rejected (design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md, §The reasoning result). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:EvaluationStatus only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le classe de valeurs fermée de the logic:resultEvaluation field (the computation axis): what the engine was ABLE à do."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EvaluationUnsupported|rdfs:label"
msgid "Evaluation Unsupported"
msgstr "Evaluation Unsupported"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EvaluationUnsupported|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:EvaluationStatus value for a request the engine has no defined procedure for (an unsupported contract, or a missing required model such as a probabilistic dependency model). Wire value `unsupported`; the information field is then logic:InfoNotEvaluated, never logic:InfoNeither."
msgstr "Le logic:EvaluationStatus valeur pour a request the engine possède no defined procedure pour (an unsupported contract, ou a missing obligatoire modèle such as a probabilistic dependency modèle)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Event|rdfs:label"
msgid "Event"
msgstr "Event"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Event|skos:definition"
msgid "A perdurant occurrence that happens in time and is composed of temporal parts: an action, a process, a happening that unfolds and is complete once it has occurred. Tokens it as an occurrence rather than an endurant; in the type-level world strata (risk, teleology, norms) the no-occurrence gate keeps reasoning over Event *types* without entailing any Event instance. Unitary: a proper temporal part of an event is not itself that event, and a completed (logic:Closed) event cannot vary — it bears no time-varying logic:Fluent (the change-asymmetry, logic:OccurrentChangeAsymmetry). An event is constituted by the process it is made of (logic:occurrentConstituent)."
msgstr "Un perdurant occurrence qui happens dans time et est composed de temporal parts: an action, a process, a happening qui unfolds et est complet once it possède occurred."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EvolutionMode|rdfs:label"
msgid "Evolution Mode"
msgstr "Evolution Mode"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/EvolutionMode|skos:definition"
msgid "The facet value class of the evolution facet: whether and how state changes over the course of reasoning. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract. Its individuals range from the static (one-state) default through state-transition to the Transaction-Logic transaction-path semantics; evolution is independent of the model-semantics facet, which is why state-change reasoning is a facet value, never a parallel profile. Commitment — whether a program's effects are committed or discarded — is a separate orthogonal facet (logic:ExecutionMode), not a value of this one: a program may be hypothetically executed (logic:HypotheticalExecution) under any evolution mode."
msgstr "Le facet valeur class de the evolution facet: whether et how état changes sur the course de raisonnement."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExactPreservation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Exact Preservation"
msgstr "Exact Preservation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExactPreservation|skos:definition"
msgid "The projection yields the same answers as the canonical model for the declared query class: neither misses canonical answers nor adds spurious ones. The strongest preservation polarity, claimable only for a certified subfragment."
msgstr "Le projection yields the same answers as the canonique modèle pour the declared requête class: neither misses canonique answers nor adds spurious ones."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExecutionMode|rdfs:label"
msgid "Execution Mode"
msgstr "exécution Mode"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExecutionMode|skos:definition"
msgid "The facet value class of the execution-commitment facet: whether a Transaction-Logic program's effects are committed or discarded. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract and ORTHOGONAL to the evolution facet — a program may be executed hypothetically under any logic:EvolutionMode, because commitment (commit vs. discard) and state-change shape are independent dimensions. Its individuals are logic:CommittedExecution (the default) and logic:HypotheticalExecution (the sandbox operator). The sandbox operator is DISTINCT from modal possibility (◇): ◇ is the standard translation over the appropriate typed accessibility relation — logic:epistemicallyPossible or logic:doxasticallyAccessible (an alethic or doxastic claim about what is possible), not over the bare logic:accessibleFrom superproperty — whereas hypothetical execution asserts a program can execute from here without committing; conflating them would let an execution sandbox masquerade as a statement about what is possible."
msgstr "Le facet valeur class de the exécution-engagement facet: whether a transaction-Logic program's effects sont committed ou discarded."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExistentialRulesFragment|rdfs:label"
msgid "Existential Rules Fragment"
msgstr "Existential Rules Fragment"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExistentialRulesFragment|skos:definition"
msgid "The formula-fragment facet value selecting the existential-rules (tuple-generating-dependency / Datalog±) class, admitting existential quantifiers in rule heads. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract; more expressive than logic:DatalogFragment (value invention) and the fragment over which acyclicity or guardedness conditions buy back decidability."
msgstr "Le formule-fragment facet valeur selecting the existential-rules (tuple-generating-dependency / Datalog±) class, admitting existential quantifiers dans règle heads."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExplicitEqualityPolicy|rdfs:label"
msgid "Explicit Equality Policy"
msgstr "Explicit Equality politique"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExplicitEqualityPolicy|skos:definition"
msgid "The equality-policy value under which two terms are one only when their identity is explicitly asserted (e.g. via owl:sameAs-style equality facts): no implicit unification beyond what is declared. Contrast logic:RdfEqualityPolicy (RDF node identity) and logic:UniqueNameEqualityPolicy (distinct names denote distinct entities)."
msgstr "Le equality-politique valeur sous qui two terms sont one uniquement lorsque their identité est explicitly asserted (e.g."


msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExplicitNegation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Explicit Negation"
msgstr "Explicit Negation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExplicitNegation|skos:definition"
msgid "The strong (explicit) negation operator: an atom is asserted false, distinct from being merely not derivable. One member of the negation-operator set facet — a program may legitimately use explicit negation and logic:DefaultNegation together — which records the permitted operator set, not a single chosen operator."
msgstr "Le strong (explicit) negation opérateur: an atom est asserted false, distinct de being merely not derivable."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExpressivenessBoundary|rdfs:label"
msgid "Expressiveness Boundary"
msgstr "Expressiveness Boundary"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExpressivenessBoundary|skos:definition"
msgid "The closed class naming which logical fragment a defining statement inhabits — the machine-readable first-order-vs-second-order axis of the loss ledger, distinct from logic:PreservationKind (answer polarity) and logic:FormulaShape (first-order constructs a Horn target cannot carry). Its individuals are logic:FirstOrder and logic:SecondOrder; the set is closed, so a misspelt value names no declared boundary."
msgstr "Le closed class naming qui logique fragment a defining statement inhabits — the machine-readable premier ordre-vs-second-order axis de the loss ledger, distinct de logic:PreservationKind (answer polarity) et logic:FormulaShape (premier ordre constructs a Horn target ne peut pas carry)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExternalSignal|rdfs:label"
msgid "External Signal"
msgstr "External Signal"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ExternalSignal|skos:definition"
msgid "A situation type the engine can learn of ONLY by external notification — a manual notification, a callback, a sensor reading, an external service response — never by computing it from the state. The thing a logic:NotificationWaitSchema logic:awaitsSignal: until the signal obtains (the engine is told), a wait on it is pending. It marks the descriptive-side input at the prescriptive-descriptive seam, distinct from a logic:precondition the engine evaluates over facts it already holds."
msgstr "Un situation type the engine peut learn de ONLY par external notification — a manual notification, a callback, a sensor reading, an external service response — jamais par computing it de the état."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FOLFragment|rdfs:label"
msgid "FOL Fragment"
msgstr "FOL Fragment"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FOLFragment|skos:definition"
msgid "The formula-fragment facet value selecting unrestricted first-order formulae. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract; the most expressive (and only semi-decidable) fragment, against which the Horn, Datalog, and existential-rules values are the decidability-bought restrictions."
msgstr "Le formule-fragment facet valeur selecting unrestricted premier ordre formulae."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Fallback|rdfs:label"
msgid "Fallback"
msgstr "Fallback"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Fallback|skos:definition"
msgid "The fallback program combinator: attempts the primary sub-program (logic:leftOperand); if it fails (the primary executional entailment does not hold from the current state), executes the alternate sub-program (logic:rightOperand). It is a PROGRAM combinator over the transaction layer path semantics, typed APART from action-level logic:compensation: a compensation undoes the EFFECT of an action that ran and reached an outcome, recovering from a realized nondeterministic outcome branch, while logic:Fallback is a STRUCTURAL OPERATOR that routes control to an alternate path when the primary program cannot succeed from the current state. The two sub-programs are binary, carried by logic:leftOperand (the primary) and logic:rightOperand (the alternate), reusing the same properties logic:SerialConjunction and logic:Choice use. A plan strong-cyclic success through recoverable failures is the quantification-level counterpart: logic:Fallback is the operator that makes recovery structurally expressible in the program body."
msgstr "Le fallback program combinator: attempts the primary sub-program (logic:leftOperand); si it fails (the primary executional implication ne fait pas hold de the current état), executes the alternate sub-program (logic:rightOperand)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FeasibilityStatus|rdfs:label"
msgid "Feasibility Status"
msgstr "Feasibility Status"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FeasibilityStatus|skos:definition"
msgid "The closed value class of the feasibility axis of a logic:GoalEvaluation: whether the goal is reachable from the situation it is judged against. Its individuals are logic:Feasible (a path to the goal exists), logic:Blocked (no path exists in the current situation but the obstruction may lift), logic:Infeasible (no path exists in any reachable situation), and logic:FeasibilityUnknown (the feasibility question has not been settled). The set is closed; a misspelt value is rejected. This axis varies independently of satisfaction, lifecycle, and goal-evaluation status — a goal may be partial in satisfaction, blocked in feasibility, and active in lifecycle at once."
msgstr "Le classe de valeurs fermée de the feasibility axis de a logic:GoalEvaluation: whether the objectif est reachable de the situation it est judged against."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FeasibilityUnknown|rdfs:label"
msgid "Feasibility Unknown"
msgstr "Feasibility inconnu"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FeasibilityUnknown|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:FeasibilityStatus value when the reachability question has not been settled — the engine has neither found a path nor proved none exists. The first-class fourth value, kept distinct from logic:Blocked so an unexamined goal is never silently read as obstructed."
msgstr "Le logic:FeasibilityStatus valeur lorsque the reachability question possède not been settled — the engine possède neither found a chemin nor proved none exists."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Feasible|rdfs:label"
msgid "Feasible"
msgstr "Feasible"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Feasible|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:FeasibilityStatus value for a goal a path can reach from the situation it is judged against — the goal is achievable. Contrast logic:Blocked (no current path, but the obstruction may lift) and logic:Infeasible (no path in any reachable situation)."
msgstr "Le logic:FeasibilityStatus valeur pour a objectif a chemin peut reach de the situation it est judged contre — the objectif est achievable."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FindingCategory|rdfs:label"
msgid "Finding Category"
msgstr "Finding catégorie"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FindingCategory|skos:definition"
msgid "The closed value class of a validator finding's KIND — an axis orthogonal to its severity, because not all findings are failures. Its individuals are logic:FindingDataShapeViolation, logic:FindingModelingDisciplineViolation, logic:FindingContradictionWitness, logic:FindingPermittedEpistemicConflict, logic:FindingUnsupportedSemanticFeature, logic:FindingIncompleteCheck, logic:FindingProjectionLoss, logic:FindingPolicyWarning, logic:FindingCorroboration and logic:FindingTransientChatter. The set is closed; a misspelt value names no declared kind and is rejected. The load-bearing case is logic:FindingPermittedEpistemicConflict: a disclosed, witnessed contradiction permitted by a glut-admitting contract is coherent and does NOT fail the gate; the mirror case is logic:FindingCorroboration, a native↔published agreement folded as non-blocking positive evidence rather than dropped; logic:FindingTransientChatter is the non-gating chatter kind for general-purpose logging witnesses (design/LOGIC-CONFORMANCE.md, §The coherence certificate)."
msgstr "Le classe de valeurs fermée de a validator finding's KIND — an axis orthogonal à its severity, parce que not tous findings sont failures."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FindingContradictionWitness|rdfs:label"
msgid "Finding Contradiction Witness"
msgstr "Finding contradiction témoin"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FindingContradictionWitness|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:FindingCategory for a within-world contradiction (a logic:InfoBoth glut) that the governing contract FORBIDS — an unpermitted, integrity-violating inconsistency. A failure. Distinguished from logic:FindingPermittedEpistemicConflict purely by the contract's logic:contradictionPolicy. Wire value `contradiction-witness`."
msgstr "Le logic:FindingCategory pour a within-monde contradiction (a logic:InfoBoth glut) qui the governing contract FORBIDS — an unpermitted, intégrité-violating inconsistency."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FindingCorroboration|rdfs:label"
msgid "Finding Corroboration"
msgstr "Finding Corroboration"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FindingCorroboration|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:FindingCategory for a native↔published AGREEMENT — the native reasoner's verdict matches the community-decided ground truth of an external-corpus case. NOT a failure and the exact opposite of a logic:FindingIncompleteCheck: it is positive corroborating evidence surfaced for the benchmark surface, coherent, and never blocks a logic:CoherenceCertificate. It is the honest, non-blocking kind an agreeing external-corpus comparison folds as, so agreements are retained as first-class findings rather than dropped. Wire value `corroboration`."
msgstr "Le logic:FindingCategory pour a native↔published AGREEMENT — the native raisonneur's verdict matches the community-decided ground vérité de an external-corpus case."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FindingDataShapeViolation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Finding Data-Shape Violation"
msgstr "Finding données-forme Violation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FindingDataShapeViolation|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:FindingCategory for a closed-world data-shape constraint breach — a SHACL shape an instance failed. A failure. Wire value `data-shape-violation`."
msgstr "Le logic:FindingCategory pour a monde fermé données-forme contrainte breach — a SHACL forme an instance failed."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FindingIncompleteCheck|rdfs:label"
msgid "Finding Incomplete Check"
msgstr "Finding incomplet vérification"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FindingIncompleteCheck|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:FindingCategory for a check that did not run to completion — a logic:BudgetExhausted or logic:Incomplete evaluation. Records that the search was bounded; it is the reason a bounded run yields a logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation rather than a logic:CoherenceCertificate. Not a failure of the data. Wire value `incomplete-check`."
msgstr "Le logic:FindingCategory pour a vérification qui did not run à completion — a logic:BudgetExhausted ou logic:incomplet evaluation."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FindingModelingDisciplineViolation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Finding Modeling-Discipline Violation"
msgstr "Finding Modeling-Discipline Violation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FindingModelingDisciplineViolation|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:FindingCategory for an ontology modeling-discipline breach — a structural/gUFO-tier rule the vocabulary itself violates, or an unsatisfiable class surfaced by reasoning. A failure. Wire value `modeling-discipline-violation`."
msgstr "Le logic:FindingCategory pour an ontology modeling-discipline breach — a structurel/gUFO-tier règle the vocabulary itself violates, ou an unsatisfiable class surfaced par raisonnement."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FindingPermittedEpistemicConflict|rdfs:label"
msgid "Finding Permitted Epistemic Conflict"
msgstr "Finding Permitted épistémique conflit"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FindingPermittedEpistemicConflict|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:FindingCategory for a disclosed, witnessed contradiction that a glut-admitting contract PERMITS — exactly the behaviour the paraconsistent contract anticipates. NOT a failure: it is coherent, surfaced for transparency, and does NOT block a logic:CoherenceCertificate. The load-bearing case for the principle that not all findings are failures. Wire value `permitted-epistemic-conflict`."
msgstr "Le logic:FindingCategory pour a disclosed, witnessed contradiction qui a glut-admitting contract PERMITS — exactly the behaviour the paraconsistent contract anticipates."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FindingPolicyWarning|rdfs:label"
msgid "Finding Policy Warning"
msgstr "Finding politique Warning"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FindingPolicyWarning|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:FindingCategory for a trust/policy advisory — an untrusted signer, a missing-but-not-required attestation, a soft governance note. Advisory, not a hard failure. Wire value `policy-warning`."
msgstr "Le logic:FindingCategory pour a trust/politique advisory — an untrusted signer, a missing-but-not-obligatoire attestation, a soft governance note."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FindingProjectionLoss|rdfs:label"
msgid "Finding Projection Loss"
msgstr "Finding projection Loss"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FindingProjectionLoss|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:FindingCategory for a construct a lowering could not carry exactly — a warning that an answer was produced through a projection whose preservation claim drops or approximates some constructs (the loss ledger). Not a failure; a fidelity disclosure. Wire value `projection-loss`."
msgstr "Le logic:FindingCategory pour a construct a lowering could not carry exactly — a warning qui an answer was produced par a projection dont preservation claim drops ou approximates some constructs (the loss ledger)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FindingTransientChatter|rdfs:label"
msgid "Finding Transient Chatter"
msgstr "Finding Transient Chatter"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FindingTransientChatter|skos:definition"
msgid "The closed CHATTER logic:FindingCategory for general-purpose logging witnesses — the ordinary note/info stream a run emits to narrate its own progress. Never a failure and never a coherence stance: it is transient bookkeeping that carries no evidential weight, contributes nothing to the gate, and can never block a logic:CoherenceCertificate. The home category for a Note or Info witness that records what happened without asserting anything about the data. Wire value `transient-chatter`."
msgstr "Le closed CHATTER logic:FindingCategory pour general-purpose logging witnesses — the ordinary note/info stream a run emits à narrate its own progress."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FindingUnsupportedSemanticFeature|rdfs:label"
msgid "Finding Unsupported Semantic Feature"
msgstr "Finding Unsupported Semantic Feature"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FindingUnsupportedSemanticFeature|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:FindingCategory for a construct the engine has no defined procedure for under the governing contract — a logic:EvaluationUnsupported outcome on a feature outside the certified fragment. A disclosure, not a defect of the data. Wire value `unsupported-semantic-feature`."
msgstr "Le logic:FindingCategory pour a construct the engine possède no defined procedure pour sous the governing contract — a logic:EvaluationUnsupported résultat sur a feature outside the certified fragment."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FirstOrder|rdfs:label"
msgid "First-Order"
msgstr "First-Order"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FirstOrder|skos:definition"
msgid "The expressiveness boundary of a defining statement authorable as a first-order logic:Formula (∀/∃ over individuals of the reified signature). First-order mathematical laws — continuity, connectedness, the T0–T4 separation axioms — sit here; the grounding peers author them as logic:Formula objects at this boundary."
msgstr "Le expressiveness boundary de a defining statement authorable as a premier ordre logic:formule (∀/∃ sur individuals de the reified signature)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FixedCollection|rdfs:label"
msgid "Fixed Collection"
msgstr "Fixed collection"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FixedCollection|skos:definition"
msgid "A logic:Collection with fixed membership: its members (via logic:memberOf) do not change over its existence, so gaining or losing a member yields a different collection — a specific deck of 52 cards, the founding signatories of a treaty. The counterpart of gufo:FixedCollection. Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. Because membership is invariant across worlds the membership relation reads rigidly; contrast logic:VariableCollection."
msgstr "Un logic:collection avec fixed membership: its members (via logic:memberOf) do not change sur its existence, so gaining ou losing a member yields a different collection — a specific deck de 52 cards, the founding signatories de a treaty."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FlagshipScenarioFailureClassConstraint|rdfs:label"
msgid "Flagship scenario failure-class constraint"
msgstr "Flagship scenario échec-class contrainte"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FlagshipScenarioFailureClassConstraint|skos:definition"
msgid "Requires every failure class named by a logic-slice flagship scenario to be a logic:LogicConformanceFailure or one of its subclasses."
msgstr "Requires chaque classe d'échec named par a logic-slice flagship scenario à be a logic:LogicConformanceFailure ou one de its subclasses."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Fluent|rdfs:label"
msgid "Fluent"
msgstr "Fluent"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Fluent|skos:definition"
msgid "A value or relation indexed to time (and world): a time-varying property whose truth changes across moments — an object's location, an account's balance, a temperature reading. The native temporal-fluent construct of the four-dimensional treatment (criticism 3), pairing with Principle-11 frame-relativity so each temporal value lives in an explicit reference system rather than as a bare literal."
msgstr "Un valeur ou relation indexed à time (and monde): a time-varying propriété dont vérité changes across moments — an object's location, an account's balance, a temperature reading."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ForbidGap|rdfs:label"
msgid "Forbid Gap"
msgstr "Forbid Gap"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ForbidGap|skos:definition"
msgid "The admissible-valuation policy that forbids the neither gap while admitting the both glut — every atom is at least true or false, but may be both. It carves out the Logic of Paradox (LP). FDE and LP share the designated set true,both; LP differs from FDE by forbidding the gap, not by its designated values — reducing the FDE↔LP difference to designated values is a formal error."
msgstr "Le admissible-évaluation politique qui forbids the neither gap while admitting the both glut — chaque atom est au moins true ou false, mais peut be both."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ForbidGapAndGlut|rdfs:label"
msgid "Forbid Gap And Glut"
msgstr "Forbid Gap And Glut"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ForbidGapAndGlut|skos:definition"
msgid "The admissible-valuation policy that forbids both the neither gap and the both glut, leaving exactly true and false. It carves classical logic out of the Belnap algebra; combined with logic:DesignateTrueOnly it recovers ordinary two-valued entailment."
msgstr "Le admissible-évaluation politique qui forbids both the neither gap et the both glut, leaving exactly true et false."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ForbidGlut|rdfs:label"
msgid "Forbid Glut"
msgstr "Forbid Glut"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ForbidGlut|skos:definition"
msgid "The admissible-valuation policy that forbids the both glut while admitting the neither gap — every atom is at most true or false, but may be neither. It carves out Strong Kleene logic (K3), the dual restriction to logic:ForbidGap; the difference between K3 and the gap-admitting logics lies in this admissible-valuation set, not in the designated values."
msgstr "Le admissible-évaluation politique qui forbids the both glut while admitting the neither gap — chaque atom est au plus true ou false, mais peut be neither."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ForbiddenPatternConstraint|rdfs:label"
msgid "Forbidden Pattern Constraint"
msgstr "Forbidden Pattern contrainte"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ForbiddenPatternConstraint|skos:definition"
msgid "Compact sugar for a forbidden-pattern constraint (P7): a logic:onClass target and a logic:forbiddenPredicate (optionally pinned to a logic:forbiddenValue). Expands to a canonical logic:Constraint ∀this. C(this) → ¬∃b. forbidden(this,b) (or the pinned-value form ¬ forbidden(this, value)). Frontend-only authoring shortcut. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:ForbiddenPatternConstraint only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Compact sugar pour a forbidden-pattern contrainte (P7): a logic:onClass target et a logic:forbiddenPredicate (optionally pinned à a logic:forbiddenValue)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FormalizationCandidate|rdfs:label"
msgid "Formalization Candidate"
msgstr "formalisation candidat"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FormalizationCandidate|skos:definition"
msgid "A typed, reviewable proposal to turn a prose constraint into a formal axiom: the governed unit of the prose-to-axiom transition. It carries its source-text hash (logic:candidateSourceHash), extraction provenance (logic:candidateExtractionProvenance), intended scope (logic:candidateScope) and reasoning contract (logic:candidateContract, ME1), its logic:FormalizationCategory, its logic:CandidateLifecycleState and reviewer decision (logic:reviewedBy), a positive competency case and a negative countermodel (logic:candidatePositiveCase / logic:candidateNegativeCase), any required logic:NonEntailmentObligation (logic:candidateNonEntailment), its projection behaviour (logic:candidateProjectionBehavior) and its logic:SemanticRiskClass. An LLM extraction always enters as a candidate, never directly as an accepted axiom; only a candidate promoted through review becomes canonical (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, §Typed formalization governance)."
msgstr "Un typed, reviewable proposal à turn a prose contrainte dans a formal axiom: the governed unit de the prose-to-axiom transition."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FormalizationCategory|rdfs:label"
msgid "Formalization Category"
msgstr "formalisation catégorie"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FormalizationCategory|skos:definition"
msgid "The closed eleven-member value class of the logic:candidateCategory facet: the kind of force a prose constraint was meant to carry. Its individuals are logic:CategoryEquivalenceDefinition, logic:CategoryNecessaryCondition, logic:CategorySufficientCondition, logic:CategoryIntegrityConstraint, logic:CategoryDerivationRule, logic:CategoryDefeasibleDefault, logic:CategoryTypicality, logic:CategoryRecommendation, logic:CategoryNonEntailmentObligation, logic:CategoryDeliberateOverlap and logic:CategoryDocumentationOnly. The set is closed and atomic (Principle 9: necessary and sufficient are two categories, not one), so a misspelt label names no declared category and is rejected rather than silently accepted (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, §Typed formalization governance)."
msgstr "Le closed eleven-member valeur class de the logic:candidateCategory facet: the kind de force a prose contrainte was meant à carry."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Formula|rdfs:label"
msgid "Formula"
msgstr "formule"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Formula|skos:definition"
msgid "A first-order formula node: the reified AST node a non-Horn logic: statement compiles into. A logic:Formula is a quantifier (carrying logic:forall or logic:exists over a body and one or more logic:quantifiedVariable bindings), a connective (logic:and, logic:or, logic:not, logic:antecedent with logic:consequent, or logic:iff over sub-formulae), or an atomic predication (logic:relation over ordered logic:argument terms). It is the unified full-FOL core of which Horn+NAF derivation rules are a recognized sub-fragment; the canonical RDF 1.2 serialization round-trips it losslessly, while weaker projections carry any formula they cannot express as flagged unsupported residue."
msgstr "Un premier ordre formule nœud: the reified AST nœud a non-Horn logic: statement compiles into."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FormulaFragment|rdfs:label"
msgid "Formula Fragment"
msgstr "formule Fragment"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FormulaFragment|skos:definition"
msgid "The facet value class of the formula-fragment facet: the syntactic class of formulae a rule set is admitted from. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract. Its individuals range from unrestricted first-order through Horn and Datalog to existential rules, fixing both expressivity and the decidability ceiling. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:FormulaFragment only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le facet valeur class de the formule-fragment facet: the syntactic class de formulae a règle set est admitted from."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FormulaShape|rdfs:label"
msgid "Formula Shape"
msgstr "formule forme"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FormulaShape|skos:definition"
msgid "The closed class of first-order shape tags a Horn-fragment projection target discloses when it cannot represent a logic:Formula. Each individual names one construct that pushes a formula beyond the binary Horn+NAF fragment, so the loss ledger records which constructs were carried-and-flagged in the canonical logic: layer instead of one opaque note. The set is closed — its individuals are logic:Disjunctive, logic:Nested, logic:Quantified, logic:StrongNegation, and logic:Variadic — so a misspelt tag names no declared value."
msgstr "Le closed class de premier ordre forme tags a Horn-fragment projection target discloses lorsque it ne peut pas represent a logic:formule."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FreeRole|rdfs:label"
msgid "Free Role"
msgstr "Free Role"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FreeRole|skos:definition"
msgid "The OntoUML FreeRole anti-pattern: an anti-rigid sortal (Role or Phase) must specialize a rigid sortal from which to inherit a principle of identity. An anti-rigid sortal with no rigid (Kind/SubKind) ancestor violates it. One half of the lowering of reasoning_lint.anti_rigidity_discipline."
msgstr "Le OntoUML FreeRole anti-pattern: an anti-rigid sortal (Role ou Phase) doit specialize a rigid sortal de qui à inherit a principle de identité."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FreshnessGuard|rdfs:label"
msgid "Freshness Guard"
msgstr "fraîcheur Guard"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FreshnessGuard|skos:definition"
msgid "A valid-time currency guard on an action-schema precondition. It declares that the datum supporting a logic:precondition (via logic:guardsPrecondition) is relied upon only when it passes TWO INDEPENDENT valid-time axes. (1) AGE HORIZON: the datum's age — the span from its logic:datumRecordedAt to the probe's logic:decisionTime — is within a declared logic:freshnessHorizon (an xsd:duration ceiling on how OLD the value may be). (2) EXPLICIT VALID-TIME WINDOW: when the guard declares a logic:freshnessWindow, the probe's logic:decisionTime must fall inside the closed absolute interval [logic:freshnessWindowStart, logic:freshnessWindowEnd] — the datum is authoritative only WITHIN that named bounding interval (e.g. 'the current episode'), regardless of how recently it was recorded. The two axes are ORTHOGONAL and neither implies the other: a datum can pass the age horizon yet fall outside the window, or vice versa. Each axis is OPTIONAL and imposes no constraint when absent (a guard may carry horizon only, window only, both, or neither). Outside either bound the datum is undetermined, not stale-but-used: the action gate yields logic:GateUndetermined rather than admitting on an out-of-window / out-of-date value or denying on a value that merely aged or is off-episode. This is GMEOW's native, canonical generalization of a decision-rule 'currency' annotation (max age → horizon) AND its 'time_window' annotation (an explicit named bounding interval → window) — the valid-time freshness discipline the typed context algebra applies, executed at the action gate."
msgstr "Un valid-time currency guard sur an action-schéma précondition."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FreshnessGuardWindowBoundsConstraint|rdfs:label"
msgid "FreshnessGuard window-bounds constraint"
msgstr "FreshnessGuard window-bounds contrainte"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FreshnessGuardWindowBoundsConstraint|skos:definition"
msgid "A closed-world integrity constraint: a logic:FreshnessGuard declaring a logic:freshnessWindow carries both a logic:freshnessWindowStart and a logic:freshnessWindowEnd — a half-declared window gates on an ill-defined interval."
msgstr "Un monde fermé intégrité contrainte: a logic:FreshnessGuard declaring a logic:freshnessWindow porte both a logic:freshnessWindowStart et a logic:freshnessWindowEnd — a half-declared window gates sur an ill-defined interval."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FullIndependence|rdfs:label"
msgid "Full Independence"
msgstr "Full Independence"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FullIndependence|skos:definition"
msgid "The well-known probability model under which every logic:probability fact is an independent Bernoulli variable — the ProbLog default, made explicit rather than assumed. The probability of a total choice is the product over the chosen facts of their probabilities times the product over the unchosen of their complements; a query's marginal is the sum of total-choice probabilities over the choices whose least Herbrand model derives it."
msgstr "Le well-known probability modèle sous qui chaque logic:probability fact est an independent Bernoulli variable — the ProbLog default, made explicit plutôt que assumed."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FunctionalComplex|rdfs:label"
msgid "Functional Complex"
msgstr "Functional Complex"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FunctionalComplex|skos:definition"
msgid "A whole whose parts play distinct functional roles — a car (engine, wheels, chassis), an organism (organs), an organization (departments): a complex object, not a mere collection of like members. The counterpart of gufo:FunctionalComplex; its parts relate to it via logic:properPartOf (mereological parthood) rather than logic:memberOf, and each part contributes a different function. Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. Contrast logic:Collection (uniform members) and logic:Quantity (homogeneous stuff)."
msgstr "Un whole dont parts play distinct functional roles — a car (engine, wheels, chassis), an organism (organs), an organization (departments): a complex object, not a mere collection de like members."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FuzzyMeasure|rdfs:label"
msgid "Fuzzy Measure"
msgstr "Fuzzy Measure"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/FuzzyMeasure|skos:definition"
msgid "The uncertainty measure carrying fuzzy (degree-of-truth) membership values. One member of the uncertainty-measure set facet, which may carry several measures at once; distinct from logic:ProbabilisticMeasure (a calibrated probability) and logic:WeightedRankingMeasure (a solver preference order)."
msgstr "Le uncertainty measure carrying fuzzy (degree-of-vérité) membership values."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GateAdmitted|rdfs:label"
msgid "Gate Admitted"
msgstr "Gate Admitted"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GateAdmitted|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:gateVerdict value for an action the gate admits: every precondition holds, every capability is available, every invariant is preserved, and every required resource is available."
msgstr "Le logic:gateVerdict valeur pour an action the gate admits: chaque précondition holds, chaque capability est available, chaque invariant est preserved, et chaque obligatoire ressource est available."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GateDenied|rdfs:label"
msgid "Gate Denied"
msgstr "Gate Denied"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GateDenied|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:gateVerdict value for an action the gate denies: a precondition, capability, invariant, or resource gate failed. The probe carries a logic:gateDenialReason naming the failing gate and, when declared, the logic:gateCompensation rollback."
msgstr "Le logic:gateVerdict valeur pour an action the gate denies: a précondition, capability, invariant, ou ressource gate failed."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GateProbe|rdfs:label"
msgid "Gate Probe"
msgstr "Gate Probe"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GateProbe|skos:definition"
msgid "A node pairing a logic:ActionSchema (via logic:probesSchema) with the state (via logic:probesState) the action-gate verdict is computed against, plus the capabilities the state makes available (logic:capabilityAvailable). The native evaluator emits a logic:gateVerdict — logic:GateAdmitted or logic:GateDenied — surfacing the precondition, capability, invariant-breach, and resource-exhaustion gates as recorded findings rather than silent passes."
msgstr "Un nœud pairing a logic:ActionSchema (via logic:probesSchema) avec the état (via logic:probesState) the action-gate verdict est computed against, plus the capabilities the état makes available (logic:capabilityAvailable)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GateUndetermined|rdfs:label"
msgid "Gate Undetermined"
msgstr "Gate Undetermined"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GateUndetermined|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:gateVerdict value for an action whose gate is neither admitted nor denied because the judgment is withheld on insufficient information — a single conclusiveness value with two causes. (1) A precondition datum fails its logic:FreshnessGuard on EITHER of two independent valid-time axes: (1a) the AGE HORIZON — the datum was recorded too long before the logic:decisionTime, its age exceeding the guard's logic:freshnessHorizon; or (1b) the EXPLICIT VALID-TIME WINDOW — the logic:decisionTime falls outside the closed [logic:freshnessWindowStart, logic:freshnessWindowEnd] interval the guard declares (an off-episode / out-of-window decision). Either way the datum is treated as undetermined rather than stale-but-usable, carrying a logic:gateUndeterminedReason that names the failing axis. The two axes are orthogonal: a datum may fail one and pass the other. (2) A logic:NotificationWaitSchema is still awaiting its logic:ExternalSignal: the engine has not been told the wait completed, carrying a logic:awaitingSignal witness. Both mirror the logic:GoalEvaluationUndetermined conclusiveness axis of goal evaluation: a judgment the evaluator declines to make on insufficient input rather than guessing — NOT a denial, since the datum may refresh or the signal may arrive."
msgstr "Le logic:gateVerdict valeur pour an action dont gate est neither admitted nor denied parce que the judgment est withheld sur insufficient information — a single conclusiveness valeur avec two causes."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GenericDependence|rdfs:label"
msgid "Generic Dependence"
msgstr "Generic Dependence"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GenericDependence|skos:definition"
msgid "A probability model for a GENERIC (unstructured) stochastic dependence between random variables: the lowering target for a math:MarkovKernel via math:probabilityModelLowering, whose conditional structure is not further factored into an explicit joint table (logic:DependencyModel) or a full-independence product (logic:FullIndependence). It records that a dependence exists without committing to its internal structure. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:GenericDependence only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Un probability modèle pour a GENERIC (unstructured) stochastic dependence entre random variables: the lowering target pour a math:MarkovKernel via math:probabilityModelLowering, dont conditional structure est not further factored dans an explicit joint table (logic:DependencyModel) ou a full-independence product (logic:FullIndependence)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GenericDependence|skos:example"
msgid "logic:GenericDependence rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ."
msgstr "logic:GenericDependence rdfs:isDefinedBy <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GetPut|rdfs:label"
msgid "GetPut"
msgstr "GetPut"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GetPut|skos:definition"
msgid "The lens law put(get(s), s) = s: getting a view from a source and immediately putting it back leaves the source unchanged. Claimable from the logic:WellBehavedLens rung upward; the acquisition-stability law."
msgstr "Le lens loi put(get(s), s) = s: getting a view de a source et immediately putting it back leaves the source unchanged."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GoalEvaluation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Goal Evaluation"
msgstr "objectif Evaluation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GoalEvaluation|skos:definition"
msgid "The reified, vantage-indexed record of whether a goal is met: one logic:GoalEvaluation per (goal, situation or world it is judged against, evaluator holding the judgment, time of judgment, criterion applied), identified by that tuple of subjects and attributed through gmeow:accordingTo. Its outcome is factored into independent axes rather than one collapsed label — logic:satisfactionStatus, logic:feasibilityStatus, logic:lifecycleStatus, logic:goalEvaluationStatus, and the logic:satisfactionDegree quantity — each varying independently. The binary gmeow:satisfiedBy edge is the conclusive projection of this record: an edge is generated from each evaluation whose satisfaction status is logic:Satisfied and whose goal-evaluation status is logic:GoalEvaluationCompleted, and a directly authored gmeow:satisfiedBy edge deterministically expands into a default such evaluation under the asserting vantage, so the flat and reified records never disagree. Two evaluators who disagree are two coexisting evaluations, each retained rather than reconciled (Principle 9)."
msgstr "Le reified, vantage-indexed record de whether a objectif est met: one logic:GoalEvaluation per (objectif, situation ou monde it est judged against, evaluator holding the judgment, time de judgment, criterion applied), identified par qui tuple de subjects et attributed par gmeow:accordingTo."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GoalEvaluationCompleted|rdfs:label"
msgid "Goal Evaluation Completed"
msgstr "objectif Evaluation Completed"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GoalEvaluationCompleted|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:GoalEvaluationStatus value for a goal evaluation that has reached a conclusive judgment. Together with satisfaction status logic:Satisfied it is the condition under which a gmeow:satisfiedBy edge is generated. A maintenance or avoidance goal reaches this only when its window closes (satisfied) or its target fails (violated)."
msgstr "Le logic:GoalEvaluationStatus valeur pour a objectif evaluation qui possède reached a conclusive judgment."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GoalEvaluationStatus|rdfs:label"
msgid "Goal Evaluation Status"
msgstr "objectif Evaluation Status"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GoalEvaluationStatus|skos:definition"
msgid "The closed value class of the goal-evaluation-completeness axis of a logic:GoalEvaluation: whether the evaluation has reached a conclusive judgment. Its individuals are logic:GoalEvaluationCompleted (a conclusive judgment), logic:GoalEvaluationUndetermined (not yet conclusive — a maintenance or avoidance goal whose window has not closed holds so far but is not yet conclusively satisfied), and logic:GoalEvaluationUnsupported (the evaluator has no defined procedure for the judgment). The set is closed; a misspelt value is rejected. DISTINCT from logic:EvaluationStatus, the engine-computation axis of a logic:ReasoningResult (what the engine was able to do): the two are orthogonal and must never be conflated — one factors a goal judgment's conclusiveness, the other a reasoning run's computational completion."
msgstr "Le classe de valeurs fermée de the objectif-evaluation-complétude axis de a logic:GoalEvaluation: whether the evaluation possède reached a conclusive judgment."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GoalEvaluationUndetermined|rdfs:label"
msgid "Goal Evaluation Undetermined"
msgstr "objectif Evaluation Undetermined"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GoalEvaluationUndetermined|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:GoalEvaluationStatus value for a goal evaluation not yet conclusive — most characteristically a maintenance or avoidance goal whose bounding window has not closed: holding so far is not conclusive satisfaction. Distinct from logic:GoalEvaluationUnsupported (no procedure exists): here the procedure exists but the judgment is open."
msgstr "Le logic:GoalEvaluationStatus valeur pour a objectif evaluation not yet conclusive — most characteristically a maintien ou évitement objectif dont bounding window possède not closed: holding so far n'est pas conclusive satisfaction."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GoalEvaluationUnsupported|rdfs:label"
msgid "Goal Evaluation Unsupported"
msgstr "objectif Evaluation Unsupported"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GoalEvaluationUnsupported|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:GoalEvaluationStatus value for a goal evaluation the evaluator has no defined procedure for — the judgment cannot be made under the applicable criterion. Distinct from logic:GoalEvaluationUndetermined (the procedure exists but the judgment is open)."
msgstr "Le logic:GoalEvaluationStatus valeur pour a objectif evaluation the evaluator possède no defined procedure pour — the judgment ne peut pas be made sous the applicable criterion."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GoalExpression|rdfs:label"
msgid "Goal Expression"
msgstr "objectif expression"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GoalExpression|skos:definition"
msgid "The typed IR term carrying the compositional structure of a goal's target so the engine can evaluate it compositionally, attached to a gmeow:Goal through logic:hasGoalCondition. Its node kind is one of nine variants: atomic (satisfied when a named situation type obtains), conjunctive and disjunctive (satisfied when all, or any, sub-expressions are), achievement (satisfied once the target first obtains along a path), maintenance (satisfied only while the target holds at every state of an interval, violated at the first failure), avoidance (the dual of maintenance — satisfied while a proscribed situation never obtains), optimization (directed at a measure, satisfied to the degree the measure is extremized rather than by a crisp boundary), conditional (a target applying only when a guard situation holds), and deadline-window (an achievement or maintenance target indexed to a bounding interval after which the window closes). Identity is STRUCTURAL: two expressions with the same node kind, operands, and bound situation type are the same term, so a goal condition is data the engine reads and writes rather than prose. The flat gmeow:hasGoal and conclusive gmeow:satisfiedBy edges are the surface views this richer form generates; projections that cannot hold the structure record the loss in the preservation ledger."
msgstr "Le typed IR terme carrying the compositional structure de a objectif's target so the engine peut evaluate it compositionally, attached à a gmeow:objectif par logic:hasGoalCondition."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GoalExpressionKind|rdfs:label"
msgid "Goal Expression Kind"
msgstr "objectif expression Kind"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GoalExpressionKind|skos:definition"
msgid "The closed value class of the node kind of a logic:GoalExpression — which of the nine compositional variants the expression is, read by the engine to evaluate it. Its individuals are logic:AtomicGoal (a named situation type obtains), logic:ConjunctiveGoal and logic:DisjunctiveGoal (all, or any, operand sub-expressions hold), logic:AchievementGoal (the target first obtains along a path), logic:MaintenanceGoal (the target holds at every state of an interval, violated at the first failure), logic:AvoidanceGoal (the dual — a proscribed situation never obtains), logic:OptimizationGoal (directed at a measure, satisfied to a degree rather than crisply), logic:ConditionalGoal (a target applying only when a guard situation holds), and logic:DeadlineWindowGoal (an achievement or maintenance target indexed to a bounding interval after which the window closes). The set is closed; a misspelt kind names no declared variant and is rejected."
msgstr "Le classe de valeurs fermée de the nœud kind de a logic:GoalExpression — qui de the nine compositional variants the expression is, read par the engine à evaluate it."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GovernanceRegime|rdfs:label"
msgid "Governance Regime"
msgstr "Governance Regime"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GovernanceRegime|skos:definition"
msgid "A declared scope within which a logic:DownwardConstraint is active, relative to which its logic:constraintVerdict is read. It carries, via logic:activationBasis, the constrained states it activates as binding — a constraint binds only when its constrained state is in the regime's basis. Governance is always regime-relative: the same whole may bind a part's state under one GovernanceRegime and leave it logic:ConstraintUnknown under another, and a binding can be quieted by a different regime without contradiction precisely because the constraint records which regime it is relative to. The holonic-governance analogue of a logic:ReductionTheory (which scopes the emergence calculus) and a logic:MereologyProfile (which scopes weak supplementation) — it scopes the downward-constraint calculus rather than asserting governance foundation-wide (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Un declared scope within qui a logic:DownwardConstraint est active, relative à qui its logic:constraintVerdict est read."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GroundedArgumentation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Grounded Argumentation"
msgstr "ancré argumentation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GroundedArgumentation|skos:definition"
msgid "The grounded Dung argumentation semantics: the unique, sceptical, least fixed point of the characteristic function — an argument is accepted only when every attack on it is defeated by an accepted argument. The argumentation-facet value that resolves conflict deterministically; contrast logic:PreferredArgumentation, which admits multiple maximal admissible sets."
msgstr "Le ancré Dung argumentation sémantique: the unique, sceptical, least fixed point de the characteristic fonction — an argument est accepté uniquement lorsque chaque attack sur it est defeated par an accepté argument."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GuardedImplicationConstraint|rdfs:label"
msgid "Guarded Implication Constraint"
msgstr "Guarded Implication contrainte"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/GuardedImplicationConstraint|skos:definition"
msgid "Compact sugar for a guarded-implication constraint (P2): a logic:onClass target, a logic:trigger predicate (optionally pinned to a logic:triggerValue), and one or more logic:requires companion predicates. Expands to a canonical logic:Constraint ∀this. C(this) ∧ trigger(this, …) → ∃ companion. Frontend-only authoring shortcut. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:GuardedImplicationConstraint only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Compact sugar pour a guarded-implication contrainte (P2): a logic:onClass target, a logic:trigger prédicat (optionally pinned à a logic:triggerValue), et one ou more logic:requires companion predicates."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Holarchy|rdfs:label"
msgid "Holarchy"
msgstr "Holarchy"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Holarchy|skos:definition"
msgid "The bounded logic:properPartOf strict partial order viewed as a nested whole/part structure — a holarchy in Koestler's sense. Because logic:properPartOf is transitive, asymmetric, and irreflexive, a holarchy is a directed acyclic graph (a DAG, not a strict ladder): an entity may be a proper part of several wholes along several paths. It is the structure over which a logic:HolonicPosition is read and logic:holonicLevel is measured (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Le bounded logic:properPartOf strict partial order viewed as a nested whole/part structure — a holarchy dans Koestler's sense."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Holon|rdfs:label"
msgid "Holon"
msgstr "Holon"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Holon|skos:definition"
msgid "The lossy unary projection of logic:HolonicPosition: an entity that, within some holarchy, is simultaneously a whole and a part — both a proper part of some larger whole and itself having a proper part. Holon-ness is never a bare property of the entity; it is a position occupied in a particular holarchy, context, interval, and path, so logic:Holon is the convenient, lossy projection of that relational logic:HolonicPosition, exactly as the standpoint-modality view projects finer axes (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section). Root wholes and atomic leaves are not holons."
msgstr "Le lossy unary projection de logic:HolonicPosition: an entity that, within some holarchy, est simultaneously a whole et a part — both a proper part de some larger whole et itself having a proper part."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/HolonIntegral|rdfs:label"
msgid "Holon Integral"
msgstr "Holon Integral"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/HolonIntegral|skos:definition"
msgid "The agency-verdict value for a holon that exhibits both Janus tendencies: under the declared logic:HolonicAgencyProfile of an logic:AgencyAssessment, the holon bears (logic:bearsProperty) both a logic:selfAssertiveBasis value (it asserts itself as a whole) and a logic:integrativeBasis value (it subordinates itself as a part) — Koestler's balanced holon. The positive, derivation-grounded verdict, reached by an actual two-face conjunction rather than by negation; the two faces are co-equal, neither privileged (Principle 9). Contrast logic:AutonomyDeficient and logic:IntegrationDeficient (one face collapsed) and logic:AgencyUnknown (neither evidenced) (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Le agentivité-verdict valeur pour a holon qui exhibits both Janus tendencies: sous the declared logic:HolonicAgencyProfile de an logic:AgencyAssessment, the holon bears (logic:bearsProperty) both a logic:selfAssertiveBasis valeur (it asserts itself as a whole) et a logic:integrativeBasis valeur (it subordinates itself as a part) — Koestler's balanced holon."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/HolonicAgencyProfile|rdfs:label"
msgid "Holonic Agency Profile"
msgstr "Holonic agentivité profil"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/HolonicAgencyProfile|skos:definition"
msgid "A declared profile of holonic agency that a holarchy may adopt, relative to which an logic:AgencyAssessment is made. It carries, via logic:selfAssertiveBasis and logic:integrativeBasis, the property-values that respectively evidence a holon's self-assertive (autonomy-as-a-whole) and integrative (subordination-as-a-part) tendencies — Koestler's two co-equal Janus faces, neither primary (Principle 9). Holonic agency is always relative to such a profile: it is a named profile a holarchy adopts, NOT a universal well-formedness rule every holon must satisfy — a bolt, a file-segment, or a process-phase needs no autonomy and is simply outside the profile. The Koestlerian-agency analogue of a logic:ReductionTheory (which scopes the emergence calculus) and a logic:GovernanceRegime (which scopes downward constraint) — it scopes the autonomy/integration calculus rather than asserting agency foundation-wide (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Un declared profil de holonic agentivité qui a holarchy peut adopt, relative à qui an logic:AgencyAssessment est made."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/HolonicFramework|rdfs:label"
msgid "Holonic Framework"
msgstr "Holonic cadre"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/HolonicFramework|skos:definition"
msgid "The compositional / systems-theory framework: the contextual, path-relative parthood of logic:HolonicPosition, the Koestlerian self-assertive/integrative assessment of logic:AgencyAssessment, emergence over a declared reduction theory, and non-transitive downward governance. Holon-ness is a position an entity occupies in a holarchy under a context over an interval, never a bare unary type (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Le compositional / systems-theory cadre: the contextual, chemin-relative parthood de logic:HolonicPosition, the Koestlerian self-assertive/integrative évaluation de logic:AgencyAssessment, emergence sur a declared reduction theory, et non-transitive downward governance."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/HolonicLevelIncoherence|rdfs:label"
msgid "Holonic Level Incoherence"
msgstr "Holonic niveau Incoherence"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/HolonicLevelIncoherence|skos:definition"
msgid "The coherence violation raised for a holon — an entity that occupies a holonic position (both a proper part of some whole and itself having a proper part) — that is DECLARED UNDER a logic:MereologyProfile (via logic:underMereologyProfile) yet occupies no logic:HolonicPosition. A holon's logic:holonicLevel is read off its logic:HolonicPosition, the canonical relational construct of which logic:Holon and a level are lossy projections; a profiled holon with no declared position has no path along which its compositional depth can be coherently measured, so its level is incoherent. It is enforced only within the profile a holon is declared under, never across all holons: a holon outside any logic:MereologyProfile is never charged, mirroring logic:WeakSupplementation. Parthood is profiled, not universal, and a holonic level is path-relative (recorded per path, e.g. as a min/max band), so a position is required only when a profile demands it. Note explicitly the non-conflation with the instantiation tower: logic:holonicLevel records mereological compositional depth in a whole/part DAG, whereas logic:orderedType is the HiLog deep-instantiation order numbering logic:instanceOf chains (an order-n type instantiates an order-(n+1) type); the two axes are orthogonal and must not be conflated. An entity high in the instantiation tower (via logic:instanceOf / logic:orderedType) but occupying no holonic position still fires this violation. Enforced by the stratified NAF rule in crates/logic/src/foundation.rs (C5; design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Le cohérence violation raised pour a holon — an entity qui occupies a holonic position (both a proper part de some whole et itself having a proper part) — qui est DECLARED UNDER a logic:MereologyProfile (via logic:underMereologyProfile) yet occupies no logic:HolonicPosition."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/HolonicPosition|rdfs:label"
msgid "Holonic Position"
msgstr "Holonic Position"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/HolonicPosition|skos:definition"
msgid "The canonical relational construct of holon-ness: an entity occupies a holonic position in a particular holarchy, under a particular context, over a particular interval, along a particular path (entity, holarchy, context, interval, path). Whether an entity is a holon is read off this position, never asserted of the entity alone; the unary logic:Holon is its lossy projection. It is reified with the role properties logic:positionEntity, logic:positionHolarchy, logic:positionContext, logic:positionInterval, and logic:positionPath, because the foundation relation is five-place and the arity-bounded reasoning surface carries it as an objectified position (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Le canonique relational construct de holon-ness: an entity occupies a holonic position dans a particular holarchy, sous a particular contexte, sur a particular interval, along a particular chemin (entity, holarchy, contexte, interval, chemin)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/HornFragment|rdfs:label"
msgid "Horn Fragment"
msgstr "Horn Fragment"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/HornFragment|skos:definition"
msgid "The formula-fragment facet value selecting Horn clauses (at most one positive literal per clause). Single-valued on a ReasoningContract; the rule fragment over which least-model semantics is well-defined and, for the function-free case, terminating — the base on which the positive-Horn, stratified-negation and procedural presets build."
msgstr "Le formule-fragment facet valeur selecting Horn clauses (au plus one positif literal per clause)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/HypotheticalExecution|rdfs:label"
msgid "Hypothetical Execution"
msgstr "Hypothetical exécution"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/HypotheticalExecution|skos:definition"
msgid "The execution-mode value realizing the sandbox/hypothetical operator: a transaction program is executed to test whether it WOULD succeed, with its effects discarded rather than committed. It asserts that a program can execute from here without committing, and is NOT modal possibility (◇) — ◇ is the standard translation over the appropriate typed accessibility relation, logic:epistemicallyPossible or logic:doxasticallyAccessible (an alethic or doxastic claim), not over the bare logic:accessibleFrom superproperty; the two share construction machinery but are separate typed operators with separate meanings. The sandbox operator of the Transaction-Logic design, kept apart from the alethic/doxastic possibility of the context algebra."
msgstr "Le exécution-mode valeur realizing the sandbox/hypothetical opérateur: a transaction program est executed à test whether it WOULD succeed, avec its effects discarded plutôt que committed."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Incomplete|rdfs:label"
msgid "Incomplete"
msgstr "incomplet"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Incomplete|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:CompletenessStatus value for an answer whose search did not exhaust the space (a budget, answer cap, or depth bound was hit, or a DL construct was undecided). Wire value `incomplete`."
msgstr "Le logic:CompletenessStatus valeur pour an answer dont search did not exhaust the space (a budget, answer cap, ou depth bound was hit, ou a DL construct was undecided)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/IncompleteClosure|rdfs:label"
msgid "Incomplete Closure"
msgstr "incomplet fermeture"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/IncompleteClosure|skos:definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a logic:ClosureAcceptanceWitness — the acceptance record of an EL→RL→DL reasoning closure — declares no logic:closureEntailedAtom, i.e. names no atom the closure entails beyond its asserted EDB. A closure that adds nothing is either trivial or truncated; the flagship's guarantee is that the native reason_all closure genuinely derives new entailed atoms, so a witness carrying none is ill-formed and the gate rejects it. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:IncompleteClosure only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le échec raised lorsque a logic:ClosureAcceptanceWitness — the acceptance record de an EL→RL→DL raisonnement fermeture — déclare no logic:closureEntailedAtom, i.e."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InconsistencyPreserving|rdfs:label"
msgid "Inconsistency Preserving"
msgstr "Inconsistency Preserving"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InconsistencyPreserving|skos:definition"
msgid "A canonical inconsistency appears as an inconsistency in the projection: the projection does not silently mask a contradiction present in the canonical model. The inconsistency-direction polarity guaranteeing canonical → projection visibility."
msgstr "Un canonique inconsistency appears as an inconsistency dans the projection: the projection ne fait pas silently mask a contradiction present dans the canonique modèle."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InconsistencyReflecting|rdfs:label"
msgid "Inconsistency Reflecting"
msgstr "Inconsistency Reflecting"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InconsistencyReflecting|skos:definition"
msgid "An inconsistency in the projection implies an inconsistency in the canonical model: the projection raises no spurious contradiction absent from the canonical model. The inconsistency-direction polarity guaranteeing projection → canonical soundness, dual to logic:InconsistencyPreserving."
msgstr "Un inconsistency dans the projection implies an inconsistency dans the canonique modèle: the projection raises no spurious contradiction absent de the canonique modèle."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/IndirectContributorNotAttributionObligation|rdfs:label"
msgid "indirect contribution must not become direct attribution"
msgstr "indirect contribution must not become direct attribution"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/IndirectContributorNotAttributionObligation|skos:definition"
msgid "The standing non-entailment obligation that a derived gmeow:indirectContributor edge stays EVIDENCE, never ENTAILMENT, of direct responsibility: the foundation must never derive gmeow:wasAttributedTo (asserted authorship, ownership, or accountability) from the generation chain that surfaces indirect contribution. Enforced by syntactic reachability over the rule strata (no rule head produces the predicate) and finite closure over the materialized derivation graph (the predicate appears in no DERIVED edge). Guards the provenance credit model against collapsing indirect production into direct responsibility."
msgstr "Le standing non-implication obligation qui a dérivé gmeow:indirectContributor edge stays preuve, jamais implication, de direct responsibility: the foundation doit jamais derive gmeow:wasAttributedTo (asserted authorship, ownership, ou accountability) de the generation chain qui surfaces indirect contribution."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Individual|rdfs:label"
msgid "Individual"
msgstr "individu"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Individual|skos:definition"
msgid "A particular: an entity that is NOT a logic:Type — it is instantiated by types (via logic:instanceOf) but has no instances of its own, sitting at the bottom of every instantiation chain (logic:orderedType 0). The counterpart of gufo:Individual; the root complementing logic:Type. Specialized by logic:ConcreteIndividual (in spacetime) and logic:AbstractIndividual (outside it). Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge."
msgstr "Un particular: an entity qui est NOT a logic:type — it est instantiated par types (via logic:instanceOf) mais possède no instances de its own, sitting at the bottom de chaque instantiation chain (logic:orderedType 0)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Infeasible|rdfs:label"
msgid "Infeasible"
msgstr "Infeasible"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Infeasible|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:FeasibilityStatus value for a goal no path can reach from any reachable situation — permanently unachievable, not merely currently obstructed. The strongest infeasibility reading; contrast logic:Blocked (the obstruction may lift)."
msgstr "Le logic:FeasibilityStatus valeur pour a objectif no chemin peut reach de tout reachable situation — permanently unachievable, not merely currently obstructed."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InfoBoth|rdfs:label"
msgid "Information Both"
msgstr "information Both"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InfoBoth|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:InformationState value when a proof AND a counterproof exist — a witnessed contradiction (glut) within one context, carried with its logic:contradictionWitness graph. Wire value `both`. A correct `both` is HIGH-assurance about a contradictory input, not a defect, and is local to its world — never globalized to owl:Nothing."
msgstr "Le logic:InformationState valeur lorsque a preuve AND a counterproof exist — a witnessed contradiction (glut) within one contexte, carried avec its logic:contradictionWitness graphe."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InfoNeither|rdfs:label"
msgid "Information Neither"
msgstr "information Neither"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InfoNeither|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:InformationState value when neither proof nor counterproof exists, established by a CONCLUSIVE evaluation (a completed run or a complete-for-the-fragment answer) — a real four-valued verdict. Wire value `neither`. NEVER interchangeable with logic:InfoUndetermined (no verdict reached) or logic:InfoNotEvaluated (the engine could not look)."
msgstr "Le logic:InformationState valeur lorsque neither preuve nor counterproof exists, established par a CONCLUSIVE evaluation (a completed run ou a complet-for-the-fragment answer) — a real quatre-valued verdict."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InfoNotEvaluated|rdfs:label"
msgid "Information Not Evaluated"
msgstr "information Not Evaluated"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InfoNotEvaluated|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:InformationState value when no information semantics were available — the engine COULD NOT look (an unsupported contract, or a missing required model such as a probabilistic dependency model). Wire value `not-evaluated`. NOT the conclusive logic:InfoNeither."
msgstr "Le logic:InformationState valeur lorsque no information sémantique were available — the engine COULD NOT look (an unsupported contract, ou a missing obligatoire modèle such as a probabilistic dependency modèle)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InfoOpposed|rdfs:label"
msgid "Information Opposed"
msgstr "information Opposed"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InfoOpposed|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:InformationState value when there is a counterproof and no proof — the FDE/paraconsistent evidence for the explicit negation. Wire value `opposed`."
msgstr "Le logic:InformationState valeur lorsque there est a counterproof et no preuve — the FDE/paraconsistent preuve pour the explicit negation."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InfoSupported|rdfs:label"
msgid "Information Supported"
msgstr "information Supported"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InfoSupported|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:InformationState value when there is a proof and no counterproof. Wire value `supported`. Provisional when the evaluation is not conclusive (logic:Incomplete); conclusive within the fragment otherwise."
msgstr "Le logic:InformationState valeur lorsque there est a preuve et no counterproof."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InfoUndetermined|rdfs:label"
msgid "Information Undetermined"
msgstr "information Undetermined"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InfoUndetermined|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:InformationState value when the evaluation did not reach a conclusive verdict — the search did not finish (budget exhausted), a partial-order tie, or a graded semantics with no discretization policy. Wire value `undetermined`. NOT the conclusive logic:InfoNeither."
msgstr "Le logic:InformationState valeur lorsque the evaluation did not reach a conclusive verdict — the search did not finish (budget épuisé), a partial-order tie, ou a graded sémantique avec no discretization politique."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InformationState|rdfs:label"
msgid "Information State"
msgstr "information état"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InformationState|skos:definition"
msgid "The closed value class of the logic:resultInformation field (the information axis): the four-valued Belnap verdict about the queried proposition plus two explicit non-results. Its individuals are logic:InfoSupported, logic:InfoOpposed, logic:InfoBoth, logic:InfoNeither (the Belnap four), logic:InfoUndetermined, and logic:InfoNotEvaluated. The three non-positive states are NEVER interchangeable: logic:InfoNeither requires a conclusive evaluation; logic:InfoUndetermined means no verdict was reached; logic:InfoNotEvaluated means the engine could not look. The set is closed; a misspelt value is rejected (design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md, §The reasoning result)."
msgstr "Le classe de valeurs fermée de the logic:resultInformation field (the information axis): the quatre-valued Belnap verdict about the queried proposition plus two explicit non-results."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InputInvalid|rdfs:label"
msgid "Input Invalid"
msgstr "Input Invalid"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InputInvalid|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:InputStatus value for an ill-formed request: no reasoning was attempted and the other four fields are vacuous. Wire value `invalid`."
msgstr "Le logic:InputStatus valeur pour an ill-formed request: no raisonnement was attempted et the other quatre fields sont vacuous."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InputStatus|rdfs:label"
msgid "Input Status"
msgstr "Input Status"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InputStatus|skos:definition"
msgid "The closed value class of the logic:resultInput field: was the request well-formed? Its individuals are logic:InputValid and logic:InputInvalid. The set is closed, so a misspelt value names no declared value and is rejected (design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md, §The reasoning result). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:InputStatus only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le classe de valeurs fermée de the logic:resultInput field: was the request bien formé?"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InputValid|rdfs:label"
msgid "Input Valid"
msgstr "Input Valid"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InputValid|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:InputStatus value for a request whose sources parsed and type-checked: reasoning was attempted. Wire value `valid`."
msgstr "Le logic:InputStatus valeur pour a request dont sources parsed et type-checked: raisonnement was attempted."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InsertUpdate|rdfs:label"
msgid "Insert Update"
msgstr "Insert Update"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InsertUpdate|skos:definition"
msgid "An elementary Transaction-Logic update of the `ins(F)` kind: it asserts one support into the successor state of a path. Insertion advances the path by materializing the support in the successor snapshot; it does not mutate the predecessor state."
msgstr "Un elementary transaction-Logic update de the `ins(F)` kind: it asserts one support dans the successor état de a chemin."


msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InstitutionMorphism|rdfs:label"
msgid "Institution Morphism"
msgstr "Institution Morphism"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/InstitutionMorphism|skos:definition"
msgid "A satisfaction-preserving morphism between theories presented as institutions: truth in the source maps to truth in the view, so logical alignment axioms (up to owl:equivalentClass when the rung allows) are licensed. The morphism kind of a faithful down-projection."
msgstr "Un satisfaction-preserving morphism entre theories presented as institutions: vérité dans the source maps à vérité dans the view, so logique alignment axioms (up à owl:equivalentClass lorsque the rung allows) sont licensed."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/IntegrationDeficient|rdfs:label"
msgid "Integration Deficient"
msgstr "Integration déficient"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/IntegrationDeficient|skos:definition"
msgid "The agency-verdict value for the second Koestlerian pathology — a 'whole' that refuses to integrate: under the declared logic:HolonicAgencyProfile, the holon bears an logic:selfAssertiveBasis value (it asserts itself as a whole) but bears no logic:integrativeBasis value, so its integrative (subordination-as-a-part) face has collapsed. Reached by negation-as-failure over the integrative marker while the self-assertive marker holds, so the verdict is profile-relative, never a bare default. The co-equal counterpart of logic:AutonomyDeficient (the opposite collapse); contrast logic:HolonIntegral (both faces) and logic:AgencyUnknown (neither evidenced) (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Le agentivité-verdict valeur pour the second Koestlerian pathology — a 'whole' qui refuses à integrate: sous the declared logic:HolonicAgencyProfile, the holon bears an logic:selfAssertiveBasis valeur (it asserts itself as a whole) mais bears no logic:integrativeBasis valeur, so its integrative (subordination-as-a-part) face possède collapsed."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/IntentNotFromDeceptionObligation|rdfs:label"
msgid "intent must not be derived from structural deception"
msgstr "intent must not be dérivé from structurel deception"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/IntentNotFromDeceptionObligation|skos:definition"
msgid "The standing non-entailment obligation that the presence of a held≠projected gap is EVIDENCE, never ENTAILMENT, of deceptive intent: the foundation must never derive gmeow:deceptiveIntentClaim (an attributed, defeasible standpoint claim) from a structural deception gap. Enforced by syntactic reachability over the rule strata (no rule head produces the predicate) and finite closure over the materialized derivation graph (the predicate appears in no DERIVED edge). Guards the deception slice held/projected model (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, §Typed formalization governance)."
msgstr "Le standing non-implication obligation qui the presence de a held≠projected gap est preuve, jamais implication, de deceptive intent: the foundation doit jamais derive gmeow:deceptiveIntentClaim (an attributed, defeasible point de vue claim) de a structurel deception gap."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/IsolationLevel|rdfs:label"
msgid "Isolation Level"
msgstr "Isolation niveau"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/IsolationLevel|skos:definition"
msgid "The declared GUARANTEE STRENGTH a schedule must meet — not a history property and not an implementation mechanism. The closed value class spanning the standard isolation spectrum up to and including full serializability and opacity. Its individuals are logic:ReadUncommittedIsolation, logic:ReadCommittedIsolation, logic:RepeatableReadIsolation, logic:SnapshotIsolation, logic:SerializableIsolation, and logic:OpacityIsolation — the strongest, under which even aborted or in-flight transactions never observe an inconsistent state, strictly stronger than serializability. The set is closed; a misspelt value is rejected. This is one of three distinct, separately-declared concurrency concerns that must NOT be conflated: a logic:IsolationLevel is a guarantee strength, a logic:SerializabilityCriterion is a property of a history, and a logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol is an implementation mechanism."
msgstr "Le declared GUARANTEE STRENGTH a schedule doit meet — not a historique propriété et not an implementation mechanism."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Isomorphism|rdfs:label"
msgid "Isomorphism"
msgstr "Isomorphism"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Isomorphism|skos:definition"
msgid "The top rung: an iso, get ∘ put = id and put ∘ get = id, a full round-trip in both directions. The only rung that licenses a confidence-1.0 equivalence. Caps: both round-trip laws claimable."
msgstr "Le top rung: an iso, get ∘ put = id et put ∘ get = id, a full round-trip dans both directions."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Iteration|rdfs:label"
msgid "Iteration"
msgstr "itération"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Iteration|skos:definition"
msgid "The iteration program combinator: repeats a body sub-program while a loop condition holds. The body is carried by logic:iterationBody and the loop condition by logic:iterationCondition. Binary left/right operand semantics do not fit iteration — a loop has a body and a separate condition, not two co-equal operands — so logic:iterationBody and logic:iterationCondition are minted as dedicated properties rather than repurposing logic:leftOperand / logic:rightOperand. A logic:Iteration is the program-level counterpart of the loop/retry structure logic:StrongCyclicPlanSuccess quantifies over: a strong-cyclic plan succeeds when every fair execution of a loop through recoverable failures terminates at the goal in finitely many steps. The loop condition is a situation type checked before each body execution; when it does not hold the iteration terminates. Typed APART from recursive goal structures and from plain goal decomposition, which carry satisfaction dependency rather than control flow."
msgstr "Le itération program combinator: repeats a body sub-program while a loop condition holds."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/JointOutcome|rdfs:label"
msgid "Joint Outcome"
msgstr "Joint résultat"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/JointOutcome|skos:definition"
msgid "One row of a logic:DependencyModel's explicit joint table: a single joint assignment of truth values to the model's correlated facts, together with logic:jointProbability for that assignment. The facts asserted true in this outcome are named by logic:outcomeAssignment; correlated facts not named are taken to be false in this outcome."
msgstr "One row de a logic:DependencyModel's explicit joint table: a single joint assignment de vérité values à the modèle's correlated facts, together avec logic:jointProbability pour qui assignment."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Kind|rdfs:label"
msgid "Kind"
msgstr "Kind"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Kind|skos:definition"
msgid "A rigid sortal that supplies a principle of identity to its instances and applies necessarily across every world in which an instance exists: an ultimate sortal under which an object falls for its whole existence. Every object instantiates exactly one ultimate Kind. Rigid (rigidlyAppliesTo) and identity-supplying (suppliesIdentity); contrast the anti-rigid Role and Phase. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:Kind only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Un rigid sortal qui supplies a principle de identité à its instances et applies necessarily across chaque monde dans qui an instance exists: an ultimate sortal sous qui an object falls pour its whole existence."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/LadderProjectionProfile|rdfs:label"
msgid "Ladder Projection Profile"
msgstr "Ladder projection profil"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/LadderProjectionProfile|skos:definition"
msgid "A declared per-dimension threshold profile governing the generated coarse projection of the multidimensional logic:CognitiveAssessment onto the gmeow:isAwareOf … gmeow:hasMastered knowledge ladder: a set of logic:DimensionThreshold rows (logic:hasThresholdRow), each binding a ladder edge to its source dimension and the minimum logic:AssessmentLevel an assessment must clear for the edge to be emitted. Making the thresholds an explicit profile keeps the ordinal chain a projection a consumer that needs one number can read, while the factored assessment stays canonical — the ladder never re-establishes mastery, understanding, knowledge and awareness as a single ordinal entailment chain in place of the independent dimensions."
msgstr "Un declared per-dimension threshold profil governing the generated coarse projection de the multidimensional logic:CognitiveAssessment sur the gmeow:isAwareOf … gmeow:hasMastered connaissance ladder: a set de logic:DimensionThreshold rows (logic:hasThresholdRow), each liaison a ladder edge à its source dimension et the minimum logic:AssessmentLevel an évaluation doit clear pour the edge à be emitted."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/LawClaim|rdfs:label"
msgid "Law Claim"
msgstr "loi Claim"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/LawClaim|skos:definition"
msgid "A claim that a logic:Correspondence satisfies a particular logic:CorrespondenceLaw (named by logic:lawClaimed), together with the discharge state of that claim: a logic:DischargeVerdict via logic:lawDischargeVerdict and, when applicable, the logic:DischargeCondition under which it was checked via logic:lawDischargeCondition. It reuses the foundation's executable discharge vocabulary rather than a parallel status enum: a law proved within a certified fragment is logic:ObligationDischarged under logic:DischargeCertifiedFragment; a refuted law is logic:ObligationViolated with its countermodel; an authored-but-unchecked or inconclusive law is logic:ObligationUnknown, carried forward. The overclaim gate fires when a correspondence claims a law its lowered legs do not satisfy (design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md, the preservation-is-the-lens-law-framework section)."
msgstr "Un claim qui a logic:correspondance satisfies a particular logic:CorrespondenceLaw (named par logic:lawClaimed), together avec the acquittement état de qui claim: a logic:DischargeVerdict via logic:lawDischargeVerdict and, lorsque applicable, the logic:DischargeCondition sous qui it was checked via logic:lawDischargeCondition."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/LeastModelSemantics|rdfs:label"
msgid "Least Model Semantics"
msgstr "Least modèle sémantique"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/LeastModelSemantics|skos:definition"
msgid "The model-semantics facet value selecting the unique least Herbrand model of a positive (or stratified) program. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract; the monotonic semantics underlying the positive-Horn and stratified-negation presets, contrasted with the well-founded and stable-model values for unstratified negation."
msgstr "Le modèle-sémantique facet valeur selecting the unique least Herbrand modèle de a positif (or stratified) program."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Lens|rdfs:label"
msgid "Lens"
msgstr "Lens"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Lens|skos:definition"
msgid "The executable asymmetric core a logic:Correspondence wraps: a get / put leg pair between a rich source S and a derived view V, with get : S → V the down-projection and put : V × S → S the up-projection. GMEOW is always the source S and the external vocabulary the view V, so down-projection (GMEOW → external) is the get leg and up-projection (external → GMEOW) is the put leg. The view is the smaller, derived thing; put folds a possibly-fresh view back into the rich source, and the ingest-with-no-prior-state case (S empty) is exactly where a witness must travel in the view — the mnemomorphism a logic:Correspondence records with logic:mnemomorphic. Both legs are logic:TransactionProgram bodies over the path semantics of the transaction layer and logic:PathShape — no new pattern language is introduced. Distinguished from logic:Correspondence, which wraps this lens with the relation, the quantitative axes, the law claims and the standpoint envelope (design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md, the orientation-convention section). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:Lens only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le executable asymmetric core a logic:correspondance wraps: a get / put leg pair entre a rich source S et a dérivé view V, avec get : S → V the down-projection et put : V × S → S the up-projection."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/LifecycleActive|rdfs:label"
msgid "Lifecycle Active"
msgstr "cycle de vie Active"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/LifecycleActive|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:LifecycleStatus value for a goal currently held and pursued — its adoption tenure open. Contrast logic:LifecycleRetired (tenure closed) and logic:LifecycleSuperseded (replaced)."
msgstr "Le logic:LifecycleStatus valeur pour a objectif currently held et pursued — its adoption tenure ouvert."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/LifecycleRetired|rdfs:label"
msgid "Lifecycle Retired"
msgstr "cycle de vie Retired"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/LifecycleRetired|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:LifecycleStatus value for a goal no longer pursued, its adoption tenure closed by supersession rather than erased — the abandoned goal remains auditable. Contrast logic:LifecycleSuperseded, where a specific replacement goal takes its place."
msgstr "Le logic:LifecycleStatus valeur pour a objectif no longer pursued, its adoption tenure closed par supersession plutôt que erased — the abandoned objectif remains auditable."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/LifecycleStatus|rdfs:label"
msgid "Lifecycle Status"
msgstr "cycle de vie Status"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/LifecycleStatus|skos:definition"
msgid "The closed value class of the lifecycle axis of a logic:GoalEvaluation: where the goal stands in its adoption history. Its individuals are logic:LifecycleActive (currently held), logic:LifecycleRetired (no longer pursued, its tenure closed), and logic:LifecycleSuperseded (replaced by another goal). The set is closed; a misspelt value is rejected. This axis varies independently of satisfaction and feasibility — goal revision is supersession, never erasure, so a retired or superseded goal remains an auditable closed tenure."
msgstr "Le classe de valeurs fermée de the cycle de vie axis de a logic:GoalEvaluation: où the objectif stands dans its adoption historique."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/LifecycleSuperseded|rdfs:label"
msgid "Lifecycle Superseded"
msgstr "cycle de vie Superseded"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/LifecycleSuperseded|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:LifecycleStatus value for a goal replaced by another — a closed tenure standing under a successor goal. Distinct from logic:LifecycleRetired (closed with no successor named)."
msgstr "Le logic:LifecycleStatus valeur pour a objectif replaced par another — a closed tenure standing sous a successor objectif."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/LogicConformanceFailure|rdfs:label"
msgid "Logic Conformance Failure"
msgstr "Logic conformité échec"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/LogicConformanceFailure|skos:definition"
msgid "The root of the logic grounding layer's typed conformance-failure lattice: every well-formedness violation the logic: slice detects is an instance of one of its subclasses, so a failure is a first-class queryable object rather than an out-of-band error string. Its five bedrock subclasses cover the flagship acceptance scenarios — an incomplete EL/RL/DL closure, a violated correspondence section obligation, an unentrenched counterfactual, an unwitnessed refutation, and an uncertified chase — plus logic:UnwiredFlagshipScenario for an acceptance scenario that does not bind all its realizing/enforcing artifacts."
msgstr "Le root de the logic grounding layer's typed conformité-échec lattice: chaque bien forméness violation the logic: slice detects est an instance de one de its subclasses, so a échec est a first-class queryable object plutôt que an out-of-band error string."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/LogicalFramework|rdfs:label"
msgid "Logical Framework"
msgstr "logique cadre"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/LogicalFramework|skos:definition"
msgid "The closed class of reasoning disciplines the canonical logic: core formalizes — each a self-contained body of constructs, axioms, and operational semantics co-resident in logic:. Its nine named individuals are logic:HolonicFramework, logic:MereologicalFramework, logic:DeonticFramework, logic:TeleologicalFramework, logic:TemporalFramework, logic:ModalFramework, logic:EpistemicFramework, logic:ProbabilisticFramework, and logic:ParaconsistentFramework. A term declares the disciplines it traffics in via logic:instantiatesFramework, and may instantiate several; absence is meaningful — a plain domain term that traffics in no special discipline carries no framework. The value names WHICH reasoning machinery a term belongs to, orthogonal to the logic:ReasoningContract facets, which describe HOW a particular evaluation is configured rather than which discipline a term inhabits. The set is closed, so a misspelt framework names no declared value and is rejected rather than silently accepted, mirroring logic:AgencyVerdict and logic:EmergenceVerdict (design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md, the unified-logic-core section)."
msgstr "Le closed class de raisonnement disciplines the logique canonique: core formalizes — each a self-contained body de constructs, axioms, et operational sémantique co-resident dans logic:."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/LossyLens|rdfs:label"
msgid "Lossy Lens"
msgstr "Lossy Lens"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/LossyLens|skos:definition"
msgid "A lens with non-injective get: one direction is faithful but the inverse needs a witness, a co-authored put-with-claim, or declared defaults. Most schema.org / FOAF downcasts live here. Caps: a single faithful direction; the put leg may not claim recovery without a logic:mnemomorphic witness."
msgstr "Un lens avec non-injective get: one direction est faithful mais the inverse needs a témoin, a co-authored put-with-claim, ou declared defaults."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MaintenanceGoal|rdfs:label"
msgid "Maintenance Goal"
msgstr "maintien objectif"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MaintenanceGoal|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:GoalExpressionKind for a goal satisfied only while its logic:boundSituationType holds at EVERY state of the interval, violated at the FIRST state it fails; while the bounding window is still open the evaluation is logic:GoalEvaluationUndetermined, not conclusively satisfied. The dual of logic:AvoidanceGoal."
msgstr "Le logic:GoalExpressionKind pour a objectif satisfied uniquement while its logic:boundSituationType holds at EVERY état de the interval, violated at the FIRST état it fails; while the bounding window est still ouvert the evaluation est logic:GoalEvaluationUndetermined, not conclusively satisfied."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MaterialRelationshipType|rdfs:label"
msgid "Material Relationship Type"
msgstr "Material relation type"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MaterialRelationshipType|skos:definition"
msgid "A logic:RelationshipType whose instances are material relations — relations founded on a logic:Relator that mediates the relata (marriage, employment, enrolment). The counterpart of gufo:MaterialRelationshipType; the relation it types holds in virtue of the mediating Relator existing (logic:mediates), so its instances are reducible to the relator and its mediation links. Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. Contrast logic:ComparativeRelationshipType, which needs no relator."
msgstr "Un logic:RelationshipType dont instances sont material relations — relations founded sur a logic:Relator qui mediates the relata (marriage, employment, enrolment)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/McpActionSchema|rdfs:label"
msgid "MCP Action Schema"
msgstr "MCP action schéma"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/McpActionSchema|skos:definition"
msgid "A logic:ActionSchema that grounds an MCP (Model Context Protocol) tool action — the opt-in marker subtype that brings an action schema under the stricter MCP-action governance profile (logic:McpActionPolicyShape). Beyond the facets every action schema carries it must always declare a logic:compensation (rollback) because an MCP tool that mutates external state must be recoverable: the dogfood case where the canonical process model governs the agent's own tool calls. A plain logic:ActionSchema is NOT required to carry compensation; typing it logic:McpActionSchema is the explicit declaration that the governance profile applies."
msgstr "Un logic:ActionSchema qui grounds an MCP (modèle contexte Protocol) tool action — the opt-in marker subtype qui brings an action schéma sous the stricter MCP-action governance profil (logic:McpActionPolicyShape)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MeasurementFrameMissing|rdfs:label"
msgid "Measurement Frame Missing"
msgstr "Measurement Frame Missing"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MeasurementFrameMissing|skos:definition"
msgid "The frame-completeness axiom as a quality constraint: a value expressed in a unit must not be asserted without the reference frame it is read in — a measurement bearing a logic:unit but no logic:referenceFrame is ill-formed. A bare magnitude is frame-independent (a logic:trueQuantity), but the moment a value is given it is expressed in a unit and frame; a value asserted without its frame is meaningless, not merely under-specified (Principle 11: separate the frame-independent structure from the frame-relative value, and never assert the value without the frame). Because the foundation chase is all-IRI, the rule keys on logic:unit — the IRI-valued witness that a framed value exists — rather than on the literal logic:measuredValue it qualifies. A unit-bearing measurement lacking a frame is the logic:violation, entailed by the foundation lowering rather than asserted by hand."
msgstr "Le frame-complétude axiom as a qualité contrainte: a valeur expressed dans a unit ne doit pas be asserted sans the reference frame it est read dans — a measurement bearing a logic:unit mais no logic:referenceFrame est ill-formed."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MediatedPropertyRequirementAssertion|rdfs:label"
msgid "mediated property requirement assertion"
msgstr "mediated propriété requirement assertion"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MediatedPropertyRequirementAssertion|skos:definition"
msgid "A central record asserting that, on a target class, every value a focus node reaches through a mediating property must itself declare at least one value of a required property — the interval that scopes a situation must carry its temporal frame (Principle 11). It names the class with logic:mediatedRequirementTarget, the mediating property with logic:mediatedRequirementVia, and the demanded property with logic:mediatedRequirementProperty; the native coherence gate joins them to raise a violation when a mediated value lacks the required property. Carries a logic:formalizes back-reference to the domain property whose prose it encodes. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:MediatedPropertyRequirementAssertion only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Un central record asserting that, sur a target class, chaque valeur a focus nœud reaches par a mediating propriété doit itself declare au moins one valeur de a obligatoire propriété — the interval qui scopes a situation doit carry its temporal frame (Principle 11)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MereologicalFramework|rdfs:label"
msgid "Mereological Framework"
msgstr "Mereological cadre"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MereologicalFramework|skos:definition"
msgid "The part-whole framework: strict parthood (logic:properPartOf, a transitive, asymmetric, irreflexive order), overlap and disjointness, and weak supplementation scoped to a declared logic:MereologyProfile rather than imposed universally. Parthood is profiled, not universal — supplementation is true of functional complexes and quantities but false of singleton collectives and in-progress assemblies (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Le part-whole cadre: strict parthood (logic:properPartOf, a transitive, asymmetric, irreflexive order), overlap et disjointness, et weak supplementation scoped à a declared logic:MereologyProfile plutôt que imposed universally."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MereologyConstraint|rdfs:label"
msgid "Mereology Constraint"
msgstr "Mereology contrainte"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MereologyConstraint|skos:definition"
msgid "A named profiled-mereology axiom a whole can violate — the family of mereological well-formedness constraints (weak supplementation and its kin) that hold only within a declared logic:MereologyProfile. Distinct from logic:Discipline, the closed set of OntoUML structural anti-patterns: mereology constraints are scoped to a profile, not asserted foundation-wide. Its named individuals are the labels a logic:violation fact may point at; the set is closed so a misspelt label names no declared constraint and is rejected rather than silently accepted."
msgstr "Un named profiled-mereology axiom a whole peut violate — the family de mereological bien forméness constraints (weak supplementation et its kin) qui hold uniquement within a declared logic:MereologyProfile."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MereologyProfile|rdfs:label"
msgid "Mereology Profile"
msgstr "Mereology profil"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MereologyProfile|skos:definition"
msgid "A declared scope within which the strong mereological axioms — weak supplementation above all — are taken to hold. Parthood is profiled, not universal: weak supplementation is true of functional complexes and quantities but false of many legitimate wholes (singleton-membered collectives, abstract aggregates, in-progress assemblies), so logic: scopes it to the MereologyProfile a whole is declared under (via logic:underMereologyProfile) rather than asserting it across all logic:properPartOf. A whole outside any profile is never charged with a logic:WeakSupplementation violation (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Un declared scope within qui the strong mereological axioms — weak supplementation above tous — sont taken à hold."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MetaLevelFormula|rdfs:label"
msgid "Meta-Level Formula"
msgstr "Meta-niveau formule"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MetaLevelFormula|skos:definition"
msgid "A formula about formulas: a statement that quotes or ranges over other propositions, distinct from the propositions it mentions. Kept apart from the object level so a meta-level quotation cannot collapse into the object-level assertion it quotes; any holds or truth predicate over it is stratified so the IR cannot encode a self-referential paradox by accident."
msgstr "Un formule about formulas: a statement qui quotes ou ranges sur other propositions, distinct de the propositions it mentions."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MixIden|rdfs:label"
msgid "Mixed Identity"
msgstr "Mixed identité"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MixIden|skos:definition"
msgid "The OntoUML MixIden anti-pattern: a sortal inherits its principle of identity from exactly one Kind. A Kind specializing another Kind, or a non-Kind sortal tracing to zero or to two-or-more Kinds, violates it. The lowering of reasoning_lint.identity_overlap."
msgstr "Le OntoUML MixIden anti-pattern: a sortal inherits its principle de identité de exactement un Kind."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MixRig|rdfs:label"
msgid "Mixed Rigidity"
msgstr "Mixed Rigidity"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MixRig|skos:definition"
msgid "The OntoUML MixRig anti-pattern: a rigid sortal (Kind or SubKind) must never specialize an anti-rigid type (Phase, Role, PhaseMixin, RoleMixin, Mixin), because a rigid type cannot inherit contingent instantiation. A rigid sortal with an anti-rigid-type ancestor violates it. The other half of the lowering of reasoning_lint.anti_rigidity_discipline."
msgstr "Le OntoUML MixRig anti-pattern: a rigid sortal (Kind ou SubKind) doit jamais specialize an anti-rigid type (Phase, Role, PhaseMixin, RoleMixin, Mixin), parce que a rigid type ne peut pas inherit contingent instantiation."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Mixin|rdfs:label"
msgid "Mixin"
msgstr "Mixin"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Mixin|skos:definition"
msgid "A semi-rigid non-sortal that classifies instances of several Kinds, applying rigidly to some instances and anti-rigidly to others: a dispersive type whose rigidity is mixed across its extension. Identity-dispersive like a Category, but semi-rigid rather than uniformly rigid."
msgstr "Un semi-rigid non-sortal qui classifies instances de several Kinds, applying rigidly à some instances et anti-rigidly à others: a dispersive type dont rigidity est mixed across its extension."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ModalFramework|rdfs:label"
msgid "Modal Framework"
msgstr "modal cadre"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ModalFramework|skos:definition"
msgid "The alethic-modality and rigidity framework: logic:World / logic:PossibleWorld with typed accessibility, and the modal notion of rigidity (logic:rigidlyAppliesTo, lowering to the constraint that a rigid type held in one world of an individual's existence is held in all). Kripke semantics realized over GMEOW's contextual index — the modal distinctions full UFO needs and OWL cannot hold (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the criticism-ledger section; design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md, the operational-semantics-modality-and-identity-supply section)."
msgstr "Le alethic-modality et rigidity cadre: logic:monde / logic:PossibleWorld avec typed accessibility, et the modal notion de rigidity (logic:rigidlyAppliesTo, lowering à the contrainte qui a rigid type held dans one monde de an individu's existence est held dans tous)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Mode|rdfs:label"
msgid "Mode"
msgstr "Mode"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Mode|skos:definition"
msgid "An aspect that is NOT directly measurable in a quality space — a belief, a skill, an intention, a symptom — whether intrinsic to a single bearer or relational across several. The counterpart of gufo:IntrinsicMode and gufo:ExtrinsicMode generalized: a logic:Aspect lacking a quality value (stated in prose, not as a subclass edge). Contrast logic:Quality, which is measurable."
msgstr "Un aspect qui est NOT directly measurable dans a qualité space — a belief, a skill, an intention, a symptom — whether intrinsic à a single bearer ou relational across several."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ModelSemantics|rdfs:label"
msgid "Model Semantics"
msgstr "modèle sémantique"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ModelSemantics|skos:definition"
msgid "The facet value class of the model-semantics facet: which models of a program are selected as authoritative. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract. Its individuals are classical entailment, the least model, the well-founded model, and the stable models — the choice that settles which entailments hold over a rule program. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:ModelSemantics only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le facet valeur class de the modèle-sémantique facet: qui models de a program sont selected as authoritative."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Module|rdfs:label"
msgid "Module"
msgstr "Module"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Module|skos:definition"
msgid "A named Common Logic module — a body of sentences grouped as a reusable theory, with its own local vocabulary and importation. The theory-structuring context of a statement, ORTHOGONAL to the epistemic logic:World / gmeow:Standpoint dimension: a module says WHERE a sentence lives (which theory), never UNDER WHOSE perspective it holds, so a module must never be conflated with a world or a standpoint — that conflation is exactly the category error the context algebra forbids. Per-statement membership is carried by logic:inModule and module-to-module importation by logic:imports; the top-level (unnamed) module is the absence of any logic:inModule. It is the construct the ingested and emitted Common Logic dialects (CLIF, CGIF, XCL) map their (module …) and (cl-imports …) forms onto."
msgstr "Un named commun Logic module — a body de sentences grouped as a reusable theory, avec its own local vocabulary et importation."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ModuleContextAxis|rdfs:label"
msgid "Module Context Axis"
msgstr "Module contexte Axis"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ModuleContextAxis|skos:definition"
msgid "The module index axis of the multi-dimensional context facet: a statement is relative to the logic:Module (Common Logic theory) it is asserted in. A theory-structuring axis that coexists with the world, standpoint, time, and path axes and indexes the same result simultaneously — orthogonal to them, never an alternative value of the world or standpoint slot. Its per-statement carrier is logic:inModule; module-to-module importation is logic:imports."
msgstr "Le module index axis de the multi-dimensional contexte facet: a statement est relative à the logic:Module (commun Logic theory) it est asserted in."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MonotonicRevision|rdfs:label"
msgid "Monotonic Revision"
msgstr "Monotonic Revision"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MonotonicRevision|skos:definition"
msgid "The revision-policy value under which new information only adds conclusions and never retracts them: there is nothing to revise because no conclusion is ever defeated. The degenerate revision policy of monotonic reasoning (the positive-Horn preset), contrasted with logic:EntrenchmentRevision and logic:TruthMaintenanceRevision, which absorb defeating information."
msgstr "Le revision-politique valeur sous qui new information uniquement adds conclusions et jamais retracts them: there n'est pashing à revise parce que no conclusion est ever defeated."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MorphismClass|rdfs:label"
msgid "Morphism Class"
msgstr "Morphism Class"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MorphismClass|skos:definition"
msgid "The ordered law-spine of a logic:Correspondence: how much invertibility it may lawfully claim, where each rung caps the laws the correspondence may assert. From strongest to floor the seven rungs are logic:Isomorphism, logic:SectionRetraction, logic:WellBehavedLens, logic:LossyLens, logic:Prism, logic:AffineCorrespondence and logic:BridgeView. The spine fuses the profunctor-optic lattice with the categorical subobject notion; composition can only weaken the rung, never strengthen it, and a logic:mnemomorphic witness is what lets a correspondence climb it. The set is closed, so a misspelt class names no declared rung and is rejected (design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md, the ordered-law-spine section)."
msgstr "Le ordered loi-spine de a logic:correspondance: how much invertibility it peut lawfully claim, où each rung caps the laws the correspondance peut assert."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MorphismKind|rdfs:label"
msgid "Morphism Kind"
msgstr "Morphism Kind"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MorphismKind|skos:definition"
msgid "The closed two-value qualifier, orthogonal to the logic:MorphismClass rung, recording the institution-theoretic split between a satisfaction-preserving morphism (logic:InstitutionMorphism) and a commitment-shifting bridge (logic:CommitmentShiftingBridge). This is the distinction the foundation already draws between a truth-preserving down-projection and a by-reference bridge; the loss ledger refuses owl:equivalentClass for the bridge kind. The set is closed, so a misspelt kind names no declared value and is rejected (design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md, the ordered-law-spine section). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:MorphismKind only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le closed two-valeur qualifier, orthogonal à the logic:MorphismClass rung, recording the institution-theoretic split entre a satisfaction-preserving morphism (logic:InstitutionMorphism) et a engagement-shifting pont (logic:CommitmentShiftingBridge)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MultiversionConcurrencyControl|rdfs:label"
msgid "Multiversion Concurrency Control"
msgstr "Multiversion concurrence contrôle"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/MultiversionConcurrencyControl|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol under which each transaction reads from a consistent version snapshot taken at its start and writes new versions independently, so readers never block writers. Its strongest enforced guarantee is logic:SnapshotIsolation — it still admits WRITE SKEW and so does NOT enforce logic:SerializableIsolation, which is exactly why declaring it under a serializable-or-stronger level is inadequate. This engine realizes snapshot isolation by construction, so a multiversion run needs no lock or timestamp events. A mechanism, not a guarantee."
msgstr "Le logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol sous qui each transaction reads de a cohérent version snapshot taken at its start et writes new versions independently, so readers jamais block writers."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Nested|rdfs:label"
msgid "Nested"
msgstr "Nested"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Nested|skos:definition"
msgid "The residue shape tag for a formula that is a connective or quantifier tree rather than a flat predication — it carries logical structure (logic:and, logic:or, logic:not, an implication, logic:iff, or a quantifier) that the flat body of a Horn rule cannot hold. Disclosed when a Horn-fragment target carries such a formula as flagged unsupported residue."
msgstr "Le residue forme tag pour a formule qui est a connective ou quantifier tree plutôt que a flat predication — it porte logique structure (logic:and, logic:or, logic:not, an implication, logic:iff, ou a quantifier) qui the flat body de a Horn règle ne peut pas hold."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/NoArgumentation|rdfs:label"
msgid "No Argumentation"
msgstr "No argumentation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/NoArgumentation|skos:definition"
msgid "The argumentation-facet value selecting no argumentation layer: conflicts are not resolved by an argumentation semantics. The default for contracts whose conflict resolution is handled by the model semantics or revision policy alone, contrasted with the grounded, preferred, and policy-specific argumentation values."
msgstr "Le argumentation-facet valeur selecting no argumentation layer: conflicts ne sont pas resolved par an argumentation sémantique."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/NoUncertainty|rdfs:label"
msgid "No Uncertainty"
msgstr "No Uncertainty"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/NoUncertainty|skos:definition"
msgid "The uncertainty-measure value carrying no graded belief: reasoning is categorical. The default of the uncertainty set facet (the empty selection), contrasted with logic:ProbabilisticMeasure, logic:WeightedRankingMeasure, and logic:FuzzyMeasure, any combination of which may be in force at once."
msgstr "Le uncertainty-measure valeur carrying no graded belief: raisonnement est categorical."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/NodeKind|rdfs:label"
msgid "Node Kind"
msgstr "nœud Kind"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/NodeKind|skos:definition"
msgid "The typed-sum tag every node of the canonical logic: IR declares. The IR is a typed sum, not an untyped triple bag: each node names its kind, and the kind governs what may be done with it — keeping a constraint distinct from a derivation rule, a query operator from a program operator, and a meta-level quotation from the object-level assertion it quotes. Its individuals are the object-level formula, the meta-level formula, the constraint, the derivation rule, the query, the transaction program, the action schema, the validation shape, and the law-bearing correspondence."
msgstr "Le typed-sum tag chaque nœud de the logique canonique: IR declares."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/NonEntailmentObligation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Non-Entailment Obligation"
msgstr "Non-implication obligation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/NonEntailmentObligation|skos:definition"
msgid "A first-class, executable record of a conclusion the foundation must NEVER draw: a deliberate non-assertion the engine is held to, not a comment the axioms happen to respect. It names the forbidden predicate (logic:obligationForbiddenPredicate), the logic:DischargeCondition under which absence-of-proof is conclusively checkable, and the logic:DischargeVerdict the check returns. Because the canonical logic is semi-decidable, an obligation is conclusively discharged only within a stated fragment or bound; outside it the verdict is logic:ObligationUnknown, carried forward, never 'proved absent'. The two standing obligations are 'intent must not be derived from structural deception' and 'counterpart must not become transitive' (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, §Typed formalization governance)."
msgstr "Un first-class, executable record de a conclusion the foundation doit NEVER draw: a deliberate non-assertion the engine est held to, not a comment the axioms happen à respect."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/NonRigidType|rdfs:label"
msgid "Non-Rigid Type"
msgstr "Non-Rigid type"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/NonRigidType|skos:definition"
msgid "A logic:Type that is not rigid: either anti-rigid (logic:AntiRigidType) or semi-rigid (logic:SemiRigidType). The counterpart of gufo:NonRigidType; the meta-type that is the union complement of logic:RigidType over the sorts — its instances are logic:Phase, logic:Role, logic:RoleMixin, logic:PhaseMixin (anti-rigid) and logic:Mixin (semi-rigid). Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. The negation of logic:RigidType, used where a discipline only needs 'not necessarily applying' rather than the stronger 'contingent for every instance'."
msgstr "Un logic:type qui n'est pas rigid: either anti-rigid (logic:AntiRigidType) ou semi-rigid (logic:SemiRigidType)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/NonSortal|rdfs:label"
msgid "Non-Sortal"
msgstr "Non-Sortal"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/NonSortal|skos:definition"
msgid "A logic:Type that aggregates instances of several different logic:Sortals and supplies NO principle of identity of its own — it spans Kinds dispersively. The counterpart of gufo:NonSortal; the meta-type whose instances are the dispersive sorts: logic:Category, logic:Mixin, logic:RoleMixin, logic:PhaseMixin. Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. Identity-dispersive (logic:suppliesIdentity holds for none of its instances); contrast logic:Sortal."
msgstr "Un logic:type qui aggregates instances de several different logic:Sortals et supplies NO principle de identité de its own — it spans Kinds dispersively."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/NotificationWaitSchema|rdfs:label"
msgid "Notification Wait Schema"
msgstr "Notification Wait schéma"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/NotificationWaitSchema|skos:definition"
msgid "A logic:ActionSchema whose completion the engine learns of ONLY by being externally told: it does not fire until a logic:ExternalSignal it logic:awaitsSignal obtains in the state — a manual-notification or callback-driven completion, the prescriptive-descriptive epistemic boundary where what the engine knows of the real world is limited to what it is informed of. The opt-in marker subtype that brings an action schema under the wait-well-formedness profile (logic:NotificationWaitShape, which requires a logic:awaitsSignal). At the action gate a wait whose signal has not obtained is neither admitted nor denied but logic:GateUndetermined, carrying a logic:awaitingSignal witness — the wait is pending (the engine has not been told), a judgment withheld rather than a failure; in a plan a wait step blocks the path until the signal is received."
msgstr "Un logic:ActionSchema dont completion the engine learns de ONLY par being externally told: it ne fait pas fire until a logic:ExternalSignal it logic:awaitsSignal obtains dans the état — a manual-notification ou callback-driven completion, the prescriptive-descriptive épistémique boundary où what the engine knows de the real monde est limited à what it est informed of."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Object|rdfs:label"
msgid "Object"
msgstr "Object"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Object|skos:definition"
msgid "A substantial endurant that bears its own principle of identity and does not inhere in another individual — a person, an organization, a physical artefact. The counterpart of gufo:Object: an independent endurant, contrasted with the aspects that existentially depend on it. Every Object is a logic:Substantial and a logic:Endurant (stated in prose, not as a subclass edge)."
msgstr "Un substantial endurant qui bears its own principle de identité et ne fait pas inhere dans another individu — a person, an organization, a physical artefact."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ObjectLevelFormula|rdfs:label"
msgid "Object-Level Formula"
msgstr "Object-niveau formule"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ObjectLevelFormula|skos:definition"
msgid "An ordinary first-order formula over the domain of discourse: the object-level node kind. Its quantifiers range over individuals in the domain, some of which may be reified predicates or types, so the object level stays first-order even where it expresses what reads as quantification over predicates or types."
msgstr "Un ordinary premier ordre formule sur the domaine de discourse: the object-niveau nœud kind."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ObligationDischarged|rdfs:label"
msgid "Discharged"
msgstr "Discharged"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ObligationDischarged|skos:definition"
msgid "The discharge verdict for an obligation conclusively checked within its declared logic:DischargeCondition: the forbidden conclusion is provably not drawn within the stated fragment or bound. Wire value `discharged`."
msgstr "Le acquittement verdict pour an obligation conclusively checked within its declared logic:DischargeCondition: the forbidden conclusion est provably not drawn within the stated fragment ou bound."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ObligationUnknown|rdfs:label"
msgid "Unknown"
msgstr "inconnu"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ObligationUnknown|skos:definition"
msgid "The discharge verdict outside any wired discharge condition: not 'proved absent' but not-yet-discharged, carried forward to the next evaluation cycle or stronger fragment. The honest verdict the semi-decidable canonical logic demands. Wire value `unknown`."
msgstr "Le acquittement verdict outside tout wired acquittement condition: not 'proved absent' mais not-yet-discharged, carried forward à the next evaluation cycle ou stronger fragment."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ObligationViolated|rdfs:label"
msgid "Violated"
msgstr "Violated"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ObligationViolated|skos:definition"
msgid "The discharge verdict when the forbidden predicate IS reachable or present in the closure: the obligation is broken and the check is a hard error. Wire value `violated`."
msgstr "Le acquittement verdict lorsque the forbidden prédicat IS reachable ou present dans the fermeture: the obligation est broken et the vérification est a erreur bloquante."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/OccurrentBoundary|rdfs:label"
msgid "Occurrent Boundary"
msgstr "Occurrent Boundary"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/OccurrentBoundary|skos:definition"
msgid "The closed class of perdurant boundary values: the two-valued result a perdurant receives via logic:occurrentBoundary. Its named individuals are logic:Open (an on-going action over an open interval — the arriving) and logic:Closed (a completed unitary event over a closed interval — the arrival). The set is closed, so a misspelt value names no declared boundary and is rejected rather than silently accepted, mirroring logic:EmergenceVerdict and logic:ConstraintVerdict. The carrier of the YAMATO/Galton action(open)/event(closed) distinction as a value, not a subclass (Principle 9)."
msgstr "Le closed class de perdurant boundary values: the two-valued résultat a perdurant receives via logic:occurrentBoundary."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/OccurrentBoundaryMismatch|rdfs:label"
msgid "Occurrent Boundary Mismatch"
msgstr "Occurrent Boundary Mismatch"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/OccurrentBoundaryMismatch|skos:definition"
msgid "The boundary-exclusivity axiom as an occurrent constraint: a perdurant must not be both on-going and completed — it must not carry both logic:occurrentBoundary logic:Open and logic:occurrentBoundary logic:Closed. The two halves of the action(open)/event(closed) distinction are mutually exclusive at a single standpoint; an occurrent bearing both is the logic:violation, entailed by the foundation lowering rather than asserted by hand."
msgstr "Le boundary-exclusivity axiom as an occurrent contrainte: a perdurant ne doit pas be both on-going et completed — it ne doit pas carry both logic:occurrentBoundary logic:ouvert et logic:occurrentBoundary logic:Closed."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/OccurrentChangeAsymmetry|rdfs:label"
msgid "Occurrent Change Asymmetry"
msgstr "Occurrent Change Asymmetry"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/OccurrentChangeAsymmetry|skos:definition"
msgid "The change-asymmetry axiom as an occurrent constraint: a completed unitary occurrent (logic:occurrentBoundary logic:Closed) must not vary — it must bear no time-varying logic:Fluent. Processes and on-going actions may change; an event, once whole, cannot (the YAMATO/Galton process-not-equal-event refinement, restoring the UFO-B four-dimensional account). A Closed occurrent that bears a logic:Fluent is the logic:violation, entailed by the foundation lowering rather than asserted by hand."
msgstr "Le change-asymmetry axiom as an occurrent contrainte: a completed unitary occurrent (logic:occurrentBoundary logic:Closed) ne doit pas vary — it doit bear no time-varying logic:Fluent."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/OccurrentConstraint|rdfs:label"
msgid "Occurrent Constraint"
msgstr "Occurrent contrainte"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/OccurrentConstraint|skos:definition"
msgid "A named occurrent well-formedness axiom a perdurant can violate — the family of constraints governing the process/event change-asymmetry and the action(open)/event(closed) boundary. Distinct from logic:Discipline (the closed set of OntoUML structural anti-patterns) and from logic:MereologyConstraint (profiled-mereology axioms): occurrent constraints govern the four-dimensional semantics of perdurants. Its named individuals are the labels a logic:violation fact may point at; the set is closed so a misspelt label names no declared constraint and is rejected rather than silently accepted."
msgstr "Un named occurrent bien forméness axiom a perdurant peut violate — the family de constraints governing the process/event change-asymmetry et the action(ouvert)/event(closed) boundary."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/OpacityIsolation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Opacity Isolation"
msgstr "Opacity Isolation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/OpacityIsolation|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:IsolationLevel guarantee under which even aborted or in-flight transactions never observe an inconsistent state — the strongest level, STRICTLY STRONGER than serializability (logic:SerializableIsolation), which constrains only committed transactions. Engine note: under the committed-only, snapshot-isolation execution model of the native evaluator, no aborted or in-flight transactions arise; opacity's additional constraints are therefore vacuously satisfied, and the isolation-adequacy verdict for logic:OpacityIsolation coincides with that of logic:SerializableIsolation by construction — both are met exactly when the witnessed schedule is conflict-serializable."
msgstr "Le logic:IsolationLevel guarantee sous qui even aborted ou in-flight transactions jamais observe an incohérent état — the strongest niveau, STRICTLY STRONGER than serializability (logic:SerializableIsolation), qui constrains uniquement committed transactions."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Open|rdfs:label"
msgid "Open"
msgstr "ouvert"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Open|skos:definition"
msgid "The occurrent-boundary value for an on-going action: a perdurant unfolding over an open temporal interval, not yet a completed whole — the arriving, the running, the prescribed-but-unexecuted plan. The action half of the YAMATO/Galton action(open)/event(closed) distinction; an occurrent that varies (bears a logic:Fluent) is properly Open, since only the unfinished can still change. Contrast logic:Closed."
msgstr "Le occurrent-boundary valeur pour an on-going action: a perdurant unfolding sur an ouvert temporal interval, not yet a completed whole — the arriving, the running, the prescribed-but-unexecuted plan."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/OpenWorldClosure|rdfs:label"
msgid "Open-World Closure"
msgstr "ouvert-monde fermeture"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/OpenWorldClosure|skos:definition"
msgid "The open-world value of the closure map: for the predicate or context key it is bound to, absence of a fact means unknown rather than false. The default for any key not explicitly closed; the closure facet is a map, so this value is read per key, with logic:ClosedWorldClosure applied only inside a logic:WorldBoundary."
msgstr "Le monde ouvert valeur de the fermeture map: pour the prédicat ou contexte key it est bound to, absence de a fact means inconnu plutôt que false."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/OptimisticValidation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Optimistic Validation"
msgstr "Optimistic Validation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/OptimisticValidation|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol that lets transactions run without locking and validates for conflicts at commit time, aborting and retrying on a detected conflict. A mechanism, not a guarantee."
msgstr "Le logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol qui lets transactions run sans locking et validates pour conflicts at commit time, aborting et retrying sur a detected conflit."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/OptimizationGoal|rdfs:label"
msgid "Optimization Goal"
msgstr "Optimization objectif"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/OptimizationGoal|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:GoalExpressionKind for a goal directed at a logic:objectiveValue read in a logic:objectiveDirection, satisfied to the DEGREE the measure is extremized (carried as logic:satisfactionDegree) rather than by a crisp boundary. Its outcome is recorded as a degree, never folded into a crisp truth value."
msgstr "Le logic:GoalExpressionKind pour a objectif directed at a logic:objectiveValue read dans a logic:objectiveDirection, satisfied à the DEGREE the measure est extremized (carried as logic:satisfactionDegree) plutôt que par a crisp boundary."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/OrDecomposition|rdfs:label"
msgid "Or-Decomposition"
msgstr "Or-décomposition"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/OrDecomposition|skos:definition"
msgid "The decomposition of a gmeow:Goal under which any one sufficient sub-goal settles the parent on its own — a disjunctive node of the and-or goal graph means–end search runs over. It groups the logic:sufficientFor sub-goals of the parent: satisfying any one settles it. The co-equal counterpart of logic:AndDecomposition (all necessary sub-goals must hold together); the two compose into the and-or goal graph. Like all decomposition it carries satisfaction dependency and is typed apart from the generic mereology spine, which carries only structural part-hood. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:OrDecomposition only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le décomposition de a gmeow:objectif sous qui tout one sufficient sub-objectif settles the parent sur its own — a disjunctive nœud de the and-or objectif graphe means–end search runs over."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Outcome|rdfs:label"
msgid "Outcome"
msgstr "résultat"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Outcome|skos:definition"
msgid "One branch of the nondeterministic outcome set of a logic:ActionSchema: a single alternative result, naming via logic:outcomeSituation the successor situation it reaches and via the reused logic:compensation the action that recovers from THIS branch specifically. Reifying each branch as an Outcome is what lets compensation be outcome-indexed rather than a single generic undo across the schema, and what lets plan-success quantification (logic:planSuccessMode) range over the branches. A logic:ActionSchema points at its branches through logic:nondeterministicOutcome."
msgstr "One branch de the nondeterministic résultat set de a logic:ActionSchema: a single alternative résultat, naming via logic:outcomeSituation the successor situation it reaches et via the reused logic:compensation the action qui recovers de THIS branch specifically."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Overlaps|rdfs:label"
msgid "overlaps"
msgstr "overlaps"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Overlaps|skos:definition"
msgid "Source and view share instances without either subsuming the other: a partial, caveated alignment. Lowers to sssom:closeMatch (an OWL equivalence is unsupported and the overclaim gate refuses one). Below the directional band, above logic:RelatedMatch. Distinct from the mereological relation logic:overlaps (shared parts of one whole); this is a relation between two aligned patterns."
msgstr "Source et view share instances sans either subsuming the other: a partial, caveated alignment."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/OwlProjection|rdfs:label"
msgid "OWL Projection"
msgstr "OWL projection"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/OwlProjection|skos:definition"
msgid "The projection-target value requesting the answer be rendered to an OWL surface (e.g. an EL or DL profile). One of several output targets a single contract may name at once; like every projection target it is a rendering request and never alters which entailments hold."
msgstr "Le projection-target valeur requesting the answer be rendered à an OWL surface (e.g."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ParaconsistentFramework|rdfs:label"
msgid "Paraconsistent Framework"
msgstr "Paraconsistent cadre"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ParaconsistentFramework|skos:definition"
msgid "The multi-valued-truth framework: the logic:BelnapBilattice (true, false, both/glut, neither/gap), the admissible-valuation policy (logic:AdmissibleValuationPolicy — the gap/glut choice distinguishing FDE, LP, K3, classical) and designated-value set carried on a logic:TruthAlgebra, and context-indexed entailment so a contradiction is localized to the contexts that disagree, witnessed explicitly, and reasoned around rather than exploding the model (design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md, the unified-logic-core section; design/LOGIC-CONTRACT.md, the truth-values-admissible-valuations-and-the-designated-value-policy section)."
msgstr "Le à valeurs multiples-vérité cadre: the logic:BelnapBilattice (true, false, both/glut, neither/gap), the admissible-évaluation politique (logic:AdmissibleValuationPolicy — the gap/glut choice distinguishing FDE, LP, K3, classical) et designated-valeur set carried sur a logic:TruthAlgebra, et contexte-indexed implication so a contradiction est localized à the contexts qui disagree, witnessed explicitly, et reasoned around plutôt que exploding the modèle (design/LOGIC-sémantique.md, the unified-logic-core section; design/LOGIC-CONTRACT.md, the vérité-values-admissible-valuations-and-the-designated-valeur-politique section)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PartiallySatisfied|rdfs:label"
msgid "Partially Satisfied"
msgstr "Partially Satisfied"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PartiallySatisfied|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:SatisfactionStatus value for a goal met in part, its extent carried as a logic:satisfactionDegree quantity. Held apart from a low logic:confidence in a logic:Satisfied evaluation: partial satisfaction is how much of the goal is achieved, never how sure the evaluator is. Contrast logic:Unsatisfied (no positive progress) and logic:Violated (a target has failed)."
msgstr "Le logic:SatisfactionStatus valeur pour a objectif met dans part, its extent carried as a logic:satisfactionDegree quantity."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Participation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Participation"
msgstr "Participation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Participation|skos:definition"
msgid "The reified involvement of an endurant in a perdurant — an actor's participation in an event, a reactant's participation in a reaction. The counterpart of gufo:Participation: a relator-like reified link binding a logic:Endurant to the logic:Perdurant it takes part in, so the role and temporal scope of the involvement can be carried on the participation itself. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:Participation only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le reified involvement de an endurant dans a perdurant — an actor's participation dans an event, a reactant's participation dans a reaction."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Path|rdfs:label"
msgid "Path"
msgstr "chemin"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Path|skos:definition"
msgid "An ordered run of states — a history — over which the typed accessibility relation logic:temporallySucceeds is read; the typed context of the context algebra that carries the Transaction-Logic state sequence, whose edges logic:transitionFromState and logic:transitionToState walk and whose positions are gmeow:State configurations, each realizing a logic:Situation. 'History' is the documented synonym. One of the distinct typed contexts (alongside logic:PossibleWorld, gmeow:EpistemicContext, gmeow:Standpoint, gmeow:Scenario, gmeow:State, gmeow:ReferenceFrame, gmeow:NarrativeReferenceFrame); no inference may cross into it by walking the bare logic:accessibleFrom superproperty, and its relation to states and situations is stated in prose, not as a subclass edge."
msgstr "Un ordered run de states — a historique — sur qui the typed accessibility relation logic:temporallySucceeds est read; the typed contexte de the contexte algebra qui porte the transaction-Logic état sequence, dont edges logic:transitionFromState et logic:transitionToState walk et dont positions sont gmeow:état configurations, each realizing a logic:situation."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PathContextAxis|rdfs:label"
msgid "Path Context Axis"
msgstr "chemin contexte Axis"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PathContextAxis|skos:definition"
msgid "The path index axis of the multi-dimensional context facet: a truth is relative to a transaction or execution path. One of several context axes that coexist on a single result — world, standpoint, time, and path index the same result simultaneously rather than being alternative values of one slot."
msgstr "Le chemin index axis de the multi-dimensional contexte facet: a vérité est relative à a transaction ou exécution chemin."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PathInvocation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Path Invocation"
msgstr "chemin Invocation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PathInvocation|skos:definition"
msgid "A by-name application of a logic:PathShape with concrete depth arguments — the canonical, reified form of a parametric call such as :nearbyOrgs(?maxDepth := 2). It carries logic:invokesPathShape (the shape applied) and logic:pathDepthArg (the value bound to the shape's logic:pathDepthParam), so a named, reusable traversal is instantiated at a specific bound without rewriting the shape. The surface syntax :name(?param := value) is a rendering of this individual, not a separate construct (Principle 17)."
msgstr "Un by-name application de a logic:PathShape avec concret depth arguments — the canonique, reified form de a parametric call such as :nearbyOrgs(?maxDepth := 2)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PathShape|rdfs:label"
msgid "Path Shape"
msgstr "chemin forme"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PathShape|skos:definition"
msgid "A named, parametric predicate-path traversal specification: a reusable description of how to walk the graph, invocable by name with a depth parameter. A PathShape carries a base step — either a named predicate (logic:pathStepPredicate) or a predicate wildcard (logic:pathWildcard true, optionally scoped by logic:pathNamespaceScope) — together with a bounded depth range (logic:pathMinDepth … logic:pathMaxDepth; an absent maximum means unbounded) and a declared depth parameter name (logic:pathDepthParam) bound at each logic:PathInvocation. It SUBSUMES and EXTENDS SPARQL 1.1 property paths (§9), which are fixed strings with no predicate wildcard, no bounded depth {1,n}, and no named or parameterized reuse: 'all nodes within n hops, by any predicate' becomes a first-class, reusable term. The PathShape is the canonical logic: form; an extended SPARQL property path and a depth-bounded Datalog program are its projections (Principle 17), and the native Datalog least-model fixpoint is its runtime. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:PathShape only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Un named, parametric prédicat-chemin traversal specification: a reusable description de how à walk the graphe, invocable par name avec a depth parameter."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PathValueTypeConstraint|rdfs:label"
msgid "Path Value Type Constraint"
msgstr "chemin valeur type contrainte"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PathValueTypeConstraint|skos:definition"
msgid "Compact sugar for a path-value type-membership constraint (P4): a logic:onClass target, a logic:valuePath predicate, and a required logic:valueClass. Expands to a canonical logic:Constraint ∀this. C(this) → ∀v. P(this,v) → D(v). Frontend-only authoring shortcut. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:PathValueTypeConstraint only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Compact sugar pour a chemin-valeur type-membership contrainte (P4): a logic:onClass target, a logic:valuePath prédicat, et a obligatoire logic:valueClass."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Perdurant|rdfs:label"
msgid "Perdurant"
msgstr "Perdurant"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Perdurant|skos:definition"
msgid "An occurrent: an individual that unfolds in time by accumulating temporal parts, so that at any single moment only a part of it is present. The four-dimensional counterpart of the endurant; logic:Event and logic:Process are perdurants (every Event is a Perdurant — the supertype relation is stated here in prose rather than as an rdfs:subClassOf edge, matching how the foundation sorts are authored). Contrast logic:Endurant, which is wholly present at each moment."
msgstr "Un occurrent: an individu qui unfolds dans time par accumulating temporal parts, so qui at tout single moment uniquement a part de it est present."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Phase|rdfs:label"
msgid "Phase"
msgstr "Phase"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Phase|skos:definition"
msgid "An anti-rigid sortal an instance falls under during a stage of its existence determined by a change in its own intrinsic state — child, adult, vacant, occupied. Anti-rigid: there is a world of existence in which the instance lacks the Phase (the anti-rigidity witness). Contrast Role, whose change is relational rather than intrinsic."
msgstr "Un anti-rigid sortal an instance falls sous during a stage de its existence determined par a change dans its own intrinsic état — child, adult, vacant, occupied."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PhaseMixin|rdfs:label"
msgid "Phase Mixin"
msgstr "Phase Mixin"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PhaseMixin|skos:definition"
msgid "An anti-rigid non-sortal that abstracts an intrinsically-determined phase shared across instances of several Kinds — living thing (a person or an animal in its living phase). Anti-rigid and identity-dispersive: a Phase generalized to span multiple Kinds without supplying identity. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:PhaseMixin only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Un anti-rigid non-sortal qui abstracts an intrinsically-determined phase shared across instances de several Kinds — living thing (a person ou an animal dans its living phase)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Plan|rdfs:label"
msgid "Plan"
msgstr "plan"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Plan|skos:definition"
msgid "A transaction program (a logic:TransactionProgram-kind node) whose primitive operations invoke action schemas and whose success criterion is a goal expression. As a program it carries the structure a decomposed goal alone cannot — ordering and serial composition, guards, branching, concurrency, loops, and fallback — all in the operators of the transaction layer. A POLICY is a plan whose branches are conditioned on what an earlier action's observation reveals rather than fixed in advance; this is a reading of a plan, NOT a separate class. Plan adoption and revision are recorded as an intention is: a plan is held over an interval and revised by suppression, never mutated. Because an action schema may carry a nondeterministic outcome set, plan success is quantified over those outcomes through logic:planSuccessMode rather than left to the bare executional-success reading. On the foundational spine a logic:Plan is a gmeow:SocialObject (a description, not a physical thing), grounded in prose per the logic-core convention rather than by a subclass edge; a process surface that specializes logic:Plan therefore also asserts its own gmeow:SocialObject or gmeow:InformationObject sort directly, since the prose grounding licenses no DL inference of it."
msgstr "Un transaction program (a logic:TransactionProgram-kind nœud) dont primitive operations invoke action schemas et dont success criterion est a objectif expression."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PlanSuccessMode|rdfs:label"
msgid "Plan Success Mode"
msgstr "plan Success Mode"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PlanSuccessMode|skos:definition"
msgid "The closed value class of the success quantification a logic:Plan declares over the nondeterministic outcomes of its action schemas. Its individuals are logic:WeakPlanSuccess (some outcome path reaches the goal), logic:StrongPlanSuccess (every outcome path reaches it), and logic:StrongCyclicPlanSuccess (every fair execution is guaranteed to reach it in finitely many steps, allowing retried loops through recoverable failures). The set is closed; a misspelt value is rejected. The quantification exists because the bare executional-success reading of the transaction layer would count the mere existence of one favourable path as success. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:PlanSuccessMode only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le classe de valeurs fermée de the success quantification a logic:plan déclare sur the nondeterministic outcomes de its action schemas."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PolicySpecificArgumentation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Policy-Specific Argumentation"
msgstr "politique-Specific argumentation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PolicySpecificArgumentation|skos:definition"
msgid "The argumentation-facet value selecting a domain- or policy-specific conflict-resolution semantics rather than a standard Dung semantics — e.g. a declared preference or priority ordering proper to a normative or legal register. Contrast logic:GroundedArgumentation and logic:PreferredArgumentation, the standard abstract-argumentation semantics."
msgstr "Le argumentation-facet valeur selecting a domaine- ou politique-specific conflit-resolution sémantique plutôt que a standard Dung sémantique — e.g."


msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PositiveHornProfile|rdfs:label"
msgid "Positive Horn Profile"
msgstr "positif Horn profil"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PositiveHornProfile|skos:definition"
msgid "The monotonic Horn-rule semantics: least-model semantics over positive (negation-free) rules, always terminating for the function-free fragment. The base case against which every richer profile adds expressivity and cost."
msgstr "Le monotonic Horn-règle sémantique: least-modèle sémantique sur positif (negation-free) rules, toujours terminating pour the fonction-free fragment."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PossibleWorld|rdfs:label"
msgid "Possible World"
msgstr "Possible monde"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PossibleWorld|skos:definition"
msgid "A typed alethic context — a logic:World of alethic possibility, one of the distinct typed contexts of the context algebra (alongside the doxastic gmeow:EpistemicContext, the perspectival gmeow:Standpoint, the hypothesized gmeow:Scenario, the gmeow:State along a logic:Path, the gmeow:ReferenceFrame, and the gmeow:NarrativeReferenceFrame). The contexts its typed accessibility relation logic:epistemicallyPossible ranges over; the modal operators (necessity, possibility) are the standard translation over that typed relation, never over a blurred union. It is a logic:World of the alethic world-type (stated in prose, not as a subclass edge), so no inference may cross into it by walking the bare logic:accessibleFrom superproperty."
msgstr "Un typed alethic contexte — a logic:monde de alethic possibility, one de the distinct typed contexts de the contexte algebra (alongside the doxastic gmeow:EpistemicContext, the perspectival gmeow:point de vue, the hypothesized gmeow:Scenario, the gmeow:état along a logic:chemin, the gmeow:ReferenceFrame, et the gmeow:NarrativeReferenceFrame)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PreferredArgumentation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Preferred Argumentation"
msgstr "Preferred argumentation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PreferredArgumentation|skos:definition"
msgid "The preferred Dung argumentation semantics: acceptance over the maximal (with respect to set inclusion) admissible sets of arguments. The credulous counterpart of logic:GroundedArgumentation — a framework may have several preferred extensions, so it admits genuine choice where the grounded semantics is uniquely sceptical."
msgstr "Le preferred Dung argumentation sémantique: acceptance sur the maximal (with respect à set inclusion) admissible sets de arguments."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PreservationKind|rdfs:label"
msgid "Preservation Kind"
msgstr "Preservation Kind"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PreservationKind|skos:definition"
msgid "The polarity of guarantee a reasoning projection makes about its answers relative to the canonical logic: model: the answer-preservation classification recorded in the loss ledger for each projection, distinct from and complementary to the complexity/decidability class. Its individuals range from exact preservation through sound under-approximation and complete over-approximation to validation-only, the unsupported floor (the construct cannot be expressed in the target at all), and the two inconsistency-direction kinds."
msgstr "Le polarity de guarantee a raisonnement projection makes about its answers relative à the logique canonique: modèle: the answer-preservation classification recorded dans the loss ledger pour each projection, distinct de et complementary à the complexity/decidability class."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Prism|rdfs:label"
msgid "Prism"
msgstr "Prism"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Prism|skos:definition"
msgid "A partial map S → V + S that matches and builds only on the in-focus case of a sum or optional: the optic for 'this correspondence applies when the source is of a particular variant, otherwise it passes through.' Caps: match / build laws on the in-focus case only. Paired with logic:AffineCorrespondence as the partial-alignment band below logic:LossyLens."
msgstr "Un partial map S → V + S qui matches et builds uniquement sur the in-focus case de a sum ou facultatif: the optic pour 'this correspondance applies lorsque the source est de a particular variant, otherwise it passes through.' Caps: match / build laws sur the in-focus case only."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ProbabilisticFramework|rdfs:label"
msgid "Probabilistic Framework"
msgstr "Probabilistic cadre"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ProbabilisticFramework|skos:definition"
msgid "The uncertainty framework: logic:probability as a graded-belief measure over a declared logic:ProbabilityModel (an independence or dependency model), with marginals computed by weighted model counting. A measure on the uncertainty facet, never a model-semantics value, and kept strictly distinct from logic:confidence (epistemic metadata), logic:weight (solver ranking), and logic:evidenceStrength (warrant) — the four are not interchangeable (design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md, the confidence-probability-weight-and-evidence section)."
msgstr "Le uncertainty cadre: logic:probability as a graded-belief measure sur a declared logic:ProbabilityModel (an independence ou dependency modèle), avec marginals computed par weighted modèle counting."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ProbabilisticMeasure|rdfs:label"
msgid "Probabilistic Measure"
msgstr "Probabilistic Measure"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ProbabilisticMeasure|skos:definition"
msgid "The uncertainty measure carrying calibrated probabilities, requiring a declared logic:ProbabilityModel. One member of the uncertainty-measure set facet (it may coexist with logic:WeightedRankingMeasure or logic:FuzzyMeasure); it is a measure carried alongside the chosen model semantics, never a model-semantics value of its own, and never the default reading of a logic:confidence number."
msgstr "Le uncertainty measure carrying calibrated probabilities, requiring a declared logic:ProbabilityModel."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ProbabilisticProfile|rdfs:label"
msgid "Probabilistic Profile"
msgstr "Probabilistic profil"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ProbabilisticProfile|skos:definition"
msgid "Probabilistic inference over logic:probability, ProbLog-style: requires an explicit independence or dependency model. Probabilistic inference is available only in this profile — it is not the default reading of every confidence number, and a logic:confidence annotation is never interpreted as a probability unless an explicit mapping to logic:probability is declared."
msgstr "Probabilistic inference sur logic:probability, ProbLog-style: exige an explicit independence ou dependency modèle."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ProbabilityModel|rdfs:label"
msgid "Probability Model"
msgstr "Probability modèle"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ProbabilityModel|skos:definition"
msgid "A declared independence or dependency model governing probabilistic inference for a rule set or world. Probabilistic inference under logic:ProbabilisticProfile is available ONLY when such a model is declared via logic:probabilityModel: the model fixes the joint distribution over the logic:probability facts so that marginals are well-defined. Absent a declared model the profile refuses to infer probabilities — it never silently assumes independence, because treating un-modelled confidence metadata as a probability model is the named failure mode this vocabulary exists to prevent."
msgstr "Un declared independence ou dependency modèle governing probabilistic inference pour a règle set ou monde."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ProceduralExecution|rdfs:label"
msgid "Procedural Execution"
msgstr "Procedural exécution"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ProceduralExecution|skos:definition"
msgid "The operational-execution property of a resource policy: SLD search control (cut) and builtins are permitted — an operational rather than purely declarative reading. This is the facet that licenses cut; cut-confinement (the AC-2 seal) is decided on it, never on the budget/bound property: a budget-bounded contract does not, by that fact alone, license cut. Only the procedural preset expands to it, but a contract assembled directly with this facet licenses cut even without the ProceduralPrologProfile preset name."
msgstr "Le operational-exécution propriété de a ressource politique: SLD search contrôle (cut) et builtins sont permitted — an operational plutôt que purely declarative reading."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ProceduralPrologProfile|rdfs:label"
msgid "Procedural Prolog Profile"
msgstr "Procedural Prolog profil"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ProceduralPrologProfile|skos:definition"
msgid "SLD resolution with cut and builtins: an operational, not purely declarative, semantics in which procedural search control (cut) and order-sensitive evaluation are permitted. Cut lives only here; artifacts using it must not project as declarative rules without recording the loss, because cut can change a program's answer set and defeats faithful-by-construction explanation."
msgstr "SLD resolution avec cut et builtins: an operational, not purely declarative, sémantique dans qui procedural search contrôle (cut) et order-sensitive evaluation sont permitted."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Process|rdfs:label"
msgid "Process"
msgstr "Process"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Process|skos:definition"
msgid "A perdurant with internal dynamics: an occurrent composed of sub-processes and phases that unfold over its temporal extent — a manufacturing run, a negotiation, a fermentation. A logic:Perdurant richer than a punctual event (stated in prose, not as a subclass edge); part of the native four-dimensional treatment that restores the UFO-B account gUFO scales back (criticism 3). Dissective: any temporal part of a process is itself that same process, and a process MAY vary over its extent (it bears time-varying logic:Fluents) — the change-bearing half of the process-not-equal-event asymmetry."
msgstr "Un perdurant avec internal dynamics: an occurrent composed de sub-processes et phases qui unfold sur its temporal extent — a manufacturing run, a negotiation, a fermentation."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ProjectionLoss|rdfs:label"
msgid "Projection Loss"
msgstr "projection Loss"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ProjectionLoss|skos:definition"
msgid "An in-band declaration that a lossy projection dropped structure its source carried — emitted into the projected graph itself, never a sidecar. GTS stays lossless; loss is declared only at the exit gate (Principle 17 / Principle 4). A loss-aware SPARQL CONSTRUCT mints one when its template omits an RDF-1.2 reification layer that its WHERE matched, so a downstream consumer of the projection can see exactly what was shed."
msgstr "Un in-band declaration qui a lossy projection dropped structure its source carried — emitted dans the projected graphe itself, jamais a sidecar."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ProjectionTarget|rdfs:label"
msgid "Projection Target"
msgstr "projection Target"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ProjectionTarget|skos:definition"
msgid "The facet value class of a projection target: a surface the answer is rendered to. The projection facet is an output request that may name one or more targets (canonical, OWL, Datalog, Common Logic, validation-only) at once; it is a standing request, not a semantic selection, and never alters which entailments hold."
msgstr "Le facet valeur class de a projection target: a surface the answer est rendered to."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PropertyCharacteristicAssertion|rdfs:label"
msgid "property characteristic assertion"
msgstr "propriété characteristic assertion"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PropertyCharacteristicAssertion|skos:definition"
msgid "A central record asserting that a named property bears a characteristic sort — one of logic:transitiveProperty, logic:symmetricProperty, logic:irreflexiveProperty, logic:asymmetricProperty or logic:functionalProperty. It names the property with logic:characterizes and the sort with logic:characteristicSort, the pair the native coherence gate joins to enforce the characteristic, and carries a logic:formalizes back-reference to the domain property whose prose it encodes. This is the canonical logic: carrier of a property characteristic: the domain slice keeps the OWL-facing declaration, the reasoning authority names and enforces it here. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Un central record asserting qui a named propriété bears a characteristic sort — one de logic:transitiveProperty, logic:symmetricProperty, logic:irreflexiveProperty, logic:asymmetricProperty ou logic:functionalProperty."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PropertyPathProjection|rdfs:label"
msgid "Property Path Projection"
msgstr "propriété chemin projection"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PropertyPathProjection|skos:definition"
msgid "The projection-target value requesting that a logic:PathShape (or a rule's path-structured body) be rendered to a SPARQL property-path surface — extended by GMEOW past SPARQL 1.1 §9 with bounded depth {n,m} and a predicate wildcard. One of several output targets a single contract may name at once; like every projection target it is a rendering request and never alters which entailments hold. A consumer restricted to standard SPARQL §9 receives the unrolled or approximated form, and that loss is declared in the loss ledger rather than hidden."
msgstr "Le projection-target valeur requesting qui a logic:PathShape (or a règle's chemin-structured body) be rendered à a SPARQL propriété-chemin surface — extended par GMEOW past SPARQL 1.1 §9 avec bounded depth {n,m} et a prédicat wildcard."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ProseField|rdfs:label"
msgid "Prose Field"
msgstr "Prose Field"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ProseField|skos:definition"
msgid "The closed three-member value class of the logic:candidateSourceField facet: which annotation field of a term's prose a logic:FormalizationCandidate harvested its axiom from. Its individuals are logic:ProseFieldDefinition, logic:ProseFieldUseWhen and logic:ProseFieldAvoidWhen, each naming the annotation property it stands for via logic:proseFieldProperty (skos:definition, gmeow:useWhen and gmeow:avoidWhen respectively). The set is closed and atomic (Principle 9), so a misspelt field names no declared value and is rejected rather than silently accepted. Read with logic:candidateFormalizes (which term) it makes harvest coverage queryable in both directions — from a harvested axiom to the exact prose field it formalizes, and from a prose field to the axioms that formalize it (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, §Typed formalization governance)."
msgstr "Le closed three-member valeur class de the logic:candidateSourceField facet: qui annotation field de a terme's prose a logic:FormalizationCandidate harvested its axiom from."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ProseFieldAvoidWhen|rdfs:label"
msgid "Avoid When"
msgstr "Avoid When"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ProseFieldAvoidWhen|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:ProseField for a term's gmeow:avoidWhen — the anti-pattern or non-applicability guidance a candidate formalized. Wire value `avoid-when`."
msgstr "Le logic:ProseField pour a terme's gmeow:avoidWhen — the anti-pattern ou non-applicability guidance a candidat formalized."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ProseFieldDefinition|rdfs:label"
msgid "Definition"
msgstr "définition"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ProseFieldDefinition|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:ProseField for a term's skos:definition — the definitional or descriptive prose a candidate formalized. Wire value `definition`."
msgstr "Le logic:ProseField pour a terme's skos:définition — the definitional ou descriptive prose a candidat formalized."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ProseFieldUseWhen|rdfs:label"
msgid "Use When"
msgstr "Use When"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ProseFieldUseWhen|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:ProseField for a term's gmeow:useWhen — the applicability guidance a candidate formalized. Wire value `use-when`."
msgstr "Le logic:ProseField pour a terme's gmeow:useWhen — the applicability guidance a candidat formalized."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PutGet|rdfs:label"
msgid "PutGet"
msgstr "PutGet"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PutGet|skos:definition"
msgid "The lens law get(put(v, s)) = v: putting a view into a source and reading it back yields exactly that view. Claimable from the logic:WellBehavedLens rung upward; the update-faithfulness law."
msgstr "Le lens loi get(put(v, s)) = v: putting a view dans a source et reading it back yields exactly qui view."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PutPut|rdfs:label"
msgid "PutPut"
msgstr "PutPut"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/PutPut|skos:definition"
msgid "The very-well-behaved lens law put(v2, put(v1, s)) = put(v2, s): a later put overwrites an earlier one with no residue. Optional even at the logic:WellBehavedLens rung; claimed only by correspondences whose put leg is genuinely history-free."
msgstr "Le very-well-behaved lens loi put(v2, put(v1, s)) = put(v2, s): a later put overwrites an earlier one avec no residue."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Quality|rdfs:label"
msgid "Quality"
msgstr "qualité"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Quality|skos:definition"
msgid "An aspect whose value is a point or region in a quality space — a mass, a temperature, a colour hue — an intrinsic, directly measurable moment. The counterpart of gufo:Quality; a logic:Aspect that takes a logic:QualityValue in a logic:QualitySpace (stated in prose, not as a subclass edge). Contrast logic:Mode, which is not directly measurable. A logic:Quality is persistent: it inheres in a bearer and endures while its measured values change, so dated observations attach to one enduring quality (by reference) rather than minting a fresh value each time. It instantiates a frame-independent generic quality via logic:genericQuality and may play an anti-rigid quality-role in a bearer-context via logic:qualityRole over logic:Role — the generic-quality/quality-role ladder (Principle 11)."
msgstr "Un aspect dont valeur est a point ou region dans a qualité space — a mass, a temperature, a colour hue — an intrinsic, directly measurable moment."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/QualityConstraint|rdfs:label"
msgid "Quality Constraint"
msgstr "qualité contrainte"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/QualityConstraint|skos:definition"
msgid "A named quality/quantity well-formedness axiom a quality or measured value can violate — the family of constraints governing the generic-quality/quality-role ladder and the true-quantity/measured-value seam. Distinct from logic:OccurrentConstraint (the four-dimensional perdurant axioms) and logic:MereologyConstraint (profiled-mereology axioms): quality constraints govern the stratification of a quality into a frame-independent generic quality, the anti-rigid role it plays in a bearer-context, and a frame-relative measured value. Its named individuals are the labels a logic:violation fact may point at; the set is closed so a misspelt label names no declared constraint and is rejected rather than silently accepted."
msgstr "Un named qualité/quantity bien forméness axiom a qualité ou measured valeur peut violate — the family de constraints governing the generic-qualité/qualité-role ladder et the true-quantity/measured-valeur seam."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/QualityRoleWithoutGeneric|rdfs:label"
msgid "Quality Role Without Generic"
msgstr "qualité Role Without Generic"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/QualityRoleWithoutGeneric|skos:definition"
msgid "The ladder-completeness axiom as a quality constraint: a quality that plays a quality-role must also instantiate the generic quality that role contextualizes — a logic:Quality with a logic:qualityRole but no logic:genericQuality is ill-formed. The generic quality (length, pressure) is the frame-independent structure; the quality-role (height, systolic pressure) is that structure playing an anti-rigid logic:Role in a bearer-context, and the role presupposes the generic it specializes (Principle 11 in role terms: the frame-relative value cannot stand without the frame-independent structure it refines). A quality bearing a role with no generic is the logic:violation, entailed by the foundation lowering rather than asserted by hand."
msgstr "Le ladder-complétude axiom as a qualité contrainte: a qualité qui plays a qualité-role doit also instantiate the generic qualité qui role contextualizes — a logic:qualité avec a logic:qualityRole mais no logic:genericQuality est ill-formed."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/QualitySpace|rdfs:label"
msgid "Quality Space"
msgstr "qualité Space"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/QualitySpace|skos:definition"
msgid "The structured space of possible values for a kind of quality — the mass scale, the temperature scale, a colour solid — within which a logic:Quality's logic:QualityValue is located. The conceptual-space structure (ordering, metric, dimensions) against which quality values are compared; it supplies the geometry a bare value would lack. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:QualitySpace only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le structured space de possible values pour a kind de qualité — the mass scale, the temperature scale, a colour solid — within qui a logic:qualité's logic:QualityValue est located."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/QualityValue|rdfs:label"
msgid "Quality Value"
msgstr "qualité valeur"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/QualityValue|skos:definition"
msgid "A point or region within a quality space that a logic:Quality takes as its value — 80 kg, 37 °C, the hue at coordinate (h,s,v). The counterpart of gufo:QualityValue; a logic:AbstractIndividual situated in a logic:QualitySpace (stated in prose, not as a subclass edge)."
msgstr "Un point ou region within a qualité space qui a logic:qualité takes as its valeur — 80 kg, 37 °C, the hue at coordinate (h,s,v)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Quantified|rdfs:label"
msgid "Quantified"
msgstr "Quantified"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Quantified|skos:definition"
msgid "The residue shape tag for a formula in which an explicit quantifier (logic:forall or logic:exists) appears — quantification nested or alternating beyond the implicit universal closure of a Horn rule. Disclosed when a Horn-fragment target carries such a formula as flagged unsupported residue."
msgstr "Le residue forme tag pour a formule dans qui an explicit quantifier (logic:forall ou logic:exists) appears — quantification nested ou alternating beyond the implicit universel fermeture de a Horn règle."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Quantity|rdfs:label"
msgid "Quantity"
msgstr "Quantity"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Quantity|skos:definition"
msgid "An amount of stuff individuated by its constitution rather than by a count of members — a portion of water, a lump of clay, a quantity of gold. The counterpart of gufo:Quantity; its identity tracks the matter that constitutes it (maximally self-connected portions of a substance), not a number of discrete units. Contrast logic:Collection, individuated by its members."
msgstr "Un amount de stuff individuated par its constitution plutôt que par a count de members — a portion de water, a lump de clay, a quantity de gold."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Query|rdfs:label"
msgid "Query"
msgstr "requête"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Query|skos:definition"
msgid "A goal to be resolved, carried together with its answer shape: the node kind that asks a question of the IR rather than asserting or deriving. Distinct from logic:DerivationRule and logic:TransactionProgram so a query operator is never read as a program operator."
msgstr "Un objectif à be resolved, carried together avec its answer forme: the nœud kind qui asks a question de the IR plutôt que asserting ou deriving."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RdfEqualityPolicy|rdfs:label"
msgid "RDF Equality Policy"
msgstr "RDF Equality politique"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RdfEqualityPolicy|skos:definition"
msgid "The equality-policy value under which term identity is RDF node identity — two IRIs are equal exactly when they are the same node, and distinct IRIs are not assumed to co-refer absent an asserted equality. The baseline graph reading; contrast logic:ExplicitEqualityPolicy and logic:UniqueNameEqualityPolicy."
msgstr "Le equality-politique valeur sous qui terme identité est RDF nœud identité — two IRIs sont equal exactly lorsque they sont the same nœud, et distinct IRIs ne sont pas assumed à co-refer absent an asserted equality."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ReadCommittedIsolation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Read Committed Isolation"
msgstr "Read Committed Isolation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ReadCommittedIsolation|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:IsolationLevel guarantee under which a transaction observes only committed writes, but successive reads of the same item may differ — dirty reads excluded, non-repeatable reads still admitted."
msgstr "Le logic:IsolationLevel guarantee sous qui a transaction observes uniquement committed writes, mais successive reads de the same item peut differ — dirty reads excluded, non-repeatable reads still admitted."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ReadUncommittedIsolation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Read Uncommitted Isolation"
msgstr "Read Uncommitted Isolation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ReadUncommittedIsolation|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:IsolationLevel guarantee under which a transaction may observe uncommitted writes of others — the weakest level of the standard spectrum, admitting dirty reads."
msgstr "Le logic:IsolationLevel guarantee sous qui a transaction peut observe uncommitted writes de others — the weakest niveau de the standard spectrum, admitting dirty reads."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ReasoningContract|rdfs:label"
msgid "Reasoning Contract"
msgstr "raisonnement Contract"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ReasoningContract|skos:definition"
msgid "A compositional specification of the reasoning semantics a rule set is interpreted under: an independent selection across orthogonal facets (formula fragment, model semantics, truth/inconsistency semantics, negation operators, closure, context, evolution, uncertainty, argumentation, revision, equality) plus two standing requests (resource policy, projection targets). The canonical form GMEOW reasons over; the historical named profiles are presets that expand to a full facet selection. Replaces the single monolithic semantic-profile axis: 'sound' is meaningless until the full contract is fixed. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:ReasoningContract only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Un compositional specification de the raisonnement sémantique a règle set est interpreted under: an independent selection across orthogonal facets (formule fragment, modèle sémantique, vérité/inconsistency sémantique, negation operators, fermeture, contexte, evolution, uncertainty, argumentation, revision, equality) plus two standing requests (ressource politique, projection targets)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ReasoningPreset|rdfs:label"
msgid "Reasoning Preset"
msgstr "raisonnement Preset"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ReasoningPreset|skos:definition"
msgid "A named ReasoningContract that fixes a common, supported facet selection — sugar the compiler expands to the full facet bundle before reasoning. The historical profile names (positive-Horn, stratified-negation, well-founded, stable-model, procedural, probabilistic) survive only as presets, not as indivisible alternatives."
msgstr "Un named ReasoningContract qui fixes a commun, supported facet selection — sugar the compiler expands à the full facet bundle avant raisonnement."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ReasoningResult|rdfs:label"
msgid "Reasoning Result"
msgstr "raisonnement résultat"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ReasoningResult|skos:definition"
msgid "The single shared result a reasoning run produces and every consumer reads (ME2): a compositional status carrying FIVE orthogonal fields, each ranging over its own value class — logic:resultInput (well-formedness), logic:resultEvaluation (what the engine could do), logic:resultCompleteness (relative to what the answer is complete), logic:resultPreservation (the set of answer-preservation polarities the lowering claims, plus the constructs it could not carry), and logic:resultInformation (the four-valued Belnap verdict plus two explicit non-results). Several fields hold at once. It additionally carries the provenance bundle: logic:contractHash, logic:query/logic:conclusion, logic:resultProof/logic:resultCounterproof, the world/standpoint/time/path context, logic:engine, logic:consumedBudget, logic:certifiedFragment, logic:contradictionWitness, and logic:resultAssumption. Authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust); this is a lossy documentation projection (Principle 17). Normative in design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md, §The reasoning result."
msgstr "Le single shared résultat a raisonnement run produces et chaque consumer reads (ME2): a compositional status carrying FIVE orthogonal fields, each ranging sur its own valeur class — logic:resultInput (bien forméness), logic:resultEvaluation (what the engine could do), logic:resultCompleteness (relative à what the answer est complet), logic:resultPreservation (the set de answer-preservation polarities the lowering claims, plus the constructs it could not carry), et logic:resultInformation (the quatre-valued Belnap verdict plus two explicit non-results)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ReductionTheory|rdfs:label"
msgid "Reduction Theory"
msgstr "Reduction Theory"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ReductionTheory|skos:definition"
msgid "A declared theory of part-whole reducibility, relative to which an logic:EmergenceAssessment is made. It carries, via logic:reductionBasis, the property-values it treats as part-reducible — reconstructible from the proper parts that bear them. Emergence is always relative to such a theory: the same whole property may be logic:Aggregate under one ReductionTheory and logic:Emergent under another, and an logic:Emergent verdict can be overturned by a later, stronger theory without contradiction precisely because the assessment records which theory it was relative to. The systems-theory analogue of a logic:MereologyProfile — it scopes the emergence calculus rather than asserting reducibility foundation-wide (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Un declared theory de part-whole reducibility, relative à qui an logic:EmergenceAssessment est made."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RefutationAcceptanceWitness|rdfs:label"
msgid "Refutation Acceptance Witness"
msgstr "réfutation Acceptance témoin"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RefutationAcceptanceWitness|skos:definition"
msgid "The acceptance record that a symmetric φ/¬φ conjecture test resolved to a refutation carrying a concrete contradiction witness, executed natively by gmeow_logic::conjecture::conjecture_test. It names, through logic:namesContradictionWitness, the logic:ContradictionWitness the refutation rests on. The flagship producer runs the native test and pins that a refutation case yields Some(witness) while a corroboration case yields None; this witness is the ontological twin the thin logic:RefutationAcceptanceWitnessShape gates. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:RefutationAcceptanceWitness only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le acceptance record qui a symmetric φ/¬φ conjecture test resolved à a réfutation carrying a concret contradiction témoin, executed natively par gmeow_logic::conjecture::conjecture_test."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RelComp|rdfs:label"
msgid "Relator Completeness"
msgstr "Relator complétude"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RelComp|skos:definition"
msgid "The OntoUML RelComp anti-pattern: a concrete Relator must mediate at least two distinct entities. Mediation is read by entity count — a relator reaches two entities either through two distinct mediation roles, or through a single non-functional role (which connects two or more entities on its own). A concrete Relator (one with no logic: subclass to defer its mediations to) that reaches fewer than two entities — a single functional role, or none — violates it. The native foundation lowering enforces it over the whole ontology; the gUFO downcast is a lossy projection of it."
msgstr "Le OntoUML RelComp anti-pattern: a concret Relator doit mediate au moins two distinct entities."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RelatedMatch|rdfs:label"
msgid "related match"
msgstr "related match"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RelatedMatch|skos:definition"
msgid "The weakest positive relation: source and view are associated (curatorially relevant) but neither equivalent, subsuming nor reliably overlapping. Lowers to sssom:relatedMatch only; no logical alignment axiom is emitted. The floor of the positive lattice, above only the negative pole logic:Disjoint."
msgstr "Le weakest positif relation: source et view sont associated (curatorially relevant) mais neither equivalent, subsuming nor reliably overlapping."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RelationalCore|rdfs:label"
msgid "Relational Core"
msgstr "Relational Core"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RelationalCore|skos:definition"
msgid "The logical-to-physical lowering waist of the correspondence calculus: a first-class Datalog±-with-stratified-negation sub-language (with aggregation and existentials — the chase) between the full-FOL logic: IR and the native execution engine. Every execution strategy, the incremental layer and the semiring annotation that carries the quantitative axes target this one dialect, so a get leg compiles to a join plan and a put / chase to a semi-naive fixpoint with existentials over the same core (design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md and design/LOGIC-IR.md, the IR-commitments section)."
msgstr "Le logique-to-physical lowering waist de the correspondance calculus: a first-class Datalog±-with-stratified-negation sub-language (with aggregation et existentials — the chase) entre the full-FOL logic: IR et the native exécution engine."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RelationshipType|rdfs:label"
msgid "Relationship Type"
msgstr "relation type"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RelationshipType|skos:definition"
msgid "A logic:Type whose instances are relationships (relators or comparative relations): the type-level classifier of how two or more entities are related. The counterpart of gufo:RelationshipType; specialized by logic:MaterialRelationshipType (founded on a logic:Relator) and logic:ComparativeRelationshipType (grounded in the relata's qualities, with no relator). Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge."
msgstr "Un logic:type dont instances sont relationships (relators ou comparatif relations): the type-niveau classifier de how two ou more entities sont related."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Relator|rdfs:label"
msgid "Relator"
msgstr "Relator"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Relator|skos:definition"
msgid "A truthmaker of a material relation: an objectified relationship — a marriage, an employment, an enrolment — that mediates two or more relata and existentially depends on each of them. A Relator must mediate at least two distinct entities (the relator-mediation discipline, RelComp); the relation it grounds holds in virtue of the Relator existing. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:Relator only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Un truthmaker de a material relation: an objectified relation — a marriage, an employment, an enrolment — qui mediates two ou more relata et existentially depends sur each de them."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RelatumDistinctnessAssertion|rdfs:label"
msgid "relatum distinctness assertion"
msgstr "relatum distinctness assertion"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RelatumDistinctnessAssertion|skos:definition"
msgid "A central record asserting that, on a target class, two named roles must bind DISTINCT values on any one focus node — the mutual-inequality integrity condition of a relator whose relata must differ (a Commitment's committed agent and beneficiary, a Criterion's reward and penalty poles). It names the class with logic:distinctnessTarget and the two roles with logic:distinctnessRole, the triple the native coherence gate joins to raise a violation when the roles coincide, and carries a logic:formalizes back-reference to the domain property whose prose it encodes. The reasoning authority names and enforces it here; the domain slice keeps the OWL-facing role declarations. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:RelatumDistinctnessAssertion only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Un central record asserting that, sur a target class, two named roles doit bind DISTINCT values sur tout one focus nœud — the mutual-inequality intégrité condition de a relator dont relata doit differ (a engagement's committed agent et beneficiary, a Criterion's reward et penalty poles)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RepeatableReadIsolation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Repeatable Read Isolation"
msgstr "Repeatable Read Isolation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RepeatableReadIsolation|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:IsolationLevel guarantee under which re-reads of an item a transaction has read return the same value — non-repeatable reads excluded, phantom rows still admitted."
msgstr "Le logic:IsolationLevel guarantee sous qui re-reads de an item a transaction possède read return the same valeur — non-repeatable reads excluded, phantom rows still admitted."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ResourcePolicy|rdfs:label"
msgid "Resource Policy"
msgstr "ressource politique"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ResourcePolicy|skos:definition"
msgid "The facet value class of the resource facet: the engine's execution discipline. It is a structured execution policy holding several independent properties together — whether a certified-complete, terminating fragment is required AND what budget or bound applies — not a single complete-vs-bounded toggle, and not a semantic selection. A contract may carry both a certified-fragment requirement and a budget at once."
msgstr "Le facet valeur class de the ressource facet: the engine's exécution discipline."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ResultAssurance|rdfs:label"
msgid "Result Assurance"
msgstr "résultat Assurance"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ResultAssurance|skos:definition"
msgid "A reified assessment that targets one logic:ReasoningResult (via logic:assuresResult) and reads its fields JOINTLY: logic:InfoSupported with logic:Incomplete is provisional, whereas logic:InfoSupported with logic:CompleteForFragment is conclusive within that fragment; a correctly returned logic:InfoBoth is high-assurance about a contradictory input, not a defect. A result assurance is DISTINCT from a reliability assessment of the reasoner: the former judges one result, the latter judges a series of runs (a logic:CognitiveAssessment). Authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust); lossy documentation projection (Principle 17). Normative in design/LOGIC-COGNITION.md."
msgstr "Un reified évaluation qui targets one logic:ReasoningResult (via logic:assuresResult) et reads its fields JOINTLY: logic:InfoSupported avec logic:incomplet est provisional, whereas logic:InfoSupported avec logic:CompleteForFragment est conclusive within qui fragment; a correctly returned logic:InfoBoth est high-assurance about a contradictory input, not a defect."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ResultColumn|rdfs:label"
msgid "Result Column"
msgstr "résultat colonne"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ResultColumn|skos:definition"
msgid "One typed column of a logic:ResultShape: a declared SELECT variable (logic:columnVariable), its term-kind (logic:columnTermKind, mandatory — an untyped column is the bag this contract eliminates), an optional pinned datatype for literal columns (logic:columnDatatype), and whether it is bound in every row (logic:columnBinding). Authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust); this is a lossy documentation projection (Principle 17). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:ResultColumn only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "One typed colonne de a logic:ResultShape: a declared SELECT variable (logic:columnVariable), its terme-kind (logic:columnTermKind, mandatory — an untyped colonne est the bag this contract eliminates), an facultatif pinned datatype pour literal columns (logic:columnDatatype), et whether it est bound dans chaque row (logic:columnBinding)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ResultShape|rdfs:label"
msgid "Result Shape"
msgstr "résultat forme"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ResultShape|skos:definition"
msgid "A schema-level type contract on a SPARQL SELECT result set: the declared columns it carries (logic:declaresColumn) and the row-set cardinality (logic:shapeCardinality, with logic:shapeRowCount in count mode). The same construct types a query's expected INPUT (logic:expectsInputShape) and its guaranteed OUTPUT (logic:producesResultShape), so a query's input→output contract is checkable before execution. It generalises the test-DSL example-row idiom: an ExpectedRow is an example-instance of the ResultShape its competency question declares. Authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust); this is a lossy documentation projection (Principle 17). Normative in design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md, §The result row schema. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:ResultShape only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Un schéma-niveau type contract sur a SPARQL SELECT résultat set: the declared columns it porte (logic:declaresColumn) et the row-set cardinality (logic:shapeCardinality, avec logic:shapeRowCount dans count mode)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RevisionPolicy|rdfs:label"
msgid "Revision Policy"
msgstr "Revision politique"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RevisionPolicy|skos:definition"
msgid "The facet value class of the revision facet: how a body of conclusions absorbs change. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract. Its individuals range from monotonic (nothing retracted) through entrenchment-ordered belief revision to truth-maintenance. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:RevisionPolicy only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le facet valeur class de the revision facet: how a body de conclusions absorbs change."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RigidType|rdfs:label"
msgid "Rigid Type"
msgstr "Rigid type"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RigidType|skos:definition"
msgid "A logic:Type that applies necessarily to each of its instances — in every world in which an instance exists it instantiates the type (logic:rigidlyAppliesTo holds for all its instances). The counterpart of gufo:RigidType; the meta-type whose instances are the rigid sorts: logic:Kind and logic:SubKind are each a logic:RigidType and a logic:Sortal, logic:Category is a logic:RigidType and a logic:NonSortal. Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. Contrast logic:AntiRigidType."
msgstr "Un logic:type qui applies necessarily à each de its instances — dans chaque monde dans qui an instance exists it instantiates the type (logic:rigidlyAppliesTo holds pour tous its instances)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RiskAdvisory|rdfs:label"
msgid "Advisory"
msgstr "Advisory"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RiskAdvisory|skos:definition"
msgid "The semantic-risk class for a candidate with no entailment consequence at all — advisory content, the lightest review. Wire value `advisory`."
msgstr "Le semantic-risk class pour a candidat avec no implication consequence at tous — advisory content, the lightest révision."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RiskCoreContaminating|rdfs:label"
msgid "Core Contaminating"
msgstr "Core Contaminating"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RiskCoreContaminating|skos:definition"
msgid "The semantic-risk class for a candidate whose wrong formalization would corrupt the reasoned core — the highest risk, demanding the strictest review. Wire value `core-contaminating`."
msgstr "Le semantic-risk class pour a candidat dont wrong formalisation would corrupt the reasoned core — the highest risk, demanding the strictest révision."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RiskProjectionOnly|rdfs:label"
msgid "Projection Only"
msgstr "projection Only"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RiskProjectionOnly|skos:definition"
msgid "The semantic-risk class for a candidate whose blast radius is confined to a lossy projection surface, leaving the reasoned core intact. Wire value `projection-only`."
msgstr "Le semantic-risk class pour a candidat dont blast radius est confined à a lossy projection surface, leaving the reasoned core intact."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Role|rdfs:label"
msgid "Role"
msgstr "Role"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Role|skos:definition"
msgid "An anti-rigid sortal an instance falls under contingently, by virtue of a relation it bears to some other entity — student, employee, defendant. Anti-rigid: there is a world of existence in which the instance lacks the Role (the anti-rigidity witness). Identity-dependent on the underlying Kind; contrast Phase, whose change is intrinsic rather than relational."
msgstr "Un anti-rigid sortal an instance falls sous contingently, par virtue de a relation it bears à some other entity — student, employee, defendant."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RoleCompositionExclusionAssertion|rdfs:label"
msgid "role composition exclusion assertion"
msgstr "role composition exclusion assertion"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RoleCompositionExclusionAssertion|skos:definition"
msgid "A central record asserting that, on a target class, the value bound by a whole role must not also be — via any of a set of composition properties — the value bound by a part role on the same focus node: a relator whose one relatum composes the other is ill-formed (an argument does not attack its own component). It names the class with logic:compositionExclusionTarget, the whole and part roles with logic:compositionExclusionWhole and logic:compositionExclusionPart, and the composition steps with logic:compositionExclusionVia; the native coherence gate joins them to raise a violation. Carries a logic:formalizes back-reference to the domain property whose prose it encodes."
msgstr "Un central record asserting that, sur a target class, the valeur bound par a whole role ne doit pas also be — via tout de a set de composition properties — the valeur bound par a part role sur the same focus nœud: a relator dont one relatum composes the other est ill-formed (an argument ne fait pas attack its own component)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RoleMixin|rdfs:label"
msgid "Role Mixin"
msgstr "Role Mixin"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RoleMixin|skos:definition"
msgid "An anti-rigid non-sortal that abstracts a relationally-acquired property shared across instances of several Kinds — customer (a person or an organization), insured party. Anti-rigid and identity-dispersive: a Role generalized to span multiple Kinds without supplying identity. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:RoleMixin only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Un anti-rigid non-sortal qui abstracts a relationally-acquired propriété shared across instances de several Kinds — customer (a person ou an organization), insured party."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RowCardinality|rdfs:label"
msgid "Row Cardinality"
msgstr "Row Cardinality"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RowCardinality|skos:definition"
msgid "The closed value class of the logic:shapeCardinality facet: the row-set contract a result shape declares. Its individuals are logic:RowsExact (the declared example rows are the complete set), logic:RowsContains (the declared rows must all appear; extras permitted) and logic:RowsCount (only the count is pinned, via logic:shapeRowCount). The set is closed, so a misspelt value names no declared mode and is rejected. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:RowCardinality only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le classe de valeurs fermée de the logic:shapeCardinality facet: the row-set contract a résultat forme declares."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RowsContains|rdfs:label"
msgid "Rows Contains"
msgstr "Rows Contains"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RowsContains|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:RowCardinality value requiring the declared example rows to all appear, with extra rows permitted. Wire value `contains`."
msgstr "Le logic:RowCardinality valeur requiring the declared example rows à tous appear, avec extra rows permitted."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RowsCount|rdfs:label"
msgid "Rows Count"
msgstr "Rows Count"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RowsCount|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:RowCardinality value pinning only the result row count (carried by logic:shapeRowCount), with no per-row content contract. Wire value `count`."
msgstr "Le logic:RowCardinality valeur pinning uniquement the résultat row count (carried par logic:shapeRowCount), avec no per-row content contract."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RowsExact|rdfs:label"
msgid "Rows Exact"
msgstr "Rows Exact"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RowsExact|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:RowCardinality value pinning the declared example rows as the complete, exact result set. Wire value `exact`."
msgstr "Le logic:RowCardinality valeur pinning the declared example rows as the complet, exact résultat set."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RuleNoClosedWorldInCounterfactual|rdfs:label"
msgid "Rule: No Closed-World Closure In Counterfactual States"
msgstr "règle: No Closed-monde fermeture In contrefactuel States"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RuleNoClosedWorldInCounterfactual|skos:definition"
msgid "The compatibility rule forbidding logic:ClosedWorldClosure — whether the contract's logic:defaultClosure or any per-key closure entry value — together with counterfactual entrenchment revision (logic:EntrenchmentRevision is the contract-internal indicator that counterfactual closest-world states are generated). The counterfactual states are open-ended, so reading absence as falsehood inside them is unsound; a contract that names both is unsupported. Authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust); this individual is a lossy documentation projection (Principle 17)."
msgstr "Le compatibilité règle forbidding logic:ClosedWorldClosure — whether the contract's logic:defaultClosure ou tout per-key fermeture entrée valeur — together avec contrefactuel entrenchment revision (logic:EntrenchmentRevision est the contract-internal indicator qui contrefactuel closest-monde states sont generated)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RuleNoParaconsistentCounterfactualRevision|rdfs:label"
msgid "Rule: No Paraconsistent Truth Under Counterfactual Revision"
msgstr "règle: No Paraconsistent vérité Under contrefactuel Revision"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RuleNoParaconsistentCounterfactualRevision|skos:definition"
msgid "The compatibility rule forbidding a paraconsistent valuation — a gap/glut-admitting logic:admissibleValuation (logic:AdmitAllFour, logic:ForbidGap, or logic:ForbidGlut) OR the logic:BelnapBilattice truth algebra — together with counterfactual entrenchment revision (logic:EntrenchmentRevision, the contract-internal indicator of counterfactual closest-world generation). The closest-world selection that generates the counterfactual states is not defined over gappy or glutty valuations; a contract that names both is unsupported. Authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust); this individual is a lossy documentation projection (Principle 17)."
msgstr "Le compatibilité règle forbidding a paraconsistent évaluation — a gap/glut-admitting logic:admissibleValuation (logic:AdmitAllFour, logic:ForbidGap, ou logic:ForbidGlut) OR the logic:BelnapBilattice vérité algebra — together avec contrefactuel entrenchment revision (logic:EntrenchmentRevision, the contract-internal indicator de contrefactuel closest-monde generation)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RuleNoProbabilisticStableModel|rdfs:label"
msgid "Rule: No Probabilistic Measure Over Stable-Model Semantics"
msgstr "règle: No Probabilistic Measure Over Stable-modèle sémantique"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RuleNoProbabilisticStableModel|skos:definition"
msgid "The compatibility rule forbidding logic:ProbabilisticMeasure in the uncertainty-measure set together with logic:StableModelSemantics as the model semantics. A calibrated probability mass is not well-defined over the multiple incomparable answer sets the stable-model semantics admits; a contract that names both is unsupported. Authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust); this individual is a lossy documentation projection (Principle 17)."
msgstr "Le compatibilité règle forbidding logic:ProbabilisticMeasure dans the uncertainty-measure set together avec logic:StableModelSemantics as the modèle sémantique."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RuleProbabilisticRequiresModel|rdfs:label"
msgid "Rule: Probabilistic Measure Requires A Declared Probability Model"
msgstr "règle: Probabilistic Measure Requires A Declared Probability modèle"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/RuleProbabilisticRequiresModel|skos:definition"
msgid "The graph-dependent compatibility rule requiring that whenever a contract carries logic:ProbabilisticMeasure, the source graph declares a logic:ProbabilityModel (via logic:probabilityModel or an individual typed logic:ProbabilityModel). Absent a declared model the contract is unsupported: a probabilistic measure is never inferred from confidence metadata and independence is never silently assumed. Because it inspects the surrounding graph it is enforced in the front-end rather than the contract-internal rule table; authored canonically in crates/logic (Rust), projected here lossily (Principle 17)."
msgstr "Le graphe-dependent compatibilité règle requiring qui whenever a contract porte logic:ProbabilisticMeasure, the source graphe déclare a logic:ProbabilityModel (via logic:probabilityModel ou an individu typed logic:ProbabilityModel)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SatisfactionStatus|rdfs:label"
msgid "Satisfaction Status"
msgstr "satisfaction Status"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SatisfactionStatus|skos:definition"
msgid "The closed value class of the satisfaction axis of a logic:GoalEvaluation: to what extent the goal is met against the situation it is judged against. Its individuals are logic:Satisfied (fully met), logic:PartiallySatisfied (met in part — held apart from a low logic:confidence in a satisfied evaluation, which is a different question), logic:Violated (a maintenance or avoidance target has failed), and logic:Unsatisfied (not met, with no positive partial progress recorded). The set is closed; a misspelt value is rejected. Together with logic:GoalEvaluationCompleted, logic:Satisfied is the condition under which a gmeow:satisfiedBy edge is generated."
msgstr "Le classe de valeurs fermée de the satisfaction axis de a logic:GoalEvaluation: à what extent the objectif est met contre the situation it est judged against."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Satisfied|rdfs:label"
msgid "Satisfied"
msgstr "Satisfied"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Satisfied|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:SatisfactionStatus value for a goal fully met against the situation it is judged against. Together with goal-evaluation status logic:GoalEvaluationCompleted it is the condition that generates a gmeow:satisfiedBy edge. Distinct from a high logic:confidence in a satisfied evaluation — how met is not how sure."
msgstr "Le logic:SatisfactionStatus valeur pour a objectif fully met contre the situation it est judged against."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SatisfiedByBackedByEvaluationConstraint|rdfs:label"
msgid "satisfiedBy backed-by-evaluation constraint"
msgstr "satisfiedBy backed-by-evaluation contrainte"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SatisfiedByBackedByEvaluationConstraint|skos:definition"
msgid "A closed-world integrity constraint: a conclusive gmeow:satisfiedBy edge is backed by a vantage-scoped logic:GoalEvaluation that evaluatesGoal this goal, was evaluatedAgainst the situation, and is Satisfied and completed."
msgstr "Un monde fermé intégrité contrainte: a conclusive gmeow:satisfiedBy edge est backed par a vantage-scoped logic:GoalEvaluation qui evaluatesGoal this objectif, was evaluatedAgainst the situation, et est Satisfied et completed."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SecondOrder|rdfs:label"
msgid "Second-Order"
msgstr "Second-Order"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SecondOrder|skos:definition"
msgid "The expressiveness boundary of a defining statement that genuinely exceeds first-order logic — quantification over families/subsets or an appeal to finiteness (e.g. compactness's 'every open cover has a finite subcover'). Not authorable as a logic:Formula; carried in the loss ledger as an honest boundary with logic:preservationKind logic:Unsupported, never as a fake first-order formula."
msgstr "Le expressiveness boundary de a defining statement qui genuinely exceeds premier ordre logic — quantification sur families/subsets ou an appeal à finiteness (e.g."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SectionAcceptanceWitness|rdfs:label"
msgid "Section Acceptance Witness"
msgstr "section Acceptance témoin"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SectionAcceptanceWitness|skos:definition"
msgid "The acceptance record that a correspondence get/put leg pair discharges its section law (put ∘ get = identity), executed natively by gmeow_logic::correspondence_exec::leg_pair_verdict. It names, through logic:dischargesSectionObligation, the section obligation the executed round-trip discharges. The flagship producer runs the native discharge and pins that a genuine inverse yields DischargeVerdict::ObligationDischarged while a broken section does not; this witness is the ontological twin the thin logic:SectionAcceptanceWitnessShape gates."
msgstr "Le acceptance record qui a correspondance get/put leg pair discharges its section loi (put ∘ get = identité), executed natively par gmeow_logic::correspondence_exec::leg_pair_verdict."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SectionLaw|rdfs:label"
msgid "Section Law"
msgstr "section loi"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SectionLaw|skos:definition"
msgid "The perfect-subsumption law put ∘ get = id_S: the source is recovered exactly from its view because the in-band complement retained everything the retraction needs (a logic:mnemomorphic witness). Claimable only at the logic:SectionRetraction rung or above; the CI-checkable form of 'GMEOW perfectly subsumes this vocabulary.'"
msgstr "Le perfect-subsumption loi put ∘ get = id_S: the source est recovered exactly de its view parce que the in-band complement retained everything the retraction needs (a logic:mnemomorphic témoin)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SectionObligationViolated|rdfs:label"
msgid "Section Obligation Violated"
msgstr "section obligation Violated"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SectionObligationViolated|skos:definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a logic:SectionAcceptanceWitness — the acceptance record of a correspondence section-law discharge — names no logic:dischargesSectionObligation edge, i.e. claims a get/put leg pair round-trips without pointing at the section obligation it discharges. The section law (put ∘ get = identity) is the correspondence's teeth; a witness that discharges no obligation is unfalsifiable, so the gate rejects it (LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:SectionObligationViolated only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le échec raised lorsque a logic:SectionAcceptanceWitness — the acceptance record de a correspondance section-loi acquittement — nomme no logic:dischargesSectionObligation edge, i.e."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SectionRetraction|rdfs:label"
msgid "Section / Retraction"
msgstr "section / Retraction"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SectionRetraction|skos:definition"
msgid "Perfect subsumption: a split mono with put ∘ get = id_S and get ∘ put idempotent on V ⊕ complement. The source embeds losslessly into the view, the augmentation being S ∖ im(get) carried in the in-band complement. Caps: the section law (lossless source recovery), but not full bidirectional iso."
msgstr "Perfect subsumption: a split mono avec put ∘ get = id_S et get ∘ put idempotent sur V ⊕ complement."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SemanticRiskClass|rdfs:label"
msgid "Semantic Risk Class"
msgstr "Semantic Risk Class"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SemanticRiskClass|skos:definition"
msgid "The closed value class of the logic:candidateSemanticRisk facet: how far a wrong formalization of a candidate would propagate, which makes the reviewer gate proportionate. Its individuals are logic:RiskCoreContaminating, logic:RiskProjectionOnly and logic:RiskAdvisory. The set is closed, so a misspelt class names no declared value and is rejected (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, §Typed formalization governance). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:SemanticRiskClass only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le classe de valeurs fermée de the logic:candidateSemanticRisk facet: how far a wrong formalisation de a candidat would propagate, qui makes the reviewer gate proportionate."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SemiRigidType|rdfs:label"
msgid "Semi-Rigid Type"
msgstr "Semi-Rigid type"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SemiRigidType|skos:definition"
msgid "A logic:Type that is rigid for some of its instances and anti-rigid for others — logic:rigidlyAppliesTo holds for part of its extension and fails for the rest. The counterpart of gufo:SemiRigidType; its sole foundation instance is logic:Mixin (a logic:SemiRigidType and a logic:NonSortal). Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. A logic:SemiRigidType is a logic:NonRigidType but not a logic:AntiRigidType (which requires contingency for every instance)."
msgstr "Un logic:type qui est rigid pour some de its instances et anti-rigid pour others — logic:rigidlyAppliesTo holds pour part de its extension et fails pour the rest."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SequenceMarker|rdfs:label"
msgid "Sequence Marker"
msgstr "Sequence Marker"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SequenceMarker|skos:definition"
msgid "A variadic argument placeholder (the Common Logic '…x' form) that binds a sequence of terms rather than a single term, generalizing the fixed arity-three atom to predications of any arity. A term-carrier argument whose value is a logic:termSequenceMarker denotes one; keeping it a distinct kind stops a single-term variable from being mistaken for a sequence one."
msgstr "Un variadic argument placeholder (the commun Logic '…x' form) qui binds a sequence de terms plutôt que a single terme, generalizing the fixed arity-three atom à predications de tout arity."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SerialConjunction|rdfs:label"
msgid "Serial Conjunction"
msgstr "sériel Conjunction"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SerialConjunction|skos:definition"
msgid "The serial-conjunction program combinator (⊗, 'do φ then ψ'): the path along which the program executes splits so that φ holds over a prefix and ψ holds over the remaining suffix. It is a PROGRAM combinator over the transaction layer's path semantics, typed APART from ordinary (at-a-state) logical conjunction — a program operator is never conflated with the logical connective that holds at a single state, matching the formula-versus-program operator typing of the IR. Its two operands are carried by logic:leftOperand (the prefix program) and logic:rightOperand (the suffix program). The base relations of the layer are elementary state transitions, this serial conjunction, and executional entailment."
msgstr "Le sériel-conjunction program combinator (⊗, 'do φ then ψ'): the chemin along qui the program executes splits so qui φ holds sur a prefix et ψ holds sur the remaining suffix."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SerializabilityCriterion|rdfs:label"
msgid "Serializability Criterion"
msgstr "Serializability Criterion"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SerializabilityCriterion|skos:definition"
msgid "A correctness property OF A HISTORY — not a protocol and not a guarantee strength. The closed value class of serializability criteria for a concurrent transaction history. Its individuals are logic:ConflictSerializability (an equivalent serial order exists reachable with no swap of conflicting operations) and logic:ViewSerializability (some serial order has the same read-from and final-write relationships). The set is closed; a misspelt value is rejected. This is one of three distinct, separately-declared concurrency concerns that must NOT be conflated: a logic:SerializabilityCriterion is a property of a history, a logic:IsolationLevel is a declared guarantee strength, and a logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol is an implementation mechanism — keeping them apart is required because they are not interchangeable and an implicit assumption about any one of them is a defect."
msgstr "Un correctness propriété OF Un historique — not a protocol et not a guarantee strength."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SerializableIsolation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Serializable Isolation"
msgstr "Serializable Isolation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SerializableIsolation|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:IsolationLevel guarantee under which the schedule is equivalent to some serial execution of the committed transactions — full serializability. Strictly weaker than logic:OpacityIsolation, which additionally constrains aborted and in-flight transactions."
msgstr "Le logic:IsolationLevel guarantee sous qui the schedule est equivalent à some sériel exécution de the committed transactions — full serializability."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SerializationAnomaly|rdfs:label"
msgid "Serialization Anomaly"
msgstr "Serialization Anomaly"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SerializationAnomaly|skos:definition"
msgid "A HISTORY-LEVEL finding: a pattern of conflicting operations, read-from edges, and happens-before arcs in a transaction history that admits no equivalent serial execution under the declared policy. Lost updates, write skew, and read/write anomalies are findings of this kind. It is DISTINCT from a contradiction witness (logic:contradictionWitness, which asserts ⊥ within a single state) and must NOT be modelled as one: the final state after a non-serializable schedule may be perfectly logically consistent while the schedule still has no equivalent serial execution, so a serialization anomaly is a property of the history, never a logical contradiction inside a state. It is surfaced as a finding with its dependency cycle or violated isolation level described; a non-serializable schedule is never silently linearized."
msgstr "Un historique-niveau finding: a pattern de conflicting operations, read-from edges, et happens-before arcs dans a transaction historique qui admits no equivalent sériel exécution sous the declared politique."


msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Situation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Situation"
msgstr "situation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Situation|skos:definition"
msgid "A reified configuration of entities and their properties standing in a state of affairs at a time — the DOLCE Description-and-Situation sense: a snapshot of how things are that can satisfy a described state (a goal-world realized by a Situation). The static counterpart of the dynamic Event. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:Situation only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Un reified configuration de entities et their properties standing dans a état de affairs at a time — the DOLCE Description-and-situation sense: a snapshot de how things sont qui peut satisfy a described état (a objectif-monde realized par a situation)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SnapshotIsolation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Snapshot Isolation"
msgstr "Snapshot Isolation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SnapshotIsolation|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:IsolationLevel guarantee under which a transaction reads from a consistent snapshot taken at its start — strong against most anomalies yet still admitting write skew, so strictly weaker than logic:SerializableIsolation."
msgstr "Le logic:IsolationLevel guarantee sous qui a transaction reads de a cohérent snapshot taken at its start — strong contre most anomalies yet still admitting write skew, so strictly weaker than logic:SerializableIsolation."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Sortal|rdfs:label"
msgid "Sortal"
msgstr "Sortal"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Sortal|skos:definition"
msgid "A logic:Type that carries a principle of identity for its instances — it answers what counts as the same instance over time. The counterpart of gufo:Sortal; the meta-type whose instances are the identity-bearing sorts: logic:Kind (which supplies identity, via logic:suppliesIdentity), logic:SubKind, logic:Phase, and logic:Role (which inherit it). Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. Contrast logic:NonSortal, which supplies no identity."
msgstr "Un logic:type qui porte a principle de identité pour its instances — it answers what counts as the same instance sur time."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SoundUnderApproximation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Sound Under-Approximation"
msgstr "Sound Under-Approximation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SoundUnderApproximation|skos:definition"
msgid "Anything the projection entails is canonically valid, but the projection may miss canonical answers: sound but incomplete. The projection never overclaims a derivation; it may under-derive."
msgstr "Anything the projection entails est canonically valid, mais the projection peut miss canonique answers: sound mais incomplet."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/StableModelProfile|rdfs:label"
msgid "Stable Model Profile"
msgstr "Stable modèle profil"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/StableModelProfile|skos:definition"
msgid "Answer-set / stable-model semantics: a program may have several stable models (possibly none), and entailment is over those models. NP-hard in the worst case; the profile that admits genuine non-determinism and disjunctive reasoning."
msgstr "Answer-set / stable-modèle sémantique: a program peut possèdent several stable models (possibly none), et implication est sur those models."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/StableModelSemantics|rdfs:label"
msgid "Stable Model Semantics"
msgstr "Stable modèle sémantique"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/StableModelSemantics|skos:definition"
msgid "The model-semantics facet value selecting answer-set (stable-model) semantics: a program may have several stable models, or none, and entailment is taken over that model set. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract; the non-deterministic, NP-hard semantics for unstratified negation, contrasted with the unique well-founded model and the unique least model."
msgstr "Le modèle-sémantique facet valeur selecting answer-set (stable-modèle) sémantique: a program peut possèdent several stable models, ou none, et implication est taken sur qui modèle set."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/StandpointContextAxis|rdfs:label"
msgid "Standpoint Context Axis"
msgstr "point de vue contexte Axis"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/StandpointContextAxis|skos:definition"
msgid "The standpoint index axis of the multi-dimensional context facet: a truth is relative to a standpoint (a perspective in the sharpening poset). One of several context axes that coexist on a single result — world, standpoint, time, and path index the same result simultaneously rather than being alternative values of one slot."
msgstr "Le point de vue index axis de the multi-dimensional contexte facet: a vérité est relative à a point de vue (a perspective dans the sharpening poset)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/StateTransitionEvolution|rdfs:label"
msgid "State-Transition Evolution"
msgstr "état-transition Evolution"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/StateTransitionEvolution|skos:definition"
msgid "The evolution-facet value under which state changes across discrete transitions between successive states, each a configuration reasoned over in turn. The state-change mode between the static default and the full transaction-path semantics; independent of the model-semantics facet."
msgstr "Le evolution-facet valeur sous qui état changes across discrete transitions entre successive states, each a configuration reasoned sur dans turn."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/StaticEvolution|rdfs:label"
msgid "Static Evolution"
msgstr "Static Evolution"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/StaticEvolution|skos:definition"
msgid "The evolution-facet value under which no state change occurs — reasoning is over a single, degenerate one-state path. The default evolution mode; contrast logic:StateTransitionEvolution and logic:TransactionPathEvolution."
msgstr "Le evolution-facet valeur sous qui no état change occurs — raisonnement est sur a single, degenerate one-état chemin."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/StereotypeCardinality|rdfs:label"
msgid "Stereotype Cardinality"
msgstr "Stereotype Cardinality"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/StereotypeCardinality|skos:definition"
msgid "The discipline that every class carries exactly one stereotype: a class with no meta-class pun, or with two or more distinct meta-class puns, violates it. The lowering of reasoning_lint.exactly_one_stereotype — the precondition every other discipline assumes."
msgstr "Le discipline qui chaque class porte exactement un stereotype: a class avec no meta-class pun, ou avec two ou more distinct meta-class puns, violates it."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/StratifiedNAFProfile|rdfs:label"
msgid "Stratified Negation-As-Failure Profile"
msgstr "Stratified Negation-As-échec profil"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/StratifiedNAFProfile|skos:definition"
msgid "Negation-as-failure under stratification: a unique perfect model with PTIME data complexity, where negated literals are evaluated only over strata already settled. Adds well-behaved negation without the multiple models of the stable-model semantics."
msgstr "Negation-as-échec sous stratification: a unique perfect modèle avec PTIME données complexity, où negated literals sont evaluated uniquement sur strata already settled."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/StrictTwoPhaseLocking|rdfs:label"
msgid "Strict Two-Phase Locking"
msgstr "Strict Two-Phase Locking"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/StrictTwoPhaseLocking|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol that holds all EXCLUSIVE (write) locks until the transaction commits or aborts, preventing cascading aborts on writes. Contrast logic:StrongStrictTwoPhaseLocking, which additionally holds shared (read) locks to commit."
msgstr "Le logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol qui holds tous EXCLUSIVE (write) locks until the transaction commits ou aborts, preventing cascading aborts sur writes."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/StrongCyclicPlanSuccess|rdfs:label"
msgid "Strong-Cyclic Plan Success"
msgstr "Strong-Cyclic plan Success"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/StrongCyclicPlanSuccess|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:PlanSuccessMode value under which a plan succeeds when every FAIR execution is guaranteed to reach the goal in finitely many steps, allowing retried loops through recoverable failures — the reading that tolerates cyclic recovery a strong plan forbids while still guaranteeing eventual success a weak plan does not. Between logic:WeakPlanSuccess and logic:StrongPlanSuccess in strength."
msgstr "Le logic:PlanSuccessMode valeur sous qui a plan succeeds lorsque chaque FAIR exécution est guaranteed à reach the objectif dans finitely many steps, allowing retried loops par recoverable failures — the reading qui tolerates cyclic recovery a strong plan forbids while still guaranteeing eventual success a weak plan ne fait pas."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/StrongNegation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Strong Negation"
msgstr "Strong Negation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/StrongNegation|skos:definition"
msgid "The residue shape tag for a formula in which strong (explicit, classical) negation (logic:not) appears — distinct from negation-as-failure, which a Horn rule body already carries. Disclosed when a Horn-fragment target carries such a formula as flagged unsupported residue."
msgstr "Le residue forme tag pour a formule dans qui strong (explicit, classical) negation (logic:not) appears — distinct de negation-as-échec, qui a Horn règle body already carries."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/StrongPlanSuccess|rdfs:label"
msgid "Strong Plan Success"
msgstr "Strong plan Success"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/StrongPlanSuccess|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:PlanSuccessMode value under which a plan succeeds when EVERY outcome path reaches the goal — the universal reading, guaranteeing the goal regardless of how nondeterminism resolves. Contrast logic:WeakPlanSuccess (some path) and logic:StrongCyclicPlanSuccess (every fair execution, allowing retried loops)."
msgstr "Le logic:PlanSuccessMode valeur sous qui a plan succeeds lorsque EVERY résultat chemin reaches the objectif — the universel reading, guaranteeing the objectif regardless de how nondeterminism resolves."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/StrongStrictTwoPhaseLocking|rdfs:label"
msgid "Strong Strict Two-Phase Locking"
msgstr "Strong Strict Two-Phase Locking"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/StrongStrictTwoPhaseLocking|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol that holds ALL locks — both shared (read) and exclusive (write) — until commit or abort, yielding the strongest, strictest two-phase-locking discipline. The strong-strict variant the design names distinctly from the strict variant (logic:StrictTwoPhaseLocking), which releases shared locks earlier."
msgstr "Le logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol qui holds tous locks — both shared (read) et exclusive (write) — until commit ou abort, yielding the strongest, strictest two-phase-locking discipline."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SubKind|rdfs:label"
msgid "Sub Kind"
msgstr "Sub Kind"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SubKind|skos:definition"
msgid "A rigid sortal that specializes a Kind without supplying its own independent principle of identity: it carries the identity criterion inherited from the Kind it specializes. Rigid like a Kind, but identity-dependent rather than identity-supplying."
msgstr "Un rigid sortal qui specializes a Kind sans supplying its own independent principle de identité: it porte the identité criterion inherited de the Kind it specializes."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SubjectGranularity|rdfs:label"
msgid "Subject Granularity"
msgstr "Subject Granularity"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SubjectGranularity|skos:definition"
msgid "The value-vocabulary class of the grain of a logic:CognitiveAssessment's subject, named via logic:subjectGranularity: a single inference, a body of reasoning, a domain of competence, or the reasoner as a whole. An OPEN value vocabulary (individuals, never subclasses), since competence is judged at different grains and a new grain is a new individual."
msgstr "Le valeur-vocabulary class de the grain de a logic:CognitiveAssessment's subject, named via logic:subjectGranularity: a single inference, a body de raisonnement, a domaine de competence, ou the raisonneur as a whole."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Substantial|rdfs:label"
msgid "Substantial"
msgstr "Substantial"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Substantial|skos:definition"
msgid "An endurant that does NOT inhere in another individual: an independent bearer that can exist on its own and onto which aspects inhere. The complement of logic:Aspect within the endurant category; every logic:Object is a Substantial (stated in prose, not as a subclass edge)."
msgstr "Un endurant qui does NOT inhere dans another individu: an independent bearer qui peut exist sur its own et sur qui aspects inhere."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SubsumedBy|rdfs:label"
msgid "subsumed by"
msgstr "subsumed by"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SubsumedBy|skos:definition"
msgid "The source pattern is narrower than the view: every source instance is a view instance but not conversely. Lowers to sssom:narrowMatch and an owl:subClassOf with the source as the subclass. The converse direction of logic:Subsumes, the second mid-lattice relation under logic:Equiv."
msgstr "Le source pattern est narrower than the view: chaque source instance est a view instance mais not conversely."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Subsumes|rdfs:label"
msgid "subsumes"
msgstr "subsumes"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Subsumes|skos:definition"
msgid "The source pattern is broader than the view: every view instance is a source instance but not conversely. Lowers to sssom:broadMatch and an owl:subClassOf with the view as the subclass. One of the two mid-lattice directional relations under logic:Equiv."
msgstr "Le source pattern est broader than the view: chaque view instance est a source instance mais not conversely."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SzsContradictoryAxioms|rdfs:label"
msgid "SZS Contradictory Axioms"
msgstr "SZS Contradictory Axioms"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SzsContradictoryAxioms|skos:definition"
msgid "The SZS status asserting the axioms are themselves contradictory (unsatisfiable independent of any conjecture). Projects to logic:ConfInconsistent, and logic:szsStrengthens logic:SzsUnsatisfiable — it is the strictly stronger outcome, entailing unsatisfiability while additionally locating the inconsistency in the axiom set. This is precisely the distinction the coarse three-bucket collapse loses, preserved verbatim as logic:rawStatusToken. A logic:SzsSuccess status."
msgstr "Le SZS status asserting the axioms sont themselves contradictory (unsatisfiable independent de tout conjecture)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SzsCounterSatisfiable|rdfs:label"
msgid "SZS Counter-Satisfiable"
msgstr "SZS Counter-Satisfiable"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SzsCounterSatisfiable|skos:definition"
msgid "The SZS status asserting the conjecture is not entailed — a counter-model exists (the negated conjecture is satisfiable together with the axioms). Projects to logic:ConfConsistent, the entailment-fails twin of the W3C mf:NegativeEntailment kind. This is the distinction from logic:SzsSatisfiable the coarse collapse loses, preserved as logic:rawStatusToken. A logic:SzsSuccess status."
msgstr "Le SZS status asserting the conjecture n'est pas entailed — a counter-modèle exists (the negated conjecture est satisfiable together avec the axioms)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SzsGaveUp|rdfs:label"
msgid "SZS Gave Up"
msgstr "SZS Gave Up"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SzsGaveUp|skos:definition"
msgid "The SZS status asserting the prover abandoned the attempt without a decision. Projects to logic:ConfIncomplete. A logic:SzsNoSuccess status."
msgstr "Le SZS status asserting the prover abandoned the attempt sans a decision."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SzsNoSuccess|rdfs:label"
msgid "SZS No-Success"
msgstr "SZS No-Success"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SzsNoSuccess|skos:definition"
msgid "The SZS no-success sort: the statuses under which the prover did NOT reach a decision — it gave up, timed out, ran out of resources, or returned an explicit unknown. Its members (logic:SzsUnknown, logic:SzsGaveUp, logic:SzsTimeout, logic:SzsResourceOut) project onto the least-informative join logic:ConfIncomplete, kept strictly distinct from a native capability gap (a hard fail, never an incomplete swallowed into agreement). The undecided half of the logic:SzsStatus partition, complement of logic:SzsSuccess."
msgstr "Le SZS no-success sort: the statuses sous qui the prover did NOT reach a decision — it gave up, timed out, ran out de resources, ou returned an explicit inconnu."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SzsResourceOut|rdfs:label"
msgid "SZS Resource Out"
msgstr "SZS ressource Out"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SzsResourceOut|skos:definition"
msgid "The SZS status asserting the prover exhausted a resource bound (memory, inferences) before deciding. Projects to logic:ConfIncomplete. A logic:SzsNoSuccess status; the resource-bounded outcome."
msgstr "Le SZS status asserting the prover épuisé a ressource bound (memory, inferences) avant deciding."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SzsSatisfiable|rdfs:label"
msgid "SZS Satisfiable"
msgstr "SZS Satisfiable"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SzsSatisfiable|skos:definition"
msgid "The SZS status asserting the axiom set has a model. Projects to logic:ConfConsistent. A logic:SzsSuccess status; the decided-negative outcome for a consistency question."
msgstr "Le SZS status asserting the axiom set possède a modèle."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SzsStatus|rdfs:label"
msgid "SZS Status"
msgstr "SZS Status"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SzsStatus|skos:definition"
msgid "The TPTP SZS result-status ontology, subsumed by reference (Principle 5 — no vendored axioms) as a first-class logic: vocabulary rather than parsed and discarded. An SZS status is the community-decided ground-truth outcome a problem carries in the external FOL soundness corpus. The vocabulary is partitioned by rdfs:subClassOf into logic:SzsSuccess (the prover decided) and logic:SzsNoSuccess (the prover did not), and the intra-branch strength order is carried by logic:szsStrengthens (logic:SzsContradictoryAxioms strengthens logic:SzsUnsatisfiable). The coarse three-bucket runner view (logic:ConformanceVerdict) is a monotone lossy projection of this ordered structure — a logic:SoundUnderApproximation that collapses distinctions the raw token preserves via logic:rawStatusToken (design/LOGIC-CONFORMANCE.md, the external FOL soundness oracle)."
msgstr "Le TPTP SZS résultat-status ontology, subsumed par reference (Principle 5 — no vendored axioms) as a first-class logic: vocabulary plutôt que parsed et discarded."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SzsSuccess|rdfs:label"
msgid "SZS Success"
msgstr "SZS Success"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SzsSuccess|skos:definition"
msgid "The SZS success sort: the statuses under which the prover reached a decision about the problem — the axiom set's satisfiability or the conjecture's entailment was settled. Its members (logic:SzsTheorem, logic:SzsUnsatisfiable, logic:SzsContradictoryAxioms, logic:SzsSatisfiable, logic:SzsCounterSatisfiable) project onto the two informative logic:ConformanceVerdict meet-elements. The decided half of the logic:SzsStatus partition, complement of logic:SzsNoSuccess. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:SzsSuccess only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le SZS success sort: the statuses sous qui the prover reached a decision about the problem — the axiom set's satisfiability ou the conjecture's implication was settled."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SzsTheorem|rdfs:label"
msgid "SZS Theorem"
msgstr "SZS Theorem"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SzsTheorem|skos:definition"
msgid "The SZS status asserting the conjecture is a theorem of the axioms — entailment holds. Projects to logic:ConfInconsistent (the negated-conjecture reduction is unsatisfiable). A logic:SzsSuccess status; the canonical positive-entailment outcome, the SZS twin of the W3C mf:PositiveEntailment kind."
msgstr "Le SZS status asserting the conjecture est a theorem de the axioms — implication holds."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SzsTimeout|rdfs:label"
msgid "SZS Timeout"
msgstr "SZS Timeout"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SzsTimeout|skos:definition"
msgid "The SZS status asserting the prover exhausted its wall-clock budget before deciding. Projects to logic:ConfIncomplete. A logic:SzsNoSuccess status; the budget-tripped outcome."
msgstr "Le SZS status asserting the prover épuisé its wall-clock budget avant deciding."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SzsUnknown|rdfs:label"
msgid "SZS Unknown"
msgstr "SZS inconnu"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SzsUnknown|skos:definition"
msgid "The SZS status asserting the prover could not determine the result. Projects to logic:ConfIncomplete. A logic:SzsNoSuccess status; the explicit undecided outcome, distinct from a native capability gap."
msgstr "Le SZS status asserting the prover could not determine the résultat."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SzsUnsatisfiable|rdfs:label"
msgid "SZS Unsatisfiable"
msgstr "SZS Unsatisfiable"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/SzsUnsatisfiable|skos:definition"
msgid "The SZS status asserting the axiom set has no model. Projects to logic:ConfInconsistent. A logic:SzsSuccess status; strengthened by logic:SzsContradictoryAxioms (which additionally asserts the inconsistency is intrinsic to the axioms, not conjecture-relative)."
msgstr "Le SZS status asserting the axiom set possède no modèle."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TeleologicalFramework|rdfs:label"
msgid "Teleological Framework"
msgstr "Teleological cadre"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TeleologicalFramework|skos:definition"
msgid "The goal-and-action framework: structured logic:GoalExpression (atomic through achievement, maintenance, avoidance, optimization, conditional, and deadline forms), the reified multi-axis logic:GoalEvaluation, and logic:ActionSchema with its precondition / effect / invariant / capability / outcome / observation / compensation facets — the structure that motivates and evaluates transactions, kept distinct from how state changes (design/LOGIC-TELEOLOGY.md, the why-goals-and-action-are-their-own-layer section)."
msgstr "Le objectif-and-action cadre: structured logic:GoalExpression (atomique par accomplissement, maintien, évitement, optimization, conditionnel, et deadline forms), the reified multi-axis logic:GoalEvaluation, et logic:ActionSchema avec its précondition / effet / invariant / capability / résultat / observation / compensation facets — the structure qui motivates et evaluates transactions, kept distinct de how état changes (design/LOGIC-TELEOLOGY.md, the why-goals-and-action-are-their-own-layer section)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TemporalFramework|rdfs:label"
msgid "Temporal Framework"
msgstr "Temporal cadre"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TemporalFramework|skos:definition"
msgid "The 4D / path framework: logic:State and logic:Path with the ordered transaction history, logic:TransactionStep instantiation from predecessor to successor, and frame-relative truth where a formula's truth is a property of the path it executes along. Time is one independent index axis of the typed context algebra, coexisting with world, standpoint, and path on a single result (design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md, the worlds-modality-and-counterfactuals section; design/LOGIC-TRANSACTION.md, the path-semantics section)."
msgstr "Le 4D / chemin cadre: logic:état et logic:chemin avec the ordered transaction historique, logic:TransactionStep instantiation de predecessor à successor, et frame-relative vérité où a formule's vérité est a propriété de the chemin it executes along."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TermKind|rdfs:label"
msgid "Term Kind"
msgstr "terme Kind"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TermKind|skos:definition"
msgid "The closed value class of the logic:columnTermKind facet: the RDF term kind a result column binds. Its individuals are logic:TermKindIri, logic:TermKindLiteral and logic:TermKindBlankNode. The set is closed, so a misspelt value names no declared kind and is rejected (design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md, §The result row schema). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:TermKind only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le classe de valeurs fermée de the logic:columnTermKind facet: the RDF terme kind a résultat colonne binds."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TermKindBlankNode|rdfs:label"
msgid "Term Kind Blank Node"
msgstr "terme Kind Blank nœud"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TermKindBlankNode|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:TermKind value for a column whose values are blank nodes. Wire value `blank-node`."
msgstr "Le logic:TermKind valeur pour a colonne dont values sont blank nodes."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TermKindIri|rdfs:label"
msgid "Term Kind IRI"
msgstr "terme Kind IRI"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TermKindIri|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:TermKind value for a column whose values are IRIs (named nodes). Wire value `iri`."
msgstr "Le logic:TermKind valeur pour a colonne dont values sont IRIs (named nodes)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TermKindLiteral|rdfs:label"
msgid "Term Kind Literal"
msgstr "terme Kind Literal"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TermKindLiteral|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:TermKind value for a column whose values are literals. A literal column may further pin its datatype with logic:columnDatatype; absent that, any literal conforms. Wire value `literal`."
msgstr "Le logic:TermKind valeur pour a colonne dont values sont literals."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TimeContextAxis|rdfs:label"
msgid "Time Context Axis"
msgstr "Time contexte Axis"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TimeContextAxis|skos:definition"
msgid "The time index axis of the multi-dimensional context facet: a truth is relative to a time (a narrative or temporal reference frame). One of several context axes that coexist on a single result — world, standpoint, time, and path index the same result simultaneously rather than being alternative values of one slot."
msgstr "Le time index axis de the multi-dimensional contexte facet: a vérité est relative à a time (a narrative ou temporal reference frame)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TimestampOrdering|rdfs:label"
msgid "Timestamp Ordering"
msgstr "Timestamp Ordering"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TimestampOrdering|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol that assigns each transaction a timestamp and orders conflicting operations by it, aborting any operation that would violate the timestamp order. A mechanism, not a guarantee."
msgstr "Le logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol qui assigns each transaction a timestamp et orders conflicting operations par it, aborting tout operation qui would violate the timestamp order."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TransactionOutcome|rdfs:label"
msgid "Transaction Outcome"
msgstr "transaction résultat"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TransactionOutcome|skos:definition"
msgid "The recorded result of executing a transaction program from a start state under executional entailment: the program succeeds iff there exists a path from the start state along which it holds, and failure leaves the start state untouched. It carries logic:outcomeOfProgram (the program executed), logic:transactionStart (the state it started from), and logic:transactionSucceeds (the boolean verdict); on success it is linked by logic:executedAlongPath to the logic:Path of states the run traversed and the per-step support is recorded as supersession. Typed APART from logic:GoalEvaluation, which records at-a-state satisfaction of a goal, and from logic:PlanSuccessMode, which classifies a plan's success mode over its nondeterministic outcome set: a logic:TransactionOutcome records ONE concrete executed run's success or failure under executional entailment, not a satisfaction judgement and not a mode classification."
msgstr "Le recorded résultat de executing a transaction program de a start état sous executional implication: the program succeeds iff there exists a chemin de the start état along qui it holds, et échec leaves the start état untouched."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TransactionPathEvolution|rdfs:label"
msgid "Transaction-Path Evolution"
msgstr "transaction-chemin Evolution"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TransactionPathEvolution|skos:definition"
msgid "The evolution-facet value selecting the Transaction-Logic state-change semantics of LOGIC-TRANSACTION.md — serial conjunction (⊗), executional entailment over a path of states, and elementary updates as supersession. It is a facet value, never a seventh profile, and is independent of the model-semantics facet; its full semantics are specified in LOGIC-TRANSACTION.md."
msgstr "Le evolution-facet valeur selecting the transaction-Logic état-change sémantique de LOGIC-transaction.md — sériel conjunction (⊗), executional implication sur a chemin de states, et elementary updates as supersession."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TransactionProgram|rdfs:label"
msgid "Transaction Program"
msgstr "transaction Program"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TransactionProgram|skos:definition"
msgid "A state-changing composite over the path semantics of the transaction layer — insertion, deletion, hypothetical execution, and supersession rather than erasure. Its combinators are typed apart from formula connectives: serial composition is not conjunction, so a program operator is never confused with a logical one."
msgstr "Un état-changing composite sur the chemin sémantique de the transaction layer — insertion, deletion, hypothetical exécution, et supersession plutôt que erasure."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TransactionStep|rdfs:label"
msgid "Transaction Step"
msgstr "transaction Step"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TransactionStep|skos:definition"
msgid "An elementary update / transaction-path step that instantiates an action schema (logic:instantiatesSchema) and carries the path edge from a predecessor state (logic:transitionFromState) to a successor state (logic:transitionToState). The native evaluator applies the schema's logic:effect over the step, computing the successor situation's support as ins/del supersession: inserted supports become active, deleted supports are recorded via the append-only supersession quartet (logic:activeInState, logic:validUntilState, logic:retiredByTransaction, logic:supersededBy) and never erased."
msgstr "Un elementary update / transaction-chemin step qui instantiates an action schéma (logic:instantiatesSchema) et porte the chemin edge de a predecessor état (logic:transitionFromState) à a successor état (logic:transitionToState)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TruthAlgebra|rdfs:label"
msgid "Truth Algebra"
msgstr "vérité Algebra"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TruthAlgebra|skos:definition"
msgid "The facet value class of the truth algebra: the lattice of truth values over which valuations range. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract. It is one of the three independent components of the truth/inconsistency facet — algebra, admissible-valuation policy, designated values — that together separate FDE, LP, K3 and classical logic; its values are the four-valued Belnap bilattice and the classical two-valued algebra. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:TruthAlgebra only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le facet valeur class de the vérité algebra: the lattice de vérité values sur qui valuations plage."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TruthMaintenanceRevision|rdfs:label"
msgid "Truth-Maintenance Revision"
msgstr "vérité-maintien Revision"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/TruthMaintenanceRevision|skos:definition"
msgid "The revision-policy value under which derived conclusions are tracked by their justifications, so retracting a premise automatically retracts the conclusions that depended on it (a truth-maintenance system). The dependency-directed counterpart of logic:EntrenchmentRevision; contrast logic:MonotonicRevision, which never retracts."
msgstr "Le revision-politique valeur sous qui dérivé conclusions sont tracked par their justifications, so retracting a premise automatically retracts the conclusions qui depended sur it (a vérité-maintien system)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Type|rdfs:label"
msgid "Type"
msgstr "type"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Type|skos:definition"
msgid "A universal: a type whose instances share a common feature, reified as a first-order individual so it can itself be the object of logic:instanceOf and carry a logic:orderedType. The counterpart of gufo:Type; first-order (its instances are logic:Individuals, logic:orderedType 1) or higher-order (its instances are themselves types). The root of the type taxonomy, complementing logic:Individual; every foundation sort (logic:Kind, logic:Role, …) and every meta-type below is a logic:Type. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:Type only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Un universel: a type dont instances share a commun feature, reified as a premier ordre individu so it peut itself be the object de logic:instanceOf et carry a logic:orderedType."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/UncertaintyMeasure|rdfs:label"
msgid "Uncertainty Measure"
msgstr "Uncertainty Measure"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/UncertaintyMeasure|skos:definition"
msgid "The facet value class of the uncertainty facet: how graded belief is carried. Set-valued on a ReasoningContract — several measures (probabilistic, weighted/ranking, fuzzy) may be in force on the same result at once, or none. Its individuals record the measures in force, not a single chosen one."
msgstr "Le facet valeur class de the uncertainty facet: how graded belief est carried."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/UncertifiedChase|rdfs:label"
msgid "Uncertified Chase"
msgstr "Uncertified Chase"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/UncertifiedChase|skos:definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a logic:ChaseAcceptanceWitness — the acceptance record of an existential-rule chase materialization — carries no logic:carriesTerminationCertificate, i.e. reports a materialized closure without the weak-acyclicity termination certificate that admits it. An uncertified chase may not terminate; the flagship's guarantee is that materialize_routed surfaces the ChaseAdmission termination certificate as a first-class gmeow:Finding, so a chase acceptance record with no certificate is ill-formed (LOGIC-RUNTIME.md)."
msgstr "Le échec raised lorsque a logic:ChaseAcceptanceWitness — the acceptance record de an existential-règle chase matérialisation — porte no logic:carriesTerminationCertificate, i.e."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/UnentrenchedCounterfactual|rdfs:label"
msgid "Unentrenched Counterfactual"
msgstr "Unentrenched contrefactuel"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/UnentrenchedCounterfactual|skos:definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a logic:CounterfactualAcceptanceWitness — the acceptance record of a Stratum-C counterfactual resolution — names no logic:selectedByEntrenchment outcome, i.e. resolves an antecedent without recording the entrenchment-ranked selection that made the result deterministic. A counterfactual whose outcome is not tied to an entrenchment ordering is a silent, arbitrary choice; the flagship's guarantee is a deterministic entrenchment-ranked selection, so a witness with none is ill-formed (LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md)."
msgstr "Le échec raised lorsque a logic:CounterfactualAcceptanceWitness — the acceptance record de a Stratum-C contrefactuel resolution — nomme no logic:selectedByEntrenchment résultat, i.e."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/UniqueNameEqualityPolicy|rdfs:label"
msgid "Unique-Name Equality Policy"
msgstr "Unique-Name Equality politique"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/UniqueNameEqualityPolicy|skos:definition"
msgid "The equality-policy value imposing the unique-name assumption: distinct names denote distinct entities unless equality is explicitly asserted. The optional strengthening of logic:RdfEqualityPolicy; contrast logic:ExplicitEqualityPolicy, which neither assumes distinctness nor unifies beyond what is declared."
msgstr "Le equality-politique valeur imposing the unique-name assumption: distinct nomme denote distinct entities unless equality est explicitly asserted."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Unsatisfied|rdfs:label"
msgid "Unsatisfied"
msgstr "Unsatisfied"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Unsatisfied|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:SatisfactionStatus value for a goal not met, with no positive partial progress recorded. Distinct from logic:Violated (an active breach of a maintenance or avoidance target) and from logic:PartiallySatisfied (some progress made)."
msgstr "Le logic:SatisfactionStatus valeur pour a objectif not met, avec no positif partial progress recorded."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Unsupported|rdfs:label"
msgid "Unsupported"
msgstr "Unsupported"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Unsupported|skos:definition"
msgid "The weakest preservation polarity: the construct cannot be expressed in the target at all. A formula that lowers to unsupported is carried and flagged in the loss ledger, never silently dropped, and every result downstream of the lowering discloses which formulas the target did not evaluate. The legalization floor — a lowering is a total function into legal output plus flagged residue, and an unsupported construct is residue, never loss in silence."
msgstr "Le weakest preservation polarity: the construct ne peut pas be expressed dans the target at tous."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/UnwiredFlagshipScenario|rdfs:label"
msgid "Unwired Flagship Scenario"
msgstr "non raccordé Flagship Scenario"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/UnwiredFlagshipScenario|skos:definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a gmeow:FlagshipScenario in the logic grounding layer is not fully wired: it is missing its worked example (gmeow:demonstratedByExample), its competency question (gmeow:demonstratedByCompetency), its producer (gmeow:demonstratedByProducer), its counter-example (gmeow:guardedByCounterExample), or its enforcing failure class (gmeow:enforcesFailureClass); or the class it names as enforcing is not a logic:LogicConformanceFailure subclass. The depth bar is a contract, not a suggestion: an acceptance scenario that does not bind all realizing/enforcing artifacts cannot claim the scenario is met, and the gate rejects it. This layer's concrete realization of the shared gmeow:UnwiredFlagshipScenario marker (enforced uniformly by the shared gmeow:FlagshipScenarioShape); it subclasses ONLY the slice failure root (never the spec-layer gmeow:UnwiredFlagshipScenario marker), so it is a typed, queryable object in this layer's own failure lattice."
msgstr "Le échec raised lorsque a gmeow:FlagshipScenario dans the logic grounding layer n'est pas fully wired: it est missing its worked example (gmeow:demonstratedByExample), its competency question (gmeow:demonstratedByCompetency), its producer (gmeow:demonstratedByProducer), its contre-exemple (gmeow:guardedByCounterExample), ou its enforcing classe d'échec (gmeow:enforcesFailureClass); ou the class it nomme as enforcing n'est pas a logic:LogicConformanceFailure subclass."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/UnwitnessedRefutation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Unwitnessed Refutation"
msgstr "Unwitnessed réfutation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/UnwitnessedRefutation|skos:definition"
msgid "The failure raised when a logic:RefutationAcceptanceWitness — the acceptance record of a symmetric φ/¬φ conjecture test whose verdict is a refutation — names no logic:namesContradictionWitness, i.e. claims the conjecture was refuted without pointing at the concrete logic:ContradictionWitness that carries the clash. A refutation with no replayable witness is an assertion, not a proof; the flagship's guarantee is that conjecture_test returns a concrete witness on a refutation, so a witness-less refutation record is ill-formed (LOGIC-CONTRACT.md)."
msgstr "Le échec raised lorsque a logic:RefutationAcceptanceWitness — the acceptance record de a symmetric φ/¬φ conjecture test dont verdict est a réfutation — nomme no logic:namesContradictionWitness, i.e."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Vague|rdfs:label"
msgid "vague"
msgstr "vague"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Vague|skos:definition"
msgid "The target relationship is ontically fuzzy: it holds to a degree or only on a shared component, with genuine borderline cases. Paired with a logic:AffineCorrespondence class for the 'similar but not quite' alignment — vagueness in the world, not uncertainty in the curator."
msgstr "Le target relation est ontically fuzzy: it holds à a degree ou uniquement sur a shared component, avec genuine borderline cases."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ValidationOnly|rdfs:label"
msgid "Validation Only"
msgstr "Validation Only"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ValidationOnly|skos:definition"
msgid "The projection detects some invalidity but is not an entailment relation: it can flag ill-formedness without computing canonical consequences. The honest label for bridge views (e.g. BFO/DOLCE) that constrain but do not reason; they carry this or no preservation claim, never logic:ExactPreservation."
msgstr "Le projection detects some invalidity mais n'est pas an implication relation: it peut flag ill-formedness sans computing canonique consequences."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ValidationOnlyProjection|rdfs:label"
msgid "Validation-Only Projection"
msgstr "Validation-Only projection"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ValidationOnlyProjection|skos:definition"
msgid "The projection-target value requesting a validation-only surface: it detects ill-formedness without computing canonical consequences (the honest output for bridge views that constrain but do not reason). One of several output targets a single contract may name at once; it never alters which entailments hold."
msgstr "Le projection-target valeur requesting a validation-only surface: it detects ill-formedness sans computing canonique consequences (the honest output pour pont views qui constrain mais do not reason)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ValidationShape|rdfs:label"
msgid "Validation Shape"
msgstr "Validation forme"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ValidationShape|skos:definition"
msgid "A closed-world data-shape condition: the SHACL-shaped subset of the IR, evaluated against a dataset rather than as an open-world entailment. The node kind for conditions checked under the closed-world reading where absence may be read as falsity."
msgstr "Un monde fermé données-forme condition: the SHACL-shaped subset de the IR, evaluated contre a dataset plutôt que as an monde ouvert implication."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/VariableCollection|rdfs:label"
msgid "Variable Collection"
msgstr "Variable collection"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/VariableCollection|skos:definition"
msgid "A logic:Collection whose membership may change over time while the collection retains its identity — a club whose roster gains and loses members, a playlist edited over the years. The counterpart of gufo:VariableCollection. Stated in prose, not as a subclass edge. Its time-varying logic:memberOf is naturally carried as a logic:Fluent (membership indexed to time/world) rather than as the static membership of a logic:FixedCollection — the four-dimensional treatment of changing membership."
msgstr "Un logic:collection dont membership peut change sur time while the collection retains its identité — a club dont roster gains et loses members, a playlist edited sur the years."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Variadic|rdfs:label"
msgid "Variadic"
msgstr "Variadic"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Variadic|skos:definition"
msgid "The residue shape tag for an atomic predication whose argument arity is not the binary Horn shape: it carries a logic:SequenceMarker or a non-binary (unary or n-ary) argument list — the generalization beyond the fixed arity-three triple. Disclosed when a Horn-fragment target carries such a formula as flagged unsupported residue."
msgstr "Le residue forme tag pour an atomique predication dont argument arity n'est pas the binary Horn forme: it porte a logic:SequenceMarker ou a non-binary (unary ou n-ary) argument list — the generalization beyond the fixed arity-three triple."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/VerdictEngineProduced|rdfs:label"
msgid "Engine Produced"
msgstr "Engine Produced"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/VerdictEngineProduced|skos:definition"
msgid "The verdict-provenance value for a conjecture whose positive/negative cases were produced by a scoped reasoning run over the standpoint, not asserted by a reviewer: the defining mark of a logic:Conjecture against a plain logic:FormalizationCandidate. Wire value `engine-produced`."
msgstr "Le verdict-provenance valeur pour a conjecture dont positif/négatif cases were produced par a scoped raisonnement run sur the point de vue, not asserted par a reviewer: the defining mark de a logic:conjecture contre a plain logic:FormalizationCandidate."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/VerdictProvenanceKind|rdfs:label"
msgid "Verdict Provenance Kind"
msgstr "verdict Provenance Kind"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/VerdictProvenanceKind|skos:definition"
msgid "The closed two-member value class of the logic:verdictProvenance facet: the one genuinely-new axis a logic:Conjecture adds over a plain logic:FormalizationCandidate — whether a candidate's positive/negative cases were ENGINE-PRODUCED by a scoped reasoning run or REVIEWER-ASSERTED by hand. Its individuals are logic:VerdictEngineProduced and logic:VerdictReviewerAsserted. The set is closed, so a misspelt provenance names no declared value and is rejected (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the conjecture-and-refutation section). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:VerdictProvenanceKind only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le closed two-member valeur class de the logic:verdictProvenance facet: the one genuinely-new axis a logic:conjecture adds sur a plain logic:FormalizationCandidate — whether a candidat's positif/négatif cases were ENGINE-PRODUCED par a scoped raisonnement run ou REVIEWER-ASSERTED par hand."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/VerdictReviewerAsserted|rdfs:label"
msgid "Reviewer Asserted"
msgstr "Reviewer Asserted"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/VerdictReviewerAsserted|skos:definition"
msgid "The verdict-provenance value for cases a reviewer asserted by hand rather than an engine deriving — the plain-candidate default, retained on the closed set so a conjecture may honestly record a hand-adjudicated case (e.g. a withdrawal) without pretending it was engine-produced. Wire value `reviewer-asserted`."
msgstr "Le verdict-provenance valeur pour cases a reviewer asserted par hand plutôt que an engine deriving — the plain-candidat default, retained sur the closed set so a conjecture peut honestly record a hand-adjudicated case (e.g."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ViewSerializability|rdfs:label"
msgid "View Serializability"
msgstr "View Serializability"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ViewSerializability|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:SerializabilityCriterion value satisfied when some serial order has the same read-from and final-write relationships as the history — equivalent on what each read observed and which write was last. A history property, not a protocol. Strictly weaker than logic:ConflictSerializability is not implied; the two are distinct criteria a history may satisfy."
msgstr "Le logic:SerializabilityCriterion valeur satisfied lorsque some sériel order possède the same read-from et final-write relationships as the historique — equivalent sur what each read observed et qui write was last."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Violated|rdfs:label"
msgid "Violated"
msgstr "Violated"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/Violated|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:SatisfactionStatus value for a goal whose target has failed — a maintenance goal that failed at some state of its interval, or an avoidance goal whose proscribed situation obtained. Stronger than logic:Unsatisfied: a violation is an active breach, not mere non-achievement."
msgstr "Le logic:SatisfactionStatus valeur pour a objectif dont target possède failed — a maintien objectif qui failed at some état de its interval, ou an évitement objectif dont proscribed situation obtained."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/WeakPlanSuccess|rdfs:label"
msgid "Weak Plan Success"
msgstr "Weak plan Success"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/WeakPlanSuccess|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:PlanSuccessMode value under which a plan succeeds when SOME outcome path reaches the goal — the existential reading. The weakest of the three; contrast logic:StrongPlanSuccess (every path) and logic:StrongCyclicPlanSuccess (every fair execution, allowing loops)."
msgstr "Le logic:PlanSuccessMode valeur sous qui a plan succeeds lorsque SOME résultat chemin reaches the objectif — the existential reading."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/WeakSupplementation|rdfs:label"
msgid "Weak Supplementation"
msgstr "Weak Supplementation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/WeakSupplementation|skos:definition"
msgid "The weak-supplementation axiom as a profiled-mereology constraint: a whole with a proper part must have another proper part disjoint from the first. It is enforced only within the logic:MereologyProfile a whole is declared under (logic:underMereologyProfile), never across all parthood; a whole with a lone proper part and no disjoint co-part, declared under a profile, is the logic:violation. The prerequisites logic:overlaps and logic:disjoint are settled first, so the axiom is never applied where overlap is undefined (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Le weak-supplementation axiom as a profiled-mereology contrainte: a whole avec a proper part doit possèdent another proper part disjoint de the first."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/WeightedRankingMeasure|rdfs:label"
msgid "Weighted Ranking Measure"
msgstr "Weighted Ranking Measure"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/WeightedRankingMeasure|skos:definition"
msgid "The uncertainty measure carrying weighted or ranking preferences over derivations. One member of the uncertainty-measure set facet (it may coexist with logic:ProbabilisticMeasure or logic:FuzzyMeasure); distinct from a calibrated probability — a ranking weight carries no probabilistic meaning unless one is separately declared."
msgstr "Le uncertainty measure carrying weighted ou ranking preferences sur derivations."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/WellBehavedLens|rdfs:label"
msgid "Well-Behaved Lens"
msgstr "Well-Behaved Lens"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/WellBehavedLens|skos:definition"
msgid "An asymmetric lens: a structured-to-flat downcast with sound update. Caps: logic:GetPut and logic:PutGet claimable (logic:PutPut optional). The workhorse rung for a faithful but non-embedding projection."
msgstr "Un asymmetric lens: a structured-to-flat downcast avec sound update."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/WellFoundedProfile|rdfs:label"
msgid "Well-Founded Profile"
msgstr "Well-Founded profil"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/WellFoundedProfile|skos:definition"
msgid "The well-founded semantics: a three-valued (true/false/undefined), total, polynomial-time semantics for normal logic programs that assigns a unique well-founded model even with unstratified negation, leaving genuinely circular literals undefined rather than branching."
msgstr "Le well-founded sémantique: a three-valued (true/false/undefined), total, polynomial-time sémantique pour normal logic programs qui assigns a unique well-founded modèle even avec unstratified negation, leaving genuinely circular literals undefined plutôt que branching."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/WellFoundedSemantics|rdfs:label"
msgid "Well-Founded Semantics"
msgstr "Well-Founded sémantique"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/WellFoundedSemantics|skos:definition"
msgid "The model-semantics facet value selecting the well-founded semantics: a unique, three-valued (true/false/undefined), total, polynomial-time model for normal programs, leaving genuinely circular literals undefined rather than branching. Single-valued on a ReasoningContract; the deterministic counterpart of the non-deterministic logic:StableModelSemantics for unstratified negation."
msgstr "Le modèle-sémantique facet valeur selecting the well-founded sémantique: a unique, three-valued (true/false/undefined), total, polynomial-time modèle pour normal programs, leaving genuinely circular literals undefined plutôt que branching."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/World|rdfs:label"
msgid "World"
msgstr "monde"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/World|skos:definition"
msgid "A reified, named context relative to which truth is evaluated — a possible world in the Kripke sense, realized by GMEOW's materialized contextual index (standpoints, narrative reference frames, goal-, ought-, feared-, and counterfactual-worlds). Truth is world-relative and entailment is world-indexed: a contradiction within one world is a witness, a contradiction across worlds is not an inconsistency in the model. Carries a world-type taxonomy (epistemic, doxastic, telic, deontic, alethic, representational, counterfactual)."
msgstr "Un reified, named contexte relative à qui vérité est evaluated — a possible monde dans the Kripke sense, realized par GMEOW's materialized contextual index (standpoints, narrative reference frames, objectif-, ought-, feared-, et contrefactuel-worlds)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/WorldBoundary|rdfs:label"
msgid "World Boundary"
msgstr "monde Boundary"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/WorldBoundary|skos:definition"
msgid "A scoped region within which the closed-world assumption applies: it demarcates where what is not derivable may be read as false, leaving the rest of the model under the open-world assumption. The scoping construct of the hybrid open/closed feature (LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md §Greenfield feature map): the closed-world (CWA) lane realized by the built-in SHACL is confined to what a WorldBoundary encloses, while logic: outside it stays open-world. Enforcement is seamed to the engine."
msgstr "Un scoped region within qui the monde fermé assumption applies: it demarcates où what n'est pas derivable peut be read as false, leaving the rest de the modèle sous the monde ouvert assumption."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/WorldContextAxis|rdfs:label"
msgid "World Context Axis"
msgstr "monde contexte Axis"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/WorldContextAxis|skos:definition"
msgid "The world index axis of the multi-dimensional context facet: a truth is relative to a logic:World (a Kripke-style possible world in the materialized contextual index). One of several context axes that coexist on a single result — world, standpoint, time, and path index the same result simultaneously rather than being alternative values of one slot."
msgstr "Le monde index axis de the multi-dimensional contexte facet: a vérité est relative à a logic:monde (a Kripke-style possible monde dans the materialized contextual index)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/accessibleFrom|rdfs:label"
msgid "accessible from"
msgstr "accessible from"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/accessibleFrom|skos:definition"
msgid "The generic Kripke accessibility abstraction between worlds: relates a world to a world from which it is reachable, generalizing the standpoint sharpening poset. It exists for uniform traversal and provenance, not for inference — the modal operators are NOT translated over this bare relation. Necessity and possibility are evaluated over the appropriate named, typed accessibility relation (necessity is truth in every accessible context of that type, possibility truth in some), never over the blurred union of all of them. That evaluation is bounded universal quantification because the world set is the finite, materialized contextual index, not the unbounded space of all logically possible worlds. logic:accessibleFrom is the generic superproperty of the six typed accessibility relations — logic:epistemicallyPossible, logic:doxasticallyAccessible, logic:deonticallyIdeal, logic:temporallySucceeds, logic:counterfactuallyCloser, and gmeow:sharpens — but only in prose: these are NOT asserted rdfs:subPropertyOf it, because the generic superproperty licenses no cross-type entailment by itself. An inference may follow a named, typed accessibility relation; it may not conclude anything by walking the bare superproperty across contexts of different types. The one pre-existing typed sub-relation, gmeow:sharpens, carries owl:TransitiveProperty in the standpoint slice, while the five logic: kernel relations assert no OWL characteristics and document their logical character in prose — an intentional asymmetry, not an oversight."
msgstr "Le generic Kripke accessibility abstraction entre worlds: relie a monde à a monde de qui it est reachable, generalizing the point de vue sharpening poset."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/actionResource|rdfs:label"
msgid "action resource"
msgstr "action ressource"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/actionResource|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ActionSchema to what the action consumes or requires — the seam to the resource-competing goal conflict (logic:competesForResource), where two goals draw on a resource an action schema declares and the supply is insufficient for both. Domain logic:ActionSchema (stated in prose). One of the eight action-theory facets. DISTINCT from logic:resourcePolicy, which is a ReasoningContract→ResourcePolicy engine-budget property — a different concept that must not be conflated with an action's consumable resource."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ActionSchema à what the action consumes ou exige — the seam à the ressource-competing objectif conflit (logic:competesForResource), où two goals draw sur a ressource an action schéma déclare et the supply est insufficient pour both."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/activationBasis|rdfs:label"
msgid "activation basis"
msgstr "activation basis"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/activationBasis|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:GovernanceRegime to a constrained state it activates as binding: the regime holds that a logic:DownwardConstraint whose logic:constraintState is this value binds its target (logic:ConstraintBinding) rather than lapsing to logic:ConstraintUnknown. The carrier that makes governance regime-relative — a state in one regime's activation basis and absent from another's receives opposite verdicts with no contradiction. Without a matching basis entry, a constraint over that state is logic:ConstraintUnknown under the regime. The governance analogue of logic:reductionBasis (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Relates a logic:GovernanceRegime à a constrained état it activates as liaison: the regime holds qui a logic:DownwardConstraint dont logic:constraintState est this valeur binds its target (logic:ConstraintBinding) plutôt que lapsing à logic:ConstraintUnknown."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/activeInState|rdfs:label"
msgid "active in state"
msgstr "active in état"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/activeInState|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a support/reified assertion to the path state in which that support was active. The transition oracle uses it to keep retired supports auditable: a `del` records the predecessor state where the support held, then advances to a successor where that support no longer holds. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:activeInState only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a support/reified assertion à the chemin état dans qui qui support was active."


msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/acyclicProperty|rdfs:label"
msgid "acyclic property"
msgstr "acyclic propriété"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/acyclicProperty|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic: property-characteristic marker for acyclicity: a property P whose transitive closure P+ is irreflexive — P(a₁,a₂) ∧ … ∧ P(aₙ,a₁) holds for no chain, so following P never returns to its start. Stronger than logic:irreflexiveProperty (which forbids only the one-step P(a,a)) yet distinct from logic:transitiveProperty ∧ logic:irreflexiveProperty: an acyclic P is deliberately NOT transitive (its successors are the immediate steps, not every reachable node), so the characteristic is enforced by the native coherence gate's internal reachability walk rather than by materialising the closure. Marks a stepwise chain such as gmeow:linkNext that must never cycle."
msgstr "Le logic: propriété-characteristic marker pour acyclicity: a propriété P dont transitive fermeture P+ est irreflexive — P(a₁,a₂) ∧ … ∧ P(aₙ,a₁) holds pour no chain, so following P jamais returns à its start."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/admissibleValuation|rdfs:label"
msgid "admissible valuation"
msgstr "admissible évaluation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/admissibleValuation|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to the logic:AdmissibleValuationPolicy it selects — the gap/glut policy fixing which Belnap values a valuation may assign. Single-valued on the contract. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:AdmissibleValuationPolicy (stated here in prose, matching the module's domain/range convention). It is one of the three independent truth-facet components and must not be conflated with logic:designatedValues."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract à the logic:AdmissibleValuationPolicy it selects — the gap/glut politique fixing qui Belnap values a évaluation peut assign."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/agencyHolon|rdfs:label"
msgid "agency holon"
msgstr "agentivité holon"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/agencyHolon|skos:definition"
msgid "The holon role of an logic:AgencyAssessment: the entity whose Janus-faced holonic agency is being assessed — the holon that bears (logic:bearsProperty) the self-assertive and integrative values the profile reasons over. One of the two role properties (with logic:agencyProfile) that reify the agency-assessment relation onto the arity-bounded reasoning surface, mirroring logic:assessmentWhole and the logic:HolonicPosition role properties. It is also a well-formedness existence guard: every verdict rule re-binds it, so a malformed assessment naming no holon receives no verdict (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:agencyHolon only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le holon role de an logic:AgencyAssessment: the entity dont Janus-faced holonic agentivité est being assessed — the holon qui bears (logic:bearsProperty) the self-assertive et integrative values the profil reasons over."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/agencyProfile|rdfs:label"
msgid "agency profile"
msgstr "agentivité profil"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/agencyProfile|skos:definition"
msgid "The profile role of an logic:AgencyAssessment: the logic:HolonicAgencyProfile the assessment is relative to. Holonic agency is never absolute — the verdict (logic:HolonIntegral / logic:AutonomyDeficient / logic:IntegrationDeficient / logic:AgencyUnknown) is read only against this declared profile's logic:selfAssertiveBasis and logic:integrativeBasis. An assessment that omits this role, or whose profile declares no basis at all, cannot evidence either tendency and receives logic:AgencyUnknown. One of the two role properties (with logic:agencyHolon) that reify the agency-assessment relation, mirroring logic:assessmentReductionTheory and logic:constraintRegime (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Le profil role de an logic:AgencyAssessment: the logic:HolonicAgencyProfile the évaluation est relative to."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/agencyVerdict|rdfs:label"
msgid "agency verdict"
msgstr "agentivité verdict"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/agencyVerdict|skos:definition"
msgid "The engine-derived outcome of an logic:AgencyAssessment: the four-valued logic:AgencyVerdict (logic:HolonIntegral, logic:AutonomyDeficient, logic:IntegrationDeficient, or logic:AgencyUnknown) the foundation lowering entails for it. Never asserted by hand — it is computed by the stratified agency rules from the assessment's holon and declared logic:HolonicAgencyProfile, the convenient OWL-projectable surface of the assessment exactly as logic:assessmentVerdict is for emergence and logic:constraintVerdict for governance. The two pathology values are reached by negation-as-failure over the two co-equal tendency markers, so each verdict is genuinely profile-relative rather than a bare default (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Le engine-dérivé résultat de an logic:AgencyAssessment: the quatre-valued logic:AgencyVerdict (logic:HolonIntegral, logic:AutonomyDeficient, logic:IntegrationDeficient, ou logic:AgencyUnknown) the foundation lowering entails pour it."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/aggComparator|rdfs:label"
msgid "aggregate comparator"
msgstr "agrégat comparator"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/aggComparator|skos:definition"
msgid "The relational comparator of a logic:AggregateConstraint's invariant (=, !=, <, <=, >, >=; the Unicode ≠/≤/≥ are accepted). The projected sh:SPARQLConstraint HAVING uses the negation of this operator, because a sh:select returns the VIOLATING focus nodes. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:aggComparator only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le relational comparator de a logic:AggregateConstraint's invariant (=, !=, <, <=, >, >=; the Unicode ≠/≤/≥ sont accepté)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/aggCompareTo|rdfs:label"
msgid "aggregate compare to"
msgstr "agrégat compare to"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/aggCompareTo|skos:definition"
msgid "The right-hand side a logic:AggregateConstraint's aggregate is compared to: an IRI object is a compared PROPERTY of the focus ($this <prop> ?rhs), and a literal is a fixed comparison value."
msgstr "Le right-hand side a logic:AggregateConstraint's agrégat est compared to: an IRI object est a compared propriété de the focus ($this <prop> ?rhs), et a literal est a fixed comparison valeur."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/aggDistinct|rdfs:label"
msgid "aggregate distinct"
msgstr "agrégat distinct"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/aggDistinct|skos:definition"
msgid "Whether a logic:AggregateConstraint aggregates over DISTINCT values (COUNT(DISTINCT ?x)). Absent means false. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:aggDistinct only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Whether a logic:AggregateConstraint aggregates sur DISTINCT values (COUNT(DISTINCT ?x))."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/aggFunction|rdfs:label"
msgid "aggregate (constraint) function"
msgstr "agrégat (contrainte) fonction"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/aggFunction|skos:definition"
msgid "The aggregate function of a logic:AggregateConstraint (COUNT, SUM, MIN, MAX) applied over logic:aggPath. Distinct from logic:aggregateFunction, which carries a reduce RULE's head aggregation; this drives a constraint's GROUP BY/HAVING violation SELECT."
msgstr "Le agrégat fonction de a logic:AggregateConstraint (COUNT, SUM, MIN, MAX) applied sur logic:aggPath."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/aggPath|rdfs:label"
msgid "aggregate path"
msgstr "agrégat chemin"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/aggPath|skos:definition"
msgid "The predicate a logic:AggregateConstraint aggregates over the focus: the objects of $this <aggPath> ?x are the values logic:aggFunction is applied to. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:aggPath only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le prédicat a logic:AggregateConstraint aggregates sur the focus: the objects de $this <aggPath> ?x sont the values logic:aggFunction est applied to."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/aggregateComparison|rdfs:label"
msgid "aggregate comparison"
msgstr "agrégat comparison"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/aggregateComparison|skos:definition"
msgid "The reified relation an expanded logic:AggregateConstraint carries as its honest FOL integrity: aggregateComparison(this, function, distinct, path, comparator, rhs). The realized FOL formula core has no aggregate node, so this predication makes the aggregate meaning complete in the FOL canon while the structured satellite drives the real GROUP BY/HAVING SPARQL projection. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:aggregateComparison only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le reified relation an expanded logic:AggregateConstraint porte as its honest FOL intégrité: aggregateComparison(this, fonction, distinct, chemin, comparator, rhs)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/aggregateFunction|rdfs:label"
msgid "aggregate function"
msgstr "agrégat fonction"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/aggregateFunction|skos:definition"
msgid "Names the aggregate function (SUM, COUNT, MIN, MAX, AVG) a logic:Rule applies in its reduce (aggregation) head: the rule binds logic:aggregateResult to this function applied to logic:aggregateVariable over the groups formed by logic:groupKey. This is the canonical logic: representation of the reduce half of the computation surface; it projects to an aggregating Datalog/Nemo rule and to a SHACL-AF GROUP-BY sub-SELECT (design/LOGIC-SHACL-AF.md). A rule with no logic:aggregateFunction is an ordinary derivation (map) rule. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:aggregateFunction only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Names the agrégat fonction (SUM, COUNT, MIN, MAX, AVG) a logic:règle applies dans its reduce (aggregation) head: the règle binds logic:aggregateResult à this fonction applied à logic:aggregateVariable sur the groups formed par logic:groupKey."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/aggregateResult|rdfs:label"
msgid "aggregate result"
msgstr "agrégat résultat"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/aggregateResult|skos:definition"
msgid "The head variable (a ?-prefixed string) a reduce rule binds to the value of logic:aggregateFunction applied to logic:aggregateVariable per group. It is the head object the rule derives for each group key, projecting to the SPARQL `(FUNC(?var) AS ?result)` of the SHACL-AF reduce surface. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:aggregateResult only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le head variable (a ?-prefixed string) a reduce règle binds à the valeur de logic:aggregateFunction applied à logic:aggregateVariable per group."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/aggregateVariable|rdfs:label"
msgid "aggregate variable"
msgstr "agrégat variable"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/aggregateVariable|skos:definition"
msgid "The rule-body variable (a ?-prefixed string) whose bindings logic:aggregateFunction aggregates within each group of a reduce rule. It must be positively bound by the rule body, exactly as a head variable must, so the aggregate ranges over a defined column. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:aggregateVariable only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le règle-body variable (a ?-prefixed string) dont bindings logic:aggregateFunction aggregates within each group de a reduce règle."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/and|rdfs:label"
msgid "and"
msgstr "and"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/and|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a conjunction logic:Formula to each of its operand sub-formulae (multi-valued, two or more). Conjunction is commutative and associative, so the canonical identity flattens nested conjunctions and is insensitive to operand order. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:and only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a conjunction logic:formule à each de its operand sub-formulae (à valeurs multiples, two ou more)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/anomalyCycle|rdfs:label"
msgid "anomaly cycle"
msgstr "anomaly cycle"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/anomalyCycle|skos:definition"
msgid "The detected dependency cycle of a logic:SerializationAnomaly, rendered as the canonical sequence of transaction IRIs joined by ' -> ' (rotated to start at the lexicographically smallest member and closed back to it, so the same history always yields the same description). Domain logic:SerializationAnomaly, range xsd:string (stated in prose). It is a human-readable DESCRIPTION of the history-level finding — the conflict-graph cycle that has no equivalent serial order — never a claim of ⊥ within a state; a non-serializable schedule is surfaced with its cycle described here, never silently linearized."
msgstr "Le detected dependency cycle de a logic:SerializationAnomaly, rendered as the canonique sequence de transaction IRIs joined par ' -> ' (rotated à start at the lexicographically smallest member et closed back à it, so the same historique toujours yields the same description)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/antecedent|rdfs:label"
msgid "antecedent"
msgstr "antecedent"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/antecedent|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a material-implication logic:Formula to its antecedent (the hypothesis). Paired with logic:consequent; the two name the implication's operands explicitly so the ordered, non-commutative reading never depends on serialization order."
msgstr "Relates a material-implication logic:formule à its antecedent (the hypothesis)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/antiConjectureObligationCandidate|rdfs:label"
msgid "anti-conjecture obligation candidate"
msgstr "anti-conjecture obligation candidat"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/antiConjectureObligationCandidate|skos:definition"
msgid "The symmetric anti-conjecture promotion leg: relates a robustly logic:ConjectureRefutedInStandpoint conjecture to a candidate logic:NonEntailmentObligation forbidding its formula — a refuted formula is not merely dropped, it becomes a first-class commitment that the foundation must NEVER draw it. Mirrors logic:conjecturePromotionCandidate (corroborated to axiom candidate) under negation (refuted to non-entailment candidate). Present exactly when the conjecture is refuted-in-standpoint. Domain logic:Conjecture, range logic:NonEntailmentObligation."
msgstr "Le symmetric anti-conjecture promotion leg: relie a robustly logic:ConjectureRefutedInStandpoint conjecture à a candidat logic:NonEntailmentObligation forbidding its formule — a refuted formule n'est pas merely dropped, it becomes a first-class engagement qui the foundation doit NEVER draw it."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/anyOf|rdfs:label"
msgid "any of"
msgstr "any of"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/anyOf|skos:definition"
msgid "A member predicate of a logic:DisjunctiveRequirednessConstraint: at least one of the logic:anyOf predicates must have a value on the focus (a disjunction of existentials). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:anyOf only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Un member prédicat de a logic:DisjunctiveRequirednessConstraint: au moins one de the logic:anyOf predicates doit possèdent a valeur sur the focus (a disjunction de existentials)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/argument|rdfs:label"
msgid "argument"
msgstr "argument"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/argument|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates an atomic-predication logic:Formula to one of its argument term-carriers. Each carrier fixes its position with logic:termIndex and its value with exactly one term-value property (logic:termIri, logic:termVariable, logic:termLiteral, or logic:termSequenceMarker), so a variadic argument list — including sequence markers — round-trips with its order and term kinds intact. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:argument only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates an atomique-predication logic:formule à one de its argument terme-carriers."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/argumentation|rdfs:label"
msgid "argumentation"
msgstr "argumentation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/argumentation|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to the logic:ArgumentationSemantics it selects — how conflicts among defeasible arguments are resolved. Single-valued on the contract. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:ArgumentationSemantics (stated in prose, matching the module's domain/range convention). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:argumentation only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract à the logic:ArgumentationSemantics it selects — how conflicts parmi defeasible arguments sont resolved."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assessedAgent|rdfs:label"
msgid "assessed agent"
msgstr "assessed agent"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assessedAgent|skos:definition"
msgid "The agent role of a logic:CognitiveAssessment: whose cognition is judged. Range gmeow:Agent (stated in prose, matching the module's convention). A well-formedness existence guard — every projection rule re-binds it, so a malformed assessment naming no agent receives no ladder edge. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:assessedAgent only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le agent role de a logic:CognitiveAssessment: dont cognition est judged."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assessmentContext|rdfs:label"
msgid "assessment context"
msgstr "évaluation contexte"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assessmentContext|skos:definition"
msgid "The task or context a logic:CognitiveAssessment holds for, since competence is context-relative: the same agent may be competent on one task and not on another, so an assessment without a context underdetermines what it claims. Range is left open (stated in prose)."
msgstr "Le task ou contexte a logic:CognitiveAssessment holds for, since competence est contexte-relative: the same agent peut be competent sur one task et not sur another, so an évaluation sans a contexte underdetermines what it claims."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assessmentDimension|rdfs:label"
msgid "assessment dimension"
msgstr "évaluation dimension"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assessmentDimension|skos:definition"
msgid "The single factored axis a logic:CognitiveAssessment judges: a logic:AssessmentDimension individual. An assessment names exactly one; the dimensions vary independently. Range logic:AssessmentDimension (stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:assessmentDimension only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le single factored axis a logic:CognitiveAssessment judges: a logic:AssessmentDimension individu."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assessmentEvaluator|rdfs:label"
msgid "assessment evaluator"
msgstr "évaluation evaluator"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assessmentEvaluator|skos:definition"
msgid "Who holds the judgment of a logic:CognitiveAssessment: the standpoint is attributed via gmeow:accordingTo, so a self-assessment (evaluator = assessed agent) and an observer's assessment coexist as two records rather than collapsing into one verdict. Range gmeow:Agent (stated in prose)."
msgstr "Who holds the judgment de a logic:CognitiveAssessment: the point de vue est attributed via gmeow:accordingTo, so a self-évaluation (evaluator = assessed agent) et an observer's évaluation coexist as two enregistre plutôt que collapsing dans one verdict."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assessmentEvidence|rdfs:label"
msgid "assessment evidence"
msgstr "évaluation preuve"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assessmentEvidence|skos:definition"
msgid "The reasoning, observations, or recorded episode a logic:CognitiveAssessment rests on — the inference commitments it cites, the gmeow:ModelInvocation that produced the reasoning, the results it grades — so an assessment is auditable against the reasoning it judges rather than standing apart from it. Range is left open (stated in prose)."
msgstr "Le raisonnement, observations, ou recorded episode a logic:CognitiveAssessment rests sur — the inference commitments it cites, the gmeow:ModelInvocation qui produced the raisonnement, the results it grades — so an évaluation est auditable contre the raisonnement it judges plutôt que standing apart de it."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assessmentLevel|rdfs:label"
msgid "assessment level"
msgstr "évaluation niveau"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assessmentLevel|skos:definition"
msgid "The value a logic:CognitiveAssessment takes on its logic:assessmentScale: an ordinal logic:AssessmentLevel individual when the scale is ordinal (the case the coarse-ladder projection reads), or a continuous literal otherwise (a Brier or logarithmic score on a continuous scale). Because the range spans both an individual and a literal it is a plain rdf:Property, not an owl:ObjectProperty (which could not carry the continuous literal) — the same open-range convention the module states in prose elsewhere."
msgstr "Le valeur a logic:CognitiveAssessment takes sur its logic:assessmentScale: an ordinal logic:AssessmentLevel individu lorsque the scale est ordinal (the case the coarse-ladder projection reads), ou a continuous literal otherwise (a Brier ou logarithmic score sur a continuous scale)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assessmentMethod|rdfs:label"
msgid "assessment method"
msgstr "évaluation method"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assessmentMethod|skos:definition"
msgid "How the judgment of a logic:CognitiveAssessment was reached — a test, a review, a scoring rule applied to a forecast series, an introspective report. Range is left open (stated in prose), so the method may be a named procedure or a free description. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:assessmentMethod only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "How the judgment de a logic:CognitiveAssessment was reached — a test, a révision, a scoring règle applied à a forecast series, an introspective report."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assessmentProperty|rdfs:label"
msgid "assessment property"
msgstr "évaluation propriété"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assessmentProperty|skos:definition"
msgid "The property role of an logic:EmergenceAssessment: the property-value whose emergence is being assessed — the thing the whole bears (logic:bearsProperty) and whose reducibility to the parts is in question. One of the three role properties (with logic:assessmentWhole and logic:assessmentReductionTheory) that reify the emergence-assessment relation onto the arity-bounded reasoning surface, mirroring the logic:HolonicPosition role properties (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:assessmentProperty only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le propriété role de an logic:EmergenceAssessment: the propriété-valeur dont emergence est being assessed — the thing the whole bears (logic:bearsProperty) et dont reducibility à the parts est dans question."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assessmentReductionTheory|rdfs:label"
msgid "assessment reduction theory"
msgstr "évaluation reduction theory"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assessmentReductionTheory|skos:definition"
msgid "The theory role of an logic:EmergenceAssessment: the logic:ReductionTheory the assessment is relative to. Emergence is never absolute — the verdict (logic:Aggregate / logic:Emergent / logic:EmergenceUnknown) is read only against this declared theory's logic:reductionBasis, and recording it is what lets a stronger theory overturn an logic:Emergent verdict without contradiction. An assessment that omits this role cannot pose the reducibility question and receives logic:EmergenceUnknown. One of the three role properties (with logic:assessmentWhole and logic:assessmentProperty) that reify the emergence-assessment relation (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Le theory role de an logic:EmergenceAssessment: the logic:ReductionTheory the évaluation est relative to."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assessmentScale|rdfs:label"
msgid "assessment scale"
msgstr "évaluation scale"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assessmentScale|skos:definition"
msgid "The named scale, ordinal or continuous, on which a logic:CognitiveAssessment's logic:assessmentLevel is read. Range is left open (stated in prose), since a scale may be the native ordinal logic:AssessmentLevel vocabulary or a foreign scale (Bloom's, SOLO, a Brier-scored continuous range). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:assessmentScale only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le named scale, ordinal ou continuous, sur qui a logic:CognitiveAssessment's logic:assessmentLevel est read."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assessmentSubject|rdfs:label"
msgid "assessment subject"
msgstr "évaluation subject"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assessmentSubject|skos:definition"
msgid "The subject role of a logic:CognitiveAssessment: what the assessment is about — a single inference, a body of reasoning, a domain of competence, or the agent as a whole. Its grain is carried by logic:subjectGranularity. Range is left open (stated in prose), since the subject may be reasoning, a domain entity, or the reasoner itself. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:assessmentSubject only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le subject role de a logic:CognitiveAssessment: what the évaluation est about — a single inference, a body de raisonnement, a domaine de competence, ou the agent as a whole."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assessmentVerdict|rdfs:label"
msgid "assessment verdict"
msgstr "évaluation verdict"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assessmentVerdict|skos:definition"
msgid "The derived outcome of an logic:EmergenceAssessment: the logic:EmergenceVerdict (logic:Aggregate, logic:Emergent, or logic:EmergenceUnknown) the foundation lowering entails for it. Never asserted by hand — it is computed by the stratified emergence rules from the assessment's whole, property, and declared logic:ReductionTheory, the convenient OWL-projectable surface of the assessment exactly as logic:isHolon projects holon-ness. logic:Emergent is reached by negation-as-failure over the aggregate derivation, so the verdict is genuinely theory-relative rather than a bare 'unflagged' default (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Le dérivé résultat de an logic:EmergenceAssessment: the logic:EmergenceVerdict (logic:agrégat, logic:Emergent, ou logic:EmergenceUnknown) the foundation lowering entails pour it."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assessmentWhole|rdfs:label"
msgid "assessment whole"
msgstr "évaluation whole"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assessmentWhole|skos:definition"
msgid "The whole role of an logic:EmergenceAssessment: the entity whose property is being assessed for emergence — the whole that bears the property and stands over the proper parts the reduction is attempted from. One of the three role properties (with logic:assessmentProperty and logic:assessmentReductionTheory) that reify the emergence-assessment relation onto the arity-bounded reasoning surface, mirroring the logic:HolonicPosition role properties (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:assessmentWhole only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le whole role de an logic:EmergenceAssessment: the entity dont propriété est being assessed pour emergence — the whole qui bears the propriété et stands sur the proper parts the reduction est attempted from."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assuresResult|rdfs:label"
msgid "assures result"
msgstr "assures résultat"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/assuresResult|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ResultAssurance to the single logic:ReasoningResult it assesses. Domain logic:ResultAssurance, range logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose, matching the module's convention). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:assuresResult only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ResultAssurance à the single logic:ReasoningResult it assesses."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/asymmetricProperty|rdfs:label"
msgid "asymmetric property"
msgstr "asymmetric propriété"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/asymmetricProperty|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic: property-characteristic marker for asymmetry: a property P such that P(a,b) entails ¬P(b,a). The logic: analogue of owl:AsymmetricProperty, minted standalone so it can co-occur with logic:transitiveProperty on the same property — the transitive ∧ asymmetric combination OWL 2 DL bars for decidability but logic: keeps and reasons over (criticism 7). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:asymmetricProperty only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le logic: propriété-characteristic marker pour asymmetry: a propriété P such qui P(a,b) entails ¬P(b,a)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/attackComponentSelfExclusion|rdfs:label"
msgid "an argument does not attack its own component"
msgstr "an argument does not attack its own component"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/attackComponentSelfExclusion|skos:definition"
msgid "Asserts that a gmeow:Attack's gmeow:attackSource (a gmeow:Argument) must not aim its gmeow:attackTarget at one of its own components — its conclusion (gmeow:argumentConclusion), a premise use (gmeow:hasPremiseUse), or an inference application (gmeow:hasInferenceApplication): an argument does not attack a part of itself. The native coherence gate raises a violation when the target is a component of the source."
msgstr "Asserts qui a gmeow:Attack's gmeow:attackSource (a gmeow:Argument) ne doit pas aim its gmeow:attackTarget at one de its own components — its conclusion (gmeow:argumentConclusion), a premise use (gmeow:hasPremiseUse), ou an inference application (gmeow:hasInferenceApplication): an argument ne fait pas attack a part de itself."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/attackRebutTargetsStandpointClaim|rdfs:label"
msgid "a rebutting attack targets a standpoint claim"
msgstr "a rebutting attack targets a point de vue claim"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/attackRebutTargetsStandpointClaim|skos:definition"
msgid "Asserts that a gmeow:Attack whose gmeow:attackKind is gmeow:attackRebut must aim its gmeow:attackTarget at a conclusion gmeow:StandpointClaim — rebutting attacks the conclusion. The native coherence gate raises a violation when the kind is rebut but the target is not a standpoint claim."
msgstr "Asserts qui a gmeow:Attack dont gmeow:attackKind est gmeow:attackRebut doit aim its gmeow:attackTarget at a conclusion gmeow:StandpointClaim — rebutting attacks the conclusion."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/attackSelfAttackExclusion|rdfs:label"
msgid "a typed attack's source and target are distinct"
msgstr "a typed attack's source and target are distinct"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/attackSelfAttackExclusion|skos:definition"
msgid "Asserts that a gmeow:Attack's gmeow:attackSource and gmeow:attackTarget must be distinct: conflict is irreflexive — nothing attacks itself. The native coherence gate raises a violation when they coincide; the generated SHACL constraint surface is its projection."
msgstr "Asserts qui a gmeow:Attack's gmeow:attackSource et gmeow:attackTarget doit be distinct: conflit est irreflexive — nothing attacks itself."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/attackUndercutTargetsInferenceApplication|rdfs:label"
msgid "an undercutting attack targets an inference application"
msgstr "an undercutting attack targets an inference application"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/attackUndercutTargetsInferenceApplication|skos:definition"
msgid "Asserts that a gmeow:Attack whose gmeow:attackKind is gmeow:attackUndercut must aim its gmeow:attackTarget at a gmeow:InferenceApplication — undercutting attacks the warrant / inferential link. The native coherence gate raises a violation when the kind is undercut but the target is not an inference application."
msgstr "Asserts qui a gmeow:Attack dont gmeow:attackKind est gmeow:attackUndercut doit aim its gmeow:attackTarget at a gmeow:InferenceApplication — undercutting attacks the warrant / inferential link."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/attackUndermineTargetsPremiseUse|rdfs:label"
msgid "an undermining attack targets a premise use"
msgstr "an undermining attack targets a premise use"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/attackUndermineTargetsPremiseUse|skos:definition"
msgid "Asserts that a gmeow:Attack whose gmeow:attackKind is gmeow:attackUndermine must aim its gmeow:attackTarget at a gmeow:PremiseUse — undermining is premise-directed. The native coherence gate raises a violation when the kind is undermine but the target is not a premise use."
msgstr "Asserts qui a gmeow:Attack dont gmeow:attackKind est gmeow:attackUndermine doit aim its gmeow:attackTarget at a gmeow:PremiseUse — undermining est premise-directed."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/awaitingSignal|rdfs:label"
msgid "awaiting signal"
msgstr "awaiting signal"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/awaitingSignal|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a node still blocked on a logic:ExternalSignal to the exact signal it is waiting on — the witness that a notification-wait is pending (the engine has not been told), never silently completed. It appears in two places, both marking the same withheld judgment. (1) On a logic:GateUndetermined logic:GateProbe over a logic:NotificationWaitSchema: the reason the gate is undetermined rather than admitted. (2) On a logic:TransactionOutcome whose executed transaction path HALTED at an un-signalled wait step: the load-bearing distinction between a PENDING (undetermined) outcome and a definite failure — both read logic:transactionSucceeds false, but only the pending one names, through this witness, the signal it still awaits, so a plan blocked on an external notification is never conflated with a genuine precondition failure. Range the awaited logic:ExternalSignal (stated in prose). In every case: the wait can still complete once the signal arrives."
msgstr "Relates a nœud still bloqué sur a logic:ExternalSignal à the exact signal it est waiting sur — the témoin qui a notification-wait est pending (the engine possède not been told), jamais silently completed."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/awaitsSignal|rdfs:label"
msgid "awaits signal"
msgstr "awaits signal"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/awaitsSignal|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:NotificationWaitSchema to the logic:ExternalSignal situation whose arrival its completion waits on. Domain logic:NotificationWaitSchema, range a logic:ExternalSignal situation (stated in prose). The wait fires only once this signal obtains in the state; until then it is pending (logic:awaitingSignal), never silently completed."
msgstr "Relates a logic:NotificationWaitSchema à the logic:ExternalSignal situation dont arrival its completion waits on."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/axiomHash|rdfs:label"
msgid "axiom hash"
msgstr "axiom hash"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/axiomHash|skos:definition"
msgid "A content-addressed digest of an axiom set inside the checked bundle, pinning exactly which axioms the coherence outcome ranged over — MULTI-valued, one per certified fragment component. Domain logic:CoherenceCertificate or logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation (stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:axiomHash only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Un content-addressed digest de an axiom set inside the checked bundle, pinning exactly qui axioms the cohérence résultat ranged sur — MULTI-valued, one per certified fragment component."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/bearsProperty|rdfs:label"
msgid "bears property"
msgstr "bears propriété"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/bearsProperty|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates an entity to a property-value it carries, for the purpose of the emergence calculus: a whole and its proper parts each bearsProperty the values an logic:EmergenceAssessment reasons over. A deliberately thin logic-layer relation — NOT a metaphysical inherence claim; the bearer relation for logic:Modes and dispositions is asserted with their own domain properties (Principle 5), and gufo:inheresIn is never asserted. Whether a borne whole property reduces to the parts that bear it is exactly what logic:EmergenceAssessment decides; crucially, no rule propagates bearsProperty down logic:properPartOf, so an logic:Emergent whole property never reaches its parts (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Relates an entity à a propriété-valeur it carries, pour the purpose de the emergence calculus: a whole et its proper parts each bearsProperty the values an logic:EmergenceAssessment reasons over."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/boundSituationType|rdfs:label"
msgid "bound situation type"
msgstr "bound situation type"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/boundSituationType|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates an atomic, achievement, maintenance, or avoidance logic:GoalExpression to the logic:Situation type it targets — the situation whose obtaining (via logic:situationObtains at a state along the path) decides the goal. Domain logic:GoalExpression, range logic:Situation (stated in prose). Part of a goal expression's STRUCTURAL identity together with its kind and operands. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:boundSituationType only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates an atomique, accomplissement, maintien, ou évitement logic:GoalExpression à the logic:situation type it targets — the situation dont obtaining (via logic:situationObtains at a état along the chemin) decides the objectif."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/branchActionSchema|rdfs:label"
msgid "branch action schema"
msgstr "branch action schéma"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/branchActionSchema|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a policy branch to the logic:ActionSchema it invokes when selected — the next action the policy takes for this observation. Domain a policy branch, range logic:ActionSchema (stated in prose). The native evaluator surfaces it as logic:nextActionSchema on the policy when the branch's logic:branchGuard matches the observation. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:branchActionSchema only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a politique branch à the logic:ActionSchema it invokes lorsque selected — the next action the politique takes pour this observation."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/branchGuard|rdfs:label"
msgid "branch guard"
msgstr "branch guard"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/branchGuard|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a policy branch to the revealed situation that selects it: when the branch's logic:branchObservation reveals (logic:reveals) this situation, the branch is selected. Domain a policy branch, range the guarding logic:Situation (stated in prose). The guard the native evaluator matches against the observation's revealed situation. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:branchGuard only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a politique branch à the revealed situation qui selects it: lorsque the branch's logic:branchObservation reveals (logic:reveals) this situation, the branch est selected."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/branchObservation|rdfs:label"
msgid "branch observation"
msgstr "branch observation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/branchObservation|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a policy branch to the observation value its selection is conditioned on — the observation whose logic:reveals decides whether this branch fires. Domain a policy branch, range the logic:observation value (stated in prose). What makes a plan's branching observation-conditioned rather than fixed in advance."
msgstr "Relates a politique branch à the observation valeur its selection est conditioned sur — the observation dont logic:reveals decides whether this branch fires."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/builtinArithmetic|rdfs:label"
msgid "arithmetic builtin"
msgstr "arithmetic primitive"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/builtinArithmetic|skos:definition"
msgid "The native basic-math builtin: derives a value by the arithmetic operations (add, subtract, multiply, divide, compare) over numeric arguments. A derivational builtin (Principle 12, in-logic): the lightweight math a foundation needs, NOT heavy numerical domain computation (n-dimensional vector operations, SLAM, trajectory updates), which stays external by reference. Gated to logic:ProceduralPrologProfile; the closed operator set is evaluated by the native physical reasoning core as binding-pattern-keyed filters and generators, with residual modes (an unbound operand, division by zero, integer overflow) declared as gaps and routed to the fallback oracle — never a wrong answer."
msgstr "Le native basic-math primitive: derives a valeur par the arithmetic operations (add, subtract, multiply, divide, compare) sur numeric arguments."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/builtinDateDifference|rdfs:label"
msgid "date-difference builtin"
msgstr "date-difference primitive"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/builtinDateDifference|skos:definition"
msgid "The native date-arithmetic builtin: derives the difference between two dates, e.g. legalAge = year(now) − year(birth). A derivational builtin (Principle 12, in-logic): the lightweight date arithmetic a foundation needs, NOT heavy temporal-domain computation (calendar/datum transforms), which stays external by reference. Gated to logic:ProceduralPrologProfile; execution is seamed to the engine."
msgstr "Le native date-arithmetic primitive: derives the difference entre two dates, e.g."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/builtinStringConcat|rdfs:label"
msgid "string-concat builtin"
msgstr "string-concat primitive"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/builtinStringConcat|skos:definition"
msgid "The native string-concatenation builtin: derives a string by joining its arguments, e.g. fullName = firstName + \" \" + lastName. A derivational builtin (Principle 12, in-logic): the lightweight string derivation a foundation needs, NOT heavy domain text processing, which stays external by reference. Gated to logic:ProceduralPrologProfile; execution is seamed to the engine."
msgstr "Le native string-concatenation primitive: derives a string par joining its arguments, e.g."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/bundleHash|rdfs:label"
msgid "bundle hash"
msgstr "bundle hash"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/bundleHash|skos:definition"
msgid "The content-addressed identity (a blake3 digest) of the exact bundle a coherence outcome was checked over. The outcome is invalid for any bundle whose canonical hash differs. Single-valued. Domain logic:CoherenceCertificate or logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation (stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:bundleHash only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le content-addressed identité (a blake3 digest) de the exact bundle a cohérence résultat was checked over."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateBullshitTruthIndifference|rdfs:label"
msgid "bullshit is the truth-indifferent modality"
msgstr "bullshit is the vérité-indifferent modality"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateBullshitTruthIndifference|skos:definition"
msgid "The equivalence-definition formalization candidate governing logic:bullshitTruthIndifference: to carry gmeow:claimModality gmeow:bullshit is exactly to be a gmeow:StandpointClaim held with gmeow:claimTruthDirectedness gmeow:truthIndifferent — Frankfurt's bullshit, neither true nor false under the standpoint. truthIndifferent uniquely selects the bullshit modality among the five, so it is definitional. Realized in the OWL / full-FOL projection (biconditional), non-monotone, disclosed in the loss ledger — NOT natively enforced. Harvested from gmeow:bullshit's skos:definition. Accepted through review with a positive case (logic:cqBullshitIndifferenceHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqBullshitIndifferenceLieRejected)."
msgstr "Le equivalence-définition formalisation candidat governing logic:bullshitTruthIndifference: à carry gmeow:claimModality gmeow:bullshit est exactly à be a gmeow:StandpointClaim held avec gmeow:claimTruthDirectedness gmeow:truthIndifferent — Frankfurt's bullshit, neither true nor false sous the point de vue."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateCategory|rdfs:label"
msgid "candidate category"
msgstr "candidat catégorie"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateCategory|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:FormalizationCandidate to the logic:FormalizationCategory recording what kind of force its prose carried. Single-valued and REQUIRED: a candidate with no category resolving to the closed set is a hard governance error, never silently bucketed. Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate, range logic:FormalizationCategory."
msgstr "Relates a logic:FormalizationCandidate à the logic:FormalizationCategory recording what kind de force its prose carried."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateContract|rdfs:label"
msgid "candidate contract"
msgstr "candidat contract"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateContract|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:FormalizationCandidate to the logic:ReasoningContract (ME1) its proposed axiom would be interpreted under — the semantics that make 'sound' meaningful for it. Single-valued. Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate, range logic:ReasoningContract. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:candidateContract only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:FormalizationCandidate à the logic:ReasoningContract (ME1) its proposé axiom would be interpreted sous — the sémantique qui make 'sound' meaningful pour it."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateCounterpartNonTransitive|rdfs:label"
msgid "counterpart stays symmetric-only, never transitive"
msgstr "counterpart stays symmetric-only, never transitive"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateCounterpartNonTransitive|skos:definition"
msgid "The deliberate-non-assertion formalization candidate carrying the standing commitment that cross-realm counterpart identity (gmeow:counterpartOf) stays non-transitive: it is symmetric by design but must never chain, so contested, standpoint-indexed, or context-dependent claims are never transitively collapsed into owl:sameAs identity. Realized as the logic:NonEntailmentObligation logic:CounterpartNonTransitivityObligation and enforced by Arm A syntactic reachability over the counterpart rule heads (no rule head produces the predicate). Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation). The semantic risk is core-contaminating: a careless transitivity rule would corrupt the reasoned core by merging entities the design keeps distinct. Its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:counterpartOf, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition) ties it to the exact prose that commits to non-transitivity, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that skos:definition text so a later edit surfaces as drift."
msgstr "Le deliberate-non-assertion formalisation candidat carrying the standing engagement qui cross-realm counterpart identité (gmeow:counterpartOf) stays non-transitive: it est symmetric par design mais doit jamais chain, so contested, point de vue-indexed, ou contexte-dependent claims sont jamais transitively collapsed dans owl:sameAs identité."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateCrossNodeGlut|rdfs:label"
msgid "a cross-node glut is opposing polarities at one shared anchor"
msgstr "a cross-nœud glut is opposing polarities at one shared anchor"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateCrossNodeGlut|skos:definition"
msgid "The derivation-rule formalization candidate governing logic:ruleCrossNodeGlut: it harvests the cross-node-glut commitment in gmeow:findingAnchor's skos:definition (the anchor is the code-blind join key that lets a reasoner join two different-code findings at one place and detect an opposing-polarity conflict the same-fingerprint merge misses) into an enforced positive-Horn rule with an inequality guard and a non-trivial-anchor guard, materialized natively as logic:ExactPreservation. Because the reified-Horn chase cannot mint a fresh witness node, the glut is carried as the gmeow:crossNodeGlutWith edge rather than a minted gmeow:CrossNodeGlutWitness. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqCrossNodeGlutHolds) and two countermodels (logic:cqCrossNodeGlutTrivialAnchorRejected, logic:cqCrossNodeGlutSamePolarityRejected). Its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:findingAnchor, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition) ties it to the exact prose, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that definition text so a later edit surfaces as drift."
msgstr "Le dérivation-règle formalisation candidat governing logic:ruleCrossNodeGlut: it harvests the cross-nœud-glut engagement dans gmeow:findingAnchor's skos:définition (the anchor est the code-blind join key qui lets a raisonneur join two different-code findings at one place et detect an opposing-polarity conflit the same-fingerprint merge misses) dans an enforced positif-Horn règle avec an inequality guard et a non-trivial-anchor guard, materialized natively as logic:ExactPreservation."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateDeceptionHeldProjectedDivergence|rdfs:label"
msgid "deception is a divergent held/projected gap"
msgstr "deception is a divergent held/projected gap"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateDeceptionHeldProjectedDivergence|skos:definition"
msgid "The necessary-condition formalization candidate governing logic:deceptionHeldProjectedDivergence: every gmeow:eventTypeDeception event carries a gmeow:heldStandpoint and a gmeow:projectedStandpoint doxastic claim whose modalities diverge — the gap is the act, not a truth verdict. A necessary, not sufficient, condition (a licensed-falsehood projection also has a gap yet is not deception; see logic:candidateLicensedFalsehoodNotDeception). Realized in the OWL / full-FOL projection (nested existential with strong negation), non-monotone, disclosed in the loss ledger — NOT natively enforced. Harvested from gmeow:eventTypeDeception's skos:definition, so an edit to that prose surfaces as drift. Accepted through review with a positive case (logic:cqDeceptionDivergenceHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqDeceptionDivergenceGapRejected)."
msgstr "Le necessary-condition formalisation candidat governing logic:deceptionHeldProjectedDivergence: chaque gmeow:eventTypeDeception event porte a gmeow:heldStandpoint et a gmeow:projectedStandpoint doxastic claim dont modalities diverge — the gap est the act, not a vérité verdict."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateDeliberateNonAssertion|rdfs:label"
msgid "candidate deliberate non-assertion"
msgstr "candidat deliberate non-assertion"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateDeliberateNonAssertion|skos:definition"
msgid "Marks a logic:FormalizationCandidate as one of the ontology's deliberate-non-assertion boundaries — an intentional refusal to over-assert that the foundation commits to and is held against: a forbidden entailment carried by a logic:NonEntailmentObligation, an integrity constraint whose violation is a finding, or a deliberately preserved class overlap. Its role is enumerability: the marked set IS the deliberate-non-assertion report, and it deliberately cuts across logic:candidateCategory (a boundary may be a logic:CategoryNonEntailmentObligation, a logic:CategoryIntegrityConstraint or a logic:CategoryDeliberateOverlap), so the whole boundary set is queryable as one report rather than inferred from an overloaded category facet (an integrity-constraint boundary is not distinguishable from an ordinary integrity constraint by category alone). Present and true on exactly the guardrail candidates; single-valued, xsd:boolean. Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate."
msgstr "Marks a logic:FormalizationCandidate as one de the ontology's deliberate-non-assertion boundaries — an intentional refusal à over-assert qui the foundation commits à et est held against: a forbidden implication carried par a logic:NonEntailmentObligation, an intégrité contrainte dont violation est a finding, ou a deliberately preserved class overlap."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateDiagnosticMetaExtensibility|rdfs:label"
msgid "a new meta-finding is added by tagging a rule, with no engine change"
msgstr "a new meta-finding is added by tagging a règle, with no engine change"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateDiagnosticMetaExtensibility|skos:definition"
msgid "The derivation-rule formalization candidate governing logic:ruleRootFinding, the extensibility demonstrator: it harvests the extension-point commitment in gmeow:DiagnosticMetaRule's skos:definition (the reasoner enumerates every gmeow:DiagnosticMetaRule and applies it, so a new meta-finding is added by authoring a new tagged rule with zero engine change) into an enforced positive-Horn rule deriving gmeow:RootFinding, materialized natively as logic:ExactPreservation. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqRootFindingHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqRootFindingNonRootRejected). Its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:DiagnosticMetaRule, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition) ties it to the exact prose, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that definition text so a later edit surfaces as drift."
msgstr "Le dérivation-règle formalisation candidat governing logic:ruleRootFinding, the extensibility demonstrator: it harvests the extension-point engagement dans gmeow:DiagnosticMetaRule's skos:définition (the raisonneur enumerates chaque gmeow:DiagnosticMetaRule et applies it, so a new meta-finding est added par authoring a new tagged règle avec zero engine change) dans an enforced positif-Horn règle deriving gmeow:RootFinding, materialized natively as logic:ExactPreservation."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateEndurantPerdurantDisjoint|rdfs:label"
msgid "endurant and perdurant are disjoint"
msgstr "endurant and perdurant are disjoint"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateEndurantPerdurantDisjoint|skos:definition"
msgid "The formalization candidate that harvests the continuant/occurrent divide from logic:Endurant's skos:definition (which contrasts logic:Perdurant, which has temporal parts) into the enforced logic:Endurant owl:disjointWith logic:Perdurant integrity constraint asserted above. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqEndurantPerdurantDisjointHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqEndurantPerdurantClashRejected); its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes logic:Endurant, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition) ties it to the exact prose, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that definition text so a later edit surfaces as drift. The native DL coherence gate reads the owl:disjointWith directly, forcing a both-endurant-and-perdurant individual to owl:Nothing."
msgstr "Le formalisation candidat qui harvests the continuant/occurrent divide de logic:Endurant's skos:définition (which contrasts logic:Perdurant, qui possède temporal parts) dans the enforced logic:Endurant owl:disjointWith logic:Perdurant intégrité contrainte asserted above."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateEntitySortalCovering|rdfs:label"
msgid "every entity is one of the four sortals"
msgstr "every entity is one of the quatre sortals"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateEntitySortalCovering|skos:definition"
msgid "The necessary-condition formalization candidate governing the class covering that every gmeow:Entity is one of {gmeow:Agent, gmeow:InformationObject, gmeow:PhysicalObject, gmeow:SocialObject}. Its source is gmeow:Entity's gmeow:howToUse prose, which enumerates the four sortals. The covering is realized ONLY in the OWL projection as an owl:unionOf (a class-covering disjunction); it is NON-monotone and is disclosed in the loss ledger — the native monotone StratifiedNAF chase does NOT enforce a disjunctive head, so this is projection-only, not natively enforced. It carries NO harvest back-link (the covering is a doc-level enumeration, not a single harvestable axiom field). Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqEntitySortalCoveringHolds) and a negative case (logic:cqEntitySortalCoveringGapRejected); logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that gmeow:howToUse text for drift detection."
msgstr "Le necessary-condition formalisation candidat governing the class covering qui chaque gmeow:Entity est one de {gmeow:Agent, gmeow:InformationObject, gmeow:PhysicalObject, gmeow:SocialObject}."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateEventSituationDisjoint|rdfs:label"
msgid "event and situation are disjoint"
msgstr "event and situation are disjoint"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateEventSituationDisjoint|skos:definition"
msgid "The formalization candidate governing the logic:Event owl:disjointWith logic:Situation integrity constraint asserted above: an occurrence that unfolds in time is disjoint from the static configuration a situation records. Unlike the other partition axioms this contrast is NOT stated in a single harvestable annotation field, so the candidate carries NO harvest back-link (neither logic:candidateFormalizes nor logic:candidateSourceField — never a half-link); its provenance records a doc-section/foundation harvest over the occurrent structure instead. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqEventSituationDisjointHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqEventSituationClashRejected); logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of logic:Event's skos:definition so an edit to that anchor prose surfaces as drift. The native DL coherence gate reads the owl:disjointWith directly, forcing a both-event-and-situation individual to owl:Nothing."
msgstr "Le formalisation candidat governing the logic:Event owl:disjointWith logic:situation intégrité contrainte asserted above: an occurrence qui unfolds dans time est disjoint de the static configuration a situation records."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateExtractionProvenance|rdfs:label"
msgid "candidate extraction provenance"
msgstr "candidat extraction provenance"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateExtractionProvenance|skos:definition"
msgid "The provenance of a candidate's extraction — what produced it (an extractor identifier, run, or model invocation reference). Records that an automated extraction is exactly that, so it enters at logic:CandidateProposed and earns no canonical force without review. Single-valued, xsd:string. Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:candidateExtractionProvenance only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le provenance de a candidat's extraction — what produced it (an extractor identifier, run, ou modèle invocation reference)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateFalsehoodIsRefutedClaim|rdfs:label"
msgid "falsehood is a refuted standpoint claim"
msgstr "falsehood is a refuted point de vue claim"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateFalsehoodIsRefutedClaim|skos:definition"
msgid "The equivalence-definition formalization candidate governing logic:falsehoodIsRefutedClaim: to carry gmeow:claimModality gmeow:refuted is exactly to be a gmeow:StandpointClaim that necessarily denies its proposition (gmeow:polarityDeny ∧ gmeow:modalForceNecessary = □¬). This pins 'falsehood = refuted StandpointClaim' as a frame-relative configuration, never a global truth flag, and ties the legacy five-value modality twin to its canonical axes. Realized in the OWL / full-FOL projection (biconditional), non-monotone, disclosed in the loss ledger — NOT natively enforced. Harvested from gmeow:refuted's skos:definition. Accepted through review with a positive case (logic:cqFalsehoodRefutedHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqFalsehoodRefutedGlobalTruthRejected)."
msgstr "Le equivalence-définition formalisation candidat governing logic:falsehoodIsRefutedClaim: à carry gmeow:claimModality gmeow:refuted est exactly à be a gmeow:StandpointClaim qui necessarily denies its proposition (gmeow:polarityDeny ∧ gmeow:modalForceNecessary = □¬)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateFindingCluster|rdfs:label"
msgid "findings sharing a root cause group under one cluster node"
msgstr "findings sharing a root cause group under one cluster nœud"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateFindingCluster|skos:definition"
msgid "The derivation-rule formalization candidate governing logic:ruleFindingCluster, logic:ruleClusterRoot, and logic:ruleFindingClusterType: it harvests the grouping commitment in gmeow:FindingCluster's skos:definition (a grouping of findings that share one gmeow:findingRootCause, its members linked by gmeow:findingCluster and its shared root carried by gmeow:clusterRoot) into three enforced positive-Horn rules over the root-cause output, materialized natively as logic:ExactPreservation. Because fresh-node minting is not expressible in the reified-Horn chase, the cluster is identified by its root finding. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqFindingClusterHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqFindingClusterDistinctRootsRejected). Its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:FindingCluster, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition) ties it to the exact prose, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that definition text so a later edit surfaces as drift."
msgstr "Le dérivation-règle formalisation candidat governing logic:ruleFindingCluster, logic:ruleClusterRoot, et logic:ruleFindingClusterType: it harvests the grouping engagement dans gmeow:FindingCluster's skos:définition (a grouping de findings qui share one gmeow:findingRootCause, its members linked par gmeow:findingCluster et its shared root carried par gmeow:clusterRoot) dans three enforced positif-Horn rules sur the root-cause output, materialized natively as logic:ExactPreservation."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateFindingRootCause|rdfs:label"
msgid "a finding's root cause is a traced childless antecedent"
msgstr "a finding's root cause is a traced childless antecedent"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateFindingRootCause|skos:definition"
msgid "The derivation-rule formalization candidate governing logic:ruleFindingHasAntecedent and logic:ruleFindingRootCause: it harvests the root-cause commitment in gmeow:findingRootCause's skos:definition (the shared root antecedent reached by following gmeow:findingAntecedent transitively up the witness DAG to a childless witness, honestly the shared root and not a dominator) into an enforced stratified-negation rule set, materialized natively as logic:ExactPreservation. The childless test is a negation-as-failure over the derived gmeow:findingHasAntecedent marker, so the contract is logic:StratifiedNAFProfile. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqFindingRootCauseHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqFindingRootCauseNonRootRejected). Its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:findingRootCause, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition) ties it to the exact prose, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that definition text so a later edit surfaces as drift."
msgstr "Le dérivation-règle formalisation candidat governing logic:ruleFindingHasAntecedent et logic:ruleFindingRootCause: it harvests the root-cause engagement dans gmeow:findingRootCause's skos:définition (the shared root antecedent reached par following gmeow:findingAntecedent transitively up the témoin DAG à a childless témoin, honestly the shared root et not a dominator) dans an enforced stratified-negation règle set, materialized natively as logic:ExactPreservation."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateFindingTraces|rdfs:label"
msgid "finding-traces is the transitive closure of the antecedent edge"
msgstr "finding-traces is the transitive fermeture of the antecedent edge"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateFindingTraces|skos:definition"
msgid "The derivation-rule formalization candidate governing logic:ruleFindingTracesBase and logic:ruleFindingTracesStep: it harvests the transitive-reachability commitment in gmeow:findingAntecedent's skos:definition (the reasoner joins UP the witness DAG, following the edge transitively to the root antecedent) into two enforced positive-Horn rules deriving the closure gmeow:findingTraces, materialized natively as logic:ExactPreservation. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqFindingTracesHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqFindingTracesNonReachRejected). Its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:findingAntecedent, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition) ties it to the exact prose, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that definition text so a later edit surfaces as drift."
msgstr "Le dérivation-règle formalisation candidat governing logic:ruleFindingTracesBase et logic:ruleFindingTracesStep: it harvests the transitive-reachability engagement dans gmeow:findingAntecedent's skos:définition (the raisonneur joins UP the témoin DAG, following the edge transitively à the root antecedent) dans two enforced positif-Horn rules deriving the fermeture gmeow:findingTraces, materialized natively as logic:ExactPreservation."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateFormalizes|rdfs:label"
msgid "candidate formalizes"
msgstr "candidat formalizes"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateFormalizes|skos:definition"
msgid "The harvest back-link: relates a logic:FormalizationCandidate to the prose-bearing term (a gmeow: or logic: term, stated in prose) whose constraint its axiom formalizes, read together with logic:candidateSourceField (which of that term's annotation fields — skos:definition, gmeow:useWhen or gmeow:avoidWhen). Where logic:candidateSourceHash anchors the candidate to its source text by hash and logic:candidateExtractionProvenance records what produced it, this names the exact ontology term the harvested axiom keeps coherent, so harvest coverage is queryable in both directions. Present exactly when the source IS a term's annotation field (a doc-section source stays recorded in provenance alone, never a fabricated term-link); single-valued. Distinct from logic:formalizes, which bridges a logic: term to a gmeow: concept and is never a reasoned axiom. Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate."
msgstr "Le harvest back-link: relie a logic:FormalizationCandidate à the prose-bearing terme (a gmeow: ou logic: terme, stated dans prose) dont contrainte its axiom formalizes, read together avec logic:candidateSourceField (which de qui terme's annotation fields — skos:définition, gmeow:useWhen ou gmeow:avoidWhen)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateFrameRelativity|rdfs:label"
msgid "measured values are frame-relative — no frame-free collapse"
msgstr "measured values are frame-relative — no frame-free collapse"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateFrameRelativity|skos:definition"
msgid "The integrity-constraint formalization candidate that harvests Principle 11 frame-relativity from logic:referenceFrame's skos:definition into the enforced logic:MeasurementFrameMissing constraint: a logic:measuredValue is meaningful only together with the logic:referenceFrame it is expressed in, so a frame-free value is ill-formed and two frame-relative values are never equated frame-free. Violation is a finding, not a derivation, materialized by the existing foundation quality discipline. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqFrameRelativityHolds — a framed value stays well-formed) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqFrameRelativityFramelessRejected — a frame-free value is the logic:MeasurementFrameMissing violation). Its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes logic:referenceFrame, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition) ties it to the exact prose, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that definition text so a later edit surfaces as drift."
msgstr "Le intégrité-contrainte formalisation candidat qui harvests Principle 11 frame-relativity de logic:referenceFrame's skos:définition dans the enforced logic:MeasurementFrameMissing contrainte: a logic:measuredValue est meaningful uniquement together avec the logic:referenceFrame it est expressed in, so a frame-free valeur est ill-formed et two frame-relative values sont jamais equated frame-free."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateFunctionalComplexKindDisjoint|rdfs:label"
msgid "individuation kinds are pairwise disjoint"
msgstr "individuation kinds are pairwise disjoint"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateFunctionalComplexKindDisjoint|skos:definition"
msgid "The net-new-enforcement formalization candidate that harvests the pairwise disjointness of the three mereological individuation kinds (logic:Collection, logic:FunctionalComplex, logic:Quantity) from their skos:definition prose into enforced owl:disjointWith integrity constraints: the demonstration that the harvest mechanism creates axioms that did NOT exist before, not merely a link to an already-typed one. None of the three was asserted owl:disjointWith on origin/main; the prose contrasts them as distinct individuation modes (logic:FunctionalComplex's Definition names both other kinds explicitly). Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqFunctionalComplexKindDisjointHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqFunctionalComplexKindDisjointOverlapRejected); its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes logic:FunctionalComplex, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition) ties it to the exact prose, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that definition text so a later edit to the prose surfaces as drift. The native DL coherence gate reads the resulting owl:disjointWith directly, forcing a two-kind individual to owl:Nothing."
msgstr "Le net-new-enforcement formalisation candidat qui harvests the pairwise disjointness de the three mereological individuation kinds (logic:collection, logic:FunctionalComplex, logic:Quantity) de their skos:définition prose dans enforced owl:disjointWith intégrité constraints: the demonstration qui the harvest mechanism creates axioms qui did NOT exist before, not merely a link à an already-typed one."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateGateFatalVerdict|rdfs:label"
msgid "the fatal gate verdict derives on the principal up-set of the truth ordering"
msgstr "the fatal gate verdict derives on the principal up-set of the vérité ordering"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateGateFatalVerdict|skos:definition"
msgid "The derivation-rule formalization candidate governing logic:ruleGateFatalVerdict: it harvests the up-set construction documented in gmeow:findingGateVerdict's skos:definition (the verdict is gmeow:gateFatal exactly on the principal up-set ↑(Error, Blocking, Binding), the meet of the severity, blocking-projected category, and standpoint axes) into an enforced positive-Horn derivation rule, materialized natively as logic:ExactPreservation — the RDF-side image of the single Rust gmeow_errors::grade::gate() policy morphism. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqGateFatalVerdictHolds) and two never-gate countermodels (logic:cqGateFatalAdvisoryNeverFatalRejected, logic:cqGateFatalPermittedConflictNeverFatalRejected). Its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:findingGateVerdict, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition) ties it to the exact prose, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that definition text so a later edit surfaces as drift."
msgstr "Le dérivation-règle formalisation candidat governing logic:ruleGateFatalVerdict: it harvests the up-set construction documented dans gmeow:findingGateVerdict's skos:définition (the verdict est gmeow:gateFatal exactly sur the principal up-set ↑(Error, Blocking, liaison), the meet de the severity, blocking-projected catégorie, et point de vue axes) dans an enforced positif-Horn dérivation règle, materialized natively as logic:ExactPreservation — the RDF-side image de the single Rust gmeow_errors::grade::gate() politique morphism."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateIndirectContributor|rdfs:label"
msgid "indirect contributor derives across the generation chain"
msgstr "indirect contributor derives across the generation chain"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateIndirectContributor|skos:definition"
msgid "The derivation-rule formalization candidate governing logic:ruleIndirectContributor: it harvests the productive composition documented in gmeow:indirectContributor's skos:definition (indirect contributors are the agents reached by composing gmeow:wasGeneratedBy with gmeow:wasAssociatedWith) into an enforced positive-Horn derivation rule, materialized natively as logic:ExactPreservation. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqIndirectContributorHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqIndirectContributorDirectAttributionRejected), and bound to the non-entailment obligation logic:IndirectContributorNotAttributionObligation that forbids the derived edge from ever becoming asserted gmeow:wasAttributedTo. Its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:indirectContributor, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition) ties it to the exact prose, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that definition text so a later edit surfaces as drift."
msgstr "Le dérivation-règle formalisation candidat governing logic:ruleIndirectContributor: it harvests the productive composition documented dans gmeow:indirectContributor's skos:définition (indirect contributors sont the agents reached par composing gmeow:wasGeneratedBy avec gmeow:wasAssociatedWith) dans an enforced positif-Horn dérivation règle, materialized natively as logic:ExactPreservation."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateInstantiatesWork|rdfs:label"
msgid "WEMI Item→Work shortcut derives across the full spine"
msgstr "WEMI Item→Work shortcut derives across the full spine"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateInstantiatesWork|skos:definition"
msgid "The derivation-rule formalization candidate governing logic:ruleInstantiatesWork: it harvests the copy-to-Work composition documented in gmeow:instantiatesWork's skos:definition (an Item instantiates the Work reached by composing gmeow:exemplifies, gmeow:embodies and gmeow:realizes) into an enforced positive-Horn derivation rule, materialized natively as logic:ExactPreservation. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqInstantiatesWorkHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqInstantiatesWorkBrokenSpineRejected). Its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:instantiatesWork, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition) ties it to the exact prose, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that definition text so a later edit surfaces as drift."
msgstr "Le dérivation-règle formalisation candidat governing logic:ruleInstantiatesWork: it harvests the copy-to-Work composition documented dans gmeow:instantiatesWork's skos:définition (an Item instantiates the Work reached par composing gmeow:exemplifies, gmeow:embodies et gmeow:realizes) dans an enforced positif-Horn dérivation règle, materialized natively as logic:ExactPreservation."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateIntentNotEntailed|rdfs:label"
msgid "deceptive intent is attributed, never entailed"
msgstr "deceptive intent is attributed, never entailed"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateIntentNotEntailed|skos:definition"
msgid "The deliberate-non-assertion formalization candidate carrying the standing commitment that deceptive intent must never be entailed: gmeow:deceptiveIntentClaim is an attributed, defeasible standpoint claim, so a held≠projected structural gap is EVIDENCE, never ENTAILMENT, of intent, and the foundation must never derive the predicate. Realized as the logic:NonEntailmentObligation logic:IntentNotFromDeceptionObligation and enforced by Arm A syntactic reachability over the rule heads plus Arm B finite closure over the materialized derivation graph. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation). The semantic risk is core-contaminating: a mis-formalization that closed this inference would corrupt the reasoned core with an entailed intent, so the guardrail protects the core, not merely a projection. Its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:deceptiveIntentClaim, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldAvoidWhen) ties it to the exact prose that forbids the entailment, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that gmeow:avoidWhen text so a later edit surfaces as drift."
msgstr "Le deliberate-non-assertion formalisation candidat carrying the standing engagement qui deceptive intent doit jamais be entailed: gmeow:deceptiveIntentClaim est an attributed, defeasible point de vue claim, so a held≠projected structurel gap est preuve, jamais implication, de intent, et the foundation doit jamais derive the prédicat."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateLicensedFalsehoodNotDeception|rdfs:label"
msgid "licensed falsehood is not deception"
msgstr "licensed falsehood is not deception"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateLicensedFalsehoodNotDeception|skos:definition"
msgid "The necessary-condition formalization candidate governing logic:licensedFalsehoodNotDeception: a gmeow:Event whose projected standpoint is gmeow:veridicalityLicensedFalsehood is excluded from gmeow:eventTypeDeception — the fiction/satire/sarcasm safety property that separates harmless non-truth-asserting frames from deception. Realized in the OWL / full-FOL projection (strong negation), non-monotone, disclosed in the loss ledger — NOT natively enforced. Harvested from gmeow:veridicalityLicensedFalsehood's skos:definition. Accepted through review with a positive case (logic:cqLicensedFalsehoodSafeHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqLicensedFalsehoodDeceptionRejected)."
msgstr "Le necessary-condition formalisation candidat governing logic:licensedFalsehoodNotDeception: a gmeow:Event dont projected point de vue est gmeow:veridicalityLicensedFalsehood est excluded de gmeow:eventTypeDeception — the fiction/satire/sarcasm safety propriété qui separates harmless non-vérité-asserting frames de deception."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateLifecycle|rdfs:label"
msgid "candidate lifecycle"
msgstr "candidat cycle de vie"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateLifecycle|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:FormalizationCandidate to its current logic:CandidateLifecycleState. Single-valued. logic:CandidateAccepted is the canonical state and is legitimate only with a recorded logic:reviewedBy decision. Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate, range logic:CandidateLifecycleState. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:candidateLifecycle only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:FormalizationCandidate à its current logic:CandidateLifecycleState."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateNegativeCase|rdfs:label"
msgid "candidate negative case"
msgstr "candidat négatif case"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateNegativeCase|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:FormalizationCandidate to a negative case or countermodel — a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion the axiom must NOT satisfy, recording the boundary the formalization must respect (range gmeow:CompetencyQuestion, stated in prose). Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate."
msgstr "Relates a logic:FormalizationCandidate à a négatif case ou countermodel — a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion the axiom doit NOT satisfy, recording the boundary the formalisation doit respect (plage gmeow:CompetencyQuestion, stated dans prose)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateNoOverTyping|rdfs:label"
msgid "an instance carries at most one ultimate Kind — no over-typing"
msgstr "an instance carries at most one ultimate Kind — no over-typing"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateNoOverTyping|skos:definition"
msgid "The integrity-constraint formalization candidate that harvests Principle 9's no-over-typing boundary from logic:MixIden's skos:definition into the enforced identity-overlap discipline: a sortal inherits its principle of identity from exactly one Kind, so an instance tracing to two-or-more disjoint Kinds is the logic:MixIden violation. Violation is a finding, not a derivation, materialized by the existing foundation identity discipline (it wraps logic:MixIden, it does not duplicate it). Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqNoOverTypingHolds — a single-Kind instance is well-formed) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqNoOverTypingTwoKindsRejected — a two-Kind instance is the logic:MixIden violation). Its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes logic:MixIden, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition) ties it to the exact prose, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that definition text so a later edit surfaces as drift."
msgstr "Le intégrité-contrainte formalisation candidat qui harvests Principle 9's no-over-typing boundary de logic:MixIden's skos:définition dans the enforced identité-overlap discipline: a sortal inherits its principle de identité de exactement un Kind, so an instance tracing à two-or-more disjoint Kinds est the logic:MixIden violation."


msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateNonEntailment|rdfs:label"
msgid "candidate non-entailment"
msgstr "candidat non-implication"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateNonEntailment|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:FormalizationCandidate to a logic:NonEntailmentObligation its axiom is required to respect — the forbidden conclusion the formalization must not let the engine draw. Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate, range logic:NonEntailmentObligation."
msgstr "Relates a logic:FormalizationCandidate à a logic:NonEntailmentObligation its axiom est obligatoire à respect — the forbidden conclusion the formalisation ne doit pas let the engine draw."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateObjectIndividuationCovering|rdfs:label"
msgid "every object is one of the three individuation kinds"
msgstr "every object is one of the three individuation kinds"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateObjectIndividuationCovering|skos:definition"
msgid "The necessary-condition formalization candidate governing the class covering that every logic:Object is one of {logic:Collection, logic:Quantity, logic:FunctionalComplex}. It completes the existing individuation-kind pairwise disjointness (logic:candidateFunctionalComplexKindDisjoint) into a full partition. The covering is realized ONLY in the OWL projection as an owl:unionOf; it is NON-monotone and disclosed in the loss ledger — the native monotone StratifiedNAF chase does NOT enforce a disjunctive head, so this is projection-only, not natively enforced. It carries NO harvest back-link. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqObjectIndividuationCoveringHolds) and a negative case (logic:cqObjectIndividuationCoveringGapRejected); logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of logic:Object's skos:definition for drift detection."
msgstr "Le necessary-condition formalisation candidat governing the class covering qui chaque logic:Object est one de {logic:collection, logic:Quantity, logic:FunctionalComplex}."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateOrgMembershipPropagation|rdfs:label"
msgid "membership propagates up the sub-organization hierarchy"
msgstr "membership propagates up the sub-organization hierarchy"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateOrgMembershipPropagation|skos:definition"
msgid "The derivation-rule formalization candidate governing logic:ruleOrgMembershipPropagation: it harvests the upward membership propagation documented in gmeow:memberOf's skos:definition (membership propagates up the organizational part/whole hierarchy via the property chain with gmeow:subOrganizationOf) into an enforced positive-Horn derivation rule, materialized natively as logic:ExactPreservation. The logic: rule is the native-chase form of the same propagation the gmeow:memberOf owl:propertyChainAxiom carries for the OWL 2 RL closure — one inference formalized across two reasoning engines (the harvest pattern), not a divergent second reading. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqOrgMembershipPropagationHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqOrgMembershipPropagationDownwardRejected). Its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:memberOf, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition) ties it to the exact prose, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that definition text so a later edit surfaces as drift."
msgstr "Le dérivation-règle formalisation candidat governing logic:ruleOrgMembershipPropagation: it harvests the upward membership propagation documented dans gmeow:memberOf's skos:définition (membership propagates up the organizational part/whole hierarchy via the propriété chain avec gmeow:subOrganizationOf) dans an enforced positif-Horn dérivation règle, materialized natively as logic:ExactPreservation."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidatePositiveCase|rdfs:label"
msgid "candidate positive case"
msgstr "candidat positif case"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidatePositiveCase|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:FormalizationCandidate to a positive competency case its proposed axiom must satisfy — a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion whose expected answer the axiom should produce (range gmeow:CompetencyQuestion, stated in prose). Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:candidatePositiveCase only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:FormalizationCandidate à a positif competency case its proposé axiom doit satisfy — a gmeow:CompetencyQuestion dont expected answer the axiom should produce (plage gmeow:CompetencyQuestion, stated dans prose)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateProjectionBehavior|rdfs:label"
msgid "candidate projection behavior"
msgstr "candidat projection behavior"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateProjectionBehavior|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:FormalizationCandidate to the logic:PreservationKind its axiom would carry under projection — how faithfully it survives down-projection to OWL/Datalog/SHACL. Reuses the loss-ledger preservation polarity rather than minting a parallel note. Single-valued. Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate, range logic:PreservationKind."
msgstr "Relates a logic:FormalizationCandidate à the logic:PreservationKind its axiom would carry sous projection — how faithfully it survives down-projection à OWL/Datalog/SHACL."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateProperPartOfAsymmetric|rdfs:label"
msgid "properPartOf is asymmetric"
msgstr "properPartOf is asymmetric"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateProperPartOfAsymmetric|skos:definition"
msgid "The worked production formalization candidate that harvests the asymmetry of logic:properPartOf from that term's skos:definition into an enforced strict-order integrity constraint: the keystone demonstration of the prose→axiom harvest mechanism. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqProperPartAsymmetryHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqProperPartAsymmetrySymmetricPairRejected); its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes logic:properPartOf, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition) ties it to the exact prose, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that definition text so a later edit to the prose surfaces as drift."
msgstr "Le worked production formalisation candidat qui harvests the asymmetry de logic:properPartOf de qui terme's skos:définition dans an enforced strict-order intégrité contrainte: the keystone demonstration de the prose→axiom harvest mechanism."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateRelatorMediation|rdfs:label"
msgid "every concrete relator mediates at least two distinct relata"
msgstr "every concret relator mediates at least two distinct relata"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateRelatorMediation|skos:definition"
msgid "The formalization candidate that generalizes the relator-mediation discipline (RelComp) from the hardcoded OntoUML seed relators to every subclass of the logic:Relator category, harvested from logic:Relator's own skos:definition ('A Relator must mediate at least two distinct entities'). The native foundation reasoner confers relator-hood on every class subClassOf logic:Relator and fires logic:violation logic:RelComp on any concrete (leaf) relator that mediates fewer than two distinct relata. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqRelatorMediationHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqRelatorMediationUnderMediatedRejected); its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes logic:Relator, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition) ties it to the exact prose, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that skos:definition text so a later edit surfaces as drift."
msgstr "Le formalisation candidat qui generalizes the relator-mediation discipline (RelComp) de the hardcoded OntoUML seed relators à chaque sous-classe de the logic:Relator catégorie, harvested de logic:Relator's own skos:définition ('Un Relator doit mediate au moins two distinct entities')."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateScope|rdfs:label"
msgid "candidate scope"
msgstr "candidat scope"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateScope|skos:definition"
msgid "The intended scope of a candidate's axiom — the terms, slice, or context it is meant to constrain. Read together with logic:candidateContract (the reasoning semantics it is interpreted under). Single-valued, xsd:string. Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:candidateScope only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le intended scope de a candidat's axiom — the terms, slice, ou contexte it est meant à constrain."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateSemanticRisk|rdfs:label"
msgid "candidate semantic risk"
msgstr "candidat semantic risk"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateSemanticRisk|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:FormalizationCandidate to its logic:SemanticRiskClass — how far a wrong formalization would propagate, which sets how strict the reviewer gate must be. Single-valued. Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate, range logic:SemanticRiskClass. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:candidateSemanticRisk only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:FormalizationCandidate à its logic:SemanticRiskClass — how far a wrong formalisation would propagate, qui sets how strict the reviewer gate doit be."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateSocialInformationOverlap|rdfs:label"
msgid "social and information objects deliberately overlap"
msgstr "social and information objects deliberately overlap"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateSocialInformationOverlap|skos:definition"
msgid "The deliberate-overlap formalization candidate governing the explicit, reviewed NON-assertion of disjointness between gmeow:SocialObject and gmeow:InformationObject: the one overlap the top-sortal partition preserves so that socially-sustained narratives may carry information content without identity clash (a founding myth is both). Its source is gmeow:SocialObject's skos:definition, which states that no disjointness with InformationObject is asserted for exactly this reason. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqSocialInformationOverlapHolds — a myth typed as both stays coherent) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqSocialInformationOverlapDisjointRejected — asserting the disjointness would force the myth to owl:Nothing, which is why the overlap must be preserved). Its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:SocialObject, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition) ties it to the exact prose, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that definition text for drift detection. The risk is advisory: this is a non-assertion, so it contaminates nothing — it records a reviewed decision NOT to constrain."
msgstr "Le deliberate-overlap formalisation candidat governing the explicit, reviewed NON-assertion de disjointness entre gmeow:SocialObject et gmeow:InformationObject: the one overlap the top-sortal partition préserve so qui socially-sustained narratives peut carry information content sans identité clash (a founding myth est both)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateSourceField|rdfs:label"
msgid "candidate source field"
msgstr "candidat source field"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateSourceField|skos:definition"
msgid "Names which annotation field of the logic:candidateFormalizes term a candidate harvested — a logic:ProseField from the closed set (logic:ProseFieldDefinition, logic:ProseFieldUseWhen, logic:ProseFieldAvoidWhen). Together with logic:candidateFormalizes it pins the harvested axiom to the exact source triple. Co-present with logic:candidateFormalizes: a candidate carrying one of the pair without the other is a hard governance error (verify.harvest-link-paired), never a half-link. Single-valued. Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate, range logic:ProseField."
msgstr "Names qui annotation field de the logic:candidateFormalizes terme a candidat harvested — a logic:ProseField de the closed set (logic:ProseFieldDefinition, logic:ProseFieldUseWhen, logic:ProseFieldAvoidWhen)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateSourceHash|rdfs:label"
msgid "candidate source hash"
msgstr "candidat source hash"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateSourceHash|skos:definition"
msgid "The content hash of the source text a logic:FormalizationCandidate was extracted from: the anchor that ties the candidate back to the exact prose it formalizes and detects drift if that prose changes. Single-valued, xsd:string. Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:candidateSourceHash only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le content hash de the source text a logic:FormalizationCandidate was extracted from: the anchor qui ties the candidat back à the exact prose it formalizes et detects drift si qui prose changes."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateTenureClaimSurfacing|rdfs:label"
msgid "a tenure's frame and position surface onto its generated claim"
msgstr "a tenure's frame and position surface onto its generated claim"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateTenureClaimSurfacing|skos:definition"
msgid "The derivation-rule formalization candidate governing logic:ruleTenureClaimVantage and logic:ruleTenureClaimObservedFeature: it harvests the tenure→claim mapping documented in gmeow:StandpointTenure's skos:definition (the tenureStandpoint maps to the claim's vantage; the tenurePosition maps to the claim's observedFeature) into two enforced positive-Horn derivation rules, materialized natively as logic:ExactPreservation. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqTenureClaimSurfacingHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqTenureClaimSurfacingSwapRejected). Its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:StandpointTenure, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldDefinition) ties it to the exact prose, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that definition text so a later edit surfaces as drift."
msgstr "Le dérivation-règle formalisation candidat governing logic:ruleTenureClaimVantage et logic:ruleTenureClaimObservedFeature: it harvests the tenure→claim mapping documented dans gmeow:StandpointTenure's skos:définition (the tenureStandpoint maps à the claim's vantage; the tenurePosition maps à the claim's observedFeature) dans two enforced positif-Horn dérivation rules, materialized natively as logic:ExactPreservation."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateTopSortalDisjoint|rdfs:label"
msgid "top sortals are pairwise disjoint"
msgstr "top sortals are pairwise disjoint"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/candidateTopSortalDisjoint|skos:definition"
msgid "The formalization candidate that harvests the pairwise disjointness of the four kernel top sortals from gmeow:PhysicalObject's gmeow:avoidWhen prose (which states the three others are disjoint with PhysicalObject by design) into the enforced owl:disjointWith integrity constraints asserted in the kernel: gmeow:Agent, gmeow:PhysicalObject, gmeow:InformationObject and gmeow:SocialObject are pairwise disjoint EXCEPT the deliberately-preserved SocialObject∩InformationObject overlap. The gmeow:Agent ⊥ gmeow:SocialObject edge is net-new on this branch. Accepted through review (logic:reviewedBy logic:reviewerLogicFoundation) with a positive case (logic:cqTopSortalDisjointHolds) and a negative countermodel (logic:cqTopSortalDisjointClashRejected); its harvest back-link (logic:candidateFormalizes gmeow:PhysicalObject, logic:candidateSourceField logic:ProseFieldAvoidWhen) ties it to the exact prose, and logic:candidateSourceHash is the sha256 of that gmeow:avoidWhen text so a later edit surfaces as drift. The native DL coherence gate reads the owl:disjointWith directly, forcing a two-sortal individual to owl:Nothing."
msgstr "Le formalisation candidat qui harvests the pairwise disjointness de the quatre kernel top sortals de gmeow:PhysicalObject's gmeow:avoidWhen prose (which states the three others sont disjoint avec PhysicalObject par design) dans the enforced owl:disjointWith intégrité constraints asserted dans the kernel: gmeow:Agent, gmeow:PhysicalObject, gmeow:InformationObject et gmeow:SocialObject sont pairwise disjoint EXCEPT the deliberately-preserved SocialObject∩InformationObject overlap."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/capability|rdfs:label"
msgid "capability"
msgstr "capability"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/capability|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ActionSchema to what an agent must be able to do to execute it — the executional precondition on the actor rather than on the state. Domain logic:ActionSchema (stated in prose). One of the eight action-theory facets, distinct from logic:precondition (a precondition on the situation, not the agent)."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ActionSchema à what an agent doit be able à do à execute it — the executional précondition sur the actor plutôt que sur the état."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/capabilityAvailable|rdfs:label"
msgid "capability available"
msgstr "capability available"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/capabilityAvailable|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a state to a capability the actor holds at it — the executional capability the gate matches an action schema's logic:capability against. Domain a state, range the available capability (stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:capabilityAvailable only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a état à a capability the actor holds at it — the executional capability the gate matches an action schéma's logic:capability against."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/carriesTerminationCertificate|rdfs:label"
msgid "carries termination certificate"
msgstr "carries terminaison certificat"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/carriesTerminationCertificate|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ChaseAcceptanceWitness to the weak-acyclicity termination-certificate evidence (xsd:string, the ChaseAdmission::WeaklyAcyclic evidence summary) that admits its chase. Domain logic:ChaseAcceptanceWitness (stated in prose). A chase acceptance record with no certificate reports a closure that may never terminate."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ChaseAcceptanceWitness à the weak-acyclicity terminaison-certificat preuve (xsd:string, the ChaseAdmission::WeaklyAcyclic preuve summary) qui admits its chase."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/causalLinkDistinctness|rdfs:label"
msgid "a causal link's antecedent and consequent are distinct"
msgstr "a causal link's antecedent and consequent are distinct"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/causalLinkDistinctness|skos:definition"
msgid "Asserts that a gmeow:CausalLink's gmeow:linkAntecedent and gmeow:linkConsequent must be distinct: nothing type-causes itself. The native coherence gate raises a violation when they coincide."
msgstr "Asserts qui a gmeow:CausalLink's gmeow:linkAntecedent et gmeow:linkConsequent doit be distinct: nothing type-causes itself."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/causalPartOf|rdfs:label"
msgid "causal part of"
msgstr "causal part of"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/causalPartOf|skos:definition"
msgid "Causal parthood among perdurants: relates a sub-occurrent that causally contributes to a larger occurrent — the ignition is a causal part of the launch, the infection a causal part of the illness. A specialization of logic:temporalPartOf (stated in prose, not as an rdfs:subPropertyOf edge, matching how the foundation parthood relations are authored): every causal part is also a temporal part of the same whole, but NOT conversely — a merely temporally-nested sub-occurrent need carry no causal contribution (causal subset-of temporal, the YAMATO/Galton occurrent-mereology refinement). Transitive (a causal part of a causal part causally contributes to the whole) but deliberately NOT asymmetric or irreflexive, since causal feedback loops are legal among occurrents — contrast logic:properPartOf, the strict-order endurant parthood. Distinct from the temporal-only nesting carried at the domain level by gmeow:subEventOf."
msgstr "Causal parthood parmi perdurants: relie a sub-occurrent qui causally contributes à a larger occurrent — the ignition est a causal part de the launch, the infection a causal part de the illness."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/certifiedFragment|rdfs:label"
msgid "certified fragment"
msgstr "certified fragment"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/certifiedFragment|skos:definition"
msgid "The certified-complete fragment reference backing a logic:CompleteForFragment claim on a logic:ReasoningResult. Single-valued. Domain logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:certifiedFragment only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le certified-complet fragment reference backing a logic:CompleteForFragment claim sur a logic:ReasoningResult."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/characteristicSort|rdfs:label"
msgid "characteristic sort"
msgstr "characteristic sort"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/characteristicSort|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion to the characteristic-sort marker it asserts — one of logic:transitiveProperty, logic:symmetricProperty, logic:irreflexiveProperty, logic:asymmetricProperty or logic:functionalProperty. Co-present with logic:characterizes: a characteristic assertion carrying one without the other names no enforceable characteristic. Domain logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion; single-valued. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:characteristicSort only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion à the characteristic-sort marker it asserts — one de logic:transitiveProperty, logic:symmetricProperty, logic:irreflexiveProperty, logic:asymmetricProperty ou logic:functionalProperty."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/characterizes|rdfs:label"
msgid "characterizes"
msgstr "characterizes"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/characterizes|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion to the property it characterises (a gmeow: or logic: property, stated in prose). Read together with logic:characteristicSort, it tells the native coherence gate which property bears which characteristic. Domain logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion; single-valued. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:characterizes only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:PropertyCharacteristicAssertion à the propriété it characterises (a gmeow: ou logic: propriété, stated dans prose)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/checkIssuedAt|rdfs:label"
msgid "check issued at"
msgstr "vérification issued at"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/checkIssuedAt|skos:definition"
msgid "The xsd:dateTime a coherence outcome was issued. INJECTED, never sampled in the deterministic fold core, so re-running with the same inputs and timestamp is byte-identical. Single-valued. Domain logic:CoherenceCertificate or logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation (stated in prose)."
msgstr "Le xsd:dateTime a cohérence résultat was issued."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/choiceMode|rdfs:label"
msgid "choice mode"
msgstr "choice mode"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/choiceMode|skos:definition"
msgid "The cardinality mode of a logic:ChoiceGroupConstraint: 'exactly-one', 'at-most-one', or 'exactly-one-of-N' (an alias of 'exactly-one'). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:choiceMode only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le cardinality mode de a logic:ChoiceGroupConstraint: 'exactly-one', 'at-most-one', ou 'exactly-one-of-N' (an alias de 'exactly-one')."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/choicePredicate|rdfs:label"
msgid "choice predicate"
msgstr "choice prédicat"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/choicePredicate|skos:definition"
msgid "A member predicate of a logic:ChoiceGroupConstraint's choice group. Multi-valued (at least two); the ∃-requiredness of each is combined per logic:choiceMode. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:choicePredicate only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Un member prédicat de a logic:ChoiceGroupConstraint's choice group."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/closedUnder|rdfs:label"
msgid "closed under"
msgstr "closed under"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/closedUnder|skos:definition"
msgid "Declares a predicate or shape closed within a logic:WorldBoundary: the closed-world-assumption toggle that says, for the named predicate inside the boundary, that the materialized extension is complete and absence may be read as falsity. The per-predicate CWA switch of the hybrid open/closed construct, enforced by the built-in SHACL (the CWA lane); outside any boundary, or for predicates not closed under one, the open-world reading holds. Enforcement is seamed to the engine."
msgstr "Declares a prédicat ou forme closed within a logic:WorldBoundary: the monde fermé-assumption toggle qui says, pour the named prédicat inside the boundary, qui the materialized extension est complet et absence peut be read as falsity."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/closureEntailedAtom|rdfs:label"
msgid "closure entailed atom"
msgstr "fermeture entailed atom"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/closureEntailedAtom|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ClosureAcceptanceWitness to a serialized atom (xsd:string, e.g. `A subClassOf C`) that the EL→RL→DL closure entails but the asserted EDB does not contain. Domain logic:ClosureAcceptanceWitness (stated in prose). At least one is required: a closure witness that entails nothing beyond its input demonstrates no reasoning."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ClosureAcceptanceWitness à a serialized atom (xsd:string, e.g."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/closureEntry|rdfs:label"
msgid "closure entry"
msgstr "fermeture entrée"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/closureEntry|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to a logic:ClosureEntry — a per-key override of the closure map binding a predicate or context key to an open- or closed-world value. The closure facet is a map, not a global flag: logic:defaultClosure gives the default for unlisted keys, while each logic:closureEntry overrides one key. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:ClosureEntry (stated in prose, matching the module's convention)."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract à a logic:ClosureEntry — a per-key override de the fermeture map liaison a prédicat ou contexte key à an ouvert- ou monde fermé valeur."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/closureKey|rdfs:label"
msgid "closure key"
msgstr "fermeture key"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/closureKey|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ClosureEntry to the predicate-or-context key it scopes: the string key whose closure value the entry fixes. Domain logic:ClosureEntry (stated in prose, matching the module's convention); range xsd:string. The key together with logic:closureValue forms one binding of the closure map. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:closureKey only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ClosureEntry à the prédicat-or-contexte key it scopes: the string key dont fermeture valeur the entrée fixes."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/closureValue|rdfs:label"
msgid "closure value"
msgstr "fermeture valeur"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/closureValue|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ClosureEntry to the logic:ClosureValue (open- or closed-world) it assigns to its key. Domain logic:ClosureEntry, range logic:ClosureValue (stated in prose, matching the module's convention). Together with logic:closureKey it forms one binding of the closure map. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:closureValue only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ClosureEntry à the logic:ClosureValue (ouvert- ou monde fermé) it assigns à its key."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/coarserThanTransitivity|rdfs:label"
msgid "coarserThan is transitive"
msgstr "coarserThan is transitive"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/coarserThanTransitivity|skos:definition"
msgid "Asserts on the canonical carrier that gmeow:coarserThan is transitive: the partial order on granularity levels its skos:definition names, which makes 'at or above a target level' well-defined. The native coherence gate reads this to close the granularity order."
msgstr "Asserts sur the canonique carrier qui gmeow:coarserThan est transitive: the partial order sur granularity levels its skos:définition names, qui makes 'at ou above a target niveau' well-defined."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/columnBinding|rdfs:label"
msgid "column binding"
msgstr "colonne liaison"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/columnBinding|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ResultColumn to the logic:ColumnBinding it declares — whether the variable is bound in every row. Single-valued. Domain logic:ResultColumn, range logic:ColumnBinding (stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:columnBinding only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ResultColumn à the logic:ColumnBinding it déclare — whether the variable est bound dans chaque row."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/columnDatatype|rdfs:label"
msgid "column datatype"
msgstr "colonne datatype"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/columnDatatype|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a literal logic:ResultColumn to the datatype IRI it pins. Single-valued and OPTIONAL: a literal column with no logic:columnDatatype accepts any literal (a declared loosening, not a half-typed column); a non-literal column carries none. Domain logic:ResultColumn, range a datatype IRI (stated in prose)."
msgstr "Relates a literal logic:ResultColumn à the datatype IRI it pins."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/columnTermKind|rdfs:label"
msgid "column term kind"
msgstr "colonne terme kind"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/columnTermKind|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ResultColumn to the logic:TermKind it requires — the mandatory RDF term kind of the column's values. Single-valued. Domain logic:ResultColumn, range logic:TermKind (stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:columnTermKind only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ResultColumn à the logic:TermKind it exige — the mandatory RDF terme kind de the colonne's values."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/columnVariable|rdfs:label"
msgid "column variable"
msgstr "colonne variable"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/columnVariable|skos:definition"
msgid "The bare SPARQL variable name (no leading '?') a logic:ResultColumn types. Single-valued, xsd:string. Domain logic:ResultColumn (stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:columnVariable only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le bare SPARQL variable name (no leading '?') a logic:ResultColumn types."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/commitmentBeneficiaryDistinctness|rdfs:label"
msgid "a commitment's beneficiary is distinct from its committed agent"
msgstr "a engagement's beneficiary is distinct from its committed agent"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/commitmentBeneficiaryDistinctness|skos:definition"
msgid "Asserts that a gmeow:Commitment's gmeow:committedAgent and gmeow:commitmentBeneficiary must be distinct: a resolution made purely to oneself is an Intention, not a Commitment. The native coherence gate raises a violation when they coincide."
msgstr "Asserts qui a gmeow:engagement's gmeow:committedAgent et gmeow:commitmentBeneficiary doit be distinct: a resolution made purely à oneself est an Intention, not a engagement."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/compensation|rdfs:label"
msgid "compensation"
msgstr "compensation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/compensation|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ActionSchema to the action that undoes this one — the basis for recoverable transactions. Tied to the realized outcome, not the schema as a whole: when the outcome set is nondeterministic each branch names the compensation that recovers from IT, so recovery matches what actually happened rather than applying one generic undo across every branch. Domain logic:ActionSchema (stated in prose). One of the eight action-theory facets."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ActionSchema à the action qui undoes this one — the basis pour recoverable transactions."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/competesForResource|rdfs:label"
msgid "competes for resource"
msgstr "competes for ressource"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/competesForResource|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates two gmeow:Goals that both draw on a resource an action schema declares (logic:actionResource), where the supply is insufficient for both. Domain gmeow:Goal, range gmeow:Goal (stated in prose). The seam between goal conflict and the action-theory resource facet. One of seven conflict relations between independently-meaningful goals, weaker than gmeow:counterGoal (constitutive opposition). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:competesForResource only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates two gmeow:Goals qui both draw sur a ressource an action schéma déclare (logic:actionResource), où the supply est insufficient pour both."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/competesWithIrreflexivity|rdfs:label"
msgid "competesWith is irreflexive"
msgstr "competesWith is irreflexive"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/competesWithIrreflexivity|skos:definition"
msgid "Asserts on the canonical carrier that gmeow:competesWith is irreflexive: a rival standpoint claim never competes with itself, as its skos:definition states. gmeow:competesWith is symmetric (owl:SymmetricProperty) but irreflexive; irreflexivity is enforced here on the canonical carrier — kept out of OWL to hold the reasoned profile within OWL 2 DL (the deception discipline) — and the native coherence gate raises a violation for a claim asserted to compete with itself; the generated SHACL constraint surface is its projection."
msgstr "Asserts sur the canonique carrier qui gmeow:competesWith est irreflexive: a rival point de vue claim jamais competes avec itself, as its skos:définition states."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/complexityClass|rdfs:label"
msgid "complexity class"
msgstr "complexity class"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/complexityClass|skos:definition"
msgid "The complexity / decidability class a projection or profile certifies — EL → PTIME, DL → decidable/N2EXPTIME, Datalog → terminating/PTIME-data — recorded alongside the preservation polarity in the loss ledger. Decidability is a projection guarantee bought by projecting down, not a canonical-layer promise: the canonical layer is maximally expressive and only semi-decidable."
msgstr "Le complexity / decidability class a projection ou profil certifies — EL → PTIME, DL → decidable/N2EXPTIME, Datalog → terminating/PTIME-données — recorded alongside the preservation polarity dans the loss ledger."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/compositionExclusionPart|rdfs:label"
msgid "composition exclusion part role"
msgstr "composition exclusion part role"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/compositionExclusionPart|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:RoleCompositionExclusionAssertion to the role whose bound value must not be a component of the whole role's value. Domain logic:RoleCompositionExclusionAssertion; single-valued."
msgstr "Relates a logic:RoleCompositionExclusionAssertion à the role dont bound valeur ne doit pas be a component de the whole role's valeur."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/compositionExclusionTarget|rdfs:label"
msgid "composition exclusion target"
msgstr "composition exclusion target"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/compositionExclusionTarget|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:RoleCompositionExclusionAssertion to the class whose focus nodes it constrains. Domain logic:RoleCompositionExclusionAssertion; single-valued. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:compositionExclusionTarget only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:RoleCompositionExclusionAssertion à the class dont focus nodes it constrains."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/compositionExclusionVia|rdfs:label"
msgid "composition exclusion via"
msgstr "composition exclusion via"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/compositionExclusionVia|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:RoleCompositionExclusionAssertion to a composition property linking the whole role's value to a component. Each asserted value is one step the exclusion ranges over; the native coherence gate raises a violation when the part role coincides with a component reached through any of them. Domain logic:RoleCompositionExclusionAssertion; multi-valued. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:compositionExclusionVia only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:RoleCompositionExclusionAssertion à a composition propriété linking the whole role's valeur à a component."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/compositionExclusionWhole|rdfs:label"
msgid "composition exclusion whole role"
msgstr "composition exclusion whole role"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/compositionExclusionWhole|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:RoleCompositionExclusionAssertion to the role binding the WHOLE whose components the part role must not coincide with. Domain logic:RoleCompositionExclusionAssertion; single-valued."
msgstr "Relates a logic:RoleCompositionExclusionAssertion à the role liaison the WHOLE dont components the part role ne doit pas coincide with."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conclusion|rdfs:label"
msgid "conclusion"
msgstr "conclusion"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conclusion|skos:definition"
msgid "The canonical conclusion text a logic:ReasoningResult's verdict is about — part of the proof certificate. Single-valued. Domain logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:conclusion only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le canonique conclusion text a logic:ReasoningResult's verdict est about — part de the preuve certificat."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/concurrentComposedFrom|rdfs:label"
msgid "concurrent composed from"
msgstr "concurrent composed from"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/concurrentComposedFrom|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a DERIVED logic:ConcurrentHistory to each of the two transaction-program operands (the logic:leftOperand and logic:rightOperand of the logic:ConcurrentComposition) whose interleaved elementary steps produced its conflict edges. Domain logic:ConcurrentHistory, range a transaction-program node (stated in prose); multi-valued (one link per operand). It is the audit trail from the history back to the authored sub-programs that gave rise to it, kept distinct from logic:precedes (an edge BETWEEN the transactions within the history) — this link points OUT to the programs, not between operations."
msgstr "Relates a dérivé logic:ConcurrentHistory à each de the two transaction-program operands (the logic:leftOperand et logic:rightOperand de the logic:ConcurrentComposition) dont interleaved elementary steps produced its conflit edges."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conditionalRangeRequiredType|rdfs:label"
msgid "conditional range required type"
msgstr "conditionnel plage obligatoire type"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conditionalRangeRequiredType|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ConditionalRangeAssertion to the class the constrained value must instantiate when the selector matches. Domain logic:ConditionalRangeAssertion; single-valued. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:conditionalRangeRequiredType only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ConditionalRangeAssertion à the class the constrained valeur doit instantiate lorsque the selector matches."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conditionalRangeSelector|rdfs:label"
msgid "conditional range selector"
msgstr "conditionnel plage selector"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conditionalRangeSelector|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ConditionalRangeAssertion to the discriminant property whose value triggers the condition. Read together with logic:conditionalRangeSelectorValue. Domain logic:ConditionalRangeAssertion; single-valued. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:conditionalRangeSelector only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ConditionalRangeAssertion à the discriminant propriété dont valeur triggers the condition."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conditionalRangeSelectorValue|rdfs:label"
msgid "conditional range selector value"
msgstr "conditionnel plage selector valeur"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conditionalRangeSelectorValue|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ConditionalRangeAssertion to the named value of the discriminant property that triggers the required-type condition. Domain logic:ConditionalRangeAssertion; single-valued. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:conditionalRangeSelectorValue only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ConditionalRangeAssertion à the named valeur de the discriminant propriété qui triggers the obligatoire-type condition."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conditionalRangeTarget|rdfs:label"
msgid "conditional range target"
msgstr "conditionnel plage target"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conditionalRangeTarget|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ConditionalRangeAssertion to the class whose focus nodes it constrains. Domain logic:ConditionalRangeAssertion; single-valued. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:conditionalRangeTarget only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ConditionalRangeAssertion à the class dont focus nodes it constrains."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conditionalRangeValue|rdfs:label"
msgid "conditional range value"
msgstr "conditionnel plage valeur"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conditionalRangeValue|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ConditionalRangeAssertion to the property whose bound value must satisfy the required type when the selector matches. Domain logic:ConditionalRangeAssertion; single-valued. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:conditionalRangeValue only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ConditionalRangeAssertion à the propriété dont bound valeur doit satisfy the obligatoire type lorsque the selector matches."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/confidence|rdfs:label"
msgid "confidence"
msgstr "confidence"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/confidence|skos:definition"
msgid "Epistemic confidence assigned to a statement by a source or process — how sure the asserter is. Normatively distinct from logic:probability: a confidence score is NOT a probability and MUST NOT be interpreted as one unless an explicit mapping to logic:probability is declared. Also distinct from logic:weight (a solver ranking) and logic:evidenceStrength (evidential warrant)."
msgstr "épistémique confidence assigned à a statement par a source ou process — how sure the asserter is."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conjectureDischargeVerdict|rdfs:label"
msgid "conjecture discharge verdict"
msgstr "conjecture acquittement verdict"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conjectureDischargeVerdict|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Conjecture to the logic:DischargeVerdict carrying its CONCLUSIVENESS — reusing the existing three-value obligation class rather than minting a parallel notion. logic:ObligationDischarged marks a conclusive result (a corroboration or a refutation within a complete fragment, or a conclusive independence for an open conjecture); logic:ObligationUnknown marks a budget-exhausted or fragment-gap run that is carried forward, never 'proved'. An open conjecture carrying logic:ObligationUnknown that is NOT in logic:ConjectureOpen is a hard error (verify.conjecture-open-if-inconclusive): a timeout may never read as refuted. Single-valued. Domain logic:Conjecture, range logic:DischargeVerdict."
msgstr "Relates a logic:conjecture à the logic:DischargeVerdict carrying its CONCLUSIVENESS — reusing the existing three-valeur obligation class plutôt que minting a parallel notion."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conjectureEntails|rdfs:label"
msgid "conjecture entails"
msgstr "conjecture entails"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conjectureEntails|skos:definition"
msgid "The corpus entailment pre-order over conjectures: logic:conjectureEntails relates a formula phi to a formula psi it entails (phi models psi), so a refutation of psi propagates contrapositively to phi (if psi is refuted, phi cannot stand). The relation is a PRE-ORDER in intent (reflexive and transitive), but its full transitive closure is NOT materialized as a stored relation: the vocabulary carries each pairwise edge and the propagation competency query (conjecture-entails-propagation.rq) reasons over those edges directly, so contrapositive propagation is queryable without the corpus-wide closure being computed as a persisted extension. Each edge is itself a conjecture test (that phi genuinely entails psi), not a bare assertion. Domain logic:Conjecture, range logic:Conjecture."
msgstr "Le corpus implication pre-order sur conjectures: logic:conjectureEntails relie a formule phi à a formule psi it entails (phi models psi), so a réfutation de psi propagates contrapositively à phi (si psi est refuted, phi ne peut pas stand)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conjectureFormula|rdfs:label"
msgid "conjecture formula"
msgstr "conjecture formule"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conjectureFormula|skos:definition"
msgid "The canonical, alpha-normalized identity of the conjectured formula: the content_key string of the full first-order AST (the alpha-normalized content identity from the full-FOL formula AST), so two conjectures that name the same formula up to bound-variable renaming share one key and cannot be double-counted. Single-valued, xsd:string. Domain logic:Conjecture."
msgstr "Le canonique, alpha-normalized identité de the conjectured formule: the content_key string de the full premier ordre AST (the alpha-normalized content identité de the full-FOL formule AST), so two conjectures qui name the same formule up à bound-variable renaming share one key et ne peut pas be double-counted."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conjectureLifecycleState|rdfs:label"
msgid "conjecture lifecycle state"
msgstr "conjecture cycle de vie état"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conjectureLifecycleState|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Conjecture to its current EPISTEMIC logic:ConjectureLifecycleState (open / corroborated / refuted-in-standpoint / withdrawn). Single-valued and REQUIRED. Orthogonal to logic:candidateLifecycle (the GOVERNANCE state inherited from the candidate spine): a conjecture may be governance-accepted yet epistemically open, so the two are never collapsed (Principle 9). Domain logic:Conjecture, range logic:ConjectureLifecycleState."
msgstr "Relates a logic:conjecture à its current épistémique logic:ConjectureLifecycleState (ouvert / corroborated / refuted-in-point de vue / retiré)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conjecturePromotionCandidate|rdfs:label"
msgid "conjecture promotion candidate"
msgstr "conjecture promotion candidat"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conjecturePromotionCandidate|skos:definition"
msgid "The POSITIVE promotion leg: relates a logic:ConjectureCorroborated conjecture to the logic:FormalizationCandidate proposing to promote its formula to a canonical axiom. The candidate still runs the ordinary reviewer gate (corroboration is provisional support, never proof), so a corroborated conjecture never becomes a canonical axiom by mere entailment. Present exactly when the conjecture is corroborated. Domain logic:Conjecture, range logic:FormalizationCandidate."
msgstr "Le positif promotion leg: relie a logic:ConjectureCorroborated conjecture à the logic:FormalizationCandidate proposing à promote its formule à a canonique axiom."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conjectureRefinedFrom|rdfs:label"
msgid "conjecture refined from"
msgstr "conjecture refined from"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conjectureRefinedFrom|skos:definition"
msgid "The Lakatos refinement edge: relates a successor conjecture to the refuted conjecture it weakens — the 'monster-barring' move where a refuted conjecture is not abandoned but replaced by a strictly weaker successor that excludes the counterexample. Read together with logic:survivesCounterexample (the witness the successor now excludes). Domain logic:Conjecture, range logic:Conjecture."
msgstr "Le Lakatos refinement edge: relie a successor conjecture à the refuted conjecture it weakens — the 'monster-barring' move où a refuted conjecture n'est pas abandoned mais replaced par a strictly weaker successor qui excludes the contre-exemple."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conjectureRefutationWitness|rdfs:label"
msgid "conjecture refutation witness"
msgstr "conjecture réfutation témoin"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conjectureRefutationWitness|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a refuted logic:Conjecture to the logic:ContradictionWitness that refutes it — the concrete counterexample naming the individual forced to owl:Nothing, the world, and the premises. Present exactly when the conjecture is logic:ConjectureRefutedInStandpoint (a refuted conjecture with no witness is a hard error, logic:ConjectureShape and verify.conjecture-refutation-witness-required; a witness on a non-refuted conjecture is meaningless). Domain logic:Conjecture, range logic:ContradictionWitness. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:conjectureRefutationWitness only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a refuted logic:conjecture à the logic:ContradictionWitness qui refutes it — the concret contre-exemple naming the individu forced à owl:Nothing, the monde, et the premises."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conjectureStandpoint|rdfs:label"
msgid "conjecture standpoint"
msgstr "conjecture point de vue"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conjectureStandpoint|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Conjecture to the reified standpoint its verdict is scoped to — a REQUIRED, single-valued IRI (a gmeow:Standpoint, stated in prose). Standpoint scoping here is REIFICATION, never a named graph: the verdict is 'the formula is refuted FROM THIS standpoint', never a global-false claim (Principle 9). A conjecture with no standpoint has an ill-scoped verdict and is a hard governance error (verify.conjecture-standpoint-scoped). Single-valued. Domain logic:Conjecture."
msgstr "Relates a logic:conjecture à the reified point de vue its verdict est scoped à — a obligatoire, à valeur unique IRI (a gmeow:point de vue, stated dans prose)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conjectureVerdict|rdfs:label"
msgid "conjecture verdict"
msgstr "conjecture verdict"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/conjectureVerdict|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Conjecture to the content-addressed reasoning-result node its verdict was read from — a logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose) produced by the scoped reasoning run over the standpoint. Where logic:conjectureLifecycleState and logic:conjectureDischargeVerdict carry the projected epistemic verdict and conclusiveness, this links back to the full result graph the projection was computed from, so the verdict is auditable against its source run. Single-valued. Domain logic:Conjecture. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:conjectureVerdict only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:conjecture à the content-addressed raisonnement-résultat nœud its verdict was read de — a logic:ReasoningResult (stated dans prose) produced par the scoped raisonnement run sur the point de vue."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/consequent|rdfs:label"
msgid "consequent"
msgstr "consequent"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/consequent|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a material-implication logic:Formula to its consequent (the conclusion). Paired with logic:antecedent; their presence marks the node as an implication, distinct from the commutative logic:iff."
msgstr "Relates a material-implication logic:formule à its consequent (the conclusion)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/constraintOverride|rdfs:label"
msgid "constraint override"
msgstr "contrainte override"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/constraintOverride|skos:definition"
msgid "The override role of a logic:DownwardConstraint: the declared exception token whose presence on the constrained target defeats the constraint. When the target bears this token (logic:bearsProperty), the constraint receives logic:ConstraintOverridden rather than logic:ConstraintBinding — a structured, declared escape hatch, not an ad-hoc one. An override quiets a governing limit; it never unmakes the part (constraint, not causation). One of the role properties that reify the downward-constraint relation onto the arity-bounded reasoning surface (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Le override role de a logic:DownwardConstraint: the declared exception token dont presence sur the constrained target defeats the contrainte."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/constraintRegime|rdfs:label"
msgid "constraint regime"
msgstr "contrainte regime"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/constraintRegime|skos:definition"
msgid "The regime role of a logic:DownwardConstraint: the logic:GovernanceRegime the constraint is relative to. Governance is never absolute — the verdict (logic:ConstraintBinding / logic:ConstraintOverridden / logic:ConstraintUnknown) is read only against this declared regime's logic:activationBasis, and recording it is what lets a different regime quiet a binding without contradiction. A constraint that omits this role, or whose constrained state is not in the regime's basis, cannot be shown to bind and receives logic:ConstraintUnknown. One of the role properties (with logic:constraintWhole, logic:constraintTarget, logic:constraintState, and logic:constraintOverride) that reify the downward-constraint relation, mirroring logic:assessmentReductionTheory (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Le regime role de a logic:DownwardConstraint: the logic:GovernanceRegime the contrainte est relative to."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/constraintState|rdfs:label"
msgid "constraint state"
msgstr "contrainte état"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/constraintState|skos:definition"
msgid "The constrained-state role of a logic:DownwardConstraint: the permissible role or state the governing whole limits on the target part — what the part may be or do within the whole. This is typically the part's functional role or gmeow:Goal set in the context of its super-whole: a part's teleological role is fixed relative to the holon it serves, which is exactly the downward face of holonic governance (cf. gmeow:Goal in the teleology slice, linked via rdfs:seeAlso). A constraint binds this state only when the declared logic:GovernanceRegime activates it (logic:activationBasis). One of the role properties that reify the downward-constraint relation onto the arity-bounded reasoning surface (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:constraintState only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le constrained-état role de a logic:DownwardConstraint: the permissible role ou état the governing whole limits sur the target part — what the part peut be ou do within the whole."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/constraintTarget|rdfs:label"
msgid "constraint target"
msgstr "contrainte target"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/constraintTarget|skos:definition"
msgid "The target role of a logic:DownwardConstraint: the proper part the governing whole constrains — the part whose permissible state is limited. The verdict is derived only for this explicitly named target; because the constraint names its target rather than cascading down logic:properPartOf, governance is NON-TRANSITIVE by default (ME9) — a constraint onto a part says nothing automatic about the part's own sub-parts. One of the role properties (with logic:constraintWhole) that reify the downward-constraint relation, mirroring logic:assessmentWhole (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Le target role de a logic:DownwardConstraint: the proper part the governing whole constrains — the part dont permissible état est limited."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/constraintVerdict|rdfs:label"
msgid "constraint verdict"
msgstr "contrainte verdict"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/constraintVerdict|skos:definition"
msgid "The engine-derived outcome of a logic:DownwardConstraint: the tri-valued logic:ConstraintVerdict (logic:ConstraintBinding, logic:ConstraintOverridden, or logic:ConstraintUnknown) the reasoner computes for the constraint from its role properties, the holarchy, and the declared logic:GovernanceRegime. Never asserted by hand — it is what the stratified downward-constraint rules conclude — mirroring logic:assessmentVerdict for emergence (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Le engine-dérivé résultat de a logic:DownwardConstraint: the tri-valued logic:ConstraintVerdict (logic:ConstraintBinding, logic:ConstraintOverridden, ou logic:ConstraintUnknown) the raisonneur computes pour the contrainte de its role properties, the holarchy, et the declared logic:GovernanceRegime."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/constraintWhole|rdfs:label"
msgid "constraint whole"
msgstr "contrainte whole"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/constraintWhole|skos:definition"
msgid "The governing-whole role of a logic:DownwardConstraint: the enclosing holon that imposes the constraint — the whole over the proper part named by logic:constraintTarget. The whole bounds the part's permissible state but does not produce it (constraint, not causation). One of the role properties (with logic:constraintTarget, logic:constraintState, logic:constraintRegime, and logic:constraintOverride) that reify the downward-constraint relation, mirroring logic:assessmentWhole and the logic:HolonicPosition role properties (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Le governing-whole role de a logic:DownwardConstraint: the enclosing holon qui imposes the contrainte — the whole sur the proper part named par logic:constraintTarget."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/consumedBudget|rdfs:label"
msgid "consumed budget"
msgstr "consumed budget"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/consumedBudget|skos:definition"
msgid "The resource budget a logic:ReasoningResult consumed, against the contract's declared allowance. Single-valued. Domain logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:consumedBudget only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le ressource budget a logic:ReasoningResult consumed, contre the contract's declared allowance."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/contextAxis|rdfs:label"
msgid "context axis"
msgstr "contexte axis"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/contextAxis|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to a logic:ContextAxis its results are indexed by. The context facet is multi-dimensional, so a contract may carry several logic:contextAxis values (world, standpoint, time, path) that coexist on one result rather than being alternative values of one slot. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:ContextAxis (stated in prose, matching the module's convention)."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract à a logic:ContextAxis its results sont indexed by."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/contractHash|rdfs:label"
msgid "contract hash"
msgstr "contract hash"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/contractHash|skos:definition"
msgid "The content-addressed identity of the reasoning contract a logic:ReasoningResult was produced under. Single-valued. Domain logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:contractHash only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le content-addressed identité de the contrat de raisonnement a logic:ReasoningResult was produced under."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/contradictionPolicy|rdfs:label"
msgid "contradiction policy"
msgstr "contradiction politique"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/contradictionPolicy|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a coherence outcome to the logic:AdmissibleValuationPolicy that decides, for the governing contract, whether a within-world glut is a forbidden violation (logic:ForbidGlut, logic:ForbidGapAndGlut) or a permitted disclosed conflict (logic:AdmitAllFour, logic:ForbidGap). The pivot that classifies each contradiction witness. Single-valued. Domain logic:CoherenceCertificate or logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation, range logic:AdmissibleValuationPolicy (stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:contradictionPolicy only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a cohérence résultat à the logic:AdmissibleValuationPolicy qui decides, pour the governing contract, whether a within-monde glut est a forbidden violation (logic:ForbidGlut, logic:ForbidGapAndGlut) ou a permitted disclosed conflit (logic:AdmitAllFour, logic:ForbidGap)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/contradictionWitness|rdfs:label"
msgid "contradiction witness"
msgstr "contradiction témoin"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/contradictionWitness|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningResult to a within-world contradiction witness justifying a logic:InfoBoth verdict — MULTI-valued. The witness is local to its world; the base store is never globalized to owl:Nothing. Domain logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose)."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ReasoningResult à a within-monde contradiction témoin justifying a logic:InfoBoth verdict — MULTI-valued."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/contradictoryGoal|rdfs:label"
msgid "contradictory goal"
msgstr "contradictory objectif"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/contradictoryGoal|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates two gmeow:Goals in contradictory conflict: satisfying one entails violating the other in EVERY world. Domain gmeow:Goal, range gmeow:Goal (stated in prose). One of seven conflict relations between independently-meaningful goals, each WEAKER than gmeow:counterGoal — the strongest, constitutive opposition that partly defines what a goal means. A witnessed conflict is surfaced as a context-indexed finding, never silently resolved."
msgstr "Relates two gmeow:Goals dans contradictory conflit: satisfying one entails violating the other dans EVERY monde."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/contraryGoal|rdfs:label"
msgid "contrary goal"
msgstr "contrary objectif"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/contraryGoal|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates two gmeow:Goals in contrary conflict: the two cannot both be satisfied, though both may fail. Domain gmeow:Goal, range gmeow:Goal (stated in prose). One of seven conflict relations between independently-meaningful goals, weaker than gmeow:counterGoal (constitutive opposition) and than logic:contradictoryGoal (which also forces one to be violated when the other is satisfied)."
msgstr "Relates two gmeow:Goals dans contrary conflit: the two ne peut pas both be satisfied, though both peut fail."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/contributesTo|rdfs:label"
msgid "contributes to"
msgstr "contributes to"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/contributesTo|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a sub-gmeow:Goal whose satisfaction advances a gmeow:Goal without settling it. Domain gmeow:Goal, range gmeow:Goal (stated in prose). One of the four decomposition relations carrying satisfaction dependency; weaker than logic:necessaryFor (required) and logic:sufficientFor (settles on its own), and distinct from gmeow:properPartOf, which carries only structural part-hood."
msgstr "Relates a sub-gmeow:objectif dont satisfaction advances a gmeow:objectif sans settling it."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/corrSzsToVerdict|rdfs:label"
msgid "SZS status → conformance verdict correspondence"
msgstr "SZS status → conformité verdict correspondance"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/corrSzsToVerdict|skos:definition"
msgid "The first-class correspondence recording the SZS-status → logic:ConformanceVerdict collapse as a monotone (Galois) lossy projection. It carries logic:preservationKind logic:SoundUnderApproximation because the three-bucket view drops the logic:SzsContradictoryAxioms/logic:SzsUnsatisfiable and logic:SzsCounterSatisfiable/logic:SzsSatisfiable distinctions (a logic:LossyLens, logic:mnemomorphic false — the coarse verdict cannot recover the source token, which is why logic:rawStatusToken preserves it). Modelling the collapse as a logic:Correspondence rather than a bespoke check means its preservation rung is verified by two concrete mechanisms: the per-correspondence loss-ledger row (the Principle-17 residue that names the dropped logic:SzsContradictoryAxioms/logic:SzsUnsatisfiable and logic:SzsCounterSatisfiable/logic:SzsSatisfiable distinctions as structured actual-drop notes), and the preservation-consistency gate, which reds the build if a non-injective rung such as this logic:LossyLens ever declares logic:ExactPreservation instead of the honest logic:SoundUnderApproximation (design/LOGIC-CORRESPONDENCE.md, the loss ledger and correspondence gates)."
msgstr "Le first-class correspondance recording the SZS-status → logic:ConformanceVerdict collapse as a monotone (Galois) lossy projection."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/correlates|rdfs:label"
msgid "correlates"
msgstr "correlates"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/correlates|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:DependencyModel to a logic:probability-annotated fact (the reified base triple) that participates in the model's explicit joint distribution. The set of correlated facts is the support over which logic:jointOutcome enumerates joint assignments; any logic:probability fact NOT correlated by the model is treated as independent. The range is intentionally left open (no rdfs:range): a correlated fact is a reified logic:probability statement, which carries no dedicated class in this standalone module."
msgstr "Relates a logic:DependencyModel à a logic:probability-annotated fact (the reified base triple) qui participates dans the modèle's explicit joint distribution."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/correspondenceRelation|rdfs:label"
msgid "correspondence relation"
msgstr "correspondance relation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/correspondenceRelation|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Correspondence to its logic:CorrespondenceRelation on the ordered lattice (equiv ⊐ subsumes / subsumedBy ⊐ overlaps ⊐ relatedMatch, disjoint the negative pole). The single authored relation from which the SSSOM predicate, EDOAL symbol and OWL-alignment strength are derived. Range logic:CorrespondenceRelation (domain stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:correspondenceRelation only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:correspondance à its logic:CorrespondenceRelation sur the ordered lattice (equiv ⊐ subsumes / subsumedBy ⊐ overlaps ⊐ relatedMatch, disjoint the négatif pole)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/counterGoalIrreflexivity|rdfs:label"
msgid "counterGoal is irreflexive"
msgstr "counterGoal is irreflexive"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/counterGoalIrreflexivity|skos:definition"
msgid "Asserts on the canonical carrier that gmeow:counterGoal is irreflexive: a goal is never its own shadow, as its skos:definition states. The native coherence gate reads this to raise a violation for a goal asserted to counter itself."
msgstr "Asserts sur the canonique carrier qui gmeow:counterGoal est irreflexive: a objectif est jamais its own shadow, as its skos:définition states."


msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/counterGoalSymmetry|rdfs:label"
msgid "counterGoal is symmetric"
msgstr "counterGoal is symmetric"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/counterGoalSymmetry|skos:definition"
msgid "Asserts on the canonical carrier that gmeow:counterGoal is symmetric: each pole of a constitutive opposition constitutes the other, as its skos:definition states. The native coherence gate reads this to mirror the opposition."
msgstr "Asserts sur the canonique carrier qui gmeow:counterGoal est symmetric: each pole de a constitutive opposition constitutes the other, as its skos:définition states."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/counterfactualOf|rdfs:label"
msgid "counterfactual of"
msgstr "contrefactuel of"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/counterfactualOf|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a constructed counterfactual world to the base world it minimally revises: the surface for Lewis/Stalnaker counterfactuals, where the antecedent-world is computed by a revision rule rather than asserted and its contents must not leak into the base graph. Closeness is declared data (a generalized sharpening poset), not a fixed semantics; under the default Deterministic Revision Profile a declared entrenchment ordering yields a single revised world, and a genuine tie returns unknown rather than branching."
msgstr "Relates a constructed contrefactuel monde à the base monde it minimally revises: the surface pour Lewis/Stalnaker counterfactuals, où the antecedent-monde est computed par a revision règle plutôt que asserted et its contents ne doit pas leak dans the base graphe."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/counterfactuallyCloser|rdfs:label"
msgid "counterfactually closer"
msgstr "counterfactually closer"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/counterfactuallyCloser|skos:definition"
msgid "The typed counterfactual accessibility relation under a declared closeness ordering (Lewis comparative similarity, a generalized closeness poset over contexts). Counterfactual reasoning is a USE of typed contexts: a counterfactual claim is truth in the counterfactually-closer accessible contexts under the ordering. Closeness is declared data, not a fixed semantics. logic:accessibleFrom is its generic superproperty in prose only — NOT asserted rdfs:subPropertyOf — so what would have been never leaks into what is by walking the bare superproperty."
msgstr "Le typed contrefactuel accessibility relation sous a declared closeness ordering (Lewis comparatif similarity, a generalized closeness poset sur contexts)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/counterpartOfSymmetry|rdfs:label"
msgid "counterpartOf is symmetric"
msgstr "counterpartOf is symmetric"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/counterpartOfSymmetry|skos:definition"
msgid "Asserts on the canonical carrier that gmeow:counterpartOf is symmetric: cross-realm counterparts recognise each other both ways, as its skos:definition states. It is deliberately NOT transitive — that non-characteristic is enforced by logic:CounterpartNonTransitivityObligation, so no transitive carrier is authored. The native coherence gate reads this to mirror the counterpart link only."
msgstr "Asserts sur the canonique carrier qui gmeow:counterpartOf est symmetric: cross-realm counterparts recognise each other both ways, as its skos:définition states."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqBullshitIndifferenceHolds|rdfs:label"
msgid "bullshit as truth-indifference holds"
msgstr "bullshit as vérité-indifference holds"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqBullshitIndifferenceHolds|skos:definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the bullshit-modality equivalence must satisfy: a gmeow:StandpointClaim whose gmeow:claimModality is gmeow:bullshit is exactly one whose gmeow:claimTruthDirectedness is gmeow:truthIndifferent (Frankfurt) — held without regard for correspondence, distinct from a lie's truth-aimed denial. The well-formed case the biconditional admits."
msgstr "Le positif competency case the bullshit-modality equivalence doit satisfy: a gmeow:StandpointClaim dont gmeow:claimModality est gmeow:bullshit est exactement un dont gmeow:claimTruthDirectedness est gmeow:truthIndifferent (Frankfurt) — held sans regard pour correspondance, distinct de a lie's vérité-aimed denial."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqBullshitIndifferenceLieRejected|rdfs:label"
msgid "bullshit conflated with lying is rejected"
msgstr "bullshit conflated with lying is rejeté"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqBullshitIndifferenceLieRejected|skos:definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the bullshit-modality equivalence must respect: conflating gmeow:bullshit with a truth-aimed lie (gmeow:truthAimed) is rejected — bullshit is indifferent to truth, a lie asserts against a believed truth. HONEST SCOPE: the equivalence is realized in the OWL / full-FOL projection; the native monotone chase does not enforce a biconditional, disclosed in the loss ledger."
msgstr "Le négatif countermodel the bullshit-modality equivalence doit respect: conflating gmeow:bullshit avec a vérité-aimed lie (gmeow:truthAimed) est rejeté — bullshit est indifferent à vérité, a lie asserts contre a believed vérité."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqCrossNodeGlutHolds|rdfs:label"
msgid "all cross-node gluts at one anchor"
msgstr "tous cross-nœud gluts at one anchor"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqCrossNodeGlutHolds|skos:definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the cross-node-glut rule must satisfy — 'all cross-node gluts at one anchor': given two distinct findings at one gmeow:NonTrivialAnchor whose categories carry opposing gmeow:categoryPolarity (one logic:InfoSupported, one logic:InfoOpposed), the reasoner must derive gmeow:crossNodeGlutWith linking them — the Supported/Opposed clash across codes the same-fingerprint merge structurally misses."
msgstr "Le positif competency case the cross-nœud-glut règle doit satisfy — 'tous cross-nœud gluts at one anchor': given two distinct findings at one gmeow:NonTrivialAnchor dont categories carry opposing gmeow:categoryPolarity (one logic:InfoSupported, one logic:InfoOpposed), the raisonneur doit derive gmeow:crossNodeGlutWith linking them — the Supported/Opposed clash across codes the same-fingerprint merge structurally misses."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqCrossNodeGlutSamePolarityRejected|rdfs:label"
msgid "same-polarity findings at one anchor are not a glut"
msgstr "same-polarity findings at one anchor are not a glut"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqCrossNodeGlutSamePolarityRejected|skos:definition"
msgid "The second negative countermodel the cross-node-glut rule must respect: two findings at one gmeow:NonTrivialAnchor whose categories carry the SAME gmeow:categoryPolarity (both logic:InfoSupported, say) derive NO gmeow:crossNodeGlutWith — a glut is an OPPOSING Belnap clash (Supported vs Opposed), never an agreement; and findings at DIFFERENT anchors never join at all. The boundary that keeps the edge to genuine coherence conflicts."
msgstr "Le second négatif countermodel the cross-nœud-glut règle doit respect: two findings at one gmeow:NonTrivialAnchor dont categories carry the SAME gmeow:categoryPolarity (both logic:InfoSupported, say) derive NO gmeow:crossNodeGlutWith — a glut est an OPPOSING Belnap clash (Supported vs Opposed), jamais an agreement; et findings at DIFFERENT anchors jamais join at tous."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqCrossNodeGlutTrivialAnchorRejected|rdfs:label"
msgid "a glut never fires on the shared empty anchor"
msgstr "a glut never fires on the shared empty anchor"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqCrossNodeGlutTrivialAnchorRejected|skos:definition"
msgid "The first negative countermodel the cross-node-glut rule must respect: two opposing-polarity findings that share an anchor which is NOT a gmeow:NonTrivialAnchor (the default empty anchor locationless findings collapse onto) derive NO gmeow:crossNodeGlutWith — the gmeow:NonTrivialAnchor guard keeps the join off the shared placeholder, so the rule fires only at anchors that name a real source position. The boundary that prevents the false-join over locationless findings."
msgstr "Le first négatif countermodel the cross-nœud-glut règle doit respect: two opposing-polarity findings qui share an anchor qui est NOT a gmeow:NonTrivialAnchor (the default empty anchor locationless findings collapse onto) derive NO gmeow:crossNodeGlutWith — the gmeow:NonTrivialAnchor guard keeps the join off the shared placeholder, so the règle fires uniquement at anchors qui name a real source position."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqDeceptionDivergenceGapRejected|rdfs:label"
msgid "deception without a divergent gap is rejected"
msgstr "deception without a divergent gap is rejeté"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqDeceptionDivergenceGapRejected|skos:definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the deception-divergence axiom must respect: a gmeow:Event typed gmeow:eventTypeDeception whose held and projected standpoints coincide (no divergent claim-state) violates the necessary condition in the OWL / full-FOL projection. HONEST SCOPE: the native monotone StratifiedNAF chase does NOT enforce this existential, negation-bearing condition, so the rejection is realized only in the projection and is disclosed in the loss ledger."
msgstr "Le négatif countermodel the deception-divergence axiom doit respect: a gmeow:Event typed gmeow:eventTypeDeception dont held et projected standpoints coincide (no divergent claim-état) violates the necessary condition dans the OWL / full-FOL projection."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqDeceptionDivergenceHolds|rdfs:label"
msgid "deception divergence holds"
msgstr "deception divergence holds"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqDeceptionDivergenceHolds|skos:definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the deception-divergence necessary-condition must satisfy: a gmeow:Event of gmeow:eventTypeDeception that carries a gmeow:heldStandpoint and a gmeow:projectedStandpoint — both gmeow:DoxasticStandpointClaims — whose claim modalities differ satisfies the axiom. The held/projected gap is the deceptive act; the well-formed case the formula admits."
msgstr "Le positif competency case the deception-divergence necessary-condition doit satisfy: a gmeow:Event de gmeow:eventTypeDeception qui porte a gmeow:heldStandpoint et a gmeow:projectedStandpoint — both gmeow:DoxasticStandpointClaims — dont claim modalities differ satisfies the axiom."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqEndurantPerdurantClashRejected|rdfs:label"
msgid "endurant/perdurant clash is rejected"
msgstr "endurant/perdurant clash is rejeté"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqEndurantPerdurantClashRejected|skos:definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the endurant/perdurant disjointness axiom must respect: an individual typed BOTH logic:Endurant and logic:Perdurant is a violation — the native DL coherence gate forces it to owl:Nothing, because logic:Endurant owl:disjointWith logic:Perdurant is asserted. A thing that is at once wholly present at every moment and composed of temporal parts is not an admissible model. The boundary the continuant/occurrent divide enforces."
msgstr "Le négatif countermodel the endurant/perdurant disjointness axiom doit respect: an individu typed BOTH logic:Endurant et logic:Perdurant est a violation — the native DL cohérence gate forces it à owl:Nothing, parce que logic:Endurant owl:disjointWith logic:Perdurant est asserted."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqEndurantPerdurantDisjointHolds|rdfs:label"
msgid "endurant/perdurant disjointness holds"
msgstr "endurant/perdurant disjointness holds"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqEndurantPerdurantDisjointHolds|skos:definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the endurant/perdurant disjointness axiom must satisfy: an individual typed logic:Endurant and NOT logic:Perdurant (a continuant wholly present at each moment) stays coherent — it is not forced to owl:Nothing — because a thing either endures through change or unfolds through it, not both."
msgstr "Le positif competency case the endurant/perdurant disjointness axiom doit satisfy: an individu typed logic:Endurant et NOT logic:Perdurant (a continuant wholly present at each moment) stays coherent — it n'est pas forced à owl:Nothing — parce que a thing either endures par change ou unfolds par it, not both."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqEntitySortalCoveringGapRejected|rdfs:label"
msgid "entity sortal covering gap is rejected"
msgstr "entity sortal covering gap is rejeté"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqEntitySortalCoveringGapRejected|skos:definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the entity-sortal covering must respect: a gmeow:Entity typed into NONE of the four sortals violates the owl:unionOf covering in the OWL-DL projection — an OWL reasoner rejects the class-covering gap. HONEST SCOPE: the native monotone StratifiedNAF gate does NOT enforce this disjunctive covering (a disjunction in the head is non-Horn), so this rejection is realized only in the OWL projection, not in the native chase, and is disclosed in the loss ledger accordingly."
msgstr "Le négatif countermodel the entity-sortal covering doit respect: a gmeow:Entity typed dans NONE de the quatre sortals violates the owl:unionOf covering dans the OWL-DL projection — an OWL raisonneur rejette the class-covering gap."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqEntitySortalCoveringHolds|rdfs:label"
msgid "entity sortal covering holds"
msgstr "entity sortal covering holds"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqEntitySortalCoveringHolds|skos:definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the entity-sortal covering must satisfy: a gmeow:Entity that is one of the four sortals (gmeow:Agent, gmeow:InformationObject, gmeow:PhysicalObject, gmeow:SocialObject) is covered by the owl:unionOf — no gap. Realized in the OWL-DL projection; it is the well-formed case the covering disjunction admits."
msgstr "Le positif competency case the entity-sortal covering doit satisfy: a gmeow:Entity qui est one de the quatre sortals (gmeow:Agent, gmeow:InformationObject, gmeow:PhysicalObject, gmeow:SocialObject) est covered par the owl:unionOf — no gap."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqEventSituationClashRejected|rdfs:label"
msgid "event/situation clash is rejected"
msgstr "event/situation clash is rejeté"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqEventSituationClashRejected|skos:definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the event/situation disjointness axiom must respect: an individual typed BOTH logic:Event and logic:Situation is a violation — the native DL coherence gate forces it to owl:Nothing, because logic:Event owl:disjointWith logic:Situation is asserted. A thing that is at once an unfolding occurrence and the static configuration a situation records is not an admissible model. The boundary the occurrent/configuration distinction enforces."
msgstr "Le négatif countermodel the event/situation disjointness axiom doit respect: an individu typed BOTH logic:Event et logic:situation est a violation — the native DL cohérence gate forces it à owl:Nothing, parce que logic:Event owl:disjointWith logic:situation est asserted."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqEventSituationDisjointHolds|rdfs:label"
msgid "event/situation disjointness holds"
msgstr "event/situation disjointness holds"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqEventSituationDisjointHolds|skos:definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the event/situation disjointness axiom must satisfy: an individual typed logic:Event and NOT logic:Situation (a perdurant occurrence composed of temporal parts) stays coherent — it is not forced to owl:Nothing — because an occurrence that unfolds in time is not the static configuration a situation records."
msgstr "Le positif competency case the event/situation disjointness axiom doit satisfy: an individu typed logic:Event et NOT logic:situation (a perdurant occurrence composed de temporal parts) stays coherent — it n'est pas forced à owl:Nothing — parce que an occurrence qui unfolds dans time n'est pas the static configuration a situation records."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqFalsehoodRefutedGlobalTruthRejected|rdfs:label"
msgid "falsehood as global truth verdict is rejected"
msgstr "falsehood as global vérité verdict is rejeté"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqFalsehoodRefutedGlobalTruthRejected|skos:definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the falsehood-as-refuted-claim equivalence must respect: reading gmeow:refuted as a frame-independent isFalse flag on the proposition — rather than as the necessarily-denying stance of one standpoint — is rejected (Principle 11: no global truth verdict). HONEST SCOPE: the equivalence is realized in the OWL / full-FOL projection; the native monotone chase does not enforce a biconditional, so this is disclosed in the loss ledger."
msgstr "Le négatif countermodel the falsehood-as-refuted-claim equivalence doit respect: reading gmeow:refuted as a frame-independent isFalse flag sur the proposition — plutôt que as the necessarily-denying stance de one point de vue — est rejeté (Principle 11: no global vérité verdict)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqFalsehoodRefutedHolds|rdfs:label"
msgid "falsehood as refuted claim holds"
msgstr "falsehood as refuted claim holds"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqFalsehoodRefutedHolds|skos:definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the falsehood-as-refuted-claim equivalence must satisfy: a gmeow:StandpointClaim whose gmeow:claimModality is gmeow:refuted is exactly one whose gmeow:claimPolarity is gmeow:polarityDeny and gmeow:claimModalForce is gmeow:modalForceNecessary (□¬ — settled-false-in-frame). The well-formed case the biconditional admits; there is no separate isFalse flag."
msgstr "Le positif competency case the falsehood-as-refuted-claim equivalence doit satisfy: a gmeow:StandpointClaim dont gmeow:claimModality est gmeow:refuted est exactement un dont gmeow:claimPolarity est gmeow:polarityDeny et gmeow:claimModalForce est gmeow:modalForceNecessary (□¬ — settled-false-in-frame)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqFindingClusterDistinctRootsRejected|rdfs:label"
msgid "findings under different roots never share a cluster"
msgstr "findings under different roots never share a cluster"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqFindingClusterDistinctRootsRejected|skos:definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the cluster rules must respect: findings with DIFFERENT gmeow:findingRootCause values land in different clusters — a finding whose root is R1 is never linked by gmeow:findingCluster to the cluster keyed by a distinct R2, and each cluster node carries only its own root. The boundary that keeps unrelated root-cause groups from merging."
msgstr "Le négatif countermodel the cluster rules doit respect: findings avec DIFFERENT gmeow:findingRootCause values land dans different clusters — a finding dont root est R1 est jamais linked par gmeow:findingCluster à the cluster keyed par a distinct R2, et each cluster nœud porte uniquement its own root."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqFindingClusterHolds|rdfs:label"
msgid "all findings sharing root R group under one cluster"
msgstr "tous findings sharing root R group under one cluster"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqFindingClusterHolds|skos:definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the cluster rules must satisfy — 'all findings sharing root R': given F2 and F3 that each gmeow:findingRootCause the root F1, the reasoner must derive gmeow:findingCluster(F2, F1), gmeow:findingCluster(F3, F1), gmeow:clusterRoot(F1, F1), and rdf:type(F1, gmeow:FindingCluster) — every finding sharing R gathered under the one root-keyed cluster node, which carries R exactly once."
msgstr "Le positif competency case the cluster rules doit satisfy — 'tous findings sharing root R': given F2 et F3 qui each gmeow:findingRootCause the root F1, the raisonneur doit derive gmeow:findingCluster(F2, F1), gmeow:findingCluster(F3, F1), gmeow:clusterRoot(F1, F1), et rdf:type(F1, gmeow:FindingCluster) — chaque finding sharing R gathered sous the one root-keyed cluster nœud, qui porte R exactly once."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqFindingRootCauseHolds|rdfs:label"
msgid "findings sharing one root all derive that childless root"
msgstr "findings sharing one root tous derive that childless root"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqFindingRootCauseHolds|skos:definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the root-cause rule must satisfy — 'the root of all findings sharing root R': given F2 and F3 that each gmeow:findingAntecedent the childless F1 (F1 has no antecedent), the reasoner must derive gmeow:findingRootCause(F2, F1) AND gmeow:findingRootCause(F3, F1), and transitively gmeow:findingRootCause(F4, F1) for an F4 that traces to F1 through F2 — the shared childless root, agreeing with the witness-DAG root-cause harvest."
msgstr "Le positif competency case the root-cause règle doit satisfy — 'the root de tous findings sharing root R': given F2 et F3 qui each gmeow:findingAntecedent the childless F1 (F1 possède no antecedent), the raisonneur doit derive gmeow:findingRootCause(F2, F1) AND gmeow:findingRootCause(F3, F1), et transitively gmeow:findingRootCause(F4, F1) pour an F4 qui traces à F1 par F2 — the shared childless root, agreeing avec the témoin-DAG root-cause harvest."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqFindingRootCauseNonRootRejected|rdfs:label"
msgid "an intermediate antecedent is never a root cause"
msgstr "an intermediate antecedent is never a root cause"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqFindingRootCauseNonRootRejected|skos:definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the root-cause rule must respect: a traced antecedent that ITSELF carries a gmeow:findingAntecedent is never derived a gmeow:findingRootCause — only a childless root qualifies. For F4 → F2 → F1, F4's root cause is F1, NEVER the intermediate F2 (which is a gmeow:findingHasAntecedent of itself); and an independent finding with no antecedent chain derives no root cause at all. The boundary the negation-as-failure over gmeow:findingHasAntecedent keeps."
msgstr "Le négatif countermodel the root-cause règle doit respect: a traced antecedent qui ITSELF porte a gmeow:findingAntecedent est jamais dérivé a gmeow:findingRootCause — uniquement a childless root qualifies."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqFindingTracesHolds|rdfs:label"
msgid "a finding traces to every antecedent up its chain"
msgstr "a finding traces to every antecedent up its chain"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqFindingTracesHolds|skos:definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the transitive-closure rules must satisfy — 'every antecedent this finding derives from, directly or transitively': given F4 gmeow:findingAntecedent F2 and F2 gmeow:findingAntecedent F1, the reasoner must derive BOTH gmeow:findingTraces(F4, F2) and gmeow:findingTraces(F4, F1), closing the witness DAG up past the intermediate."
msgstr "Le positif competency case the transitive-fermeture rules doit satisfy — 'every antecedent this finding derives from, directly ou transitively': given F4 gmeow:findingAntecedent F2 et F2 gmeow:findingAntecedent F1, the raisonneur doit derive BOTH gmeow:findingTraces(F4, F2) et gmeow:findingTraces(F4, F1), closing the témoin DAG up past the intermediate."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqFindingTracesNonReachRejected|rdfs:label"
msgid "a finding never traces to an unconnected finding"
msgstr "a finding never traces to an unconnected finding"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqFindingTracesNonReachRejected|skos:definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the transitive-closure rules must respect: gmeow:findingTraces is exactly the reachability closure of gmeow:findingAntecedent — a finding with no antecedent chain to another finding never traces to it, and the closure is directed (a root antecedent does not trace DOWN to its downstream witnesses). Two findings in disjoint witness DAGs share no gmeow:findingTraces edge."
msgstr "Le négatif countermodel the transitive-fermeture rules doit respect: gmeow:findingTraces est exactly the reachability fermeture de gmeow:findingAntecedent — a finding avec no antecedent chain à another finding jamais traces à it, et the fermeture est directed (a root antecedent ne fait pas trace DOWN à its downstream witnesses)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqFrameRelativityFramelessRejected|rdfs:label"
msgid "a frame-free value is rejected"
msgstr "a frame-free valeur is rejeté"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqFrameRelativityFramelessRejected|skos:definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the frame-relativity constraint must respect: a logic:measuredValue asserted with no logic:referenceFrame is the logic:MeasurementFrameMissing violation — a frame-free value collapse the foundation catches as a finding, never admits as a well-formed model. The boundary Principle 11 enforces: a value asserted without its frame is ill-formed, and two frame-relative values are never equated frame-free."
msgstr "Le négatif countermodel the frame-relativity contrainte doit respect: a logic:measuredValue asserted avec no logic:referenceFrame est the logic:MeasurementFrameMissing violation — a frame-free valeur collapse the foundation catches as a finding, jamais admits as a bien formé modèle."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqFrameRelativityHolds|rdfs:label"
msgid "a framed value stays well-formed"
msgstr "a framed valeur stays well-formed"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqFrameRelativityHolds|skos:definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the frame-relativity constraint must satisfy: a logic:measuredValue expressed together with its logic:referenceFrame is well-formed — it carries no logic:MeasurementFrameMissing violation — because the value is meaningful only paired with the frame it is expressed in (Principle 11)."
msgstr "Le positif competency case the frame-relativity contrainte doit satisfy: a logic:measuredValue expressed together avec its logic:referenceFrame est bien formé — it porte no logic:MeasurementFrameMissing violation — parce que the valeur est meaningful uniquement paired avec the frame it est expressed dans (Principle 11)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqFunctionalComplexKindDisjointHolds|rdfs:label"
msgid "individuation-kind disjointness holds"
msgstr "individuation-kind disjointness holds"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqFunctionalComplexKindDisjointHolds|skos:definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the individuation-kind disjointness axioms must satisfy: an individual typed logic:FunctionalComplex and NOT also logic:Collection or logic:Quantity stays coherent — it is not forced to owl:Nothing — because a whole is individuated in exactly one of the three modes the prose contrasts."
msgstr "Le positif competency case the individuation-kind disjointness axioms doit satisfy: an individu typed logic:FunctionalComplex et NOT also logic:collection ou logic:Quantity stays coherent — it n'est pas forced à owl:Nothing — parce que a whole est individuated dans exactement un de the three modes the prose contrasts."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqFunctionalComplexKindDisjointOverlapRejected|rdfs:label"
msgid "individuation-kind overlap is rejected"
msgstr "individuation-kind overlap is rejeté"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqFunctionalComplexKindDisjointOverlapRejected|skos:definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the individuation-kind disjointness axioms must respect: an individual typed BOTH logic:FunctionalComplex and logic:Collection is a violation — the native DL coherence gate forces it to owl:Nothing — so a whole individuated at once by distinct functional roles and by member count is not an admissible model. The boundary the harvested constraint enforces."
msgstr "Le négatif countermodel the individuation-kind disjointness axioms doit respect: an individu typed BOTH logic:FunctionalComplex et logic:collection est a violation — the native DL cohérence gate forces it à owl:Nothing — so a whole individuated at once par distinct functional roles et par member count n'est pas an admissible modèle."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqGateFatalAdvisoryNeverFatalRejected|rdfs:label"
msgid "an advisory-standpoint finding is never derived fatal"
msgstr "an advisory-point de vue finding is never dérivé fatal"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqGateFatalAdvisoryNeverFatalRejected|skos:definition"
msgid "The first never-gate countermodel the gate rule must respect: a finding whose gmeow:findingStandpoint is gmeow:standpointAdvisory is NEVER derived gmeow:findingGateVerdict gmeow:gateFatal, no matter how loud its severity or how blocking its category — the standpoint axis is below the Binding top, so the meet cannot reach Fatal. The boundary that keeps advice from ever failing the gate, mirroring Rust gate() returning Collected for every advisory grade."
msgstr "Le first never-gate countermodel the gate règle doit respect: a finding dont gmeow:findingStandpoint est gmeow:standpointAdvisory est NEVER dérivé gmeow:findingGateVerdict gmeow:gateFatal, no matter how loud its severity ou how blocking its catégorie — the point de vue axis est below the liaison top, so the meet ne peut pas reach Fatal."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqGateFatalPermittedConflictNeverFatalRejected|rdfs:label"
msgid "a permitted-epistemic-conflict finding is never derived fatal"
msgstr "a permitted-épistémique-conflit finding is never dérivé fatal"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqGateFatalPermittedConflictNeverFatalRejected|skos:definition"
msgid "The second never-gate countermodel the gate rule must respect: a finding whose gmeow:findingCategory is logic:FindingPermittedEpistemicConflict — whose gmeow:categoryBlocking projection is gmeow:blockingCoherent — is NEVER derived gmeow:findingGateVerdict gmeow:gateFatal, even at gmeow:severityError and gmeow:standpointBinding, because its Blocking axis is below the Blocking top. The load-bearing boundary that a disclosed, coherent contradiction a glut-admitting contract permits does not fail the gate, mirroring Rust gate() returning Collected for every Coherent-category grade."
msgstr "Le second never-gate countermodel the gate règle doit respect: a finding dont gmeow:findingCategory est logic:FindingPermittedEpistemicConflict — dont gmeow:categoryBlocking projection est gmeow:blockingCoherent — est NEVER dérivé gmeow:findingGateVerdict gmeow:gateFatal, even at gmeow:severityError et gmeow:standpointBinding, parce que its Blocking axis est below the Blocking top."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqGateFatalVerdictHolds|rdfs:label"
msgid "the fatal verdict is derived on the top of all three truth axes"
msgstr "the fatal verdict is dérivé on the top of tous three vérité axes"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqGateFatalVerdictHolds|skos:definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the gate rule must satisfy: given a finding with gmeow:findingSeverity gmeow:severityError, a gmeow:findingCategory whose gmeow:categoryBlocking is gmeow:blockingBlocking (a failure kind), and gmeow:findingStandpoint gmeow:standpointBinding, the reasoner must derive gmeow:findingGateVerdict gmeow:gateFatal — the principal up-set ↑(Error, Blocking, Binding) the harvested prose commits to, agreeing with Rust gate() returning Fatal."
msgstr "Le positif competency case the gate règle doit satisfy: given a finding avec gmeow:findingSeverity gmeow:severityError, a gmeow:findingCategory dont gmeow:categoryBlocking est gmeow:blockingBlocking (a échec kind), et gmeow:findingStandpoint gmeow:standpointBinding, the raisonneur doit derive gmeow:findingGateVerdict gmeow:gateFatal — the principal up-set ↑(Error, Blocking, liaison) the harvested prose commits to, agreeing avec Rust gate() returning Fatal."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqIndirectContributorDirectAttributionRejected|rdfs:label"
msgid "indirect contribution is not derived as direct attribution"
msgstr "indirect contribution is not dérivé as direct attribution"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqIndirectContributorDirectAttributionRejected|skos:definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the indirect-contribution rule must respect: the derived gmeow:indirectContributor edge must never appear as gmeow:wasAttributedTo — deriving direct, asserted responsibility from the generation chain is a violation, the boundary the non-entailment obligation holds the formalization to."
msgstr "Le négatif countermodel the indirect-contribution règle doit respect: the dérivé gmeow:indirectContributor edge doit jamais appear as gmeow:wasAttributedTo — deriving direct, asserted responsibility de the generation chain est a violation, the boundary the non-implication obligation holds the formalisation to."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqIndirectContributorHolds|rdfs:label"
msgid "indirect contributor is derived across the generation chain"
msgstr "indirect contributor is dérivé across the generation chain"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqIndirectContributorHolds|skos:definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the indirect-contribution rule must satisfy: given an entity gmeow:wasGeneratedBy an activity that gmeow:wasAssociatedWith an agent, the reasoner must derive gmeow:indirectContributor from the entity to that agent — the productive composition the harvested prose commits to."
msgstr "Le positif competency case the indirect-contribution règle doit satisfy: given an entity gmeow:wasGeneratedBy an activity qui gmeow:wasAssociatedWith an agent, the raisonneur doit derive gmeow:indirectContributor de the entity à qui agent — the productive composition the harvested prose commits to."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqInstantiatesWorkBrokenSpineRejected|rdfs:label"
msgid "broken WEMI spine derives no Item→Work edge"
msgstr "broken WEMI spine derives no Item→Work edge"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqInstantiatesWorkBrokenSpineRejected|skos:definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the WEMI-instantiation rule must respect: an Item whose spine is broken — a Manifestation that embodies no Expression, or an Expression that realizes no Work — derives NO gmeow:instantiatesWork edge, because the derivation is the conjunction of all three R-relations. The boundary that keeps the shortcut from short-circuiting an incomplete spine."
msgstr "Le négatif countermodel the WEMI-instantiation règle doit respect: an Item dont spine est broken — a Manifestation qui embodies no expression, ou an expression qui realizes no Work — derives NO gmeow:instantiatesWork edge, parce que the dérivation est the conjunction de tous three R-relations."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqInstantiatesWorkHolds|rdfs:label"
msgid "Item→Work shortcut is derived across the full WEMI spine"
msgstr "Item→Work shortcut is dérivé across the full WEMI spine"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqInstantiatesWorkHolds|skos:definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the WEMI-instantiation rule must satisfy: given an Item that gmeow:exemplifies a Manifestation that gmeow:embodies an Expression that gmeow:realizes a Work, the reasoner must derive gmeow:instantiatesWork from the Item to that Work — the copy-to-Work composition the harvested prose commits to."
msgstr "Le positif competency case the WEMI-instantiation règle doit satisfy: given an Item qui gmeow:exemplifies a Manifestation qui gmeow:embodies an expression qui gmeow:realizes a Work, the raisonneur doit derive gmeow:instantiatesWork de the Item à qui Work — the copy-to-Work composition the harvested prose commits to."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqLicensedFalsehoodDeceptionRejected|rdfs:label"
msgid "licensed falsehood classified as deception is rejected"
msgstr "licensed falsehood classified as deception is rejeté"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqLicensedFalsehoodDeceptionRejected|skos:definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the licensed-falsehood safety partition must respect: classifying a socially-licensed non-truth-asserting projection (a novel, a satire) as deception is rejected — the audience understands the non-asserting frame. HONEST SCOPE: the exclusion is realized in the OWL / full-FOL projection (strong negation in the head); the native monotone chase does not enforce it, disclosed in the loss ledger."
msgstr "Le négatif countermodel the licensed-falsehood safety partition doit respect: classifying a socially-licensed non-vérité-asserting projection (a novel, a satire) as deception est rejeté — the audience understands the non-asserting frame."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqLicensedFalsehoodSafeHolds|rdfs:label"
msgid "licensed falsehood is not deception holds"
msgstr "licensed falsehood is not deception holds"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqLicensedFalsehoodSafeHolds|skos:definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the licensed-falsehood safety partition must satisfy: a gmeow:Event whose gmeow:projectedStandpoint carries gmeow:claimVeridicality gmeow:veridicalityLicensedFalsehood (fiction, satire, sarcasm) is NOT a gmeow:eventTypeDeception, even though it carries a held/projected gap. The well-formed case the exclusion admits."
msgstr "Le positif competency case the licensed-falsehood safety partition doit satisfy: a gmeow:Event dont gmeow:projectedStandpoint porte gmeow:claimVeridicality gmeow:veridicalityLicensedFalsehood (fiction, satire, sarcasm) est NOT a gmeow:eventTypeDeception, even though it porte a held/projected gap."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqNoOverTypingHolds|rdfs:label"
msgid "a single-Kind instance is well-formed"
msgstr "a single-Kind instance is well-formed"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqNoOverTypingHolds|skos:definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the no-over-typing constraint must satisfy: an object whose sortal traces its principle of identity to exactly one ultimate logic:Kind is well-formed — it carries no logic:MixIden violation — because a Kind supplies a single principle of identity (Principle 9's refusal to over-type)."
msgstr "Le positif competency case the no-over-typing contrainte doit satisfy: an object dont sortal traces its principle de identité à exactement un ultimate logic:Kind est bien formé — it porte no logic:MixIden violation — parce que a Kind supplies a single principle de identité (Principle 9's refusal à over-type)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqNoOverTypingTwoKindsRejected|rdfs:label"
msgid "a two-Kind instance is rejected"
msgstr "a two-Kind instance is rejeté"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqNoOverTypingTwoKindsRejected|skos:definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the no-over-typing constraint must respect: a sortal tracing its identity to two-or-more disjoint logic:Kinds is the logic:MixIden violation — over-typing the foundation catches as a finding, never admits as a well-formed model. The boundary Principle 9 enforces: co-equal facets are not fused into two disjoint identity-supplying Kinds on one instance."
msgstr "Le négatif countermodel the no-over-typing contrainte doit respect: a sortal tracing its identité à two-or-more disjoint logic:Kinds est the logic:MixIden violation — over-typing the foundation catches as a finding, jamais admits as a bien formé modèle."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqObjectIndividuationCoveringGapRejected|rdfs:label"
msgid "object individuation covering gap is rejected"
msgstr "object individuation covering gap is rejeté"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqObjectIndividuationCoveringGapRejected|skos:definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the object-individuation covering must respect: a logic:Object typed into NONE of the three individuation kinds violates the owl:unionOf covering in the OWL-DL projection — an OWL reasoner rejects the class-covering gap. HONEST SCOPE: the native monotone StratifiedNAF gate does NOT enforce this disjunctive covering, so this rejection is realized only in the OWL projection and is disclosed in the loss ledger."
msgstr "Le négatif countermodel the object-individuation covering doit respect: a logic:Object typed dans NONE de the three individuation kinds violates the owl:unionOf covering dans the OWL-DL projection — an OWL raisonneur rejette the class-covering gap."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqObjectIndividuationCoveringHolds|rdfs:label"
msgid "object individuation covering holds"
msgstr "object individuation covering holds"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqObjectIndividuationCoveringHolds|skos:definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the object-individuation covering must satisfy: a logic:Object that is one of the three individuation kinds (logic:Collection, logic:Quantity, logic:FunctionalComplex) is covered by the owl:unionOf — no gap. Realized in the OWL-DL projection; the well-formed case the covering disjunction admits, completing the individuation-kind pairwise disjointness into a partition."
msgstr "Le positif competency case the object-individuation covering doit satisfy: a logic:Object qui est one de the three individuation kinds (logic:collection, logic:Quantity, logic:FunctionalComplex) est covered par the owl:unionOf — no gap."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqOrgMembershipPropagationDownwardRejected|rdfs:label"
msgid "membership does not propagate down or sideways"
msgstr "membership does not propagate down or sideways"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqOrgMembershipPropagationDownwardRejected|skos:definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the membership-propagation rule must respect: membership climbs the sub-organization chain UP only — a member of a parent organization is NOT thereby a member of its sub-organizations, and an agent outside the hierarchy gains no derived membership. The direction boundary the frontier-variable rule keeps, deriving parent membership from child membership and never the reverse."
msgstr "Le négatif countermodel the membership-propagation règle doit respect: membership climbs the sub-organization chain UP uniquement — a member de a parent organization est NOT thereby a member de its sub-organizations, et an agent outside the hierarchy gains no dérivé membership."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqOrgMembershipPropagationHolds|rdfs:label"
msgid "membership propagates up the sub-organization hierarchy"
msgstr "membership propagates up the sub-organization hierarchy"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqOrgMembershipPropagationHolds|skos:definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the membership-propagation rule must satisfy: given an agent gmeow:memberOf a department that is gmeow:subOrganizationOf a company, the reasoner must derive gmeow:memberOf from the agent to the company — and, recursively, to every further containing organization — the upward propagation the harvested prose commits to."
msgstr "Le positif competency case the membership-propagation règle doit satisfy: given an agent gmeow:memberOf a department qui est gmeow:subOrganizationOf a company, the raisonneur doit derive gmeow:memberOf de the agent à the company — and, recursively, à chaque further containing organization — the upward propagation the harvested prose commits to."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqProperPartAsymmetryHolds|rdfs:label"
msgid "properPartOf asymmetry holds"
msgstr "properPartOf asymmetry holds"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqProperPartAsymmetryHolds|skos:definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the properPartOf-asymmetry axiom must satisfy: given logic:properPartOf(a,b), the reasoner must not also hold logic:properPartOf(b,a) — the strict-order reading the harvested prose commits to."
msgstr "Le positif competency case the properPartOf-asymmetry axiom doit satisfy: given logic:properPartOf(a,b), the raisonneur ne doit pas also hold logic:properPartOf(b,a) — the strict-order reading the harvested prose commits to."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqProperPartAsymmetrySymmetricPairRejected|rdfs:label"
msgid "properPartOf symmetric pair is rejected"
msgstr "properPartOf symmetric pair is rejeté"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqProperPartAsymmetrySymmetricPairRejected|skos:definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the properPartOf-asymmetry axiom must respect: a purported model asserting both logic:properPartOf(a,b) and logic:properPartOf(b,a) is a violation, not an admissible model — the boundary the formalization must not cross."
msgstr "Le négatif countermodel the properPartOf-asymmetry axiom doit respect: a purported modèle asserting both logic:properPartOf(a,b) et logic:properPartOf(b,a) est a violation, not an admissible modèle — the boundary the formalisation ne doit pas cross."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqRelatorMediationHolds|rdfs:label"
msgid "relator mediation holds"
msgstr "relator mediation holds"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqRelatorMediationHolds|skos:definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the relator-mediation discipline (RelComp) must satisfy: a concrete relator that mediates at least two distinct relata stays coherent — it fires no logic:violation logic:RelComp. gmeow:Commitment, which mediates gmeow:committedAgent, gmeow:commitmentBeneficiary and gmeow:intentionGoal, is well-mediated and passes."
msgstr "Le positif competency case the relator-mediation discipline (RelComp) doit satisfy: a concret relator qui mediates au moins two distinct relata stays coherent — it fires no logic:violation logic:RelComp."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqRelatorMediationUnderMediatedRejected|rdfs:label"
msgid "under-mediated relator rejected"
msgstr "under-mediated relator rejeté"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqRelatorMediationUnderMediatedRejected|skos:definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the relator-mediation discipline must reject: a concrete relator that mediates fewer than two distinct relata is degenerate and fires logic:violation logic:RelComp — an objectified relation that connects only one entity grounds no material relation, so it is not a relator."
msgstr "Le négatif countermodel the relator-mediation discipline doit reject: a concret relator qui mediates fewer than two distinct relata est degenerate et fires logic:violation logic:RelComp — an objectified relation qui connects uniquement one entity grounds no material relation, so it n'est pas a relator."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqRootFindingHolds|rdfs:label"
msgid "a witnessed root is marked a root finding"
msgstr "a witnessed root is marked a root finding"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqRootFindingHolds|skos:definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the root-finding rule must satisfy — 'which findings are root causes': given F2 gmeow:findingRootCause F1, the reasoner must derive rdf:type(F1, gmeow:RootFinding); and it must fire through the gmeow:DiagnosticMetaRule class discovery exactly like the other meta-rules, so a consumer selecting rules by that type runs it with no engine change."
msgstr "Le positif competency case the root-finding règle doit satisfy — 'which findings sont root causes': given F2 gmeow:findingRootCause F1, the raisonneur doit derive rdf:type(F1, gmeow:RootFinding); et it doit fire par the gmeow:DiagnosticMetaRule class discovery exactly like the other meta-rules, so a consumer selecting rules par qui type runs it avec no engine change."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqRootFindingNonRootRejected|rdfs:label"
msgid "a non-root finding is never a root finding"
msgstr "a non-root finding is never a root finding"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqRootFindingNonRootRejected|skos:definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the root-finding rule must respect: a finding that is NOT the gmeow:findingRootCause of any finding is never typed gmeow:RootFinding — the marker names exactly the witnessed roots, so a downstream witness or an independent finding with no dependents carries no gmeow:RootFinding type."
msgstr "Le négatif countermodel the root-finding règle doit respect: a finding qui est NOT the gmeow:findingRootCause de tout finding est jamais typed gmeow:RootFinding — the marker nomme exactly the witnessed roots, so a downstream témoin ou an independent finding avec no dependents porte no gmeow:RootFinding type."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqSocialInformationOverlapDisjointRejected|rdfs:label"
msgid "social/information disjointness is rejected"
msgstr "social/information disjointness is rejeté"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqSocialInformationOverlapDisjointRejected|skos:definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel that explains WHY the social/information overlap must be preserved: IF gmeow:SocialObject were wrongly asserted owl:disjointWith gmeow:InformationObject, then a founding myth typed as both would be forced to owl:Nothing by the coherence gate — collapsing a legitimate model. The rejected disjointness is the mistake this deliberate non-assertion guards against; asserting it is the boundary the partition must NOT cross."
msgstr "Le négatif countermodel qui explains WHY the social/information overlap doit be preserved: IF gmeow:SocialObject were wrongly asserted owl:disjointWith gmeow:InformationObject, then a founding myth typed as both would be forced à owl:Nothing par the cohérence gate — collapsing a legitimate modèle."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqSocialInformationOverlapHolds|rdfs:label"
msgid "social/information overlap holds"
msgstr "social/information overlap holds"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqSocialInformationOverlapHolds|skos:definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the deliberate social/information overlap must satisfy: an individual typed BOTH gmeow:SocialObject and gmeow:InformationObject — a founding myth that is at once socially sustained and information-bearing — stays coherent and is NOT forced to owl:Nothing, precisely because no disjointness between the two is asserted. The overlap the top-sortal partition deliberately preserves."
msgstr "Le positif competency case the deliberate social/information overlap doit satisfy: an individu typed BOTH gmeow:SocialObject et gmeow:InformationObject — a founding myth qui est at once socially sustained et information-bearing — stays coherent et est NOT forced à owl:Nothing, precisely parce que no disjointness entre the two est asserted."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqTenureClaimSurfacingHolds|rdfs:label"
msgid "a tenure's frame and position surface onto its generated claim"
msgstr "a tenure's frame and position surface onto its generated claim"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqTenureClaimSurfacingHolds|skos:definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the tenure-claim-surfacing rules must satisfy: given a gmeow:StandpointTenure that gmeow:standpointClaim a claim, gmeow:tenureStandpoint a standpoint, and gmeow:tenurePosition a position, the reasoner must derive gmeow:vantage from the claim to that standpoint AND gmeow:observedFeature from the claim to that position — the tenure→claim mapping the harvested prose commits to."
msgstr "Le positif competency case the tenure-claim-surfacing rules doit satisfy: given a gmeow:StandpointTenure qui gmeow:standpointClaim a claim, gmeow:tenureStandpoint a point de vue, et gmeow:tenurePosition a position, the raisonneur doit derive gmeow:vantage de the claim à qui point de vue AND gmeow:observedFeature de the claim à qui position — the tenure→claim mapping the harvested prose commits to."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqTenureClaimSurfacingSwapRejected|rdfs:label"
msgid "the tenure→claim mapping is never swapped"
msgstr "the tenure→claim mapping is never swapped"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqTenureClaimSurfacingSwapRejected|skos:definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the tenure-claim-surfacing rules must respect: the mapping is directional and specific — the tenureStandpoint becomes the claim's gmeow:vantage (never its gmeow:observedFeature) and the tenurePosition becomes the claim's gmeow:observedFeature (never its gmeow:vantage), and a tenure with no gmeow:standpointClaim surfaces nothing. The boundary that keeps frame and position from being crossed onto the wrong role."
msgstr "Le négatif countermodel the tenure-claim-surfacing rules doit respect: the mapping est directional et specific — the tenureStandpoint becomes the claim's gmeow:vantage (never its gmeow:observedFeature) et the tenurePosition becomes the claim's gmeow:observedFeature (never its gmeow:vantage), et a tenure avec no gmeow:standpointClaim surfaces nothing."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqTopSortalDisjointClashRejected|rdfs:label"
msgid "top-sortal clash is rejected"
msgstr "top-sortal clash is rejeté"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqTopSortalDisjointClashRejected|skos:definition"
msgid "The negative countermodel the top-sortal disjointness axioms must respect: an individual typed BOTH gmeow:Agent and gmeow:SocialObject is a violation — the native DL coherence gate forces it to owl:Nothing, because gmeow:Agent owl:disjointWith gmeow:SocialObject is asserted (net-new on this branch). A thing that both acts and bears responsibility yet exists purely by social convention is not an admissible model. The boundary the disjointness enforces."
msgstr "Le négatif countermodel the top-sortal disjointness axioms doit respect: an individu typed BOTH gmeow:Agent et gmeow:SocialObject est a violation — the native DL cohérence gate forces it à owl:Nothing, parce que gmeow:Agent owl:disjointWith gmeow:SocialObject est asserted (net-new sur this branch)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqTopSortalDisjointHolds|rdfs:label"
msgid "top-sortal disjointness holds"
msgstr "top-sortal disjointness holds"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/cqTopSortalDisjointHolds|skos:definition"
msgid "The positive competency case the top-sortal disjointness axioms must satisfy: an individual typed into exactly one of the four kernel top sortals (gmeow:Agent, gmeow:InformationObject, gmeow:PhysicalObject, gmeow:SocialObject) stays coherent — it is not forced to owl:Nothing — because each thing is individuated under a single top sortal (save the deliberately-preserved social∩information overlap)."
msgstr "Le positif competency case the top-sortal disjointness axioms doit satisfy: an individu typed dans exactement un de the quatre kernel top sortals (gmeow:Agent, gmeow:InformationObject, gmeow:PhysicalObject, gmeow:SocialObject) stays coherent — it n'est pas forced à owl:Nothing — parce que each thing est individuated sous a single top sortal (save the deliberately-preserved social∩information overlap)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/criterionPoleDistinctness|rdfs:label"
msgid "a criterion's reward and penalty poles are distinct"
msgstr "a criterion's reward and penalty poles are distinct"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/criterionPoleDistinctness|skos:definition"
msgid "Asserts that a gmeow:Criterion's gmeow:rewardPole and gmeow:penaltyPole must be distinct: one pole is no axis. The native coherence gate raises a violation when they coincide."
msgstr "Asserts qui a gmeow:Criterion's gmeow:rewardPole et gmeow:penaltyPole doit be distinct: one pole est no axis."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/crossMode|rdfs:label"
msgid "cross mode"
msgstr "cross mode"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/crossMode|skos:definition"
msgid "The mode of a logic:CrossNodeConstraint: 'co-occur' (the two roles must be present together) or 'differ' (the two roles must never bind the same value)."
msgstr "Le mode de a logic:CrossNodeConstraint: 'co-occur' (the two roles doit be present together) ou 'differ' (the two roles doit jamais bind the same valeur)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dagCycleWitness|rdfs:label"
msgid "DAG cycle witness"
msgstr "DAG cycle témoin"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dagCycleWitness|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates an `unsupported` DAG-workflow verdict to a disclosed offending edge or cycle member — the back-edge or logic:Iteration that places a plan outside the certified acyclic fragment — MULTI-valued (a graph may carry several cycles). Mirrors the witness-disclosure discipline of logic:forbiddenViolationWitness: the certifier never silently truncates a cyclic plan, it surfaces exactly which edges break acyclicity while the plan stays valid under a non-DAG contract. Domain a reasoning result or coherence outcome carrying the `unsupported` evaluation status, range a flow edge or process node (stated in prose)."
msgstr "Relates an `unsupported` DAG-workflow verdict à a disclosed offending edge ou cycle member — the back-edge ou logic:itération qui places a plan outside the certified acyclic fragment — MULTI-valued (a graphe peut carry several cycles)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dataflowConsumes|rdfs:label"
msgid "dataflow consumes"
msgstr "dataflow consumes"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dataflowConsumes|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a process node — a logic:Plan step, a pipeline stage, or a procedure step — to an upstream node whose product it reads: the canonical binary dataflow dependency, oriented consumer -> producer (an executor inverts it to schedule producers first). The transitive closure must be acyclic for the DAG-workflow profile (logic:DagWorkflowResource); a cycle takes the plan out of the certified acyclic fragment and is disclosed through logic:dagCycleWitness, never silently dropped. Domain and range a process node (stated in prose, matching the module's convention). The reified FLOW-GRAPH counterpart is logic:DataFlowEdge; downstream surfaces such as gmeow:dataflowConsumes specialize this property."
msgstr "Relates a process nœud — a logic:plan step, a pipeline stage, ou a procedure step — à an upstream nœud dont product it reads: the canonique binary dataflow dependency, oriented consumer -> producer (an executor inverts it à schedule producers first)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dataflowProduces|rdfs:label"
msgid "dataflow produces"
msgstr "dataflow produces"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dataflowProduces|skos:definition"
msgid "The inverse of logic:dataflowConsumes: relates a process node to a downstream node that reads its product (producer -> consumer). The canonical authored direction is logic:dataflowConsumes, so this inverse is normally left to be inferred rather than asserted. Domain and range a process node (stated in prose)."
msgstr "Le inverse de logic:dataflowConsumes: relie a process nœud à a downstream nœud qui reads its product (producer -> consumer)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/datumRecordedAt|rdfs:label"
msgid "datum recorded at"
msgstr "datum recorded at"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/datumRecordedAt|skos:definition"
msgid "The xsd:dateTime at which the datum supporting a guarded precondition situation was recorded — the start of the age span a logic:FreshnessGuard measures against its logic:freshnessHorizon. Domain a precondition situation, range xsd:dateTime (stated in prose). Compared against logic:decisionTime in a single timescale; a missing value under a declared freshness guard is a hard error, never a silent pass."
msgstr "Le xsd:dateTime at qui the datum supporting a guarded précondition situation was recorded — the start de the age span a logic:FreshnessGuard measures contre its logic:freshnessHorizon."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/deadlineWindow|rdfs:label"
msgid "deadline window"
msgstr "deadline window"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/deadlineWindow|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a deadline-window logic:GoalExpression to the bounding interval after which its window closes — until the window closes the evaluation is logic:GoalEvaluationUndetermined, and once it closes the judgment becomes conclusive. Domain logic:GoalExpression (stated in prose); the range is the bounding interval, left open in this standalone module. The companion of the goal's operand (its achievement or maintenance target). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:deadlineWindow only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a deadline-window logic:GoalExpression à the bounding interval après qui its window closes — until the window closes the evaluation est logic:GoalEvaluationUndetermined, et once it closes the judgment becomes conclusive."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/decisionTime|rdfs:label"
msgid "decision time"
msgstr "decision time"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/decisionTime|skos:definition"
msgid "The xsd:dateTime a logic:GateProbe is judged at — the \"now\" against which a logic:FreshnessGuard measures the age of a precondition datum. Domain logic:GateProbe, range xsd:dateTime (stated in prose). When a probe gates a schema carrying a freshness guard, a missing logic:decisionTime is a hard error, never a silent pass: the age comparison has no reference point and the evaluator refuses to guess."
msgstr "Le xsd:dateTime a logic:GateProbe est judged at — the \"now\" contre qui a logic:FreshnessGuard measures the age de a précondition datum."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/declaredIsolationLevel|rdfs:label"
msgid "declared isolation level"
msgstr "declared isolation niveau"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/declaredIsolationLevel|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to the logic:IsolationLevel guarantee strength its concurrent transactions must meet. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:IsolationLevel (stated in prose); at most one per contract, from the closed isolation-level set (a value outside it is a hard error). It is kept DISTINCT from logic:declaredProtocol (the mechanism that would enforce the level) and from logic:serializabilityCriterion (a history property): an isolation level is the guarantee STRENGTH required, neither the mechanism that achieves it nor the property a particular history happens to have. The native evaluator classifies whether the witnessed schedule meets this declared strength and records the result as logic:isolationLevelAdequacy."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract à the logic:IsolationLevel guarantee strength its concurrent transactions doit meet."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/declaredProtocol|rdfs:label"
msgid "declared protocol"
msgstr "declared protocol"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/declaredProtocol|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to the logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol its concurrent transactions are to be enforced under — the IMPLEMENTATION MECHANISM (strict / strong-strict two-phase locking, timestamp ordering, or optimistic validation) declared for the run. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol (stated in prose); at most one per contract, from the closed protocol set (a value outside it is a hard error). It is kept DISTINCT from the guarantee strength the mechanism is meant to achieve (logic:declaredIsolationLevel) and from the history property it produces (logic:serializabilityCriterion): a protocol is HOW a guarantee is enforced, never the guarantee itself. The native evaluator classifies whether the witnessed schedule respects this protocol's discipline over the run's recorded protocol events and records the verdict as logic:protocolEnforced."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract à the logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol its concurrent transactions sont à be enforced sous — the IMPLEMENTATION MECHANISM (strict / strong-strict two-phase locking, timestamp ordering, ou optimistic validation) declared pour the run."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/declaresColumn|rdfs:label"
msgid "declares column"
msgstr "declares colonne"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/declaresColumn|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ResultShape to a logic:ResultColumn it declares. Set-valued: a shape declares one column per SELECT variable it types. Domain logic:ResultShape, range logic:ResultColumn (stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:declaresColumn only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ResultShape à a logic:ResultColumn it declares."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/defaultClosure|rdfs:label"
msgid "default closure"
msgstr "default fermeture"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/defaultClosure|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to the logic:ClosureValue that is the default of its closure map — the open- or closed-world reading applied to any predicate or context key not overridden by a logic:closureEntry. The closure facet is a map; this is its default, normally open-world, with closed-world confined to keys inside a logic:WorldBoundary. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:ClosureValue (stated in prose, matching the module's convention)."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract à the logic:ClosureValue qui est the default de its fermeture map — the ouvert- ou monde fermé reading applied à tout prédicat ou contexte key not overridden par a logic:closureEntry."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/defaultLadderProfile|rdfs:label"
msgid "default ladder projection profile"
msgstr "default ladder projection profil"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/defaultLadderProfile|skos:definition"
msgid "The shipped default logic:LadderProjectionProfile the coarse-ladder projection rules read: awareness ≥ emerging emits gmeow:isAwareOf, declarative familiarity ≥ competent emits gmeow:knowsAbout, conceptual understanding ≥ competent emits gmeow:understands, and procedural competence ≥ strong together with transfer ≥ strong emit gmeow:hasMastered."
msgstr "Le shipped default logic:LadderProjectionProfile the coarse-ladder projection rules read: awareness ≥ emerging emits gmeow:isAwareOf, declarative familiarity ≥ competent emits gmeow:knowsAbout, conceptual understanding ≥ competent emits gmeow:understands, et procedural competence ≥ strong together avec transfer ≥ strong emit gmeow:hasMastered."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/defeasibleStrength|rdfs:label"
msgid "defeasible strength"
msgstr "defeasible strength"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/defeasibleStrength|skos:definition"
msgid "A solver-layer measure of how strongly a logic:DefeasibleEvidence supports its logic:evidenceFor target before any defeater — a ranking annotation, never asserted as a reasoned axiom and never a probability. Range is left open (an ordinal label or a numeric weight), stated in prose."
msgstr "Un solver-layer measure de how strongly a logic:DefeasibleEvidence supports its logic:evidenceFor target avant tout defeater — a ranking annotation, jamais asserted as a reasoned axiom et jamais a probability."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/del|rdfs:label"
msgid "del"
msgstr "del"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/del|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:DeleteUpdate to the support/fact it retires. The `del(F)` primitive removes F from the active support set of the successor state, records supersession provenance, and leaves the predecessor state and historical support intact. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:del only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:DeleteUpdate à the support/fact it retires."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/deonticallyIdeal|rdfs:label"
msgid "deontically ideal"
msgstr "deontically ideal"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/deonticallyIdeal|skos:definition"
msgid "The typed deontic accessibility relation: a context is deontically ideal — an ought-world — relative to an issuer. Deontic reasoning is a USE of typed contexts, not a separate context type: a deontic claim is truth in the deontically-ideal accessible contexts of an issuer. Deontic accessibility is serial — every context from which an obligation is read has at least one accessible ideal context — so the 'satisfied in every ideal context' condition is never vacuously true; an empty ideal set yields undetermined rather than vacuous truth. logic:accessibleFrom is its generic superproperty in prose only — NOT asserted rdfs:subPropertyOf — so what is ideal never leaks into what is."
msgstr "Le typed deontic accessibility relation: a contexte est deontically ideal — an ought-monde — relative à an issuer."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/deonticallyIncompatible|rdfs:label"
msgid "deontically incompatible"
msgstr "deontically incompatible"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/deonticallyIncompatible|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates two gmeow:Goals whose conjunction a norm makes impermissible even where it is physically reachable. Domain gmeow:Goal, range gmeow:Goal (stated in prose). One of seven conflict relations between independently-meaningful goals, weaker than gmeow:counterGoal (constitutive opposition). Deontic force arrives with the norms vocabulary, which ranges over goals — the dependency points toward the goal layer, never the reverse."
msgstr "Relates two gmeow:Goals dont conjunction a norm makes impermissible even où it est physically reachable."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/derivedHistory|rdfs:label"
msgid "derived history"
msgstr "dérivé historique"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/derivedHistory|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:TransactionOutcome of a logic:ConcurrentComposition run to the logic:ConcurrentHistory the native evaluator derived from the interleaved execution of its two legs. Domain logic:TransactionOutcome, range logic:ConcurrentHistory (stated in prose). It SEPARATES the executional-entailment verdict (the outcome — does a path exist) from the derived concurrency surface (the history — how the conflicting operations were ordered and whether that ordering is serializable): a concurrent run records BOTH, linked by this property, so neither the verdict nor the serializability finding is conflated with the other."
msgstr "Relates a logic:TransactionOutcome de a logic:ConcurrentComposition run à the logic:ConcurrentHistory the native evaluator dérivé de the interleaved exécution de its two legs."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/designatedValues|rdfs:label"
msgid "designated values"
msgstr "designated values"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/designatedValues|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to the logic:DesignatedValueSet it selects — which truth values count as holding for consequence. Single-valued on the contract. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:DesignatedValueSet (stated in prose, matching the module's convention). One of the three independent truth-facet components; it must not be conflated with logic:admissibleValuation, since FDE and LP share a designated set and differ only in their admissible valuations."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract à the logic:DesignatedValueSet it selects — qui vérité values count as holding pour consequence."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dimensionAwareness|rdfs:label"
msgid "dimension: awareness"
msgstr "dimension: awareness"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dimensionAwareness|skos:definition"
msgid "The awareness dimension: whether the agent registers the subject at all. The shallowest factored axis; the source of the gmeow:isAwareOf rung of the coarse knowledge ladder under a declared threshold."
msgstr "Le awareness dimension: whether the agent registers the subject at tous."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dimensionCalibration|rdfs:label"
msgid "dimension: calibration"
msgstr "dimension: calibration"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dimensionCalibration|skos:definition"
msgid "The calibration dimension: whether the agent's confidence matches its accuracy. Assessed against an explicit forecast protocol (a forecast/outcome series, a scoring rule, a reference class and observation window), kept apart from a single logic:confidence value and from the metacognition vocabulary's qualitative gmeow:CalibrationStatus."
msgstr "Le calibration dimension: whether the agent's confidence matches its accuracy."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dimensionConceptualUnderstanding|rdfs:label"
msgid "dimension: conceptual understanding"
msgstr "dimension: conceptual understanding"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dimensionConceptualUnderstanding|skos:definition"
msgid "The conceptual-understanding dimension: whether the agent grasps WHY — the structure behind the facts, beyond reciting them. The source of the gmeow:understands rung of the coarse knowledge ladder under a declared threshold."
msgstr "Le conceptual-understanding dimension: whether the agent grasps WHY — the structure behind the facts, beyond reciting them."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dimensionDeclarativeFamiliarity|rdfs:label"
msgid "dimension: declarative familiarity"
msgstr "dimension: declarative familiarity"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dimensionDeclarativeFamiliarity|skos:definition"
msgid "The declarative-familiarity dimension: what the agent knows THAT — the facts it can state about the subject. The source of the gmeow:knowsAbout rung of the coarse knowledge ladder under a declared threshold."
msgstr "Le declarative-familiarity dimension: what the agent knows THAT — the facts it peut état about the subject."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dimensionExplanatoryAbility|rdfs:label"
msgid "dimension: explanatory ability"
msgstr "dimension: explanatory ability"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dimensionExplanatoryAbility|skos:definition"
msgid "The explanatory-ability dimension: whether the agent can produce an account others can follow and check — the seam to the solver-layer gmeow:explanatoryScore and gmeow:systematicity measurements, which feed this dimension but are never asserted as reasoned axioms."
msgstr "Le explanatory-ability dimension: whether the agent peut produce an account others peut follow et vérification — the seam à the solver-layer gmeow:explanatoryScore et gmeow:systematicity measurements, qui feed this dimension mais sont jamais asserted as reasoned axioms."


msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dimensionMetacognition|rdfs:label"
msgid "dimension: metacognition"
msgstr "dimension: metacognition"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dimensionMetacognition|skos:definition"
msgid "The metacognition dimension: whether the agent models its own competence, including the limits of its own knowledge. Reads the metacognition vocabulary's second-order posture — gmeow:awareOfNotKnowing, gmeow:epistemicSelfTrust, and reflection that can defeat one's own inference — as its subject."
msgstr "Le metacognition dimension: whether the agent models its own competence, including the limits de its own connaissance."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dimensionProceduralCompetence|rdfs:label"
msgid "dimension: procedural competence"
msgstr "dimension: procedural competence"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dimensionProceduralCompetence|skos:definition"
msgid "The procedural-competence dimension: what the agent knows HOW to do — its working command of the subject. Read together with the transfer dimension, the source of the gmeow:hasMastered rung of the coarse knowledge ladder under a declared threshold."
msgstr "Le procedural-competence dimension: what the agent knows HOW à do — its working command de the subject."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dimensionReliability|rdfs:label"
msgid "dimension: reliability"
msgstr "dimension: reliability"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dimensionReliability|skos:definition"
msgid "The reliability dimension: how dependably an agent or engine reasons as a disposition, relative to a reference class (a task, domain, or distribution) and read from MANY results with their expected or observed outcomes — a metric over the series (accuracy, soundness-violation rate, recall, calibration, robustness) across a stated interval. Distinct from the single-run logic:ResultAssurance: a reliable reasoner may correctly return a contradiction verdict on contradictory input, and a completed internally-supported result may still be wrong, so reliability is never read from one result's assurance. The dimension design §Result assurance and reasoner reliability are distinct introduces alongside the eight factored dimensions."
msgstr "Le reliability dimension: how dependably an agent ou engine reasons as a disposition, relative à a reference class (a task, domaine, ou distribution) et read de MANY results avec their expected ou observed outcomes — a metric sur the series (accuracy, soundness-violation rate, recall, calibration, robustness) across a stated interval."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dimensionTransfer|rdfs:label"
msgid "dimension: transfer"
msgstr "dimension: transfer"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dimensionTransfer|skos:definition"
msgid "The transfer dimension: whether competence in one context carries to another — the axis a single ordinal ladder most conspicuously hides, since fluency in a narrow task says nothing about generalization. Read together with procedural competence, the source of the gmeow:hasMastered rung of the coarse knowledge ladder under a declared threshold."
msgstr "Le transfer dimension: whether competence dans one contexte porte à another — the axis a single ordinal ladder most conspicuously hides, since fluency dans a narrow task says nothing about generalization."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dischargeObligation|rdfs:label"
msgid "discharge obligation"
msgstr "acquittement obligation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dischargeObligation|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates an individual to an anti-rigid type it instantiates contingently, carrying the standing obligation to construct or cite a world of existence in which the individual lacks that type (the anti-rigidity witness). The instance-level diagnostic the anti-rigidity lowering emits under the witness-obligation policy (the default; LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md §Anti-rigidity needs a witness policy): for an individual x typed by an anti-rigid Role or Phase T in a world, a logic:dischargeObligation fact is entailed in that world. It is an obligation, NOT a violation — anti-rigid instantiation is licensed on the promise that the counter-world is satisfiable on demand (its construction happens on demand); the lighter schema-only policy emits nothing instance-level, the stricter witness-required policy emits logic:witnessRequiredViolation instead. Like the other derived diagnostics it is never asserted by hand."
msgstr "Relates an individu à an anti-rigid type it instantiates contingently, carrying the standing obligation à construct ou cite a monde de existence dans qui the individu lacks qui type (the anti-rigidity témoin)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dischargesSectionObligation|rdfs:label"
msgid "discharges section obligation"
msgstr "discharges section obligation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/dischargesSectionObligation|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:SectionAcceptanceWitness to the section obligation (an IRI) its executed get/put round-trip discharges. Domain logic:SectionAcceptanceWitness (stated in prose). Exactly the edge whose absence makes the discharge unfalsifiable: a section witness that names no obligation asserts a round-trip without saying which law it satisfies. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:dischargesSectionObligation only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:SectionAcceptanceWitness à the section obligation (an IRI) its executed get/put round-trip discharges."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/disjoint|rdfs:label"
msgid "disjoint"
msgstr "disjoint"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/disjoint|skos:definition"
msgid "Mereological disjointness: two entities share no part — the negation of logic:overlaps. A primitive notion of profiled mereology, settled (alongside logic:overlaps) before weak supplementation is stated, so logic:WeakSupplementation is never applied to wholes for which overlap is undefined. The 'another part disjoint from the first' clause of weak supplementation is read against this relation (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Mereological disjointness: two entities share no part — the negation de logic:overlaps."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/distinctBody|rdfs:label"
msgid "distinct body"
msgstr "distinct body"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/distinctBody|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Rule to an inequality body guard: a reified node carrying rdf:subject and rdf:object (two rule variables, and — unlike logic:body — no rdf:predicate) that must bind to DISTINCT values for the rule to fire, projecting to the Datalog/Nemo inequality constraint ?A != ?B. Parallel to logic:negatedBody as an additive rule-structural surface: it lets a rule detect 'at least two distinct values' (e.g. a class carrying more than one stereotype, or a relator mediating two distinct relata) that set-semantic Datalog cannot otherwise express. An inequality guard introduces no negative dependency edge, so it leaves a rule's stratification class unchanged."
msgstr "Relates a logic:règle à an inequality body guard: a reified nœud carrying rdf:subject et rdf:object (two règle variables, et — unlike logic:body — no rdf:prédicat) qui doit bind à DISTINCT values pour the règle à fire, projecting à the Datalog/Nemo inequality contrainte ?Un != ?B."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/distinctnessRole|rdfs:label"
msgid "distinctness role"
msgstr "distinctness role"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/distinctnessRole|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:RelatumDistinctnessAssertion to one of the two roles that must bind distinct values on a focus node. Exactly two are asserted per record; the native coherence gate raises a violation when both roles bind the same value on one focus node. Domain logic:RelatumDistinctnessAssertion; two-valued. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:distinctnessRole only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:RelatumDistinctnessAssertion à one de the two roles qui doit bind distinct values sur a focus nœud."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/distinctnessTarget|rdfs:label"
msgid "distinctness target"
msgstr "distinctness target"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/distinctnessTarget|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:RelatumDistinctnessAssertion to the class whose focus nodes it constrains (the relator class). Read together with logic:distinctnessRole, it tells the native coherence gate which class bears the mutual-inequality condition. Domain logic:RelatumDistinctnessAssertion; single-valued. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:distinctnessTarget only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:RelatumDistinctnessAssertion à the class dont focus nodes it constrains (the relator class)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/doxasticallyAccessible|rdfs:label"
msgid "doxastically accessible"
msgstr "doxastically accessible"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/doxasticallyAccessible|skos:definition"
msgid "The typed doxastic accessibility relation between gmeow:EpistemicContexts — what an agent's beliefs hold accessible. It need not be reflexive (an agent may believe a falsehood); this character is documented in prose, not asserted as an OWL characteristic, matching the kernel convention. logic:accessibleFrom is its generic superproperty in prose only — NOT asserted rdfs:subPropertyOf — so the bare superproperty licenses no cross-type entailment and what is believed never leaks into what is true."
msgstr "Le typed doxastic accessibility relation entre gmeow:EpistemicContexts — what an agent's beliefs hold accessible."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/editionOfFunctionality|rdfs:label"
msgid "editionOf is functional"
msgstr "editionOf is functional"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/editionOfFunctionality|skos:definition"
msgid "Asserts on the canonical carrier that gmeow:editionOf is functional: an edition editions exactly one work, as its skos:definition states. Functionality is enforced by gmeow:editionOf's owl:FunctionalProperty declaration through native DL consistency; this records the characteristic on the canonical carrier."
msgstr "Asserts sur the canonique carrier qui gmeow:editionOf est functional: an edition editions exactement un work, as its skos:définition states."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/effect|rdfs:label"
msgid "effect"
msgstr "effet"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/effect|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ActionSchema to the change it introduces, expressed as the supersession primitives of the transaction layer (ins/del), NEVER as physical erasure — executing an occurrence is the elementary update whose ins/del a transaction path records. Domain logic:ActionSchema (stated in prose). One of the eight action-theory facets."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ActionSchema à the change it introduces, expressed as the supersession primitives de the transaction layer (ins/del), NEVER as physical erasure — executing an occurrence est the elementary update dont ins/del a transaction chemin records."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/engine|rdfs:label"
msgid "engine"
msgstr "engine"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/engine|skos:definition"
msgid "The engine identity + version that produced a logic:ReasoningResult. Single-valued. Domain logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:engine only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le engine identité + version qui produced a logic:ReasoningResult."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/epistemicallyPossible|rdfs:label"
msgid "epistemically possible"
msgstr "epistemically possible"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/epistemicallyPossible|skos:definition"
msgid "The typed alethic accessibility relation between logic:PossibleWorlds — a world is epistemically (alethically) accessible from another. logic:accessibleFrom is its generic superproperty in prose only: it is NOT asserted rdfs:subPropertyOf logic:accessibleFrom, because the generic superproperty licenses no cross-type entailment and a subproperty edge would manufacture exactly that inference. The modal operators are the standard translation over THIS relation, never over a blurred union of accessibility relations. It asserts no OWL characteristic; its logical character is documented in prose, matching the kernel convention."
msgstr "Le typed alethic accessibility relation entre logic:PossibleWorlds — a monde est epistemically (alethically) accessible de another."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/equalityPolicy|rdfs:label"
msgid "equality policy"
msgstr "equality politique"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/equalityPolicy|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to the logic:EqualityPolicy it selects — when two terms denote one entity. Single-valued on the contract. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:EqualityPolicy (stated in prose, matching the module's convention). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:equalityPolicy only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract à the logic:EqualityPolicy it selects — lorsque two terms denote one entity."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/evaluatedAgainst|rdfs:label"
msgid "evaluated against"
msgstr "evaluated against"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/evaluatedAgainst|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:GoalEvaluation to the situation or world it is judged against. Domain logic:GoalEvaluation (stated in prose); the range ranges over a situation (logic:Situation) or a world/context, left open in this standalone module. One of the subjects in the identifying tuple of an evaluation. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:evaluatedAgainst only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:GoalEvaluation à the situation ou monde it est judged against."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/evaluatesGoal|rdfs:label"
msgid "evaluates goal"
msgstr "evaluates objectif"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/evaluatesGoal|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:GoalEvaluation to the gmeow:Goal it judges. Domain logic:GoalEvaluation, range gmeow:Goal (stated in prose). One of the subjects in the identifying tuple of an evaluation (goal, situation/world, evaluator, time, criterion). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:evaluatesGoal only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:GoalEvaluation à the gmeow:objectif it judges."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/evaluationCriterion|rdfs:label"
msgid "evaluation criterion"
msgstr "evaluation criterion"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/evaluationCriterion|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:GoalEvaluation to the criterion applied in reaching its judgment — the standard against which satisfaction, feasibility, and the quantities are read. Domain logic:GoalEvaluation (stated in prose). One of the subjects in the identifying tuple of an evaluation; two evaluations differing only in criterion are distinct records. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:evaluationCriterion only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:GoalEvaluation à the criterion applied dans reaching its judgment — the standard contre qui satisfaction, feasibility, et the quantities sont read."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/evaluationEvaluator|rdfs:label"
msgid "evaluation evaluator"
msgstr "evaluation evaluator"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/evaluationEvaluator|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:GoalEvaluation to the vantage holding the judgment — the evaluator the record is attributed to. Domain logic:GoalEvaluation (stated in prose). Aligns with gmeow:accordingTo: a goal evaluation is a vantage-indexed claim, never a global verdict, so two evaluators who disagree are two coexisting evaluations rather than one elected winner (Principle 9). One of the subjects in the identifying tuple of an evaluation."
msgstr "Relates a logic:GoalEvaluation à the vantage holding the judgment — the evaluator the record est attributed to."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/evaluationTime|rdfs:label"
msgid "evaluation time"
msgstr "evaluation time"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/evaluationTime|skos:definition"
msgid "The time of judgment component of the logic:GoalEvaluation identifying tuple: when this evaluation was made. Domain logic:GoalEvaluation (stated in prose); range xsd:dateTime (a full ISO-8601 instant, never xsd:date). Two evaluations of the same goal, situation, evaluator, and criterion made at different times are distinct records. When no explicit time is recorded the identifying tuple component is absent, not defaulted — absence means the time of judgment is unspecified rather than unknown."
msgstr "Le time de judgment component de the logic:GoalEvaluation identifying tuple: lorsque this evaluation was made."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/evidenceFor|rdfs:label"
msgid "evidence for"
msgstr "preuve for"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/evidenceFor|skos:definition"
msgid "The relation or claim a logic:DefeasibleEvidence defeasibly supports — the 'to' side (e.g. gmeow:knowsAbout). Defeasible support, never strict entailment: the supported edge is not materialized from the evidence under the default reasoning. Range is left open (a property or a claim), stated in prose."
msgstr "Le relation ou claim a logic:DefeasibleEvidence defeasibly supports — the 'to' side (e.g."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/evidenceProperty|rdfs:label"
msgid "evidence property"
msgstr "preuve propriété"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/evidenceProperty|skos:definition"
msgid "The evidential relation a logic:DefeasibleEvidence declares to bear defeasibly on another — the 'from' side (e.g. gmeow:hasSkill). Range is left open (a property or a claim), stated in prose; the object is used by punning, the gmeow:pairsWith convention. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:evidenceProperty only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le evidential relation a logic:DefeasibleEvidence déclare à bear defeasibly sur another — the 'from' side (e.g."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/evidenceStrength|rdfs:label"
msgid "evidence strength"
msgstr "preuve strength"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/evidenceStrength|skos:definition"
msgid "Evidential support for a statement, provenance-derived and reusing the evidence-slice warrant axes (source tier, evidence class): how well-warranted a claim is by its evidence. Normatively distinct from logic:probability, logic:confidence, and logic:weight — an evidential warrant is not a calibrated probability, an asserter's confidence, or a solver ranking, and is not interchangeable with any of them."
msgstr "Evidential support pour a statement, provenance-dérivé et reusing the preuve-slice warrant axes (source tier, preuve class): how well-warranted a claim est par its preuve."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/evolution|rdfs:label"
msgid "evolution"
msgstr "evolution"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/evolution|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to the logic:EvolutionMode it selects — whether and how state changes. Single-valued on the contract. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:EvolutionMode (stated in prose, matching the module's convention). Evolution is independent of the model-semantics facet, which is why state-change reasoning (logic:TransactionPathEvolution) is a facet value, never a parallel profile."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract à the logic:EvolutionMode it selects — whether et how état changes."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/executedAlongPath|rdfs:label"
msgid "executed along path"
msgstr "executed along chemin"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/executedAlongPath|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a program run — a logic:Plan or a logic:TransactionOutcome — to the logic:Path along which it executed: the executed history that realizes the program. Domain logic:Plan or logic:TransactionOutcome, range logic:Path (stated in prose). This is the one link the four-notion chain intention -> plan -> action -> transaction-path did not already have: intention reaches its goal and action through gmeow:intentionGoal / gmeow:motivates, a logic:Plan reaches the same goal through logic:planGoal, and an action occurrence reaches its type through logic:instantiatesSchema, but no existing term tied a program to the run that executed it. It CONNECTS the program to its path but does NOT subsume either: a plan is the program (what is intended to be done), a path is the executed run (how state actually changed); the link records that this program ran along that history without conflating the two."
msgstr "Relates a program run — a logic:plan ou a logic:TransactionOutcome — à the logic:chemin along qui it executed: the executed historique qui realizes the program."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/executedHypotheticallyAs|rdfs:label"
msgid "executed hypothetically as"
msgstr "executed hypothetically as"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/executedHypotheticallyAs|skos:definition"
msgid "The content-addressed witness (a digest) of a hypothetical (sandbox) transaction run: present on a logic:TransactionOutcome exactly when the program executed under logic:HypotheticalExecution, recording the identity of the discarded run whose verdict (logic:transactionSucceeds) was computed without committing its effects. The run's effect substrate — the executed logic:Path, the per-step logic:TransactionStep records, and the supersession quads — is intentionally ABSENT, because the sandbox operator tests without committing; this digest is therefore the sole standing trace that the run occurred and what it ranged over. Nothing is asserted to be erased, only never emitted, so suppression-never-erasure holds for free. Single-valued. Domain logic:TransactionOutcome, range xsd:string (stated in prose). The committed counterpart (logic:CommittedExecution) emits the full effect substrate and carries no such witness."
msgstr "Le content-addressed témoin (a digest) de a hypothetical (sandbox) transaction run: present sur a logic:TransactionOutcome exactly lorsque the program executed sous logic:HypotheticalExecution, recording the identité de the discarded run dont verdict (logic:transactionSucceeds) was computed sans committing its effects."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/executedUnderContract|rdfs:label"
msgid "executed under contract"
msgstr "executed under contract"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/executedUnderContract|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a transaction-program node — a transaction-program combinator root (logic:SerialConjunction, logic:Choice, logic:Fallback, or logic:Iteration) marked executable by logic:transitionFromState — to the logic:ReasoningContract it executes under, whose logic:executionMode selects whether the program's effects are committed (logic:CommittedExecution, the default) or discarded (logic:HypotheticalExecution, the sandbox operator). This is the link by which a program reaches the execution-commitment facet: without it the contract-level logic:executionMode could not select commit-versus-discard for a concrete run. Single-valued — a program names at most one governing contract; absence resolves to the default committed execution. Domain a transaction-program node, range logic:ReasoningContract (stated in prose, matching the module's domain/range convention)."
msgstr "Relates a transaction-program nœud — a transaction-program combinator root (logic:SerialConjunction, logic:Choice, logic:Fallback, ou logic:itération) marked executable par logic:transitionFromState — à the logic:ReasoningContract it executes under, dont logic:executionMode selects whether the program's effects sont committed (logic:CommittedExecution, the default) ou discarded (logic:HypotheticalExecution, the sandbox opérateur)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/executionMode|rdfs:label"
msgid "execution mode"
msgstr "exécution mode"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/executionMode|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to the logic:ExecutionMode it selects — whether transaction effects are committed (logic:CommittedExecution, the default) or discarded (logic:HypotheticalExecution, the sandbox operator). Single-valued on the contract. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:ExecutionMode (stated in prose, matching the module's domain/range convention). Independent of logic:evolution: a hypothetical run may compose with any evolution mode. This facet carries the sandbox operator, which is distinct from modal possibility — modal possibility is computed as the standard translation over the appropriate typed accessibility relation (logic:epistemicallyPossible / logic:doxasticallyAccessible), never over the bare logic:accessibleFrom superproperty and never reified as a possibility class."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract à the logic:ExecutionMode it selects — whether transaction effects sont committed (logic:CommittedExecution, the default) ou discarded (logic:HypotheticalExecution, the sandbox opérateur)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/exists|rdfs:label"
msgid "exists"
msgstr "exists"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/exists|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates an existential-quantifier logic:Formula to its body formula. The bound variables are carried by logic:quantifiedVariable. Existential witnesses are Skolemized only at the evaluable-lowering layer; the AST node pins the binder and body, not the witness identity."
msgstr "Relates an existential-quantifier logic:formule à its body formule."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/expandsToFacet|rdfs:label"
msgid "expands to facet"
msgstr "expands to facet"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/expandsToFacet|skos:definition"
msgid "Links a logic:ReasoningPreset to a facet value it expands to. A preset's full facet selection is the set of its logic:expandsToFacet values plus any facet-specific properties; the compiler expands the preset to this bundle before reasoning, so a preset reference and its expanded facet set are interchangeable. Domain logic:ReasoningPreset (stated in prose, matching the module's convention). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:expandsToFacet only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Links a logic:ReasoningPreset à a facet valeur it expands to."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/expectsInputShape|rdfs:label"
msgid "expects input shape"
msgstr "expects input forme"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/expectsInputShape|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a query (or a competency question) to the logic:ResultShape its input is expected to satisfy. The producer feeding the query must satisfy this shape (structural input→output compatibility) BEFORE execution; a mismatch is a hard, surfaced error. Single-valued. Range logic:ResultShape (stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:expectsInputShape only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a requête (or a competency question) à the logic:ResultShape its input est expected à satisfy."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/expressivenessBoundary|rdfs:label"
msgid "expressiveness boundary"
msgstr "expressiveness boundary"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/expressivenessBoundary|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a defining law or a loss-ledger boundary record to the logic:ExpressivenessBoundary its statement inhabits. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:expressivenessBoundary only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a defining loi ou a loss-ledger boundary record à the logic:ExpressivenessBoundary its statement inhabits."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/feasibilityStatus|rdfs:label"
msgid "feasibility status"
msgstr "feasibility status"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/feasibilityStatus|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:GoalEvaluation to the logic:FeasibilityStatus it carries — the feasibility axis of the factored outcome. Domain logic:GoalEvaluation, range logic:FeasibilityStatus (stated in prose). Varies independently of satisfaction, lifecycle, and goal-evaluation status. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:feasibilityStatus only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:GoalEvaluation à the logic:FeasibilityStatus it porte — the feasibility axis de the factored résultat."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/flowFrom|rdfs:label"
msgid "flow from"
msgstr "flux from"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/flowFrom|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a reified flow edge (logic:ControlFlowEdge or logic:DataFlowEdge) to its source process node — the predecessor in a control-flow edge, the producer in a dataflow edge. Domain a flow edge, range a process node (stated in prose). Paired with logic:flowTo; the two mediation legs that make a flow edge a well-formed Relator. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:flowFrom only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a reified flux edge (logic:ControlFlowEdge ou logic:DataFlowEdge) à its source process nœud — the predecessor dans a contrôle-flux edge, the producer dans a dataflow edge."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/flowTo|rdfs:label"
msgid "flow to"
msgstr "flux to"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/flowTo|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a reified flow edge (logic:ControlFlowEdge or logic:DataFlowEdge) to its target process node — the successor in a control-flow edge, the consumer in a dataflow edge. Domain a flow edge, range a process node (stated in prose). Paired with logic:flowFrom. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:flowTo only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a reified flux edge (logic:ControlFlowEdge ou logic:DataFlowEdge) à its target process nœud — the successor dans a contrôle-flux edge, the consumer dans a dataflow edge."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/forall|rdfs:label"
msgid "for all"
msgstr "for tous"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/forall|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a universal-quantifier logic:Formula to its body formula. The bound variables are carried by logic:quantifiedVariable; their block order is significant. Universal quantification ranges over individuals in the domain of discourse (the object level stays first-order). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:forall only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a universel-quantifier logic:formule à its body formule."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/forbiddenPredicate|rdfs:label"
msgid "forbidden predicate"
msgstr "forbidden prédicat"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/forbiddenPredicate|skos:definition"
msgid "The forbidden predicate of a logic:ForbiddenPatternConstraint: the focus must carry no value on this predicate (or, when logic:forbiddenValue is present, not that specific value)."
msgstr "Le forbidden prédicat de a logic:ForbiddenPatternConstraint: the focus doit carry no valeur sur this prédicat (or, lorsque logic:forbiddenValue est present, not qui specific valeur)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/forbiddenValue|rdfs:label"
msgid "forbidden value"
msgstr "forbidden valeur"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/forbiddenValue|skos:definition"
msgid "An optional fixed object value that narrows a logic:ForbiddenPatternConstraint to forbid only forbiddenPredicate(this, value) rather than any value on the predicate. An IRI or a literal."
msgstr "Un facultatif fixed object valeur qui narrows a logic:ForbiddenPatternConstraint à forbid uniquement forbiddenPredicate(this, valeur) plutôt que tout valeur sur the prédicat."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/forbiddenViolationWitness|rdfs:label"
msgid "forbidden violation witness"
msgstr "forbidden violation témoin"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/forbiddenViolationWitness|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a coherence outcome to a within-world contradiction the contract FORBIDS (a logic:FindingContradictionWitness) — MULTI-valued. A NON-EMPTY set blocks issuance: a logic:CoherenceCertificate is issued only when this set is empty. Domain logic:CoherenceCertificate or logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation (stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:forbiddenViolationWitness only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a cohérence résultat à a within-monde contradiction the contract FORBIDS (a logic:FindingContradictionWitness) — MULTI-valued."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/formalizes|rdfs:label"
msgid "formalizes"
msgstr "formalizes"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/formalizes|skos:definition"
msgid "A bridge annotation from a logic: foundational term to the gmeow: domain concept it formalizes: the central reasoning vocabulary (argumentation semantics, Belnap information states) names the domain construct that mirrors it, so the domain term's documentation can surface the formalization without the domain slice ever asserting a logic: triple. Subject is a logic: term, object a gmeow: term, both stated in prose; an annotation property, never a reasoned axiom, so it carries no DL or EL profile weight."
msgstr "Un pont annotation de a logic: foundational terme à the gmeow: domaine concept it formalizes: the central raisonnement vocabulary (argumentation sémantique, Belnap information states) nomme the domaine construct qui mirrors it, so the domaine terme's documentation peut surface the formalisation sans the domaine slice ever asserting a logic: triple."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/formulaFragment|rdfs:label"
msgid "formula fragment"
msgstr "formule fragment"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/formulaFragment|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to the logic:FormulaFragment it selects — the syntactic class of admitted formulae. Single-valued on the contract. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:FormulaFragment (stated in prose, matching the module's convention). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:formulaFragment only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract à the logic:FormulaFragment it selects — the syntactic class de admitted formulae."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/freshnessGuard|rdfs:label"
msgid "freshness guard"
msgstr "fraîcheur guard"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/freshnessGuard|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ActionSchema to a logic:FreshnessGuard it carries — the valid-time currency guard on one of its preconditions. Domain logic:ActionSchema, range logic:FreshnessGuard (stated in prose). MULTI-valued: a schema may guard several preconditions, each with its own horizon. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:freshnessGuard only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ActionSchema à a logic:FreshnessGuard it porte — the valid-time currency guard sur one de its preconditions."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/freshnessHorizon|rdfs:label"
msgid "freshness horizon"
msgstr "fraîcheur horizon"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/freshnessHorizon|skos:definition"
msgid "The maximum admissible age of a guarded precondition datum, as an xsd:duration measured from the datum's logic:datumRecordedAt to the probe's logic:decisionTime. Domain logic:FreshnessGuard, range xsd:duration (stated in prose). Only fixed-length designators are admissible (weeks / days / hours / minutes / seconds); a nominal-length designator (years / months, which are not fixed spans) is a hard error, because the age comparison would be ill-defined."
msgstr "Le maximum admissible age de a guarded précondition datum, as an xsd:duration measured de the datum's logic:datumRecordedAt à the probe's logic:decisionTime."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/freshnessWindow|rdfs:label"
msgid "freshness window"
msgstr "fraîcheur window"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/freshnessWindow|skos:definition"
msgid "Marks that a logic:FreshnessGuard carries an EXPLICIT absolute valid-time interval — the closed [logic:freshnessWindowStart, logic:freshnessWindowEnd] window within which the guarded datum is authoritative, DISTINCT from and orthogonal to the age ceiling logic:freshnessHorizon. This is GMEOW's native subsumption of an openEHR decision-rule 'time_window' annotation (a named bounding interval such as 'the current episode'), as opposed to 'currency' (a max age → logic:freshnessHorizon). Domain logic:FreshnessGuard, range a string literal naming the window (stated in prose); the interval bounds are carried by logic:freshnessWindowStart / logic:freshnessWindowEnd. The property is OPTIONAL: ABSENT-WINDOW SEMANTICS impose NO constraint on this axis — a guard with no logic:freshnessWindow is gated by its logic:freshnessHorizon alone (or, if it declares neither, by nothing). When PRESENT, a probe whose logic:decisionTime falls OUTSIDE the closed interval yields logic:GateUndetermined (not admitted, not denied) — the datum is undetermined off-window, never stale-but-used — with a logic:gateUndeterminedReason naming the window bounds and the decision time. Independent of the age horizon: a datum can be within its horizon yet outside its window, or vice versa; the first axis to fail is reported."
msgstr "Marks qui a logic:FreshnessGuard porte an EXPLICIT absolute valid-time interval — the closed [logic:freshnessWindowStart, logic:freshnessWindowEnd] window within qui the guarded datum est authoritative, DISTINCT de et orthogonal à the age ceiling logic:freshnessHorizon."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/freshnessWindowEnd|rdfs:label"
msgid "freshness window end"
msgstr "fraîcheur window end"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/freshnessWindowEnd|skos:definition"
msgid "The inclusive upper bound of a logic:FreshnessGuard's explicit valid-time logic:freshnessWindow, as an xsd:dateTime. Domain logic:FreshnessGuard, range xsd:dateTime (stated in prose). Together with logic:freshnessWindowStart it defines the closed absolute interval [start, end] within which the guarded datum is authoritative; a probe's logic:decisionTime after this end falls outside the window and yields logic:GateUndetermined. This axis is DISTINCT from the age ceiling logic:freshnessHorizon — it bounds WHEN the decision may be taken, not how OLD the datum may be. Required exactly once when a window is declared (paired with logic:freshnessWindowStart); a declared window with a missing bound, a malformed xsd:dateTime, or end before start is a hard error. When no window is declared this bound is absent and the window axis imposes no constraint."
msgstr "Le inclusive upper bound de a logic:FreshnessGuard's explicit valid-time logic:freshnessWindow, as an xsd:dateTime."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/freshnessWindowStart|rdfs:label"
msgid "freshness window start"
msgstr "fraîcheur window start"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/freshnessWindowStart|skos:definition"
msgid "The inclusive lower bound of a logic:FreshnessGuard's explicit valid-time logic:freshnessWindow, as an xsd:dateTime. Domain logic:FreshnessGuard, range xsd:dateTime (stated in prose). Together with logic:freshnessWindowEnd it defines the closed absolute interval [start, end] within which the guarded datum is authoritative; a probe's logic:decisionTime before this start falls outside the window and yields logic:GateUndetermined. This axis is DISTINCT from the age ceiling logic:freshnessHorizon — it bounds WHEN the decision may be taken, not how OLD the datum may be. Required exactly once when a window is declared (paired with logic:freshnessWindowEnd); a declared window with a missing bound, a malformed xsd:dateTime, or end before start is a hard error. When no window is declared this bound is absent and the window axis imposes no constraint."
msgstr "Le inclusive lower bound de a logic:FreshnessGuard's explicit valid-time logic:freshnessWindow, as an xsd:dateTime."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/functionalProperty|rdfs:label"
msgid "functional property"
msgstr "functional propriété"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/functionalProperty|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic: property-characteristic marker for functionality: a property P such that P(a,b) ∧ P(a,c) entails b = c. The logic: analogue of owl:FunctionalProperty, minted standalone so the characteristic can be asserted on the canonical reasoning carrier alongside the others; functionality is already lifted into the foundation chase for the relator-mediation count, so a functional carrier records the characteristic centrally rather than adding a second enforcement path."
msgstr "Le logic: propriété-characteristic marker pour functionality: a propriété P such qui P(a,b) ∧ P(a,c) entails b = c."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/gateCompensation|rdfs:label"
msgid "gate compensation"
msgstr "gate compensation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/gateCompensation|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a denied logic:GateProbe to the logic:compensation (rollback) the schema would run on denial. Domain logic:GateProbe, range the compensation action (stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:gateCompensation only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a denied logic:GateProbe à the logic:compensation (rollback) the schéma would run sur denial."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/gateDenialReason|rdfs:label"
msgid "gate denial reason"
msgstr "gate denial reason"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/gateDenialReason|skos:definition"
msgid "A human-readable reason on a denied logic:GateProbe naming the failing gate — the unmet precondition, the unavailable capability, the breached invariant, or the unavailable resource. Domain logic:GateProbe, range a string literal (stated in prose). A breach is a surfaced verdict, never a silent pass."
msgstr "Un human-readable reason sur a denied logic:GateProbe naming the failing gate — the unmet précondition, the unavailable capability, the breached invariant, ou the unavailable ressource."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/gateUndeterminedReason|rdfs:label"
msgid "gate undetermined reason"
msgstr "gate undetermined reason"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/gateUndeterminedReason|skos:definition"
msgid "A human-readable reason on a logic:GateUndetermined logic:GateProbe naming the specific cause of the withheld judgment: for a logic:FreshnessGuard failure, WHICH valid-time axis failed and its bounds — either the age exceeding the logic:freshnessHorizon, or the logic:decisionTime falling outside the [logic:freshnessWindowStart, logic:freshnessWindowEnd] logic:freshnessWindow interval (the two axes are independent and the reason names whichever failed first). Domain logic:GateProbe, range a string literal (stated in prose). The undetermined verdict is surfaced, never a silent pass or a spurious denial."
msgstr "Un human-readable reason sur a logic:GateUndetermined logic:GateProbe naming the specific cause de the withheld judgment: pour a logic:FreshnessGuard échec, WHICH valid-time axis failed et its bounds — either the age exceeding the logic:freshnessHorizon, ou the logic:decisionTime falling outside the [logic:freshnessWindowStart, logic:freshnessWindowEnd] logic:freshnessWindow interval (the two axes sont independent et the reason nomme whichever failed first)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/gateVerdict|rdfs:label"
msgid "gate verdict"
msgstr "gate verdict"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/gateVerdict|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:GateProbe to its action-gate verdict, one of logic:GateAdmitted, logic:GateDenied, or logic:GateUndetermined. Domain logic:GateProbe (stated in prose). The materialized verdict of the precondition / capability / invariant / resource / freshness gate. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:gateVerdict only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:GateProbe à its action-gate verdict, one de logic:GateAdmitted, logic:GateDenied, ou logic:GateUndetermined."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/genericQuality|rdfs:label"
msgid "generic quality"
msgstr "generic qualité"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/genericQuality|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Quality to the basic generic quality it instantiates — length, mass, pressure, temperature: the frame-independent kind of quality, prior to any bearer-context or role. The frame-independent leg of the generic-quality/quality-role ladder (Principle 11: the structure invariant across frames), paired with logic:qualityRole (the anti-rigid logic:Role that generic quality plays in a bearer-context — height being length in a body-context). A quality that plays a logic:qualityRole must instantiate its logic:genericQuality, or it is the logic:QualityRoleWithoutGeneric violation. Domain logic:Quality (stated in prose, matching the module's convention). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:genericQuality only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:qualité à the basic generic qualité it instantiates — length, mass, pressure, temperature: the frame-independent kind de qualité, prior à tout bearer-contexte ou role."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/getLeg|rdfs:label"
msgid "get leg"
msgstr "get leg"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/getLeg|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Lens to the logic:TransactionProgram that realizes its get leg — the down-projection get : S → V from the GMEOW source to the external view. Reuses the transaction layer's path semantics and logic:PathShape; no new pattern language. Domain logic:Lens, range logic:TransactionProgram. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:getLeg only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:Lens à the logic:TransactionProgram qui realizes its get leg — the down-projection get : S → V de the GMEOW source à the external view."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/goalEvaluationStatus|rdfs:label"
msgid "goal evaluation status"
msgstr "objectif evaluation status"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/goalEvaluationStatus|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:GoalEvaluation to the logic:GoalEvaluationStatus it carries — whether the evaluation is conclusive. Domain logic:GoalEvaluation, range logic:GoalEvaluationStatus (stated in prose). Together with satisfaction status logic:Satisfied, the value logic:GoalEvaluationCompleted is the condition under which a gmeow:satisfiedBy edge is generated. DISTINCT from logic:resultEvaluation, which carries the engine-computation logic:EvaluationStatus of a logic:ReasoningResult."
msgstr "Relates a logic:GoalEvaluation à the logic:GoalEvaluationStatus it porte — whether the evaluation est conclusive."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/goalExpressionKind|rdfs:label"
msgid "goal expression kind"
msgstr "objectif expression kind"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/goalExpressionKind|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:GoalExpression to its logic:GoalExpressionKind — which of the nine compositional variants it is. Domain logic:GoalExpression, range logic:GoalExpressionKind (stated in prose). The engine reads this to dispatch the compositional evaluation. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:goalExpressionKind only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:GoalExpression à its logic:GoalExpressionKind — qui de the nine compositional variants it is."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/goalWellFoundedModel|rdfs:label"
msgid "well-founded model goal"
msgstr "well-founded modèle objectif"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/goalWellFoundedModel|skos:definition"
msgid "The success criterion of the well-founded materializer's phase plan: the total (two-valued) well-founded model of the rules over every world is computed and its derived non-EDB rows emitted. The gmeow:Goal logic:wellFoundedMaterializerPlan is arranged to reach; a partial model is a hard failure, never a partial success."
msgstr "Le success criterion de the well-founded materializer's phase plan: the total (two-valued) well-founded modèle de the rules sur chaque monde est computed et its dérivé non-EDB rows emitted."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/granularityAgent|rdfs:label"
msgid "granularity: agent"
msgstr "granularity: agent"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/granularityAgent|skos:definition"
msgid "The coarsest grain of an assessment subject: the reasoner as a whole — the grain at which a reliability assessment of an agent or engine is made."
msgstr "Le coarsest grain de an évaluation subject: the raisonneur as a whole — the grain at qui a reliability évaluation de an agent ou engine est made."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/granularityBodyOfReasoning|rdfs:label"
msgid "granularity: body of reasoning"
msgstr "granularity: body of raisonnement"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/granularityBodyOfReasoning|skos:definition"
msgid "An intermediate grain of an assessment subject: a connected body of reasoning — a derivation, a proof, an episode of inference — judged as a whole rather than one step."
msgstr "Un intermediate grain de an évaluation subject: a connected body de raisonnement — a dérivation, a preuve, an episode de inference — judged as a whole plutôt que one step."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/granularityDomain|rdfs:label"
msgid "granularity: domain"
msgstr "granularity: domaine"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/granularityDomain|skos:definition"
msgid "A broad grain of an assessment subject: a domain of competence — the agent's standing in a field rather than on any one episode."
msgstr "Un broad grain de an évaluation subject: a domaine de competence — the agent's standing dans a field plutôt que sur tout one episode."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/granularityInference|rdfs:label"
msgid "granularity: inference"
msgstr "granularity: inference"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/granularityInference|skos:definition"
msgid "The finest grain of an assessment subject: a single inference — one logic:InferenceProcess or commitment being judged."
msgstr "Le finest grain de an évaluation subject: a single inference — one logic:InferenceProcess ou engagement being judged."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/groupKey|rdfs:label"
msgid "group key"
msgstr "group key"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/groupKey|skos:definition"
msgid "A group-by variable (a ?-prefixed string) over which a reduce rule partitions its body bindings before aggregating: logic:aggregateFunction is computed once per distinct tuple of logic:groupKey values. The group keys are set-semantic (their order does not change meaning); the SHACL-AF reduce surface realizes a single-group-key reduce as the focus node ($this) of a GROUP-BY sub-SELECT."
msgstr "Un group-by variable (a ?-prefixed string) sur qui a reduce règle partitions its body bindings avant aggregating: logic:aggregateFunction est computed once per distinct tuple de logic:groupKey values."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/guardSituation|rdfs:label"
msgid "guard situation"
msgstr "guard situation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/guardSituation|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a conditional logic:GoalExpression to the logic:Situation type that guards it — the goal's target (its operand) applies only when the guard holds (via logic:situationObtains). Domain logic:GoalExpression, range logic:Situation (stated in prose). When the guard is false the conditional goal prescribes nothing: the evaluation reflects does-not-apply rather than asserting satisfied or violated."
msgstr "Relates a conditionnel logic:GoalExpression à the logic:situation type qui guards it — the objectif's target (its operand) applies uniquement lorsque the guard holds (via logic:situationObtains)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/guardsPrecondition|rdfs:label"
msgid "guards precondition"
msgstr "guards précondition"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/guardsPrecondition|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:FreshnessGuard to the logic:precondition situation it guards — the situation whose supporting datum must be current for the gate to admit. Domain logic:FreshnessGuard, range the guarded precondition situation (stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:guardsPrecondition only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:FreshnessGuard à the logic:précondition situation it guards — the situation dont supporting datum doit be current pour the gate à admit."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/happensBefore|rdfs:label"
msgid "happens before"
msgstr "happens before"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/happensBefore|skos:definition"
msgid "A schedule-order edge of a logic:ConcurrentHistory: 'earlier happensBefore later' records that the earlier logic:TransactionStep is scheduled before the later one in the witnessed index-order interleaving AND the two conflict (they share a situation that at least one writes). Domain and range logic:TransactionStep (stated in prose). Emitted only for CROSS-transaction conflicting pairs — the schedule order between the two legs' operations that view- and conflict-serializability both read. It is the step-level witnessed-order companion to logic:readsFrom; it is kept DISTINCT from logic:precedes, which lifts conflict order to the TRANSACTION level for cycle detection, and from logic:temporallySucceeds, which orders the states of a single executed path rather than operations across legs."
msgstr "Un schedule-order edge de a logic:ConcurrentHistory: 'earlier happensBefore later' enregistre qui the earlier logic:TransactionStep est scheduled avant the later one dans the witnessed index-order interleaving AND the two conflit (they share a situation qui au moins one writes)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/hasDeterminacy|rdfs:label"
msgid "has determinacy"
msgstr "has détermination"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/hasDeterminacy|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Correspondence to its logic:Determinacy — whether the target relationship is ontically logic:Crisp or logic:Vague. Kept separate from logic:confidence so a vague-but-confident alignment is not mis-recorded as a low-confidence equivalence. Range logic:Determinacy (domain stated in prose)."
msgstr "Relates a logic:correspondance à its logic:déterminaison — whether the target relation est ontically logic:Crisp ou logic:Vague."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/hasFormula|rdfs:label"
msgid "has formula"
msgstr "has formule"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/hasFormula|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a program or container to a top-level logic:Formula it asserts. Top-level formulae are reached by this property; sub-formulae are reached by the connective and quantifier properties, so a formula referenced as another's component is not also a top-level assertion."
msgstr "Relates a program ou container à a top-niveau logic:formule it asserts."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/hasGoalCondition|rdfs:label"
msgid "has goal condition"
msgstr "has objectif condition"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/hasGoalCondition|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a gmeow:Goal to the logic:GoalExpression carrying the compositional structure of its target. Domain gmeow:Goal, range logic:GoalExpression (stated in prose, matching the module's domain/range convention). The flat gmeow:hasGoal and conclusive gmeow:satisfiedBy edges are the surface views this richer condition generates; gmeow:intentionGoal stays functional and ranges over gmeow:Goal — goal structure lives on the goal through this property, leaving the functional edge untouched. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:hasGoalCondition only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a gmeow:objectif à the logic:GoalExpression carrying the compositional structure de its target."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/hasHolonicPosition|rdfs:label"
msgid "has holonic position"
msgstr "has holonic position"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/hasHolonicPosition|skos:definition"
msgid "The derived marker that an entity occupies at least one logic:HolonicPosition within a holarchy. Never asserted by hand; it is entailed by the foundation lowering, settling in stratum 1 the moment any logic:positionEntity reifier names the entity. It is the negation-as-failure target that arms the logic:HolonicLevelIncoherence rule (a profiled holon occupying NO position is incoherent), and the positive companion to logic:multiplyPositioned (which fires when an entity occupies SEVERAL distinct positions). It tracks compositional positioning only and is orthogonal to the HiLog logic:orderedType instantiation tower — the two axes never feed one another."
msgstr "Le dérivé marker qui an entity occupies au moins one logic:HolonicPosition within a holarchy."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/hasLawClaim|rdfs:label"
msgid "has law claim"
msgstr "has loi claim"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/hasLawClaim|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Correspondence to a logic:LawClaim it makes — a claimed logic:CorrespondenceLaw with its discharge state. Multi-valued: a correspondence may claim several laws, each capped by its logic:MorphismClass rung. Range logic:LawClaim (domain stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:hasLawClaim only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:correspondance à a logic:LawClaim it makes — a claimed logic:CorrespondenceLaw avec its acquittement état."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/hasLens|rdfs:label"
msgid "has lens"
msgstr "has lens"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/hasLens|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Correspondence to the logic:Lens that is its executable get / put core. Single-valued: each correspondence wraps exactly one lens, around which it adds the relation, axes, law claims and standpoint envelope. Range logic:Lens (domain stated in prose, matching the module's convention). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:hasLens only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:correspondance à the logic:Lens qui est its executable get / put core."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/hasThresholdRow|rdfs:label"
msgid "has threshold row"
msgstr "has threshold row"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/hasThresholdRow|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:LadderProjectionProfile to one of its logic:DimensionThreshold rows. Range logic:DimensionThreshold (stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:hasThresholdRow only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:LadderProjectionProfile à one de its logic:DimensionThreshold rows."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/holonicLevel|rdfs:label"
msgid "holonic level"
msgstr "holonic niveau"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/holonicLevel|skos:definition"
msgid "The compositional depth at which an entity sits within a holarchy, measured along one path: how many proper-part steps lie between the entity and a root whole. It is a literal read off a logic:HolonicPosition (hence rdfs:domain logic:HolonicPosition), never an intrinsic attribute of the entity — holarchies are DAGs, so an entity has no single global level; two paths may place the same entity at different depths and both are correct, and the level is therefore recorded per position (per path). The per-entity min/max band across an entity's positions is materialized separately as logic:holonicLevelMin and logic:holonicLevelMax. Distinct from logic:orderedType: logic:orderedType is the HiLog deep-instantiation order (an order-n type instantiates an order-(n+1) type), a property of the instantiation tower, whereas logic:holonicLevel is mereological compositional depth in a whole/part DAG; the two must not be conflated (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Le compositional depth at qui an entity sits within a holarchy, measured along one chemin: how many proper-part steps lie entre the entity et a root whole."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/holonicLevelMax|rdfs:label"
msgid "holonic level max"
msgstr "holonic niveau max"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/holonicLevelMax|skos:definition"
msgid "The deepest of the logic:holonicLevel values an entity carries across all the logic:HolonicPositions it occupies within a holarchy — the upper endpoint of the path-relative depth band. Because holarchies are DAGs, a single intrinsic level is ill-defined, so the band (min..max) is stored instead of one value. NOTE — honest scope: this endpoint is operator-asserted, NOT engine-verified. The all-IRI logic:StratifiedNAFProfile foundation chase cannot compare or aggregate the integer literals, so it cannot derive or check that this value is the true maximum of the borne per-position levels; the engine grounds only that a non-trivial band exists, via the derived marker logic:multiplyPositioned (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Le deepest de the logic:holonicLevel values an entity porte across tous the logic:HolonicPositions it occupies within a holarchy — the upper endpoint de the chemin-relative depth band."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/holonicLevelMin|rdfs:label"
msgid "holonic level min"
msgstr "holonic niveau min"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/holonicLevelMin|skos:definition"
msgid "The shallowest of the logic:holonicLevel values an entity carries across all the logic:HolonicPositions it occupies within a holarchy — the lower endpoint of the path-relative depth band. Because holarchies are DAGs, a single intrinsic level is ill-defined, so the band (min..max) is stored instead of one value. NOTE — honest scope: this endpoint is operator-asserted, NOT engine-verified. The all-IRI logic:StratifiedNAFProfile foundation chase cannot compare or aggregate the integer literals, so it cannot derive or check that this value is the true minimum of the borne per-position levels; the engine grounds only that a non-trivial band exists, via the derived marker logic:multiplyPositioned (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Le shallowest de the logic:holonicLevel values an entity porte across tous the logic:HolonicPositions it occupies within a holarchy — the lower endpoint de the chemin-relative depth band."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/iff|rdfs:label"
msgid "if and only if"
msgstr "if and only if"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/iff|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a biconditional logic:Formula to each of its two operand sub-formulae. The biconditional is commutative, so the canonical identity is insensitive to which operand is which — unlike the ordered logic:antecedent / logic:consequent of an implication."
msgstr "Relates a biconditional logic:formule à each de its two operand sub-formulae."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/imports|rdfs:label"
msgid "imports"
msgstr "imports"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/imports|skos:definition"
msgid "Common Logic importation between logic:Modules: the importing module has, as part of its own theory, every sentence of the imported module. The module-to-module edge onto which the Common Logic (cl-imports …) directive maps. Importation composes transitively in the Common Logic reading, but this is documented in prose rather than asserted as owl:TransitiveProperty, matching the kernel convention that logic: relations carry no OWL characteristics and state their logical character in prose; the engine, not an OWL entailment, closes the import graph."
msgstr "commun Logic importation entre logic:Modules: the importing module has, as part de its own theory, chaque sentence de the imported module."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/inModule|rdfs:label"
msgid "in module"
msgstr "in module"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/inModule|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a statement (an axiom or rule, carried on its reifier) to the logic:Module it is asserted in — the per-statement carrier of the module context axis, parallel to how logic:standpoint carries the world axis. A statement with no logic:inModule belongs to the top-level module. It never licenses cross-module entailment on its own: importation (logic:imports) governs which modules' sentences a module sees, and the bare membership edge is index and provenance, not an inference-bearing relation. It asserts no OWL characteristic; its logical character is documented in prose, matching the kernel convention."
msgstr "Relates a statement (an axiom ou règle, carried sur its reifier) à the logic:Module it est asserted dans — the per-statement carrier de the module contexte axis, parallel à how logic:point de vue porte the monde axis."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/inferencePremiseConclusionDistinctness|rdfs:label"
msgid "an inference commitment's premise and conclusion are distinct"
msgstr "an inference engagement's premise and conclusion are distinct"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/inferencePremiseConclusionDistinctness|skos:definition"
msgid "Asserts that a gmeow:InferenceCommitment's gmeow:premise and gmeow:conclusion must be distinct: an argument cannot assume what it proves — no premise is also the conclusion. The native coherence gate raises a violation when a premise coincides with the conclusion; the generated SHACL constraint surface is its projection."
msgstr "Asserts qui a gmeow:InferenceCommitment's gmeow:premise et gmeow:conclusion doit be distinct: an argument ne peut pas assume what it proves — no premise est also the conclusion."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/inhabitationIntervalFrameRequirement|rdfs:label"
msgid "an inhabitation tenure's interval carries its temporal frame"
msgstr "an inhabitation tenure's interval carries its temporal frame"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/inhabitationIntervalFrameRequirement|skos:definition"
msgid "Asserts that every gmeow:TimeInterval a gmeow:InhabitationTenure scopes via gmeow:duringInterval must declare at least one gmeow:hasTemporalFrame — an interval asserted without its frame is ill-formed (Principle 11: the interval carries its frame). The native coherence gate raises a violation when a scoping interval lacks a frame."
msgstr "Asserts qui chaque gmeow:TimeInterval a gmeow:InhabitationTenure scopes via gmeow:duringInterval doit declare au moins one gmeow:hasTemporalFrame — an interval asserted sans its frame est ill-formed (Principle 11: the interval porte its frame)."


msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ins|rdfs:label"
msgid "ins"
msgstr "ins"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ins|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:InsertUpdate to the support/fact it asserts. The `ins(F)` primitive makes F active in the successor state while leaving the predecessor state untouched. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:ins only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:InsertUpdate à the support/fact it asserts."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/instanceOf|rdfs:label"
msgid "instance of"
msgstr "instance of"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/instanceOf|skos:definition"
msgid "HiLog deep instantiation: relates an individual or a type to a (possibly higher-order) type it instantiates, across any number of meta-levels. The first-class multi-level primitive that replaces OWL punning (criticism 5): types are reified as first-order individuals so 'an instance of a type that is itself an instance of a metatype' is ordinary first-order quantification rather than a punning trick. The general relation of which logic:suppliesIdentity is the identity-supplying specialization."
msgstr "HiLog deep instantiation: relie an individu ou a type à a (possibly higher-order) type it instantiates, across tout number de meta-levels."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/instantiatesFramework|rdfs:label"
msgid "instantiates framework"
msgstr "instantiates cadre"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/instantiatesFramework|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a term to the closed logic:LogicalFramework discipline(s) it traffics in — the reasoning machinery the term belongs to (logic:HolonicPosition instantiates logic:HolonicFramework; gmeow:Norm instantiates logic:DeonticFramework). Multi-valued: a term may inhabit several frameworks (a logic:GoalEvaluation that ranges over deontic-ideal worlds is both teleological and deontic). Classifying metadata, orthogonal to the logic:ReasoningContract facets that configure a particular evaluation; the range is the closed class, so an undeclared value is rejected. Absence is meaningful — a plain domain term that traffics in no special discipline carries no framework, and none is asserted (design/LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md, the unified-logic-core section). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:instantiatesFramework only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a terme à the closed logic:LogicalFramework discipline(s) it traffics dans — the raisonnement machinery the terme belongs à (logic:HolonicPosition instantiates logic:HolonicFramework; gmeow:Norm instantiates logic:DeonticFramework)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/instantiatesPlan|rdfs:label"
msgid "instantiates plan"
msgstr "instantiates plan"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/instantiatesPlan|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates an executed action occurrence — a materialized logic:TransactionStep (a gmeow:Event minted per run position) — to the logic:Plan program it was executed under. Domain the occurrence, range logic:Plan (stated in prose). It is the plan-level companion of logic:instantiatesSchema: where that link records the reusable type an occurrence instantiates (Event to ActionSchema), this records the whole plan the occurrence realizes (Event to Plan). The pair is a load-bearing in-band recovery witness — the executed record carries, in band, a back-reference to both the schema and the plan it instantiates — so a correspondence's put leg can recover the planned skeleton from an execution record (the mnemomorphism's in-band complement at the process layer) rather than synthesizing a plausible plan. Without it the descriptive run and the prescriptive plan are only externally related; with it the planned portion round-trips."
msgstr "Relates an executed action occurrence — a materialized logic:TransactionStep (a gmeow:Event minted per run position) — à the logic:plan program it was executed under."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/instantiatesSchema|rdfs:label"
msgid "instantiates schema"
msgstr "instantiates schéma"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/instantiatesSchema|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a gmeow:Event (an action occurrence — a particular event executed along a particular path) to the logic:ActionSchema it instantiates. Domain gmeow:Event, range logic:ActionSchema (stated in prose). The occurrence is the same perdurant an intentional moment links to through gmeow:motivates; the schema is the reusable type it instantiates. The schema names what an action does; the path records that it was done and what changed. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:instantiatesSchema only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a gmeow:Event (an action occurrence — a particular event executed along a particular chemin) à the logic:ActionSchema it instantiates."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/integrativeBasis|rdfs:label"
msgid "integrative basis"
msgstr "integrative basis"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/integrativeBasis|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:HolonicAgencyProfile to a property-value that evidences the integrative tendency: the profile holds that a holon bearing this value (logic:bearsProperty) subordinates itself as a part to a larger whole — Koestler's integrative face. The carrier that makes integration profile-relative, the co-equal twin of logic:selfAssertiveBasis (neither privileged, Principle 9). Without a borne integrative value a holon's integration face is not evidenced, contributing — together with the self-assertive face — to the logic:AgencyVerdict (logic:IntegrationDeficient or logic:HolonIntegral). The integration analogue of logic:reductionBasis and logic:activationBasis (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Relates a logic:HolonicAgencyProfile à a propriété-valeur qui evidences the integrative tendency: the profil holds qui a holon bearing this valeur (logic:bearsProperty) subordinates itself as a part à a larger whole — Koestler's integrative face."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/integrity|rdfs:label"
msgid "integrity"
msgstr "intégrité"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/integrity|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Constraint to its closed-world integrity condition: the reified logic:Formula whose violation is a finding, not a derivation. Reuses the realized full-FOL formula core verbatim — the condition is an outer range-restricted universal (logic:forall over a bound focus) whose logic:antecedent guard names the class or predicate the focus ranges over and whose logic:consequent is the per-focus condition — so a constraint needs no bespoke shape DSL. The focus target (a class, or the subjects/objects of a predicate) is derived from that guard, never authored twice."
msgstr "Relates a logic:contrainte à its monde fermé intégrité condition: the reified logic:formule dont violation est a finding, not a dérivation."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/invariant|rdfs:label"
msgid "invariant"
msgstr "invariant"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/invariant|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ActionSchema to what the action must preserve across its execution — the condition that holds before, during, and after. Domain logic:ActionSchema (stated in prose). One of the eight action-theory facets, distinct from logic:precondition (what must hold to begin) and logic:effect (what changes)."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ActionSchema à what the action doit preserve across its exécution — the condition qui holds before, during, et after."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/invokesBuiltin|rdfs:label"
msgid "invokes builtin"
msgstr "invokes primitive"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/invokesBuiltin|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Rule to a logic:Builtin it calls in its body: the dependency edge recording that a rule uses a native computational primitive, and therefore requires logic:ProceduralPrologProfile (where builtins are gated). Lets the compiler check that a rule invoking a builtin declares the procedural profile and records the loss when such a rule is projected to a declarative semantics. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:invokesBuiltin only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:règle à a logic:primitive it calls dans its body: the dependency edge recording qui a règle uses a native computational primitive, et donc exige logic:ProceduralPrologProfile (where builtins sont gated)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/invokesPathShape|rdfs:label"
msgid "invokes path shape"
msgstr "invokes chemin forme"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/invokesPathShape|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:PathInvocation to the logic:PathShape it applies by name: the dependency edge recording which reusable traversal a parametric call instantiates. Paired with logic:pathDepthArg, which supplies the concrete bound for the shape's logic:pathDepthParam. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:invokesPathShape only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:PathInvocation à the logic:PathShape it applies par name: the dependency edge recording qui reusable traversal a parametric call instantiates."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/irreflexiveProperty|rdfs:label"
msgid "irreflexive property"
msgstr "irreflexive propriété"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/irreflexiveProperty|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic: property-characteristic marker for irreflexivity: a property P such that P(a,a) holds for no a. The logic: analogue of owl:IrreflexiveProperty, used together with logic:transitiveProperty and logic:asymmetricProperty to make logic:properPartOf a genuine strict partial order (criticism 7). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:irreflexiveProperty only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le logic: propriété-characteristic marker pour irreflexivity: a propriété P such qui P(a,a) holds pour no a."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/isHolon|rdfs:label"
msgid "is holon"
msgstr "is holon"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/isHolon|skos:definition"
msgid "The derived marker that projects holon-ness onto an entity: it holds of an entity that, within a holarchy, is simultaneously a proper part of some whole and itself has a proper part. It is the reasoning-surface marker (mirroring logic:isClass-style stereotype markers) from which the unary logic:Holon class is the OWL projection; the faithful construct is the relational logic:HolonicPosition, of which both are lossy projections. Never asserted by hand; it is entailed by the foundation lowering."
msgstr "Le dérivé marker qui projects holon-ness sur an entity: it holds de an entity that, within a holarchy, est simultaneously a proper part de some whole et itself possède a proper part."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/isolationInadequacyReason|rdfs:label"
msgid "isolation inadequacy reason"
msgstr "isolation inadequacy reason"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/isolationInadequacyReason|skos:definition"
msgid "A human-readable description of WHY a logic:ConcurrentHistory's witnessed schedule fails to meet its declared logic:IsolationLevel — present exactly when logic:isolationLevelAdequacy is false. Domain logic:ConcurrentHistory, range xsd:string (stated in prose). In the snapshot-isolation model this is the case of a schedule that is not conflict-serializable (a write-skew or lost-update cycle) declared under logic:SerializableIsolation or logic:OpacityIsolation, and the reason names that: the schedule is not conflict-serializable, so it does not meet the declared strength. It is a guarantee-level finding, never a claim of logical contradiction within a state."
msgstr "Un human-readable description de WHY a logic:ConcurrentHistory's witnessed schedule fails à meet its declared logic:IsolationLevel — present exactly lorsque logic:isolationLevelAdequacy est false."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/isolationLevelAdequacy|rdfs:label"
msgid "isolation level adequacy"
msgstr "isolation niveau adequacy"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/isolationLevelAdequacy|skos:definition"
msgid "The boolean verdict of classifying a logic:ConcurrentHistory's witnessed schedule against the logic:IsolationLevel its run declared (logic:declaredIsolationLevel): true iff the schedule meets that declared guarantee strength. Domain logic:ConcurrentHistory, range xsd:boolean (stated in prose); present only when a level is declared. Because the concurrent evaluator realizes snapshot isolation, every level up to logic:SnapshotIsolation is adequate by construction; logic:SerializableIsolation and logic:OpacityIsolation are adequate iff the schedule is conflict-serializable — a write-skew cycle (which snapshot admits) is adequate for snapshot yet INADEQUATE for serializability. A false verdict carries a logic:isolationInadequacyReason. It is guarantee-strength adequacy, kept distinct from logic:protocolEnforced (mechanism soundness) and logic:satisfiesCriterion (the history property)."
msgstr "Le boolean verdict de classifying a logic:ConcurrentHistory's witnessed schedule contre the logic:IsolationLevel its run declared (logic:declaredIsolationLevel): true iff the schedule meets qui declared guarantee strength."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/iterationBody|rdfs:label"
msgid "iteration body"
msgstr "itération body"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/iterationBody|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Iteration combinator to the sub-program that constitutes its loop body — the program executed on each iteration pass. Domain logic:Iteration, range a transaction-program node (stated in prose). Paired with logic:iterationCondition, which carries the guard situation checked before each pass. Distinct from logic:leftOperand / logic:rightOperand (binary co-equal operands of serial, choice, concurrent, and fallback combinators): a loop body is not co-equal with a loop condition."
msgstr "Relates a logic:itération combinator à the sub-program qui constitutes its loop body — the program executed sur each itération pass."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/iterationCondition|rdfs:label"
msgid "iteration condition"
msgstr "itération condition"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/iterationCondition|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Iteration combinator to the situation type that gates each pass of the loop body — the loop is executed while this situation obtains at the current state; when it does not hold the iteration terminates. Domain logic:Iteration, range logic:Situation (stated in prose). Paired with logic:iterationBody. Reuses the situation-type pattern of logic:guardSituation and logic:boundSituationType: the engine reads this against the current path state via logic:situationObtains."
msgstr "Relates a logic:itération combinator à the situation type qui gates each pass de the loop body — the loop est executed while this situation obtains at the current état; lorsque it ne fait pas hold the itération terminates."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/jointOutcome|rdfs:label"
msgid "joint outcome"
msgstr "joint résultat"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/jointOutcome|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:DependencyModel to one logic:JointOutcome of its explicit joint table. The outcomes a model declares must be mutually exclusive and exhaustive over the assignments to its logic:correlates set, and their logic:jointProbability values must sum to one. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:jointOutcome only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:DependencyModel à one logic:JointOutcome de its explicit joint table."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/jointProbability|rdfs:label"
msgid "joint probability"
msgstr "joint probability"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/jointProbability|skos:definition"
msgid "The probability mass a logic:DependencyModel assigns to one logic:JointOutcome — the joint probability of that exact assignment of truth values to the model's correlated facts. Distinct from logic:probability (a per-fact marginal): the joint outcomes of a model partition its correlated sample space and their logic:jointProbability values sum to one. The range is intentionally left open (no rdfs:range), matching the other quantitative axes (logic:probability, logic:confidence, logic:weight, logic:evidenceStrength), which this standalone module declares without an xsd range: the value is a unit-interval decimal."
msgstr "Le probability mass a logic:DependencyModel assigns à one logic:JointOutcome — the joint probability de qui exact assignment de vérité values à the modèle's correlated facts."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ladderRowAwareness|rdfs:label"
msgid "ladder row: awareness → is aware of"
msgstr "ladder row: awareness → is aware of"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ladderRowAwareness|skos:definition"
msgid "The default-profile row emitting gmeow:isAwareOf when the awareness dimension reaches logic:levelEmerging."
msgstr "Le default-profil row emitting gmeow:isAwareOf lorsque the awareness dimension reaches logic:levelEmerging."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ladderRowConceptual|rdfs:label"
msgid "ladder row: conceptual understanding → understands"
msgstr "ladder row: conceptual understanding → understands"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ladderRowConceptual|skos:definition"
msgid "The default-profile row emitting gmeow:understands when the conceptual-understanding dimension reaches logic:levelCompetent."
msgstr "Le default-profil row emitting gmeow:understands lorsque the conceptual-understanding dimension reaches logic:levelCompetent."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ladderRowDeclarative|rdfs:label"
msgid "ladder row: declarative familiarity → knows about"
msgstr "ladder row: declarative familiarity → knows about"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ladderRowDeclarative|skos:definition"
msgid "The default-profile row emitting gmeow:knowsAbout when the declarative-familiarity dimension reaches logic:levelCompetent."
msgstr "Le default-profil row emitting gmeow:knowsAbout lorsque the declarative-familiarity dimension reaches logic:levelCompetent."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ladderRowProceduralMastery|rdfs:label"
msgid "ladder row: procedural competence → has mastered"
msgstr "ladder row: procedural competence → has mastered"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ladderRowProceduralMastery|skos:definition"
msgid "The procedural half of the default-profile gmeow:hasMastered rung: procedural competence must reach logic:levelStrong. Read together with logic:ladderRowTransferMastery — both must clear for gmeow:hasMastered."
msgstr "Le procedural half de the default-profil gmeow:hasMastered rung: procedural competence doit reach logic:levelStrong."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ladderRowTransferMastery|rdfs:label"
msgid "ladder row: transfer → has mastered"
msgstr "ladder row: transfer → has mastered"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ladderRowTransferMastery|skos:definition"
msgid "The transfer half of the default-profile gmeow:hasMastered rung: transfer must reach logic:levelStrong. Read together with logic:ladderRowProceduralMastery — both must clear for gmeow:hasMastered, so mastery of one narrow task never implies broad command."
msgstr "Le transfer half de the default-profil gmeow:hasMastered rung: transfer doit reach logic:levelStrong."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/lawClaimed|rdfs:label"
msgid "law claimed"
msgstr "loi claimed"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/lawClaimed|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:LawClaim to the logic:CorrespondenceLaw it asserts (logic:GetPut, logic:PutGet, logic:PutPut or logic:SectionLaw). Domain logic:LawClaim, range logic:CorrespondenceLaw. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:lawClaimed only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:LawClaim à the logic:CorrespondenceLaw it asserts (logic:GetPut, logic:PutGet, logic:PutPut ou logic:SectionLaw)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/lawDischargeCondition|rdfs:label"
msgid "law discharge condition"
msgstr "loi acquittement condition"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/lawDischargeCondition|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:LawClaim to the logic:DischargeCondition under which its logic:lawDischargeVerdict is conclusively checkable (for example logic:DischargeCertifiedFragment for a law proved within a certified complete fragment). Optional: a law carrying logic:ObligationUnknown with no condition is an authored-but-unverified claim. Reuses the foundation's discharge-condition value class. Domain logic:LawClaim, range logic:DischargeCondition. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:lawDischargeCondition only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:LawClaim à the logic:DischargeCondition sous qui its logic:lawDischargeVerdict est conclusively checkable (for example logic:DischargeCertifiedFragment pour a loi proved within a certified complet fragment)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/lawDischargeVerdict|rdfs:label"
msgid "law discharge verdict"
msgstr "loi acquittement verdict"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/lawDischargeVerdict|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:LawClaim to the logic:DischargeVerdict its check returned — logic:ObligationDischarged, logic:ObligationUnknown or logic:ObligationViolated. Reuses the foundation's discharge-verdict value class (the law-claim analogue of logic:obligationDischargeVerdict, which is domain-locked to logic:NonEntailmentObligation): an unchecked or inconclusive law is logic:ObligationUnknown, never silently passed. Domain logic:LawClaim, range logic:DischargeVerdict."
msgstr "Relates a logic:LawClaim à the logic:DischargeVerdict its vérification returned — logic:ObligationDischarged, logic:ObligationUnknown ou logic:ObligationViolated."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/leftOperand|rdfs:label"
msgid "left operand"
msgstr "left operand"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/leftOperand|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a binary transaction-program combinator (for example a logic:SerialConjunction) to its left/prefix operand — the program that holds over the prefix of the executing path. Range a transaction-program node (stated in prose). Paired with logic:rightOperand. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:leftOperand only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a binary transaction-program combinator (for example a logic:SerialConjunction) à its left/prefix operand — the program qui holds sur the prefix de the executing chemin."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/levelAtOrAbove|rdfs:label"
msgid "level at or above"
msgstr "niveau at or above"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/levelAtOrAbove|skos:definition"
msgid "Orders the ordinal assessment scale: relates a logic:AssessmentLevel to itself and to every level it surpasses (logic:levelStrong logic:levelAtOrAbove logic:levelCompetent). Reflexive-and-transitive on the levels, so the coarse-ladder projection can test 'the assessed level is at or above the threshold level' by a single body atom, with no numeric comparison (which would force a procedural profile). The full reflexive-transitive closure is asserted on the level individuals so the test needs no transitive computation in the rule engine. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:levelAtOrAbove only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Orders the ordinal évaluation scale: relie a logic:AssessmentLevel à itself et à chaque niveau it surpasses (logic:levelStrong logic:levelAtOrAbove logic:levelCompetent)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/levelCompetent|rdfs:label"
msgid "level: competent"
msgstr "niveau: competent"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/levelCompetent|skos:definition"
msgid "The third ordinal assessment level: the dimension is solidly evidenced. Surpasses logic:levelEmerging and logic:levelNone on the logic:levelAtOrAbove order."
msgstr "Le third ordinal évaluation niveau: the dimension est solidly evidenced."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/levelEmerging|rdfs:label"
msgid "level: emerging"
msgstr "niveau: emerging"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/levelEmerging|skos:definition"
msgid "The second ordinal assessment level: the dimension is weakly evidenced. Surpasses logic:levelNone on the logic:levelAtOrAbove order."
msgstr "Le second ordinal évaluation niveau: the dimension est weakly evidenced."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/levelNone|rdfs:label"
msgid "level: none"
msgstr "niveau: none"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/levelNone|skos:definition"
msgid "The lowest ordinal assessment level: the dimension is not evidenced at all. Clears no ladder rung's threshold."
msgstr "Le lowest ordinal évaluation niveau: the dimension n'est pas evidenced at tous."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/levelStrong|rdfs:label"
msgid "level: strong"
msgstr "niveau: strong"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/levelStrong|skos:definition"
msgid "The highest ordinal assessment level: the dimension is strongly evidenced. Surpasses every lower level on the logic:levelAtOrAbove order."
msgstr "Le highest ordinal évaluation niveau: the dimension est strongly evidenced."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/lifecycleStatus|rdfs:label"
msgid "lifecycle status"
msgstr "cycle de vie status"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/lifecycleStatus|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:GoalEvaluation to the logic:LifecycleStatus it carries — the lifecycle axis of the factored outcome. Domain logic:GoalEvaluation, range logic:LifecycleStatus (stated in prose). Varies independently of satisfaction, feasibility, and goal-evaluation status. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:lifecycleStatus only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:GoalEvaluation à the logic:LifecycleStatus it porte — the cycle de vie axis de the factored résultat."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/linkNextAcyclicity|rdfs:label"
msgid "linkNext is acyclic"
msgstr "linkNext is acyclic"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/linkNextAcyclicity|skos:definition"
msgid "Asserts on the canonical carrier that gmeow:linkNext is acyclic: a causal-cascade walk never reaches itself through gmeow:linkNext, as the Cascade prose states. linkNext is deliberately NOT transitive (it names the immediate next link, not every downstream one), so the native coherence gate enforces this with an internal reachability walk that raises a violation on any cycle, never by materialising the closure; the generated SHACL constraint surface is its projection."
msgstr "Asserts sur the canonique carrier qui gmeow:linkNext est acyclic: a causal-cascade walk jamais reaches itself par gmeow:linkNext, as the Cascade prose states."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/loadBearing|rdfs:label"
msgid "load bearing"
msgstr "load bearing"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/loadBearing|skos:definition"
msgid "Types an annotation as load-bearing (true) or droppable (false, the default). A droppable annotation — a display hint or scope note — must never carry correctness: dropping it only pessimizes a result, so a lowering may drop it silently. A load-bearing annotation — an in-band complement or a quantitative axis — is needed by the inverse leg for put after get to equal the identity, so a lowering must either preserve it or record its loss in the ledger. Without this bit a section / retraction (perfect-subsumption) claim cannot be verified, which is why it is part of the node from the start."
msgstr "Types an annotation as load-bearing (true) ou droppable (false, the default)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/lockAcquired|rdfs:label"
msgid "lock acquired"
msgstr "lock acquired"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/lockAcquired|skos:definition"
msgid "Records that the action a transaction step performs ACQUIRES an exclusive lock on a situation — a recorded event of a two-phase-locking protocol. Declared on the action schema (logic:ActionSchema) a step instantiates, range the locked situation (stated in prose); the native evaluator reads the acquire/release events in each leg's step order to classify the lock discipline. Under logic:StrictTwoPhaseLocking the schedule is well-formed iff each leg is two-phase (no acquire follows any release within the leg); under logic:StrongStrictTwoPhaseLocking, additionally, no lock is released before the leg's final (commit) step. It is a recorded protocol EVENT the classifier reads, kept distinct from logic:lockReleased (its releasing counterpart) and from the situation-validity vocabulary (logic:situationObtains), which is about what holds, not what is locked."
msgstr "Records qui the action a transaction step performs ACQUIRES an exclusive lock sur a situation — a recorded event de a two-phase-locking protocol."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/lockReleased|rdfs:label"
msgid "lock released"
msgstr "lock released"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/lockReleased|skos:definition"
msgid "Records that the action a transaction step performs RELEASES its exclusive lock on a situation — the releasing counterpart of logic:lockAcquired and a recorded event of a two-phase-locking protocol. Declared on the action schema (logic:ActionSchema) a step instantiates, range the released situation (stated in prose). The native evaluator reads releases in each leg's step order: a release before any remaining acquire breaks the two-phase discipline (logic:StrictTwoPhaseLocking), and a release before the leg's final step breaks the held-to-commit discipline (logic:StrongStrictTwoPhaseLocking). It is a recorded protocol EVENT the classifier reads, never a derived verdict."
msgstr "Records qui the action a transaction step performs RELEASES its exclusive lock sur a situation — the releasing counterpart de logic:lockAcquired et a recorded event de a two-phase-locking protocol."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/lossCode|rdfs:label"
msgid "loss code"
msgstr "loss code"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/lossCode|skos:definition"
msgid "The stable machine code of a logic:ProjectionLoss — reifier-layer-dropped, annotation-layer-dropped, or standpoint-scope-dropped — naming exactly which structure the projection shed. The codes are shared verbatim with the conversion loss ledger so in-band and contract-level loss declarations agree. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:lossCode only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le stable machine code de a logic:ProjectionLoss — reifier-layer-dropped, annotation-layer-dropped, ou point de vue-scope-dropped — naming exactly qui structure the projection shed."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/lostReifies|rdfs:label"
msgid "lost reifies"
msgstr "lost reifies"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/lostReifies|skos:definition"
msgid "Points from a logic:ProjectionLoss to the RDF-1.2 triple term whose reifier (and any annotations) the projection dropped, so a consumer can recover which statement lost its reification layer. The object is a quoted triple term; its range is intentionally left open (stated in prose) to keep the OWL down-projection DL-clean. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:lostReifies only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Points de a logic:ProjectionLoss à the RDF-1.2 triple terme dont reifier (and tout annotations) the projection dropped, so a consumer peut recover qui statement lost its reification layer."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/lowerPriorityUnderPolicy|rdfs:label"
msgid "lower priority under policy"
msgstr "lower priority under politique"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/lowerPriorityUnderPolicy|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates two gmeow:Goals where, under a governing priority ordering established by an applicable policy, one goal is deprioritised in favour of the other — a conflict resolved by policy precedence rather than by logical, temporal, or deontic impossibility. Domain gmeow:Goal, range gmeow:Goal (stated in prose). One of seven conflict relations between independently-meaningful goals, weaker than gmeow:counterGoal (constitutive opposition). Distinct from logic:deonticallyIncompatible: the conjunction is not normatively impermissible — it is merely ranked lower by the policy ordering; and distinct from logic:competesForResource: the deprioritisation is a priority decision, not an exhaustion of supply."
msgstr "Relates two gmeow:Goals where, sous a governing priority ordering established par an applicable politique, one objectif est deprioritised dans favour de the other — a conflit resolved par politique precedence plutôt que par logique, temporal, ou deontic impossibility."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/measuredValue|rdfs:label"
msgid "measured value"
msgstr "measured valeur"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/measuredValue|skos:definition"
msgid "The frame-relative magnitude of a measurement: the numeric value a measured quantity takes once expressed in a unit and reference frame — the 37 of 37 °C, the 120 of 120 mmHg. The frame-relative leg of the true-quantity/measured-value seam (Principle 11), paired with logic:referenceFrame: the value is meaningful only together with the frame it is expressed in, so a logic:measuredValue asserted without a logic:referenceFrame is the logic:MeasurementFrameMissing violation. Contrast logic:trueQuantity, the frame-independent magnitude the value measures. The foundation-level seam predicate the domain property gmeow:value grounds onto by sub-property, so a domain measurement lifts into the constraint's scope. The range is intentionally left open (no rdfs:range), matching the module's quantitative-axis convention. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:measuredValue only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le frame-relative magnitude de a measurement: the numeric valeur a measured quantity takes once expressed dans a unit et reference frame — the 37 de 37 °C, the 120 de 120 mmHg."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/mediatedRequirementProperty|rdfs:label"
msgid "mediated requirement property"
msgstr "mediated requirement propriété"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/mediatedRequirementProperty|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:MediatedPropertyRequirementAssertion to the property each mediated value must declare at least once. Domain logic:MediatedPropertyRequirementAssertion; single-valued. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:mediatedRequirementProperty only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:MediatedPropertyRequirementAssertion à the propriété each mediated valeur doit declare au moins once."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/mediatedRequirementTarget|rdfs:label"
msgid "mediated requirement target"
msgstr "mediated requirement target"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/mediatedRequirementTarget|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:MediatedPropertyRequirementAssertion to the class whose focus nodes it constrains. Domain logic:MediatedPropertyRequirementAssertion; single-valued. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:mediatedRequirementTarget only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:MediatedPropertyRequirementAssertion à the class dont focus nodes it constrains."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/mediatedRequirementVia|rdfs:label"
msgid "mediated requirement via"
msgstr "mediated requirement via"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/mediatedRequirementVia|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:MediatedPropertyRequirementAssertion to the mediating property whose values must carry the required property. Domain logic:MediatedPropertyRequirementAssertion; single-valued. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:mediatedRequirementVia only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:MediatedPropertyRequirementAssertion à the mediating propriété dont values doit carry the obligatoire propriété."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/mediates|rdfs:label"
msgid "mediates"
msgstr "mediates"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/mediates|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a Relator to a mediation role — the relationship between an objectified relation and each of its relata, on which the Relator existentially depends. A Relator must mediate at least two distinct entities (the relator-mediation discipline, RelComp), reached either through two distinct roles or through a single non-functional role; the material relation the Relator grounds holds in virtue of these mediation links. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:mediates only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a Relator à a mediation role — the relation entre an objectified relation et each de its relata, sur qui the Relator existentially depends."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/memberOf|rdfs:label"
msgid "member of"
msgstr "member of"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/memberOf|skos:definition"
msgid "The member-collection relation: relates a member to a logic:Collection it belongs to, where the members are the relevant units of the whole. Distinct from logic:partOf and logic:properPartOf: collection membership is not mereological parthood — a team member is a member of, not a proper part of, the team, and membership does not inherit parthood's transitivity through the collection."
msgstr "Le member-collection relation: relie a member à a logic:collection it belongs to, où the members sont the relevant units de the whole."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/message|rdfs:label"
msgid "message"
msgstr "message"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/message|skos:definition"
msgid "The advisory human-readable message a logic:Constraint violation attaches (projected to sh:message). Presentation-only and load-bearing-false: it carries no identity, so two constraints differing only in their message are the same constraint. Absent means no message. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:message only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le advisory human-readable message a logic:contrainte violation attaches (projected à sh:message)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/mnemomorphic|rdfs:label"
msgid "mnemomorphic"
msgstr "mnemomorphic"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/mnemomorphic|skos:definition"
msgid "Whether a logic:Correspondence's forward get leg retains a source witness — factoring through the graph of the correspondence so that put is obtained by projecting along the retained witness rather than synthesizing a plausible source. The bit is orthogonal to the logic:MorphismClass rung but is what lets a correspondence climb it: a retained witness is what discharges put ∘ get = id (the logic:SectionLaw), the dividing line between recoverable subsumption and reconstructed approximation. True or false (default false); a false value bars any section / retraction claim. Range xsd:boolean (domain left open, like logic:loadBearing)."
msgstr "Whether a logic:correspondance's forward get leg retains a source témoin — factoring par the graphe de the correspondance so qui put est obtained par projecting along the retained témoin plutôt que synthesizing a plausible source."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/modelSemantics|rdfs:label"
msgid "model semantics"
msgstr "modèle sémantique"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/modelSemantics|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to the logic:ModelSemantics it selects — which models are authoritative. Single-valued on the contract. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:ModelSemantics (stated in prose, matching the module's convention). Probabilistic reasoning is never a value here — graded belief is carried on logic:uncertaintyMeasure alongside whatever model semantics is in force."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract à the logic:ModelSemantics it selects — qui models sont authoritative."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/morphismClass|rdfs:label"
msgid "morphism class"
msgstr "morphism class"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/morphismClass|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Correspondence to its rung on the ordered law-spine (logic:MorphismClass), which caps the logic:CorrespondenceLaw values it may claim. Composition can only weaken this rung. Range logic:MorphismClass (domain stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:morphismClass only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:correspondance à its rung sur the ordered loi-spine (logic:MorphismClass), qui caps the logic:CorrespondenceLaw values it peut claim."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/morphismKind|rdfs:label"
msgid "morphism kind"
msgstr "morphism kind"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/morphismKind|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Correspondence to its logic:MorphismKind — the satisfaction-preserving / commitment-shifting split orthogonal to the rung. A logic:CommitmentShiftingBridge value makes the loss ledger refuse owl:equivalentClass. Range logic:MorphismKind (domain stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:morphismKind only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:correspondance à its logic:MorphismKind — the satisfaction-preserving / engagement-shifting split orthogonal à the rung."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/multiplyPositioned|rdfs:label"
msgid "multiply positioned"
msgstr "multiply positioned"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/multiplyPositioned|skos:definition"
msgid "The derived marker that an entity occupies two or more distinct logic:HolonicPositions — the structural signature of a DAG node sitting on multiple paths through a holarchy, the ground on which a non-trivial path-relative depth band (logic:holonicLevelMin .. logic:holonicLevelMax) exists. It is the positive companion to logic:HolonicLevelIncoherence: where the incoherence violation fires for a profiled holon that occupies NO position, this marker certifies that a holon occupies SEVERAL, so its level is genuinely path-relative rather than single-valued. Never asserted by hand; it is entailed by the foundation lowering by negation-of-equality over the position set (two distinct positionEntity reifiers for the same entity), all-IRI and without any numeric comparison. It grounds only the band's existence, not its endpoint values, which the logic:StratifiedNAFProfile chase cannot compute (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Le dérivé marker qui an entity occupies two ou more distinct logic:HolonicPositions — the structurel signature de a DAG nœud sitting sur multiple paths par a holarchy, the ground sur qui a non-trivial chemin-relative depth band (logic:holonicLevelMin .."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/namesContradictionWitness|rdfs:label"
msgid "names contradiction witness"
msgstr "names contradiction témoin"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/namesContradictionWitness|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:RefutationAcceptanceWitness to the concrete logic:ContradictionWitness (an IRI) its refutation rests on — the individual forced to owl:Nothing and the jointly-inconsistent premises. Domain logic:RefutationAcceptanceWitness (stated in prose). A refutation naming no witness is an unreplayable assertion, not a proof."
msgstr "Relates a logic:RefutationAcceptanceWitness à the concret logic:ContradictionWitness (an IRI) its réfutation rests sur — the individu forced à owl:Nothing et the jointly-incohérent premises."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/naryArg0|rdfs:label"
msgid "n-ary argument 0"
msgstr "n-ary argument 0"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/naryArg0|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a reifier node to the term in argument position 0 of the n-ary tuple it reifies. The flat-binary positional predicate the evaluable lowering emits for the first argument of a fixed-arity n-ary atom Rel(a₀,…): logic:naryArg0(R, a₀) beside logic:instanceOf(R, Rel). Directly evaluable in the binary relational core; the zero-based position is fixed in the predicate itself so no separate index carrier is needed. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:naryArg0 only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a reifier nœud à the terme dans argument position 0 de the n-ary tuple it reifies."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/naryArg1|rdfs:label"
msgid "n-ary argument 1"
msgstr "n-ary argument 1"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/naryArg1|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a reifier node to the term in argument position 1 of the n-ary tuple it reifies. The flat-binary positional predicate the evaluable lowering emits for the second argument of a fixed-arity n-ary atom; companion to logic:naryArg0. Directly evaluable in the binary relational core. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:naryArg1 only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a reifier nœud à the terme dans argument position 1 de the n-ary tuple it reifies."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/naryArg2|rdfs:label"
msgid "n-ary argument 2"
msgstr "n-ary argument 2"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/naryArg2|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a reifier node to the term in argument position 2 of the n-ary tuple it reifies. The flat-binary positional predicate the evaluable lowering emits for the third argument of a fixed-arity n-ary atom; companion to logic:naryArg0 and logic:naryArg1. Directly evaluable in the binary relational core. The enumerated positional predicates run 0 … N for the maximum fixed arity in play (ternary here); a higher arity extends the closed set with the next positional predicate. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:naryArg2 only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a reifier nœud à the terme dans argument position 2 de the n-ary tuple it reifies."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/necessaryFor|rdfs:label"
msgid "necessary for"
msgstr "necessary for"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/necessaryFor|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a sub-gmeow:Goal that must be satisfied for a gmeow:Goal to be satisfied. Domain gmeow:Goal, range gmeow:Goal (stated in prose). The relation an logic:AndDecomposition groups: all necessary sub-goals must hold together. One of the four decomposition relations carrying satisfaction dependency, typed apart from gmeow:properPartOf (structural part-hood) — the satisfaction dependency planning needs that part-hood alone does not express."
msgstr "Relates a sub-gmeow:objectif qui doit be satisfied pour a gmeow:objectif à be satisfied."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/negatedBody|rdfs:label"
msgid "negated body"
msgstr "negated body"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/negatedBody|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Rule to a negated (negation-as-failure) body atom: the antecedent literal that must NOT be derivable for the rule to fire. Parallel to logic:body (the positive antecedent atoms) but read under closed-world negation, so a rule with any logic:negatedBody atom requires at least logic:StratifiedNAFProfile rather than logic:PositiveHornProfile. The atom itself is a reified rdf:subject/rdf:predicate/rdf:object triple exactly as for logic:body; only its polarity differs."
msgstr "Relates a logic:règle à a negated (negation-as-échec) body atom: the antecedent literal qui doit NOT be derivable pour the règle à fire."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/negationOperator|rdfs:label"
msgid "negation operator"
msgstr "negation opérateur"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/negationOperator|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to a logic:NegationOperator its programs may use. Set-valued on the contract: a program may legitimately use explicit (strong) negation and negation-as-failure together, so this records the permitted operator set, not a single chosen operator. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:NegationOperator (stated in prose, matching the module's convention)."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract à a logic:NegationOperator its programs peut use."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/nextActionSchema|rdfs:label"
msgid "next action schema"
msgstr "next action schéma"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/nextActionSchema|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a policy to the logic:ActionSchema its selected branch invokes — the next action chosen from what an observation revealed. Domain a policy, range logic:ActionSchema (stated in prose). Surfaced by the native evaluator alongside logic:selectedBranch so a policy reading is possible from the materialized output. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:nextActionSchema only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a politique à the logic:ActionSchema its selected branch invokes — the next action chosen de what an observation revealed."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/nondeterministicOutcome|rdfs:label"
msgid "nondeterministic outcome"
msgstr "nondeterministic résultat"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/nondeterministicOutcome|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ActionSchema to one of its alternative effects, each reified as a logic:Outcome node naming via logic:outcomeSituation the distinct successor situation it reaches — multi-valued, so an action whose result is not fixed is represented faithfully rather than collapsed to a single effect. The outcome set this enumerates is why plan success must be quantified (logic:planSuccessMode) and why compensation is outcome-indexed: each logic:Outcome branch carries its own logic:compensation. Domain logic:ActionSchema, range logic:Outcome (stated in prose). One of the eight action-theory facets."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ActionSchema à one de its alternative effects, each reified as a logic:résultat nœud naming via logic:outcomeSituation the distinct successor situation it reaches — à valeurs multiples, so an action dont résultat n'est pas fixed est represented faithfully plutôt que collapsed à a single effet."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/not|rdfs:label"
msgid "not"
msgstr "not"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/not|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a strong-negation logic:Formula to its single negated sub-formula. This is explicit (classical) negation and is kept distinct from negation-as-failure, which is a body-literal flag on a derivation rule (logic:negatedBody): the two are never conflated."
msgstr "Relates a strong-negation logic:formule à its single negated sub-formule."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/objectiveDirection|rdfs:label"
msgid "objective direction"
msgstr "objective direction"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/objectiveDirection|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates an optimization-goal logic:GoalEvaluation to the direction and unit/frame against which its logic:objectiveValue is read — whether the measure is to be maximized or minimized, and in what units the value is stated. Domain logic:GoalEvaluation (stated in prose); the range is left open so the direction/unit-frame may be carried as a structured value. The companion of logic:objectiveValue: a value without its direction and frame is uninterpretable. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:objectiveDirection only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates an optimization-objectif logic:GoalEvaluation à the direction et unit/frame contre qui its logic:objectiveValue est read — whether the measure est à be maximized ou minimized, et dans what units the valeur est stated."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/objectiveValue|rdfs:label"
msgid "objective value"
msgstr "objective valeur"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/objectiveValue|skos:definition"
msgid "The measured quantity an optimization goal extremizes, carried on a logic:GoalEvaluation. Domain logic:GoalEvaluation (stated in prose). The range is intentionally left open (no rdfs:range), matching the module's quantitative axes; its direction and unit/frame are carried by logic:objectiveDirection. NEVER folded into a truth value and never into an uncertainty measure — DISTINCT from logic:confidence, logic:probability, logic:weight, logic:evidenceStrength, from logic:satisfactionDegree, and from logic:utility. A probability over outcomes is never the objective value being optimized."
msgstr "Le measured quantity an optimization objectif extremizes, carried sur a logic:GoalEvaluation."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/obligationDischargeCondition|rdfs:label"
msgid "obligation discharge condition"
msgstr "obligation acquittement condition"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/obligationDischargeCondition|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:NonEntailmentObligation to the logic:DischargeCondition under which its absence-of-proof is conclusively checkable. An obligation declaring a condition the engine does not wire (anything other than logic:DischargeSyntacticReachability or logic:DischargeFiniteClosure) is a hard error, never a silent pass. Domain logic:NonEntailmentObligation, range logic:DischargeCondition."
msgstr "Relates a logic:NonEntailmentObligation à the logic:DischargeCondition sous qui its absence-of-preuve est conclusively checkable."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/obligationDischargeVerdict|rdfs:label"
msgid "obligation discharge verdict"
msgstr "obligation acquittement verdict"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/obligationDischargeVerdict|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:NonEntailmentObligation to the logic:DischargeVerdict the check returned — logic:ObligationDischarged, logic:ObligationUnknown or logic:ObligationViolated. Computed by the engine, not asserted by hand. Domain logic:NonEntailmentObligation, range logic:DischargeVerdict."
msgstr "Relates a logic:NonEntailmentObligation à the logic:DischargeVerdict the vérification returned — logic:ObligationDischarged, logic:ObligationUnknown ou logic:ObligationViolated."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/obligationForbiddenPredicate|rdfs:label"
msgid "obligation forbidden predicate"
msgstr "obligation forbidden prédicat"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/obligationForbiddenPredicate|skos:definition"
msgid "The IRI of the predicate a logic:NonEntailmentObligation forbids the closure from ever containing (and forbids any rule head from producing). The check reads this IRI, then either proves it unreachable over the rule strata (logic:DischargeSyntacticReachability) or absent from the materialized closure (logic:DischargeFiniteClosure). Single-valued, xsd:anyURI. Domain logic:NonEntailmentObligation. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:obligationForbiddenPredicate only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le IRI de the prédicat a logic:NonEntailmentObligation forbids the fermeture de ever containing (and forbids tout règle head de producing)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/observation|rdfs:label"
msgid "observation"
msgstr "observation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/observation|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ActionSchema to what executing the action reveals — the seam to the cognitive layer (design/LOGIC-COGNITION.md). A plan whose next action is chosen from what an earlier action's observation reveals is a policy. Domain logic:ActionSchema (stated in prose). One of the eight action-theory facets; a NEW facet, not a reuse of any cognition term."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ActionSchema à what executing the action reveals — the seam à the cognitif layer (design/LOGIC-COGNITION.md)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/occurrentBoundary|rdfs:label"
msgid "occurrent boundary"
msgstr "occurrent boundary"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/occurrentBoundary|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a perdurant to its boundary value — logic:Open (an on-going action, an open temporal interval: the arriving) or logic:Closed (a completed unitary event, a closed interval: the arrival). The action(open)/event(closed) typing of the YAMATO/Galton refinement, carried as a VALUE rather than a subclass (Principle 9): the same occurrence is open while it unfolds and closed once whole, so boundedness is an indexed value, not a rigid kind. The formal name for the prescriptive-to-descriptive seam — an open action is the doing, the closed event its done record. An occurrent bearing both logic:Open and logic:Closed is the logic:OccurrentBoundaryMismatch violation."
msgstr "Relates a perdurant à its boundary valeur — logic:ouvert (an on-going action, an ouvert temporal interval: the arriving) ou logic:Closed (a completed unitary event, a closed interval: the arrival)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/occurrentConstituent|rdfs:label"
msgid "occurrent constituent"
msgstr "occurrent constituent"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/occurrentConstituent|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a unitary occurrent to a process that constitutes it: the change-stuff an event is made of — a marathon is constituted by the running, a fermentation-event by the fermenting. The constitutive reading of the YAMATO/Galton dictum that events are made of processes: distinct from temporal parthood (logic:temporalPartOf) and from causal parthood (logic:causalPartOf), and carries NO parthood-subsumption rule, so an event's constituting process is not thereby asserted a temporal part of it — constitution, not parthood. The bridge from the unitary, completed logic:Event to the dissective logic:Process whose unfolding it bounds."
msgstr "Relates a unitary occurrent à a process qui constitutes it: the change-stuff an event est made de — a marathon est constituted par the running, a fermentation-event par the fermenting."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/onClass|rdfs:label"
msgid "on class"
msgstr "on class"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/onClass|skos:definition"
msgid "The target class of a compact constraint-sugar record: the focus nodes the expanded logic:Constraint ranges over (rdf:type(this, C) becomes the range-restricting ∀ guard, from which the shape target is derived). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:onClass only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le target class de a compact contrainte-sugar record: the focus nodes the expanded logic:contrainte ranges sur (rdf:type(this, C) becomes the plage-restricting ∀ guard, de qui the forme target est dérivé)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/operand|rdfs:label"
msgid "operand"
msgstr "operand"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/operand|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a compositional logic:GoalExpression (conjunctive, disjunctive, conditional, or deadline-window) to one of its sub-expressions — multi-valued, so a conjunction or disjunction over several sub-goals is carried faithfully. Domain logic:GoalExpression, range logic:GoalExpression (stated in prose). For a conjunctive goal every operand must be satisfied; for a disjunctive goal any one suffices; a conditional or deadline-window goal carries its single guarded/windowed target as its operand. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:operand only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a compositional logic:GoalExpression (conjonctif, disjunctive, conditionnel, ou deadline-window) à one de its sub-expressions — à valeurs multiples, so a conjunction ou disjunction sur several sub-goals est carried faithfully."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/or|rdfs:label"
msgid "or"
msgstr "or"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/or|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a disjunction logic:Formula to each of its operand sub-formulae (multi-valued, two or more). Disjunction is commutative and associative, so the canonical identity flattens nested disjunctions and is insensitive to operand order. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:or only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a disjunction logic:formule à each de its operand sub-formulae (à valeurs multiples, two ou more)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/orderedType|rdfs:label"
msgid "ordered type"
msgstr "ordered type"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/orderedType|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a type to its order (level) in the multi-level hierarchy: a first-order type is order 1, a type whose instances are first-order types is order 2, and so on. Makes the deep-instantiation level explicit so logic:instanceOf chains can be checked for level coherence (an order-n type instantiates an order-(n+1) type), the well-formedness condition that keeps HiLog multi-level modeling stratified. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:orderedType only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a type à its order (niveau) dans the multi-niveau hierarchy: a premier ordre type est order 1, a type dont instances sont premier ordre types est order 2, et so on."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/outcomeAssignment|rdfs:label"
msgid "outcome assignment"
msgstr "résultat assignment"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/outcomeAssignment|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:JointOutcome to a correlated logic:probability fact (the reified base triple) that is TRUE in this outcome. Correlated facts of the model that are not named by any logic:outcomeAssignment of an outcome are false in that outcome — the assignment is read as the positive set, the complement against the model's logic:correlates support. The range is intentionally left open (no rdfs:range), for the same reason as logic:correlates: its object is a reified logic:probability statement, which carries no dedicated class in this standalone module."
msgstr "Relates a logic:JointOutcome à a correlated logic:probability fact (the reified base triple) qui est TRUE dans this résultat."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/outcomeOfProgram|rdfs:label"
msgid "outcome of program"
msgstr "résultat of program"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/outcomeOfProgram|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:TransactionOutcome to the transaction program whose execution it records — a transaction-program combinator node (logic:SerialConjunction, logic:Choice, logic:Fallback, or logic:Iteration). Domain logic:TransactionOutcome, range a transaction-program node (stated in prose). It ties the verdict back to the program that produced it without conflating the outcome (a run record) with the program (the structure that was run). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:outcomeOfProgram only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:TransactionOutcome à the transaction program dont exécution it enregistre — a transaction-program combinator nœud (logic:SerialConjunction, logic:Choice, logic:Fallback, ou logic:itération)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/outcomeSituation|rdfs:label"
msgid "outcome situation"
msgstr "résultat situation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/outcomeSituation|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Outcome (one branch of an action schema's nondeterministic outcome set) to the successor logic:Situation it reaches. Domain logic:Outcome, range logic:Situation (stated in prose). The branch's own logic:compensation recovers from this specific successor, so recovery is outcome-indexed rather than a single generic undo."
msgstr "Relates a logic:résultat (one branch de an action schéma's nondeterministic résultat set) à the successor logic:situation it reaches."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/overlaps|rdfs:label"
msgid "overlaps"
msgstr "overlaps"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/overlaps|skos:definition"
msgid "Mereological overlap: two entities share a common part. The primitive sharing notion that must be settled before disjointness or weak supplementation can be stated — logic:disjoint is its negation, and logic:WeakSupplementation is never applied where overlap is undefined. It is derived from logic:properPartOf: entities that share a proper part overlap, and a proper part overlaps its whole. Symmetric in intent (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Mereological overlap: two entities share a commun part."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/overridesIrreflexivity|rdfs:label"
msgid "overrides is irreflexive"
msgstr "overrides is irreflexive"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/overridesIrreflexivity|skos:definition"
msgid "Asserts on the canonical carrier that gmeow:overrides is irreflexive: a norm never overrides itself, as its skos:definition states. The native coherence gate reads this to raise a violation for a norm asserted to override itself; the generated SHACL constraint surface is its projection."
msgstr "Asserts sur the canonique carrier qui gmeow:overrides est irreflexive: a norm jamais overrides itself, as its skos:définition states."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/partOf|rdfs:label"
msgid "part of"
msgstr "part of"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/partOf|skos:definition"
msgid "The general (reflexive) parthood relation: relates an entity to a whole it is part of, where every entity is trivially part of itself. The mereological base relation over which logic:properPartOf is the strict (irreflexive) restriction. Distinct from logic:memberOf, which relates a member to a collection without the part being a part of the whole in the mereological sense."
msgstr "Le general (reflexive) parthood relation: relie an entity à a whole it est part of, où chaque entity est trivially part de itself."


msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/partOfTransitivity|rdfs:label"
msgid "partOf is transitive"
msgstr "partOf is transitive"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/partOfTransitivity|skos:definition"
msgid "Asserts on the canonical carrier that gmeow:partOf is transitive: the universal part-to-whole spine its skos:definition names as transitive and intentionally broad. The native coherence gate reads this to close the parthood spine."
msgstr "Asserts sur the canonique carrier qui gmeow:partOf est transitive: the universel part-to-whole spine its skos:définition nomme as transitive et intentionally broad."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/pathDepthArg|rdfs:label"
msgid "path depth argument"
msgstr "chemin depth argument"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/pathDepthArg|skos:definition"
msgid "The concrete depth bound supplied at a logic:PathInvocation for the named depth parameter of the invoked logic:PathShape (its logic:pathDepthParam): the value of ?maxDepth in :name(?maxDepth := 2). Bounds the traversal to at most this many hops for this invocation without altering the shape itself. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:pathDepthArg only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le concret depth bound supplied at a logic:PathInvocation pour the named depth parameter de the invoked logic:PathShape (its logic:pathDepthParam): the valeur de ?maxDepth dans :name(?maxDepth := 2)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/pathDepthParam|rdfs:label"
msgid "path depth parameter"
msgstr "chemin depth parameter"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/pathDepthParam|skos:definition"
msgid "The name of the depth parameter a logic:PathShape exposes for parametric invocation — 'maxDepth' in :nearbyOrgs(?maxDepth := 2). A logic:PathInvocation binds this parameter with logic:pathDepthArg. Default-absent: a shape with a fixed depth and no exposed parameter carries no logic:pathDepthParam and is invoked without an argument. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:pathDepthParam only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le name de the depth parameter a logic:PathShape exposes pour parametric invocation — 'maxDepth' dans :nearbyOrgs(?maxDepth := 2)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/pathMaxDepth|rdfs:label"
msgid "path maximum depth"
msgstr "chemin maximum depth"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/pathMaxDepth|skos:definition"
msgid "The inclusive upper bound on the traversal length of a logic:PathShape — the n in a bounded {min,n} path. Default-absent: a shape with no logic:pathMaxDepth is unbounded (the SPARQL-+ / transitive-closure reading), traversing arbitrarily many hops. When present it makes the path a bounded {1,n} traversal, which SPARQL 1.1 §9 cannot express directly."
msgstr "Le inclusive upper bound sur the traversal length de a logic:PathShape — the n dans a bounded {min,n} chemin."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/pathMinDepth|rdfs:label"
msgid "path minimum depth"
msgstr "chemin minimum depth"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/pathMinDepth|skos:definition"
msgid "The inclusive lower bound on the traversal length of a logic:PathShape — the min in a bounded {min,max} path. Default-absent: a shape with no logic:pathMinDepth starts at one hop (min = 1). Must not exceed logic:pathMaxDepth when both are present; a minimum above the maximum is a malformed shape and is rejected by the frontend, not silently repaired."
msgstr "Le inclusive lower bound sur the traversal length de a logic:PathShape — the min dans a bounded {min,max} chemin."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/pathNamespaceScope|rdfs:label"
msgid "path namespace scope"
msgstr "chemin namespace scope"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/pathNamespaceScope|skos:definition"
msgid "A predicate-namespace IRI prefix that scopes a wildcard step of a logic:PathShape: when logic:pathWildcard is true, only predicates whose IRI begins with this namespace are traversed. Bounds the fan-out of an otherwise any-predicate walk to a single vocabulary. Default-absent on a wildcard shape: the wildcard matches predicates in any namespace. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:pathNamespaceScope only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Un prédicat-namespace IRI prefix qui scopes a wildcard step de a logic:PathShape: lorsque logic:pathWildcard est true, uniquement predicates dont IRI begins avec this namespace sont traversed."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/pathStepPredicate|rdfs:label"
msgid "path step predicate"
msgstr "chemin step prédicat"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/pathStepPredicate|skos:definition"
msgid "The named predicate that each hop of a logic:PathShape traverses. Present on a named-predicate path; absent on a wildcard path (where logic:pathWildcard is true instead). A shape that carries BOTH a logic:pathStepPredicate and logic:pathWildcard true is malformed — the base step is a named predicate XOR a wildcard — and is rejected by the frontend rather than silently resolved."
msgstr "Le named prédicat qui each hop de a logic:PathShape traverses."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/pathWildcard|rdfs:label"
msgid "path wildcard"
msgstr "chemin wildcard"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/pathWildcard|skos:definition"
msgid "Marks a logic:PathShape whose step matches ANY predicate rather than one named predicate — the 'any predicate within n hops' traversal that SPARQL 1.1 §9 property paths cannot express. When true the step is unconstrained except by an optional logic:pathNamespaceScope; mutually exclusive with logic:pathStepPredicate. Default-absent (false): the path follows the named logic:pathStepPredicate."
msgstr "Marks a logic:PathShape dont step matches ANY prédicat plutôt que one named prédicat — the 'any prédicat within n hops' traversal qui SPARQL 1.1 §9 propriété paths ne peut pas express."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/permittedConflictWitness|rdfs:label"
msgid "permitted conflict witness"
msgstr "permitted conflit témoin"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/permittedConflictWitness|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a coherence outcome to a disclosed, witnessed contradiction the contract PERMITS (a logic:FindingPermittedEpistemicConflict) — MULTI-valued. Present permitted witnesses do NOT block a logic:CoherenceCertificate; they are surfaced for transparency. Domain logic:CoherenceCertificate or logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation (stated in prose)."
msgstr "Relates a cohérence résultat à a disclosed, witnessed contradiction the contract PERMITS (a logic:FindingPermittedEpistemicConflict) — MULTI-valued."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/planBody|rdfs:label"
msgid "plan body"
msgstr "plan body"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/planBody|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Plan to the ROOT node of its program TREE — the structured-program form an interpreter walks, distinct from logic:planFlowEdge, which gathers the binary-edge FLOW-GRAPH form the Tarjan acyclicity certifier runs over. The root is normally a transaction-program combinator (logic:SerialConjunction, logic:Choice, logic:ConcurrentComposition, logic:Fallback, or logic:Iteration), but a single-step plan roots directly at a logic:ActionSchema leaf — no synthetic wrapper combinator is required. Single-valued: a plan has one program root, from which the whole tree is reachable through logic:leftOperand / logic:rightOperand / logic:iterationBody / logic:iterationCondition. A plan whose program tree carries a logic:Iteration loop is OUTSIDE the certified acyclic DAG fragment by construction — the loop is legitimate canonical program structure, not a well-formedness defect — so such a plan does NOT run logic:executedUnderContract the DAG-workflow profile. Domain logic:Plan, range a transaction-program combinator node OR a logic:ActionSchema leaf (stated in prose, matching the module's domain/range convention)."
msgstr "Relates a logic:plan à the ROOT nœud de its program TREE — the structured-program form an interpreter walks, distinct de logic:planFlowEdge, qui gathers the binary-edge flux-graphe form the Tarjan acyclicity certifier runs over."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/planBranch|rdfs:label"
msgid "plan branch"
msgstr "plan branch"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/planBranch|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a plan to one of its observation-conditioned branches. A plan that carries logic:planBranch branches whose choice depends on what an earlier action's logic:observation reveals is a POLICY — a reading of a plan, not a separate class (see logic:Plan). Domain a plan, range a branch (stated in prose)."
msgstr "Relates a plan à one de its observation-conditioned branches."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/planCertification|rdfs:label"
msgid "plan certification"
msgstr "plan certification"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/planCertification|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Plan to the logic:ReasoningResult recording its DAG-workflow certification verdict — the result the acyclicity certifier emits when the plan runs logic:executedUnderContract a contract requesting logic:DagWorkflowResource. The result carries logic:resultEvaluation (logic:EvaluationCompleted on an acyclic plan, logic:EvaluationUnsupported on a cyclic one) and logic:resultCompleteness (logic:CompleteForFragment when certified), and on a cyclic plan it discloses the offending cycle members through logic:dagCycleWitness — so the `unsupported` verdict and its witness are reachable from the plan rather than computed and discarded. Domain logic:Plan, range logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose). The plan stays valid canonically under a non-DAG contract; this link records only what the DAG profile certified over it."
msgstr "Relates a logic:plan à the logic:ReasoningResult recording its DAG-workflow certification verdict — the résultat the acyclicity certifier emits lorsque the plan runs logic:executedUnderContract a contract requesting logic:DagWorkflowResource."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/planFlowEdge|rdfs:label"
msgid "plan flow edge"
msgstr "plan flux edge"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/planFlowEdge|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Plan to a reified flow edge (logic:ControlFlowEdge or logic:DataFlowEdge) that constitutes its FLOW-GRAPH — the binary-edge form the DAG-workflow acyclicity certifier runs Tarjan SCC over, each edge mediating a source (logic:flowFrom) and a target (logic:flowTo) process node. MULTI-valued: a plan gathers all the control-flow and dataflow edges of its process graph. The canonical-plan counterpart of the build pipeline's gmeow:hasStage stage-membership — where a pipeline gathers gmeow:PipelineStage members whose gmeow:dataflowConsumes edges form its graph, a logic:Plan gathers its reified flow edges directly — so a plan's flow graph is reachable from the plan rather than left as free-standing edges. A plan whose planFlowEdge closure is acyclic is certified logic:CompleteForFragment under logic:DagWorkflowResource; a cyclic closure resolves to the `unsupported` verdict (logic:EvaluationUnsupported) with the offending members disclosed by logic:dagCycleWitness, never silently truncated. Domain logic:Plan, range logic:ControlFlowEdge or logic:DataFlowEdge (stated in prose)."
msgstr "Relates a logic:plan à a reified flux edge (logic:ControlFlowEdge ou logic:DataFlowEdge) qui constitutes its flux-graphe — the binary-edge form the DAG-workflow acyclicity certifier runs Tarjan SCC over, each edge mediating a source (logic:flowFrom) et a target (logic:flowTo) process nœud."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/planGoal|rdfs:label"
msgid "plan goal"
msgstr "plan objectif"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/planGoal|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Plan to the gmeow:Goal that is its success criterion — the goal the plan's steps, invoking action schemas, are arranged to reach. Domain logic:Plan, range gmeow:Goal (stated in prose). The plan's success against this goal is quantified over nondeterministic outcomes through logic:planSuccessMode. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:planGoal only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:plan à the gmeow:objectif qui est its success criterion — the objectif the plan's steps, invoking action schemas, sont arranged à reach."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/planSuccessMode|rdfs:label"
msgid "plan success mode"
msgstr "plan success mode"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/planSuccessMode|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Plan to the logic:PlanSuccessMode quantifying its success over the nondeterministic outcomes of its action schemas. Domain logic:Plan, range logic:PlanSuccessMode (stated in prose). The quantification exists because the bare executional-success reading of the transaction layer would count one favourable path as success; this declares whether some, every, or every fair execution must reach the goal. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:planSuccessMode only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:plan à the logic:PlanSuccessMode quantifying its success sur the nondeterministic outcomes de its action schemas."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/positionContext|rdfs:label"
msgid "position context"
msgstr "position contexte"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/positionContext|skos:definition"
msgid "The context role of a logic:HolonicPosition: the context under which the position is occupied. Holon-ness is contextual — an entity that is a holon under one context need not be under another. One of the five role properties (with logic:positionEntity, logic:positionHolarchy, logic:positionInterval, logic:positionPath) that reify the five-place holonic-position relation onto the arity-bounded reasoning surface."
msgstr "Le contexte role de a logic:HolonicPosition: the contexte sous qui the position est occupied."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/positionEntity|rdfs:label"
msgid "position entity"
msgstr "position entity"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/positionEntity|skos:definition"
msgid "The entity role of a logic:HolonicPosition: the individual that occupies the holonic position — the thing that is a holon along the position's path. One of the five role properties (with logic:positionHolarchy, logic:positionContext, logic:positionInterval, logic:positionPath) that reify the five-place holonic-position relation onto the arity-bounded reasoning surface. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:positionEntity only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le entity role de a logic:HolonicPosition: the individu qui occupies the holonic position — the thing qui est a holon along the position's chemin."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/positionHolarchy|rdfs:label"
msgid "position holarchy"
msgstr "position holarchy"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/positionHolarchy|skos:definition"
msgid "The holarchy role of a logic:HolonicPosition: the logic:Holarchy within which the position is occupied. Holon-ness is always relative to a holarchy; the same entity may occupy holonic positions in several holarchies. One of the five role properties (with logic:positionEntity, logic:positionContext, logic:positionInterval, logic:positionPath) that reify the five-place holonic-position relation. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:positionHolarchy only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le holarchy role de a logic:HolonicPosition: the logic:Holarchy within qui the position est occupied."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/positionInterval|rdfs:label"
msgid "position interval"
msgstr "position interval"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/positionInterval|skos:definition"
msgid "The interval role of a logic:HolonicPosition: the interval over which the position is occupied. Holon-ness is temporally bounded — an entity may occupy a holonic position over one interval and not another. One of the five role properties (with logic:positionEntity, logic:positionHolarchy, logic:positionContext, logic:positionPath) that reify the five-place holonic-position relation."
msgstr "Le interval role de a logic:HolonicPosition: the interval sur qui the position est occupied."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/positionPath|rdfs:label"
msgid "position path"
msgstr "position chemin"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/positionPath|skos:definition"
msgid "The path role of a logic:HolonicPosition: the path through the holarchy along which the position is read. Holarchies are DAGs, so a holonic position — and the logic:holonicLevel measured at it — is meaningful only relative to a path; two paths may place the same entity at different depths, and both are correct. One of the five role properties (with logic:positionEntity, logic:positionHolarchy, logic:positionContext, logic:positionInterval) that reify the five-place holonic-position relation. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:positionPath only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le chemin role de a logic:HolonicPosition: the chemin par the holarchy along qui the position est read."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/precedenceTenureDistinctness|rdfs:label"
msgid "a precedence tenure's higher and lower norms are distinct"
msgstr "a precedence tenure's higher and lower norms are distinct"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/precedenceTenureDistinctness|skos:definition"
msgid "Asserts that a gmeow:PrecedenceTenure's gmeow:precedenceHigher and gmeow:precedenceLower norms must be distinct: a norm does not take precedence over itself. The native coherence gate raises a violation when they coincide."
msgstr "Asserts qui a gmeow:PrecedenceTenure's gmeow:precedenceHigher et gmeow:precedenceLower norms doit be distinct: a norm ne fait pas take precedence sur itself."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/precedes|rdfs:label"
msgid "precedes"
msgstr "precedes"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/precedes|skos:definition"
msgid "A conflict (precedence) edge in a logic:ConcurrentHistory: 'from precedes to' orders the conflicting operation of transaction 'from' before that of transaction 'to' in the witnessed schedule. Two operations conflict when they touch the same item and at least one writes it; the edge direction records which came first in the interleaving. Domain and range are transaction-program nodes (stated in prose). A CYCLE over logic:precedes is a serialization anomaly (logic:SerializationAnomaly) — between two transactions it requires edges in BOTH directions, the write-skew / lost-update shape — and is NEVER a logical contradiction (logic:contradictionWitness): it is a property of the history, not of any single state."
msgstr "Un conflit (precedence) edge dans a logic:ConcurrentHistory: 'from precedes to' orders the conflicting operation de transaction 'from' avant qui de transaction 'to' dans the witnessed schedule."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/precondition|rdfs:label"
msgid "precondition"
msgstr "précondition"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/precondition|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ActionSchema to the situation that must hold for the action to apply — the gate on the elementary state transition the schema grounds. Domain logic:ActionSchema (stated in prose, matching the module's domain/range convention). One of the eight action-theory facets means–end reasoning reads. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:precondition only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ActionSchema à the situation qui doit hold pour the action à apply — the gate sur the elementary état transition the schéma grounds."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/preservationKind|rdfs:label"
msgid "preservation kind"
msgstr "preservation kind"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/preservationKind|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a projection (or projection-report entry) to the logic:PreservationKind it claims: the machine-readable preservation polarity in the loss ledger. Lets a report say not just 'dropped modality' but, e.g., 'OWL-EL is a logic:SoundUnderApproximation for subclass entailments under profile X; PTIME'. The projections conformance category checks that each emitted projection matches its declared preservation kind."
msgstr "Relates a projection (or projection-report entrée) à the logic:PreservationKind it claims: the machine-readable preservation polarity dans the loss ledger."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/preventsGoal|rdfs:label"
msgid "prevents goal"
msgstr "prevents objectif"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/preventsGoal|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates two gmeow:Goals where achieving one closes the path to the other. Domain gmeow:Goal, range gmeow:Goal (stated in prose). One of seven conflict relations between independently-meaningful goals, weaker than gmeow:counterGoal (constitutive opposition). Distinct from logic:contradictoryGoal: prevention closes a path, it does not entail violation in every world."
msgstr "Relates two gmeow:Goals où achieving one closes the chemin à the other."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/probability|rdfs:label"
msgid "probability"
msgstr "probability"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/probability|skos:definition"
msgid "A calibrated probability under probabilistic fact/event semantics, requiring an explicit independence or dependency model. Distinct from logic:confidence, logic:weight, and logic:evidenceStrength and not interchangeable with them: probabilistic inference is available only in logic:ProbabilisticProfile. A logic:confidence annotation is NOT a probability unless an explicit mapping to this property is declared."
msgstr "Un calibrated probability sous probabilistic fact/event sémantique, requiring an explicit independence ou dependency modèle."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/probabilityModel|rdfs:label"
msgid "probability model"
msgstr "probability modèle"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/probabilityModel|skos:definition"
msgid "Links a rule set or world to the logic:ProbabilityModel that governs its probabilistic inference. Required for any probabilistic query under logic:ProbabilisticProfile: with no logic:probabilityModel declared, probabilistic inference returns unknown rather than assuming independence over the logic:probability facts."
msgstr "Links a règle set ou monde à the logic:ProbabilityModel qui governs its probabilistic inference."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/probesSchema|rdfs:label"
msgid "probes schema"
msgstr "probes schéma"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/probesSchema|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:GateProbe to the logic:ActionSchema it gates. Domain logic:GateProbe, range logic:ActionSchema (stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:probesSchema only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:GateProbe à the logic:ActionSchema it gates."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/probesState|rdfs:label"
msgid "probes state"
msgstr "probes état"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/probesState|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:GateProbe to the state the schema is gated against — the state whose logic:situationObtains and logic:resourceSupply facts the gate reads. Domain logic:GateProbe, range a state (stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:probesState only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:GateProbe à the état the schéma est gated contre — the état dont logic:situationObtains et logic:resourceSupply facts the gate reads."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/producesResultShape|rdfs:label"
msgid "produces result shape"
msgstr "produces résultat forme"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/producesResultShape|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a query (or a competency question) to the logic:ResultShape its result set is guaranteed to satisfy. The query's bindings are validated against this shape after execution; a mismatch is a hard, surfaced error. Single-valued. Range logic:ResultShape (stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:producesResultShape only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a requête (or a competency question) à the logic:ResultShape its résultat set est guaranteed à satisfy."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/projectionTarget|rdfs:label"
msgid "projection target"
msgstr "projection target"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/projectionTarget|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to a logic:ProjectionTarget it requests the answer be rendered to. A standing output request, possibly naming several targets at once (canonical, OWL, Datalog, Common Logic, validation-only); it is not a semantic selection and never alters which entailments hold. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:ProjectionTarget (stated in prose, matching the module's convention)."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract à a logic:ProjectionTarget it requests the answer be rendered to."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/projectsLadderEdge|rdfs:label"
msgid "projects ladder edge"
msgstr "projects ladder edge"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/projectsLadderEdge|skos:definition"
msgid "The ladder property a logic:DimensionThreshold row emits when its dimension clears its threshold: gmeow:isAwareOf, gmeow:knowsAbout, gmeow:understands or gmeow:hasMastered. Range is left open (the gmeow: ladder properties), stated in prose to keep the OWL down-projection clean. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:projectsLadderEdge only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le ladder propriété a logic:DimensionThreshold row emits lorsque its dimension clears its threshold: gmeow:isAwareOf, gmeow:knowsAbout, gmeow:understands ou gmeow:hasMastered."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/projectsToVerdict|rdfs:label"
msgid "projects to verdict"
msgstr "projects to verdict"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/projectsToVerdict|skos:definition"
msgid "The machine-readable image of the SZS→conformance-verdict collapse: relates a logic:SzsStatus individual to the logic:ConformanceVerdict its outcome projects onto. Domain logic:SzsStatus, range logic:ConformanceVerdict (stated in prose). This is the dogfooded, on-gate-checkable form of the native crates/conformance/src/external/status.rs::outcome_for_szs table — the monotone map whose lossiness (many statuses to one verdict) is declared by logic:corrSzsToVerdict and whose per-status edges the no-drift gate compares against the Rust table so the ontology and the code can never disagree."
msgstr "Le machine-readable image de the SZS→conformité-verdict collapse: relie a logic:SzsStatus individu à the logic:ConformanceVerdict its résultat projects onto."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/properPartOf|rdfs:label"
msgid "proper part of"
msgstr "proper part of"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/properPartOf|skos:definition"
msgid "STRICT parthood: relates an entity to a whole it is part of but NOT identical to. Transitive, asymmetric, and irreflexive — a genuine strict partial order (proper-part-of, ancestor). This exact combination is illegal in OWL 2 DL, which globally forbids a property being both transitive and asymmetric (criticism 7, LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md §OWL 2 criticisms); logic: imposes no such global restriction and reasons over it completely, recovering decidability by projection rather than by crippling the canon. The deliberate OWL-2-criticism demonstrator."
msgstr "STRICT parthood: relie an entity à a whole it est part de mais NOT identical to."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/proseFieldProperty|rdfs:label"
msgid "prose field property"
msgstr "prose field propriété"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/proseFieldProperty|skos:definition"
msgid "Names the annotation property a logic:ProseField value stands for — the exact term-level field (skos:definition, gmeow:useWhen or gmeow:avoidWhen) whose prose a harvested candidate formalizes. An annotation property, so the closed logic:ProseField set links to the real field IRI without punning it into the reasoned core. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:proseFieldProperty only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Names the propriété d'annotation a logic:ProseField valeur stands pour — the exact terme-niveau field (skos:définition, gmeow:useWhen ou gmeow:avoidWhen) dont prose a harvested candidat formalizes."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/protocolEnforced|rdfs:label"
msgid "protocol enforced"
msgstr "protocol enforced"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/protocolEnforced|skos:definition"
msgid "The boolean verdict of classifying a logic:ConcurrentHistory's witnessed schedule against the logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol its run declared (logic:declaredProtocol): true iff the schedule respects that protocol's discipline over the run's recorded protocol events (timestamps for logic:TimestampOrdering; lock acquire/release events for the two-phase-locking protocols; cross-leg read-write disjointness for logic:OptimisticValidation). Domain logic:ConcurrentHistory, range xsd:boolean (stated in prose); present only when a protocol is declared. A false verdict carries a human-readable logic:protocolViolationReason. This is HOW-a-guarantee-is-enforced verification, kept distinct from logic:satisfiesCriterion (the history property the schedule satisfies) and logic:isolationLevelAdequacy (whether the schedule meets a declared guarantee strength); a declared protocol whose required events are absent is a hard error, never a false-by-default."
msgstr "Le boolean verdict de classifying a logic:ConcurrentHistory's witnessed schedule contre the logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol its run declared (logic:declaredProtocol): true iff the schedule respects qui protocol's discipline sur the run's recorded protocol events (timestamps pour logic:TimestampOrdering; lock acquire/release events pour the two-phase-locking protocols; cross-leg read-write disjointness pour logic:OptimisticValidation)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/protocolLevelAdequacy|rdfs:label"
msgid "protocol level adequacy"
msgstr "protocol niveau adequacy"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/protocolLevelAdequacy|skos:definition"
msgid "The boolean verdict of classifying whether the logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol a run declares (logic:declaredProtocol) is strong enough to guarantee the logic:IsolationLevel it also declares (logic:declaredIsolationLevel): true iff the protocol's guaranteed ceiling level is at least the declared level. Domain logic:ConcurrentHistory, range xsd:boolean (stated in prose); present only when a run declares BOTH a protocol and a level — otherwise there is no pairing to judge. The guaranteed ceilings are logic:SnapshotIsolation for logic:MultiversionConcurrencyControl and logic:SerializableIsolation (coincident with logic:OpacityIsolation for committed-only histories) for logic:StrictTwoPhaseLocking, logic:StrongStrictTwoPhaseLocking, logic:TimestampOrdering, and logic:OptimisticValidation. The one inadequate pairing this vocabulary admits is logic:MultiversionConcurrencyControl declared under logic:SerializableIsolation or logic:OpacityIsolation, since its snapshot ceiling still admits write skew; a false verdict carries a logic:protocolLevelInadequacyReason. It is a CONSISTENCY CROSS-CHECK between two declarations — kept distinct from logic:protocolEnforced (whether the witnessed schedule respects the mechanism) and logic:isolationLevelAdequacy (whether the witnessed schedule meets the strength) — and never infers the level from the protocol nor the protocol from the level."
msgstr "Le boolean verdict de classifying whether the logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol a run déclare (logic:declaredProtocol) est strong enough à guarantee the logic:IsolationLevel it also déclare (logic:declaredIsolationLevel): true iff the protocol's guaranteed ceiling niveau est au moins the declared niveau."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/protocolLevelInadequacyReason|rdfs:label"
msgid "protocol level inadequacy reason"
msgstr "protocol niveau inadequacy reason"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/protocolLevelInadequacyReason|skos:definition"
msgid "A human-readable description of WHY a run's declared logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol cannot guarantee its declared logic:IsolationLevel — present exactly when logic:protocolLevelAdequacy is false. Domain logic:ConcurrentHistory, range xsd:string (stated in prose). In this vocabulary the case is logic:MultiversionConcurrencyControl declared under logic:SerializableIsolation or logic:OpacityIsolation, and the reason names it: the protocol's guaranteed ceiling is snapshot isolation, which admits write skew, so it does not reach the declared serializable-or-stronger level. It is a declaration-consistency finding, never a claim of logical contradiction within a state."
msgstr "Un human-readable description de WHY a run's declared logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol ne peut pas guarantee its declared logic:IsolationLevel — present exactly lorsque logic:protocolLevelAdequacy est false."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/protocolViolationReason|rdfs:label"
msgid "protocol violation reason"
msgstr "protocol violation reason"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/protocolViolationReason|skos:definition"
msgid "A human-readable description of WHY a logic:ConcurrentHistory's witnessed schedule fails the concurrency-control protocol its run declared — present exactly when logic:protocolEnforced is false. Domain logic:ConcurrentHistory, range xsd:string (stated in prose). It names the discipline the schedule breaks (a non-two-phase lock order, a lock released before commit, a conflict edge against timestamp order, or a cross-leg read-write conflict that optimistic validation would abort), so a protocol failure is surfaced with its cause rather than as a bare boolean. It is a description of a mechanism-level finding, never a claim of logical contradiction within a state."
msgstr "Un human-readable description de WHY a logic:ConcurrentHistory's witnessed schedule fails the concurrence-contrôle protocol its run declared — present exactly lorsque logic:protocolEnforced est false."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/putLeg|rdfs:label"
msgid "put leg"
msgstr "put leg"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/putLeg|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Lens to the logic:TransactionProgram that realizes its put leg — the up-projection put : V × S → S folding a view back into the rich GMEOW source. A lawful put comes only from a logic:mnemomorphic witness or a co-authored put-with-claim; naive backward execution of the get leg is a candidate preimage, never a lawful put. Domain logic:Lens, range logic:TransactionProgram."
msgstr "Relates a logic:Lens à the logic:TransactionProgram qui realizes its put leg — the up-projection put : V × S → S folding a view back dans the rich GMEOW source."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/qualityRole|rdfs:label"
msgid "quality role"
msgstr "qualité role"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/qualityRole|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Quality to the anti-rigid logic:Role its generic quality plays in a bearer-context — height being length playing a role in a human-body context, systolic pressure being pressure playing a role in the arterial-blood-pressure context. The frame-relative leg of the generic-quality/quality-role ladder (Principle 11 stated in role terms), paired with logic:genericQuality: the role contextualizes the frame-independent generic quality, and reuses the existing anti-rigid logic:Role machinery rather than minting a parallel one. A quality bearing a logic:qualityRole with no logic:genericQuality is the logic:QualityRoleWithoutGeneric violation. Domain logic:Quality, range logic:Role (stated in prose, matching the module's convention)."
msgstr "Relates a logic:qualité à the anti-rigid logic:Role its generic qualité plays dans a bearer-contexte — height being length playing a role dans a human-body contexte, systolic pressure being pressure playing a role dans the arterial-blood-pressure contexte."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/quantifiedVariable|rdfs:label"
msgid "quantified variable"
msgstr "quantified variable"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/quantifiedVariable|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a quantifier logic:Formula to one of its bound-variable term-carriers. Each carrier fixes its position in the binder block with logic:termIndex and its name with logic:termVariable; block order is significant, because bound-variable renaming preserves meaning but reordering a quantifier prefix does not."
msgstr "Relates a quantifier logic:formule à one de its bound-variable terme-carriers."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/query|rdfs:label"
msgid "query"
msgstr "requête"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/query|skos:definition"
msgid "The canonical query text a logic:ReasoningResult answers — part of the proof certificate. Single-valued. Domain logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:query only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le canonique requête text a logic:ReasoningResult answers — part de the preuve certificat."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/rawStatusToken|rdfs:label"
msgid "raw status token"
msgstr "raw status token"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/rawStatusToken|skos:definition"
msgid "The verbatim external result-status token carried as provenance, so the coarse logic:ConformanceVerdict projection never discards the distinction the community source drew. Domain a logic:SzsStatus individual or a conformance comparison, range xsd:string (stated in prose): the exact SZS token (e.g. \"ContradictoryAxioms\") or W3C manifest kind before the lossy collapse. This realizes maximal information flow — logic:SzsContradictoryAxioms and logic:SzsUnsatisfiable both project to logic:ConfInconsistent, yet stay distinguishable on the folded individual through this token (design/LOGIC-CONFORMANCE.md, the external FOL soundness oracle)."
msgstr "Le verbatim external résultat-status token carried as provenance, so the coarse logic:ConformanceVerdict projection jamais discards the distinction the community source drew."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/readsFrom|rdfs:label"
msgid "reads from"
msgstr "reads from"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/readsFrom|skos:definition"
msgid "A read-dependency edge of a logic:ConcurrentHistory: 'reader readsFrom writer' records that the reading logic:TransactionStep observed, for a situation in its read set (its schema's logic:precondition), the value written by the writer logic:TransactionStep — the last step to write that situation before the reader in the witnessed interleaving. Domain and range logic:TransactionStep (stated in prose). Emitted only for CROSS-transaction read dependencies (a step reading from the OTHER leg's write), which is where the read-from relation can differ from a serial order and therefore where it carries view-serializability information; intra-leg read dependencies are fixed by the leg's own order and carry none. Together with logic:happensBefore it is the view-serializability surface, kept DISTINCT from logic:precedes, which is the transaction-level conflict edge over which conflict-serializability is decided."
msgstr "Un read-dependency edge de a logic:ConcurrentHistory: 'reader readsFrom writer' enregistre qui the reading logic:TransactionStep observed, pour a situation dans its read set (its schéma's logic:précondition), the valeur written par the writer logic:TransactionStep — the last step à write qui situation avant the reader dans the witnessed interleaving."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/reductionBasis|rdfs:label"
msgid "reduction basis"
msgstr "reduction basis"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/reductionBasis|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReductionTheory to a property-value it treats as part-reducible: the theory holds that a whole bearing this property has it in virtue of its proper parts bearing it, so under that theory the property is an logic:Aggregate rather than an emergent one. The carrier that makes emergence theory-relative — a property in one theory's reduction basis and absent from another's receives opposite verdicts with no contradiction. Without a matching basis entry, a borne whole property is assessed logic:Emergent under the theory (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ReductionTheory à a propriété-valeur it treats as part-reducible: the theory holds qui a whole bearing this propriété possède it dans virtue de its proper parts bearing it, so sous qui theory the propriété est an logic:agrégat plutôt que an emergent one."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/referenceFrame|rdfs:label"
msgid "reference frame"
msgstr "reference frame"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/referenceFrame|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a measurement to the reference frame its logic:measuredValue is expressed in — the coordinate system, datum, unit system, or platform space that fixes what the value means. The frame leg of the true-quantity/measured-value seam (Principle 11: a value asserted without its frame is ill-formed); a logic:measuredValue with no logic:referenceFrame is the logic:MeasurementFrameMissing violation. The foundation-level seam predicate the domain property gmeow:referenceFrame grounds onto by sub-property, so a domain measurement lifts into the constraint's scope. Domain a measurement, range a reference frame (stated in prose, matching the module's convention). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:referenceFrame only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a measurement à the reference frame its logic:measuredValue est expressed dans — the coordinate system, datum, unit system, ou platform space qui fixes what the valeur means."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/refinesGoal|rdfs:label"
msgid "refines goal"
msgstr "refines objectif"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/refinesGoal|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a sub-gmeow:Goal to a coarser gmeow:Goal it makes precise. Domain gmeow:Goal, range gmeow:Goal (stated in prose). One of the four decomposition relations carrying satisfaction dependency, typed apart from gmeow:properPartOf (structural part-hood): a sub-goal may be both a proper part and refine its parent, yet part-hood alone does not express the refinement."
msgstr "Relates a sub-gmeow:objectif à a coarser gmeow:objectif it makes precise."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/relation|rdfs:label"
msgid "relation"
msgstr "relation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/relation|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates an atomic-predication logic:Formula to the relation it predicates, over its ordered logic:argument terms. The relation is reified as a logic:Type individual per the HiLog reflection (see logic:instanceOf and logic:orderedType): predicating over a reified relation individual keeps the object level first-order rather than admitting a predicate variable, so no separate relation or predicate class is minted."
msgstr "Relates an atomique-predication logic:formule à the relation it predicates, sur its ordered logic:argument terms."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/requires|rdfs:label"
msgid "requires"
msgstr "requires"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/requires|skos:definition"
msgid "A required companion predicate of a logic:GuardedImplicationConstraint: when the guard holds, ∃ a value on this predicate is required. Multi-valued (a conjunction of existentials). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:requires only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Un obligatoire companion prédicat de a logic:GuardedImplicationConstraint: lorsque the guard holds, ∃ a valeur sur this prédicat est obligatoire."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/resourceExhausted|rdfs:label"
msgid "resource exhausted"
msgstr "ressource épuisé"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/resourceExhausted|skos:definition"
msgid "A boolean marker on a resource that has been depleted: a resource flagged logic:resourceExhausted \"true\" is unavailable even where a state supplies it (logic:resourceSupply), so an action requiring it via logic:actionResource is gated. Domain a resource, range xsd:boolean (stated in prose). The depletion half of the representation-level resource facet, kept distinct from engine-budget exhaustion."
msgstr "Un boolean marker sur a ressource qui possède been depleted: a ressource flagged logic:resourceExhausted \"true\" est unavailable even où a état supplies it (logic:resourceSupply), so an action requiring it via logic:actionResource est gated."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/resourcePolicy|rdfs:label"
msgid "resource policy"
msgstr "ressource politique"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/resourcePolicy|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to the logic:ResourcePolicy it requests — the engine's execution discipline. A standing request, not a semantic selection; the resource policy holds several independent properties together (a certified-fragment requirement AND a budget), so a contract may carry both logic:CertifiedFragmentResource and logic:BudgetBoundedResource. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:ResourcePolicy (stated in prose, matching the module's convention)."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract à the logic:ResourcePolicy it requests — the engine's exécution discipline."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/resourceSupply|rdfs:label"
msgid "resource supply"
msgstr "ressource supply"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/resourceSupply|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a state to a resource it supplies, recording resource availability at that state for the logic:actionResource facet. The native evaluator gates an action whose required logic:actionResource a state does not supply (or that is flagged logic:resourceExhausted). Domain a state, range the supplied resource (stated in prose). This is the representation-level resource seam to logic:competesForResource — it evaluates the represented resource facet only and is NOT a real build engine-lock."
msgstr "Relates a état à a ressource it supplies, recording ressource availability at qui état pour the logic:actionResource facet."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/resultAssumption|rdfs:label"
msgid "result assumption"
msgstr "résultat assumption"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/resultAssumption|skos:definition"
msgid "A declared closure/identity/revision/witness-policy assumption a logic:ReasoningResult rests on (e.g. closed-world, unique-name, entrenchment-revision, skolem-witness) — MULTI-valued. Domain logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:resultAssumption only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Un declared fermeture/identité/revision/témoin-politique assumption a logic:ReasoningResult rests sur (e.g."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/resultCompleteness|rdfs:label"
msgid "result completeness"
msgstr "résultat complétude"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/resultCompleteness|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningResult to the logic:CompletenessStatus of its answer. Single-valued. Domain logic:ReasoningResult, range logic:CompletenessStatus (stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:resultCompleteness only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ReasoningResult à the logic:CompletenessStatus de its answer."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/resultCounterproof|rdfs:label"
msgid "result counterproof"
msgstr "résultat counterproof"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/resultCounterproof|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningResult to the derivation that proves the explicit negation of its conclusion (the same machinery as logic:resultProof), present iff the negation is derivable. A result carrying BOTH a proof and a counterproof is logic:InfoBoth. Domain logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:resultCounterproof only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ReasoningResult à the dérivation qui proves the explicit negation de its conclusion (the same machinery as logic:resultProof), present iff the negation est derivable."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/resultEvaluation|rdfs:label"
msgid "result evaluation"
msgstr "résultat evaluation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/resultEvaluation|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningResult to the logic:EvaluationStatus the engine reached (the computation axis). Single-valued. Domain logic:ReasoningResult, range logic:EvaluationStatus (stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:resultEvaluation only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ReasoningResult à the logic:EvaluationStatus the engine reached (the computation axis)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/resultInformation|rdfs:label"
msgid "result information"
msgstr "résultat information"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/resultInformation|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningResult to the logic:InformationState verdict about the queried proposition (the information axis). Single-valued. Domain logic:ReasoningResult, range logic:InformationState (stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:resultInformation only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ReasoningResult à the logic:InformationState verdict about the queried proposition (the information axis)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/resultInput|rdfs:label"
msgid "result input"
msgstr "résultat input"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/resultInput|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningResult to the logic:InputStatus it received. Single-valued. Domain logic:ReasoningResult, range logic:InputStatus (stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:resultInput only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ReasoningResult à the logic:InputStatus it received."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/resultPreservation|rdfs:label"
msgid "result preservation"
msgstr "résultat preservation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/resultPreservation|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningResult to each logic:PreservationKind polarity that co-holds for it — MULTI-valued, because the preservation field is a SET of polarities, not a single choice (logic:ValidationOnly is excluded; it names a lowering's purpose, not an answer-preservation polarity). Domain logic:ReasoningResult, range logic:PreservationKind (stated in prose)."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ReasoningResult à each logic:PreservationKind polarity qui co-holds pour it — MULTI-valued, parce que the preservation field est a SET de polarities, not a single choice (logic:ValidationOnly est excluded; it nomme a lowering's purpose, not an answer-preservation polarity)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/resultProof|rdfs:label"
msgid "result proof"
msgstr "résultat preuve"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/resultProof|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningResult to the derivation that proves its conclusion (a content-addressed handle into the explanation/proof tree), present iff the conclusion is derivable. Domain logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:resultProof only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ReasoningResult à the dérivation qui proves its conclusion (a content-addressed handle dans the explanation/preuve tree), present iff the conclusion est derivable."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/resultRowSchema|rdfs:label"
msgid "result row schema"
msgstr "résultat row schéma"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/resultRowSchema|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningResult to the logic:ResultShape its bindings are contracted to — the row-schema facet of the typed result. Single-valued; absent for surfaces with no row schema (e.g. a pure DL-consistency verdict). The schema is the caller's DECLARED contract, validated against the bindings, never synthesised from them. Domain logic:ReasoningResult, range logic:ResultShape (stated in prose)."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ReasoningResult à the logic:ResultShape its bindings sont contracted à — the row-schéma facet de the typed résultat."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/retiredByTransaction|rdfs:label"
msgid "retired by transaction"
msgstr "retired by transaction"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/retiredByTransaction|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a retired support/reified assertion to the elementary update or transaction-path step that retired it. It is transition provenance: it explains why the support no longer holds in the successor state without deleting the support from the historical path. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:retiredByTransaction only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a retired support/reified assertion à the elementary update ou transaction-chemin step qui retired it."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/reveals|rdfs:label"
msgid "reveals"
msgstr "reveals"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/reveals|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates the observation value an action schema names through logic:observation to the situation that executing the action reveals. The native evaluator surfaces the revealed situation in the materialized output so a policy can branch on it. Domain the logic:observation value, range the revealed logic:Situation (stated in prose). The reading half of the observation facet's seam to the cognitive layer (design/LOGIC-COGNITION.md). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:reveals only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates the observation valeur an action schéma nomme par logic:observation à the situation qui executing the action reveals."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/reviewedBy|rdfs:label"
msgid "reviewed by"
msgstr "reviewed by"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/reviewedBy|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:FormalizationCandidate to the reviewer decision that promoted it — a provenance/agent individual recording who reviewed it and when (range stated in prose, a reviewer provenance node, so the keystone gate is machine-auditable rather than trusting a free literal). Its presence is what a logic:CandidateAccepted candidate is checked against. Single-valued. Domain logic:FormalizationCandidate."
msgstr "Relates a logic:FormalizationCandidate à the reviewer decision qui promoted it — a provenance/agent individu recording who reviewed it et lorsque (plage stated dans prose, a reviewer provenance nœud, so the keystone gate est machine-auditable plutôt que trusting a free literal)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/reviewerLogicFoundation|rdfs:label"
msgid "logic foundation maintainer"
msgstr "logic foundation maintainer"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/reviewerLogicFoundation|skos:definition"
msgid "The reviewer-decision provenance node the logic foundation records against an accepted logic:FormalizationCandidate: an auditable IRI (never a free literal) standing for the maintainer authority that adjudicated the prose-to-axiom promotion, so the reviewer gate is machine-checkable."
msgstr "Le reviewer-decision provenance nœud the logic foundation enregistre contre an accepté logic:FormalizationCandidate: an auditable IRI (never a free literal) standing pour the maintainer authority qui adjudicated the prose-to-axiom promotion, so the reviewer gate est machine-checkable."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/revision|rdfs:label"
msgid "revision"
msgstr "revision"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/revision|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to the logic:RevisionPolicy it selects — how change is absorbed. Single-valued on the contract. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:RevisionPolicy (stated in prose, matching the module's convention). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:revision only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract à the logic:RevisionPolicy it selects — how change est absorbed."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/rightOperand|rdfs:label"
msgid "right operand"
msgstr "right operand"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/rightOperand|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a binary transaction-program combinator (for example a logic:SerialConjunction) to its right/suffix operand — the program that holds over the suffix of the executing path. Range a transaction-program node (stated in prose). Paired with logic:leftOperand. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:rightOperand only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a binary transaction-program combinator (for example a logic:SerialConjunction) à its right/suffix operand — the program qui holds sur the suffix de the executing chemin."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/rigidityViolation|rdfs:label"
msgid "rigidity violation"
msgstr "rigidity violation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/rigidityViolation|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates an individual to a rigid type it fails to persist as across worlds: the derived diagnostic of the positive cross-world rigidity discipline (the fourth OntoUML discipline, the one the type-only lint cannot express). For an individual x and a rigid type T, if x instantiates T in some world but still exists in another world where it is NOT typed T, a logic:rigidityViolation fact is entailed in that other world. Unlike logic:violation it is not produced by an in-world Datalog rule — rigidity quantifies over pairs of worlds and the chase is world-local, so it is evaluated by bounded closure over the finite materialized world set (LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md §Operational semantics). It is never asserted by hand; its presence is a machine-checkable proof that a rigid type's instantiation did not carry over to a world where the individual persists."
msgstr "Relates an individu à a rigid type it fails à persist as across worlds: the dérivé diagnostic de the positif cross-monde rigidity discipline (the fourth OntoUML discipline, the one the type-only lint ne peut pas express)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/rigidlyAppliesTo|rdfs:label"
msgid "rigidly applies to"
msgstr "rigidly applies to"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/rigidlyAppliesTo|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a rigid type to the individuals it necessarily classifies: for every individual and every pair of worlds in which the individual exists, if it instantiates the type in one world it instantiates it in the other. The modal rigidity constraint; a Kind rigidly applies to its instances, an anti-rigid Role or Phase does not (the same constraint negated). Lowered to a universally quantified, world-indexed rule evaluated by closure over the finite materialized world set, needing no native modal operator."
msgstr "Relates a rigid type à the individuals it necessarily classifies: pour chaque individu et chaque pair de worlds dans qui the individu exists, si it instantiates the type dans one monde it instantiates it dans the other."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/roleA|rdfs:label"
msgid "role A"
msgstr "role A"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/roleA|skos:definition"
msgid "The first role predicate of a logic:CrossNodeConstraint (paired with logic:roleB under logic:crossMode). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:roleA only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le first role prédicat de a logic:CrossNodeConstraint (paired avec logic:roleB sous logic:crossMode)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/roleB|rdfs:label"
msgid "role B"
msgstr "role B"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/roleB|skos:definition"
msgid "The second role predicate of a logic:CrossNodeConstraint (paired with logic:roleA under logic:crossMode). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:roleB only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le second role prédicat de a logic:CrossNodeConstraint (paired avec logic:roleUn sous logic:crossMode)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleClusterRoot|rdfs:label"
msgid "carry the shared root on the root-keyed cluster node"
msgstr "carry the shared root on the root-keyed cluster nœud"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleClusterRoot|skos:definition"
msgid "Emits gmeow:clusterRoot(root, root) whenever some finding gmeow:findingRootCause a root: the root-keyed cluster node carries its shared root once. Positive Horn (logic:PositiveHornProfile); monotone; materialized natively. The self-edge follows from identifying the cluster with its root finding — the cluster node (the root) names R exactly once, matching every member's gmeow:findingRootCause."
msgstr "Emits gmeow:clusterRoot(root, root) whenever some finding gmeow:findingRootCause a root: the root-keyed cluster nœud porte its shared root once."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleCrossNodeGlut|rdfs:label"
msgid "derive a cross-node glut edge from opposing polarities at one anchor"
msgstr "derive a cross-nœud glut edge from opposing polarities at one anchor"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleCrossNodeGlut|skos:definition"
msgid "Emits gmeow:crossNodeGlutWith(f1, f2) whenever two DISTINCT findings share one gmeow:findingAnchor that is a gmeow:NonTrivialAnchor, f1's gmeow:findingCategory has gmeow:categoryPolarity logic:InfoSupported, and f2's has logic:InfoOpposed: an opposing-polarity Belnap clash at one real source position, the cross-code coherence conflict the same-fingerprint merge (which keys on the code) cannot see. Positive Horn (logic:PositiveHornProfile) with a logic:distinctBody inequality guard (f1 ≠ f2) and the gmeow:NonTrivialAnchor guard that keeps it off the shared empty anchor of locationless findings; monotone; materialized natively (logic:ExactPreservation). Because the reified-Horn chase cannot mint a fresh witness node, the glut is carried as this directed edge (Supported → Opposed) rather than a minted gmeow:CrossNodeGlutWitness."
msgstr "Emits gmeow:crossNodeGlutWith(f1, f2) whenever two DISTINCT findings share one gmeow:findingAnchor qui est a gmeow:NonTrivialAnchor, f1's gmeow:findingCategory possède gmeow:categoryPolarity logic:InfoSupported, et f2's possède logic:InfoOpposed: an opposing-polarity Belnap clash at one real source position, the cross-code cohérence conflit the same-fingerprint merge (which keys sur the code) ne peut pas see."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFindingCluster|rdfs:label"
msgid "link a finding to the cluster keyed by its root cause"
msgstr "link a finding to the cluster keyed by its root cause"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFindingCluster|skos:definition"
msgid "Emits gmeow:findingCluster(finding, root) whenever a finding gmeow:findingRootCause a root: the finding's membership in the cluster keyed by that shared root. Positive Horn (logic:PositiveHornProfile) over the root-cause output (stratified above it); monotone; materialized natively. The cluster node is the root finding itself (fresh-node minting is not expressible in the reified-Horn chase), so gmeow:findingCluster points at the shared root, which logic:ruleFindingClusterType types gmeow:FindingCluster and logic:ruleClusterRoot links to itself."
msgstr "Emits gmeow:findingCluster(finding, root) whenever a finding gmeow:findingRootCause a root: the finding's membership dans the cluster keyed par qui shared root."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFindingClusterType|rdfs:label"
msgid "type the root-keyed cluster node as a finding cluster"
msgstr "type the root-keyed cluster nœud as a finding cluster"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFindingClusterType|skos:definition"
msgid "Emits rdf:type(root, gmeow:FindingCluster) whenever some finding gmeow:findingRootCause a root: the root-keyed grouping node is a gmeow:FindingCluster. Positive Horn (logic:PositiveHornProfile); monotone; materialized natively. Types the shared root as the cluster it heads, so the readable 'N findings share root R' surface is a first-class typed node."
msgstr "Emits rdf:type(root, gmeow:FindingCluster) whenever some finding gmeow:findingRootCause a root: the root-keyed grouping nœud est a gmeow:FindingCluster."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFindingHasAntecedent|rdfs:label"
msgid "mark a finding that has at least one antecedent"
msgstr "mark a finding that has at least one antecedent"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFindingHasAntecedent|skos:definition"
msgid "Emits the self-edge gmeow:findingHasAntecedent(finding, finding) whenever a finding gmeow:findingAntecedent anything: the positive one-place marker of a non-root finding, carried on a DEDICATED relation (not rdf:type). Positive Horn (logic:PositiveHornProfile); monotone; materialized natively. It exists so the stratified root-cause rule can express 'has no antecedent of its own' as a single negation-as-failure over gmeow:findingHasAntecedent — the marker settles in a lower stratum than the NAF that reads it. Its own relation (rather than rdf:type) is load-bearing: negating rdf:type would form a negative cycle with the downstream rules that derive rdf:type from gmeow:findingRootCause, breaking stratification."
msgstr "Emits the self-edge gmeow:findingHasAntecedent(finding, finding) whenever a finding gmeow:findingAntecedent anything: the positif one-place marker de a non-root finding, carried sur a DEDICATED relation (not rdf:type)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFindingRootCause|rdfs:label"
msgid "derive a finding's root cause as a traced childless antecedent"
msgstr "derive a finding's root cause as a traced childless antecedent"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFindingRootCause|skos:definition"
msgid "Emits gmeow:findingRootCause(finding, root) whenever a finding gmeow:findingTraces a root that is NOT a gmeow:findingHasAntecedent of itself — i.e. the finding reaches the root up the witness DAG and the root has no antecedent of its own. The negation-as-failure over gmeow:findingHasAntecedent makes this logic:StratifiedNAFProfile (the marker is derived in a lower stratum than this rule reads it); materialized natively (logic:ExactPreservation). Honestly the shared ROOT antecedent, not a lowest-common-dominator: it names a childless root the finding derives from, without claiming uniqueness."
msgstr "Emits gmeow:findingRootCause(finding, root) whenever a finding gmeow:findingTraces a root qui est NOT a gmeow:findingHasAntecedent de itself — i.e."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFindingTracesBase|rdfs:label"
msgid "base case: a finding traces to its direct antecedent"
msgstr "base case: a finding traces to its direct antecedent"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFindingTracesBase|skos:definition"
msgid "Emits gmeow:findingTraces(finding, antecedent) whenever a finding gmeow:findingAntecedent an antecedent: the base case of the transitive closure of the witness-DAG derivation edge. Positive Horn (logic:PositiveHornProfile); monotone; materialized natively (logic:ExactPreservation). Paired with logic:ruleFindingTracesStep, which closes it recursively up the chain."
msgstr "Emits gmeow:findingTraces(finding, antecedent) whenever a finding gmeow:findingAntecedent an antecedent: the base case de the transitive fermeture de the témoin-DAG dérivation edge."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFindingTracesStep|rdfs:label"
msgid "recursive step: a finding traces to its antecedent's antecedents"
msgstr "recursive step: a finding traces to its antecedent's antecedents"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleFindingTracesStep|skos:definition"
msgid "Emits gmeow:findingTraces(finding, root) whenever a finding gmeow:findingAntecedent an intermediate finding that gmeow:findingTraces the root: the recursive step that closes gmeow:findingTraces transitively up the witness DAG. Positive Horn (logic:PositiveHornProfile); monotone recursion the native chase settles to fixpoint; materialized natively (logic:ExactPreservation). Paired with logic:ruleFindingTracesBase."
msgstr "Emits gmeow:findingTraces(finding, root) whenever a finding gmeow:findingAntecedent an intermediate finding qui gmeow:findingTraces the root: the recursive step qui closes gmeow:findingTraces transitively up the témoin DAG."


msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleGateFatalVerdict|rdfs:label"
msgid "derive the fatal gate verdict on the principal up-set of the truth ordering"
msgstr "derive the fatal gate verdict on the principal up-set of the vérité ordering"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleGateFatalVerdict|skos:definition"
msgid "Emits gmeow:findingGateVerdict(finding, gmeow:gateFatal) whenever a finding's gmeow:findingSeverity is gmeow:severityError, its gmeow:findingCategory's gmeow:categoryBlocking projection is gmeow:blockingBlocking, and its gmeow:findingStandpoint is gmeow:standpointBinding: the principal up-set ↑(Error, Blocking, Binding) of the truth ordering, the meet of three monotone axis-maps. The RDF-side derivation of the single Rust gmeow_errors::grade::gate() policy morphism. Positive Horn; monotone; materialized natively (logic:ExactPreservation). Because Fatal is reachable only from the top of all three axes, an advisory-standpoint or Coherent-category finding is structurally unable to be derived Fatal — the two never-gate theorems fall out of the up-set construction, not a special case."
msgstr "Emits gmeow:findingGateVerdict(finding, gmeow:gateFatal) whenever a finding's gmeow:findingSeverity est gmeow:severityError, its gmeow:findingCategory's gmeow:categoryBlocking projection est gmeow:blockingBlocking, et its gmeow:findingStandpoint est gmeow:standpointBinding: the principal up-set ↑(Error, Blocking, liaison) de the vérité ordering, the meet de three monotone axis-maps."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleIndirectContributor|rdfs:label"
msgid "derive indirect contributor across the provenance generation chain"
msgstr "derive indirect contributor across the provenance generation chain"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleIndirectContributor|skos:definition"
msgid "Emits gmeow:indirectContributor(entity, agent) whenever the entity gmeow:wasGeneratedBy an activity that gmeow:wasAssociatedWith the agent: the productive composition wasGeneratedBy ∘ wasAssociatedWith that surfaces the agents behind an entity's production. Positive Horn; monotone; materialized natively. It never derives gmeow:wasAttributedTo — indirect contribution is a reasoned consequence, not asserted direct responsibility."
msgstr "Emits gmeow:indirectContributor(entity, agent) whenever the entity gmeow:wasGeneratedBy an activity qui gmeow:wasAssociatedWith the agent: the productive composition wasGeneratedBy ∘ wasAssociatedWith qui surfaces the agents behind an entity's production."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleInstantiatesWork|rdfs:label"
msgid "derive the WEMI Item→Work shortcut across the full spine"
msgstr "derive the WEMI Item→Work shortcut across the full spine"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleInstantiatesWork|skos:definition"
msgid "Emits gmeow:instantiatesWork(item, work) whenever an Item gmeow:exemplifies a Manifestation that gmeow:embodies an Expression that gmeow:realizes the Work: the productive composition exemplifies ∘ embodies ∘ realizes that links a concrete copy directly to the abstract Work it carries. Positive Horn; monotone; materialized natively. The conjunction of all three R-relations means a broken spine (a missing tier) derives nothing."
msgstr "Emits gmeow:instantiatesWork(item, work) whenever an Item gmeow:exemplifies a Manifestation qui gmeow:embodies an expression qui gmeow:realizes the Work: the productive composition exemplifies ∘ embodies ∘ realizes qui links a concret copy directly à the abstrait Work it carries."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleOrgMembershipPropagation|rdfs:label"
msgid "propagate membership up the sub-organization hierarchy"
msgstr "propagate membership up the sub-organization hierarchy"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleOrgMembershipPropagation|skos:definition"
msgid "Emits gmeow:memberOf(agent, parent) whenever the agent gmeow:memberOf an organization that is gmeow:subOrganizationOf the parent: membership climbs the organizational part/whole hierarchy, so a department member is a member of the containing organization. Positive Horn and recursive on gmeow:memberOf — one rule carries membership up an arbitrarily deep nest of sub-organizations without needing gmeow:subOrganizationOf transitivity. Monotone; materialized natively. The native-chase form of the propagation the gmeow:memberOf owl:propertyChainAxiom ( gmeow:memberOf gmeow:subOrganizationOf ) expresses for the OWL 2 RL closure — the same inference in the logic: engine, not a divergent reading."
msgstr "Emits gmeow:memberOf(agent, parent) whenever the agent gmeow:memberOf an organization qui est gmeow:subOrganizationOf the parent: membership climbs the organizational part/whole hierarchy, so a department member est a member de the containing organization."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleProjectHasMastered|rdfs:label"
msgid "project ladder edge: has mastered"
msgstr "project ladder edge: has mastered"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleProjectHasMastered|skos:definition"
msgid "Emits gmeow:hasMastered only when BOTH a procedural-competence assessment and a transfer assessment of the same agent on the same subject clear their gmeow:hasMastered rows, where both rows belong to the SAME logic:LadderProjectionProfile. The two-row conjunction is why mastery of one narrow task no longer implies broad command — transfer must clear too — and the shared-profile join is why a procedural threshold from one profile can never be mixed with a transfer threshold from another. Positive Horn; thresholds read from the profile."
msgstr "Emits gmeow:hasMastered uniquement lorsque BOTH a procedural-competence évaluation et a transfer évaluation de the same agent sur the same subject clear their gmeow:hasMastered rows, où both rows belong à the SAME logic:LadderProjectionProfile."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleProjectIsAwareOf|rdfs:label"
msgid "project ladder edge: is aware of"
msgstr "project ladder edge: is aware of"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleProjectIsAwareOf|skos:definition"
msgid "Emits gmeow:isAwareOf from an assessment whose dimension and level clear the gmeow:isAwareOf row of a logic:LadderProjectionProfile. Positive Horn; the threshold is read from the profile, not hard-coded."
msgstr "Emits gmeow:isAwareOf de an évaluation dont dimension et niveau clear the gmeow:isAwareOf row de a logic:LadderProjectionProfile."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleProjectKnowsAbout|rdfs:label"
msgid "project ladder edge: knows about"
msgstr "project ladder edge: knows about"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleProjectKnowsAbout|skos:definition"
msgid "Emits gmeow:knowsAbout from an assessment whose dimension and level clear the gmeow:knowsAbout row of a logic:LadderProjectionProfile. Positive Horn; the threshold is read from the profile. The canonical source of a gmeow:knowsAbout edge — never gmeow:hasSkill."
msgstr "Emits gmeow:knowsAbout de an évaluation dont dimension et niveau clear the gmeow:knowsAbout row de a logic:LadderProjectionProfile."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleProjectUnderstands|rdfs:label"
msgid "project ladder edge: understands"
msgstr "project ladder edge: understands"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleProjectUnderstands|skos:definition"
msgid "Emits gmeow:understands from an assessment whose dimension and level clear the gmeow:understands row of a logic:LadderProjectionProfile. Positive Horn; the threshold is read from the profile."
msgstr "Emits gmeow:understands de an évaluation dont dimension et niveau clear the gmeow:understands row de a logic:LadderProjectionProfile."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleRootFinding|rdfs:label"
msgid "mark a finding that is some finding's root cause"
msgstr "mark a finding that is some finding's root cause"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleRootFinding|skos:definition"
msgid "Emits rdf:type(root, gmeow:RootFinding) whenever some finding gmeow:findingRootCause a root: the childless root antecedent surfaced as a one-place marker. Positive Horn (logic:PositiveHornProfile) over the root-cause output (stratified above it); monotone; materialized natively (logic:ExactPreservation). Authored as the third member of the diagnostic meta-fold to demonstrate that a new meta-finding is added by tagging a rule gmeow:DiagnosticMetaRule — the reasoner discovers and runs it by TYPE, with no engine change."
msgstr "Emits rdf:type(root, gmeow:RootFinding) whenever some finding gmeow:findingRootCause a root: the childless root antecedent surfaced as a one-place marker."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleTenureClaimObservedFeature|rdfs:label"
msgid "surface a tenure's position as its claim's observed feature"
msgstr "surface a tenure's position as its claim's observed feature"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleTenureClaimObservedFeature|skos:definition"
msgid "Emits gmeow:observedFeature(claim, position) whenever a gmeow:StandpointTenure gmeow:standpointClaim a claim and gmeow:tenurePosition a position: the tenure's held position becomes the observedFeature of its generated gmeow:StandpointClaim observation, so 'what is claimed' reads uniformly on the observation spine. Positive Horn; monotone; materialized natively."
msgstr "Emits gmeow:observedFeature(claim, position) whenever a gmeow:StandpointTenure gmeow:standpointClaim a claim et gmeow:tenurePosition a position: the tenure's held position becomes the observedFeature de its generated gmeow:StandpointClaim observation, so 'what est claimed' reads uniformly sur the observation spine."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleTenureClaimVantage|rdfs:label"
msgid "surface a tenure's standpoint as its claim's vantage"
msgstr "surface a tenure's point de vue as its claim's vantage"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/ruleTenureClaimVantage|skos:definition"
msgid "Emits gmeow:vantage(claim, standpoint) whenever a gmeow:StandpointTenure gmeow:standpointClaim a claim and gmeow:tenureStandpoint a standpoint: the tenure's frame becomes the vantage of its generated gmeow:StandpointClaim observation, so 'whose frame' reads uniformly across tenures and bare observations. Positive Horn; monotone; materialized natively."
msgstr "Emits gmeow:vantage(claim, point de vue) whenever a gmeow:StandpointTenure gmeow:standpointClaim a claim et gmeow:tenureStandpoint a point de vue: the tenure's frame becomes the vantage de its generated gmeow:StandpointClaim observation, so 'whose frame' reads uniformly across tenures et bare observations."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/satisfactionDegree|rdfs:label"
msgid "satisfaction degree"
msgstr "satisfaction degree"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/satisfactionDegree|skos:definition"
msgid "The quantity carried on a logic:GoalEvaluation for a goal met to a degree rather than crisply — how much of the goal is achieved. Domain logic:GoalEvaluation (stated in prose). The range is intentionally left open (no rdfs:range), matching the other quantitative axes (logic:confidence, logic:probability, logic:weight, logic:evidenceStrength): the value is a unit-interval decimal. DISTINCT from those uncertainty measures and from logic:objectiveValue and logic:utility — how much of the goal is met is never how sure the evaluator is, never the measure an optimization goal extremizes, and never how desirable the outcome is; none substitutes for another."
msgstr "Le quantity carried sur a logic:GoalEvaluation pour a objectif met à a degree plutôt que crisply — how much de the objectif est achieved."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/satisfactionStatus|rdfs:label"
msgid "satisfaction status"
msgstr "satisfaction status"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/satisfactionStatus|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:GoalEvaluation to the logic:SatisfactionStatus it carries — the satisfaction axis of the factored outcome. Domain logic:GoalEvaluation, range logic:SatisfactionStatus (stated in prose). Varies independently of feasibility, lifecycle, and goal-evaluation status. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:satisfactionStatus only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:GoalEvaluation à the logic:SatisfactionStatus it porte — the satisfaction axis de the factored résultat."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/satisfiesCriterion|rdfs:label"
msgid "satisfies criterion"
msgstr "satisfies criterion"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/satisfiesCriterion|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ConcurrentHistory to each logic:SerializabilityCriterion its witnessed schedule actually SATISFIES — the classification RESULT, as opposed to logic:serializabilityCriterion, which names the criterion the history is judged against. The native evaluator emits logic:ConflictSerializability when the logic:precedes conflict graph is acyclic and logic:ViewSerializability when the witnessed interleaving is view-equivalent to one of the two serial orders of its legs. Domain logic:ConcurrentHistory, range logic:SerializabilityCriterion (stated in prose); multi-valued. Because conflict-serializability is strictly stronger, a history that satisfies logic:ConflictSerializability always also satisfies logic:ViewSerializability; a conflict-CYCLIC history may satisfy logic:ViewSerializability alone. Absence of a criterion here is the honest record that the schedule does not satisfy it — the corresponding logic:SerializationAnomaly finding carries the violated criterion — never a silent linearization."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ConcurrentHistory à each logic:SerializabilityCriterion its witnessed schedule actually SATISFIES — the classification résultat, par opposition à logic:serializabilityCriterion, qui nomme the criterion the historique est judged against."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/selectedBranch|rdfs:label"
msgid "selected branch"
msgstr "selected branch"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/selectedBranch|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a policy to the branch the native evaluator selected because its logic:branchGuard matched the situation an earlier action's observation revealed (logic:reveals). Domain a policy, range the selected branch (stated in prose). The materialized record of an observation-conditioned policy decision. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:selectedBranch only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a politique à the branch the native evaluator selected parce que its logic:branchGuard matched the situation an earlier action's observation revealed (logic:reveals)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/selectedByEntrenchment|rdfs:label"
msgid "selected by entrenchment"
msgstr "selected by entrenchment"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/selectedByEntrenchment|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:CounterfactualAcceptanceWitness to the outcome (an IRI) the entrenchment ranking deterministically selected when resolving the counterfactual antecedent. Domain logic:CounterfactualAcceptanceWitness (stated in prose). Its absence marks an unentrenched, arbitrary counterfactual: an outcome chosen without a recorded ordering is a silent guess. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:selectedByEntrenchment only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:CounterfactualAcceptanceWitness à the résultat (an IRI) the entrenchment ranking deterministically selected lorsque resolving the contrefactuel antecedent."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/selfAssertiveBasis|rdfs:label"
msgid "self-assertive basis"
msgstr "self-assertive basis"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/selfAssertiveBasis|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:HolonicAgencyProfile to a property-value that evidences the self-assertive (autonomy) tendency: the profile holds that a holon bearing this value (logic:bearsProperty) asserts itself as a whole — Koestler's self-assertive face. The carrier that makes autonomy profile-relative, the co-equal twin of logic:integrativeBasis (neither privileged, Principle 9). Without a borne self-assertive value a holon's autonomy face is not evidenced, contributing — together with the integrative face — to the logic:AgencyVerdict (logic:AutonomyDeficient or logic:HolonIntegral). The autonomy analogue of logic:reductionBasis and logic:activationBasis (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Relates a logic:HolonicAgencyProfile à a propriété-valeur qui evidences the self-assertive (autonomie) tendency: the profil holds qui a holon bearing this valeur (logic:bearsProperty) asserts itself as a whole — Koestler's self-assertive face."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/serializabilityCriterion|rdfs:label"
msgid "serializability criterion"
msgstr "serializability criterion"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/serializabilityCriterion|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ConcurrentHistory to the logic:SerializabilityCriterion its schedule is classified against — logic:ConflictSerializability (the default when none is stated) or logic:ViewSerializability. Domain logic:ConcurrentHistory, range logic:SerializabilityCriterion (stated in prose). This is the history-property dimension only: it is kept SEPARATE from logic:IsolationLevel (a declared guarantee strength) and logic:ConcurrencyControlProtocol (an implementation mechanism), the two other concurrency concerns the layer never conflates. The criterion a detected anomaly violates is recorded on the finding through logic:violatedCriterion."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ConcurrentHistory à the logic:SerializabilityCriterion its schedule est classified contre — logic:ConflictSerializability (the default lorsque none est stated) ou logic:ViewSerializability."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/severity|rdfs:label"
msgid "severity"
msgstr "severity"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/severity|skos:definition"
msgid "The severity a logic:Constraint violation reports at, as one of the SHACL local names 'Violation', 'Warning', or 'Info'. Absent means the SHACL default 'Violation'. Carried on the canonical constraint so the projected sh:SPARQLConstraint reproduces the authored sh:severity rather than re-deriving one."
msgstr "Le severity a logic:contrainte violation reports at, as one de the SHACL local nomme 'Violation', 'Warning', ou 'Info'."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/shapeCardinality|rdfs:label"
msgid "shape cardinality"
msgstr "forme cardinality"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/shapeCardinality|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ResultShape to the logic:RowCardinality it declares — the row-set contract. Single-valued. Domain logic:ResultShape, range logic:RowCardinality (stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:shapeCardinality only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ResultShape à the logic:RowCardinality it déclare — the row-set contract."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/shapeRowCount|rdfs:label"
msgid "shape row count"
msgstr "forme row count"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/shapeRowCount|skos:definition"
msgid "The pinned result row count for a logic:ResultShape in logic:RowsCount mode. Single-valued, xsd:nonNegativeInteger. Domain logic:ResultShape (stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:shapeRowCount only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le pinned résultat row count pour a logic:ResultShape dans logic:RowsCount mode."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/sharpensTransitivity|rdfs:label"
msgid "sharpens is transitive"
msgstr "sharpens is transitive"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/sharpensTransitivity|skos:definition"
msgid "Asserts on the canonical carrier that gmeow:sharpens is transitive: the standpoint refinement order its skos:definition names (Standpoint Logic's coverage relation). The native coherence gate reads this to close the refinement order."
msgstr "Asserts sur the canonique carrier qui gmeow:sharpens est transitive: the point de vue refinement order its skos:définition nomme (point de vue Logic's coverage relation)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/situationObtains|rdfs:label"
msgid "situation obtains"
msgstr "situation obtains"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/situationObtains|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a gmeow:State (a configuration along a logic:Path) to a logic:Situation type that obtains at it — the engine reads this to decide whether an atomic goal's logic:boundSituationType, or a conditional goal's logic:guardSituation, holds at a given state. Domain gmeow:State, range logic:Situation (stated in prose). It records that a situation type is realized at a state without mutating that state, mirroring the prose 'each gmeow:State realizes a logic:Situation' on logic:Path. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:situationObtains only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a gmeow:état (a configuration along a logic:chemin) à a logic:situation type qui obtains at it — the engine reads this à decide whether an atomique objectif's logic:boundSituationType, ou a conditionnel objectif's logic:guardSituation, holds at a given état."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/skillEvidenceForKnowsAbout|rdfs:label"
msgid "skill is defeasible evidence for knowing about"
msgstr "skill is defeasible preuve for knowing about"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/skillEvidenceForKnowsAbout|skos:definition"
msgid "The shipped declaration recasting expertise's former gmeow:hasSkill ⊑ gmeow:knowsAbout: possessing a skill in a subject is DEFEASIBLE evidence that the agent knows about it, not a strict subproperty entailment — tacit competence and descriptive, fact-level knowing-about come apart. The supported gmeow:knowsAbout edge is never materialized from gmeow:hasSkill under the default reasoning (its only shipped source is the declarative-familiarity ladder projection); a consumer opting into defeasible reasoning draws it, defeated when the competence is purely tacit."
msgstr "Le shipped declaration recasting expertise's former gmeow:hasSkill ⊑ gmeow:knowsAbout: possessing a skill dans a subject est DEFEASIBLE preuve qui the agent knows about it, not a strict subproperty implication — tacit competence et descriptive, fact-niveau knowing-about come apart."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/sourceDimension|rdfs:label"
msgid "source dimension"
msgstr "source dimension"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/sourceDimension|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:AssessmentDimension a logic:DimensionThreshold row reads: the factored axis whose assessment level is tested against the row's logic:thresholdLevel. Range logic:AssessmentDimension (stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:sourceDimension only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le logic:AssessmentDimension a logic:DimensionThreshold row reads: the factored axis dont évaluation niveau est tested contre the row's logic:thresholdLevel."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/subEventOfTransitivity|rdfs:label"
msgid "subEventOf is transitive"
msgstr "subEventOf is transitive"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/subEventOfTransitivity|skos:definition"
msgid "Asserts on the canonical carrier that gmeow:subEventOf is transitive: a part of a part is a part — the reading its own skos:definition commits to (CIDOC-CRM P9). The native coherence gate reads this to close the sub-event relation."
msgstr "Asserts sur the canonique carrier qui gmeow:subEventOf est transitive: a part de a part est a part — the reading its own skos:définition commits à (CIDOC-CRM P9)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/subjectGranularity|rdfs:label"
msgid "subject granularity"
msgstr "subject granularity"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/subjectGranularity|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:CognitiveAssessment to the logic:SubjectGranularity individual recording the grain of its logic:assessmentSubject (inference, body-of-reasoning, domain, or agent). Range logic:SubjectGranularity (stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:subjectGranularity only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:CognitiveAssessment à the logic:SubjectGranularity individu recording the grain de its logic:assessmentSubject (inference, body-of-raisonnement, domaine, ou agent)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/sufficientFor|rdfs:label"
msgid "sufficient for"
msgstr "sufficient for"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/sufficientFor|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a sub-gmeow:Goal whose satisfaction settles a gmeow:Goal on its own. Domain gmeow:Goal, range gmeow:Goal (stated in prose). The relation an logic:OrDecomposition groups: any one sufficient sub-goal settles the parent. One of the four decomposition relations carrying satisfaction dependency, distinct from gmeow:properPartOf (structural part-hood)."
msgstr "Relates a sub-gmeow:objectif dont satisfaction settles a gmeow:objectif sur its own."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/summarizesResult|rdfs:label"
msgid "summarizes result"
msgstr "summarizes résultat"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/summarizesResult|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a coherence outcome (logic:CoherenceCertificate or logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation) to the single logic:ReasoningResult whose completion status, contract (logic:contractHash), certified fragment (logic:certifiedFragment), consumed budget (logic:consumedBudget), assumptions (logic:resultAssumption) and preservation losses it certifies over. The completeness gate (certificate vs attestation) reads this result's logic:resultEvaluation and logic:resultCompleteness. Single-valued. Domain logic:CoherenceCertificate or logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation, range logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:summarizesResult only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a cohérence résultat (logic:CoherenceCertificate ou logic:CoherenceCheckAttestation) à the single logic:ReasoningResult dont completion status, contract (logic:contractHash), certified fragment (logic:certifiedFragment), consumed budget (logic:consumedBudget), assumptions (logic:resultAssumption) et preservation losses it certifies over."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/supersededBy|rdfs:label"
msgid "superseded by"
msgstr "superseded by"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/supersededBy|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a retired support/reified assertion version to the update or successor support that supersedes it in the append-only store. It is the missing counterpart that, together with logic:activeInState, logic:validUntilState, and logic:retiredByTransaction, makes every `del` a supersession rather than an erasure: the retired version is never removed, it is recorded as superseded by the version that took its place. The substrate therefore stays monotonic and append-only — a superseded assertion remains recoverable, and the supersession chain reconstructs the full history of what replaced what. Suppression-not-erasure: `del` removes a support, it does not destroy the historical record. Domain a retired support/reified assertion version, range the superseding update or successor support (stated in prose)."
msgstr "Relates a retired support/reified assertion version à the update ou successor support qui supersedes it dans the append-only store."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/supersededTerm|rdfs:label"
msgid "superseded term"
msgstr "superseded terme"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/supersededTerm|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a supersession logic:Correspondence to the old term it records as superseded — the source endpoint of a greenfield migration crossing (e.g. a removed class or property the correspondence maps onto its replacement at a rung). Names the endpoint so the supersession ledger is queryable by the migrated-from term. Domain logic:Correspondence, range any term (stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:supersededTerm only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a supersession logic:correspondance à the old terme it enregistre as superseded — the source endpoint de a greenfield migration crossing (e.g."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/supersedingTerm|rdfs:label"
msgid "superseding term"
msgstr "superseding terme"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/supersedingTerm|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a supersession logic:Correspondence to the replacement term it records as superseding the old one — the target endpoint of a greenfield migration crossing. Paired with logic:supersededTerm, it makes the correspondence's rung (logic:morphismClass) queryable per migrated term. Domain logic:Correspondence, range any term (stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:supersedingTerm only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a supersession logic:correspondance à the replacement terme it enregistre as superseding the old one — the target endpoint de a greenfield migration crossing."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/suppliesIdentity|rdfs:label"
msgid "supplies identity"
msgstr "supplies identité"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/suppliesIdentity|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates an ultimate sortal to an individual whose principle of identity it supplies: the second-order identity-supply relation, reified as a first-order relation over punned type individuals (HiLog/F-logic style) so that 'every object instantiates exactly one ultimate sortal' becomes a first-order counting constraint. Kinds supply identity; SubKinds, Roles, and Phases inherit it; non-sortals (Category, Mixin, RoleMixin, PhaseMixin) supply none. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:suppliesIdentity only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates an ultimate sortal à an individu dont principle de identité it supplies: the second-order identité-supply relation, reified as a premier ordre relation sur punned type individuals (HiLog/F-logic style) so qui 'every object instantiates exactement un ultimate sortal' becomes a premier ordre counting contrainte."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/supportSelfSupportExclusion|rdfs:label"
msgid "a support's source and target are distinct"
msgstr "a support's source and target are distinct"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/supportSelfSupportExclusion|skos:definition"
msgid "Asserts that a gmeow:Support's gmeow:supportSource and gmeow:supportTarget must be distinct: support is irreflexive — a structure does not support itself. The native coherence gate raises a violation when they coincide; the generated SHACL constraint surface is its projection."
msgstr "Asserts qui a gmeow:Support's gmeow:supportSource et gmeow:supportTarget doit be distinct: support est irreflexive — a structure ne fait pas support itself."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/survivesCounterexample|rdfs:label"
msgid "survives counterexample"
msgstr "survives counterexample"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/survivesCounterexample|skos:definition"
msgid "The Lakatos survival edge: relates a refined successor conjecture to the logic:ContradictionWitness that refuted its predecessor and which the successor now EXCLUDES — the evidence that the refinement did real work, not just relabelled the claim. Paired with logic:conjectureRefinedFrom, it lets the corpus show a refinement chain where each successor demonstrably survives a witness that killed its parent. Domain logic:Conjecture, range logic:ContradictionWitness."
msgstr "Le Lakatos survival edge: relie a refined successor conjecture à the logic:ContradictionWitness qui refuted its predecessor et qui the successor now EXCLUDES — the preuve qui the refinement did real work, not just relabelled the claim."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/symmetricProperty|rdfs:label"
msgid "symmetric property"
msgstr "symmetric propriété"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/symmetricProperty|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic: property-characteristic marker for symmetry: a property P such that P(a,b) entails P(b,a). The logic: analogue of owl:SymmetricProperty, minted standalone so the characteristic can be asserted on the canonical reasoning carrier alongside the others and reasoned over natively — including together with logic:irreflexiveProperty, for a constitutive-opposition relation that holds both ways but never of a thing and itself."
msgstr "Le logic: propriété-characteristic marker pour symmetry: a propriété P such qui P(a,b) entails P(b,a)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/szsStrengthens|rdfs:label"
msgid "SZS strengthens"
msgstr "SZS strengthens"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/szsStrengthens|skos:definition"
msgid "The strength order over logic:SzsStatus: relates a status to a weaker status it entails (logic:SzsContradictoryAxioms szsStrengthens logic:SzsUnsatisfiable — contradictory axioms entail, and are strictly stronger than, bare unsatisfiability). Domain and range logic:SzsStatus (stated in prose); transitive. The intra-branch partial order that makes the SZS vocabulary an ordered structure rather than a flat token set, mirroring gmeow:coarserThan over granularity levels; the ordering the monotone logic:ConformanceVerdict projection respects."
msgstr "Le strength order sur logic:SzsStatus: relie a status à a weaker status it entails (logic:SzsContradictoryAxioms szsStrengthens logic:SzsUnsatisfiable — contradictory axioms entail, et sont strictly stronger than, bare unsatisfiability)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/temporalPartOf|rdfs:label"
msgid "temporal part of"
msgstr "temporal part of"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/temporalPartOf|skos:definition"
msgid "Parthood among perdurants: relates a temporal part of an occurrent to the larger occurrent it is a phase of — the first act is a temporal part of the play. The four-dimensional parthood relation, distinct from the endurant parthood of logic:partOf / logic:properPartOf: it carves a perdurant along its temporal extent into sub-occurrents."
msgstr "Parthood parmi perdurants: relie a temporal part de an occurrent à the larger occurrent it est a phase de — the first act est a temporal part de the play."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/temporallyIncompatible|rdfs:label"
msgid "temporally incompatible"
msgstr "temporally incompatible"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/temporallyIncompatible|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates two gmeow:Goals each achievable on its own but not within the windows both require. Domain gmeow:Goal, range gmeow:Goal (stated in prose). One of seven conflict relations between independently-meaningful goals, weaker than gmeow:counterGoal (constitutive opposition); the conflict is in the scheduling, not in the goals' content."
msgstr "Relates two gmeow:Goals each achievable sur its own mais not within the windows both require."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/temporallySucceeds|rdfs:label"
msgid "temporally succeeds"
msgstr "temporally succeeds"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/temporallySucceeds|skos:definition"
msgid "The typed temporal accessibility relation along a logic:Path: one gmeow:State succeeds another in the ordered run of states. A strict order (irreflexive and transitive) — its character is documented in prose, not asserted as OWL characteristics, matching the kernel convention. logic:accessibleFrom is its generic superproperty in prose only — NOT asserted rdfs:subPropertyOf — so the bare superproperty licenses no cross-type entailment across context types."
msgstr "Le typed temporal accessibility relation along a logic:chemin: one gmeow:état succeeds another dans the ordered run de states."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/termDistinct|rdfs:label"
msgid "term distinct"
msgstr "terme distinct"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/termDistinct|skos:definition"
msgid "A comparison relation the procedural-constraint SPARQL fragment lowers to a FILTER ( ?a != ?b ) over two already-bound terms (rather than a triple pattern). The inequality peer of logic:termEqual; it binds nothing, only tests inequality."
msgstr "Un comparison relation the procedural-contrainte SPARQL fragment lowers à a FILTER ( ?a != ?b ) sur two already-bound terms (plutôt que a triple pattern)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/termEqual|rdfs:label"
msgid "term equal"
msgstr "terme equal"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/termEqual|skos:definition"
msgid "A comparison relation the procedural-constraint SPARQL fragment lowers to a FILTER ( ?a = ?b ) over two already-bound terms (rather than a triple pattern). Used by the cross-node inequality expansion; it binds nothing, only tests equality."
msgstr "Un comparison relation the procedural-contrainte SPARQL fragment lowers à a FILTER ( ?a = ?b ) sur two already-bound terms (plutôt que a triple pattern)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/termIndex|rdfs:label"
msgid "term index"
msgstr "terme index"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/termIndex|skos:definition"
msgid "The zero-based ordinal of a term-carrier within its ordered list — an argument within an atomic predication, or a bound variable within a quantifier block. Fixing position explicitly makes the variadic, order-significant lists round-trip independent of RDF statement order. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:termIndex only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le zero-based ordinal de a terme-carrier within its ordered list — an argument within an atomique predication, ou a bound variable within a quantifier block."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/termIri|rdfs:label"
msgid "term IRI"
msgstr "terme IRI"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/termIri|skos:definition"
msgid "Carries an IRI-constant term value on an argument term-carrier: the argument is an individual (or a reified relation or type) named by this IRI. One of the four mutually exclusive term-value properties; exactly one is present on each carrier. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:termIri only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Carries an IRI-constant terme valeur sur an argument terme-carrier: the argument est an individu (or a reified relation ou type) named par this IRI."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/termLiteral|rdfs:label"
msgid "term literal"
msgstr "terme literal"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/termLiteral|skos:definition"
msgid "Carries a data-literal term value (its lexical form) on an argument term-carrier; the term's datatype rides on the companion logic:termLiteralDatatype. One of the four mutually exclusive term-value properties. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:termLiteral only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Carries a données-literal terme valeur (its lexical form) sur an argument terme-carrier; the terme's datatype rides sur the companion logic:termLiteralDatatype."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/termLiteralDatatype|rdfs:label"
msgid "term literal datatype"
msgstr "terme literal datatype"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/termLiteralDatatype|skos:definition"
msgid "Carries the datatype IRI of a literal term value on an argument term-carrier that also bears logic:termLiteral. Absent for a plain literal. Held separately from the literal so the typed-literal term round-trips losslessly regardless of how an intermediate reader handles literal datatypes. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:termLiteralDatatype only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Carries the datatype IRI de a literal terme valeur sur an argument terme-carrier qui also bears logic:termLiteral."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/termSequenceMarker|rdfs:label"
msgid "term sequence marker"
msgstr "terme sequence marker"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/termSequenceMarker|skos:definition"
msgid "Carries a sequence-marker term value (the authored marker name) on an argument term-carrier: the argument is a logic:SequenceMarker binding a sequence of terms rather than a single one. One of the four mutually exclusive term-value properties."
msgstr "Carries a sequence-marker terme valeur (the authored marker name) sur an argument terme-carrier: the argument est a logic:SequenceMarker liaison a sequence de terms plutôt que a single one."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/termVariable|rdfs:label"
msgid "term variable"
msgstr "terme variable"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/termVariable|skos:definition"
msgid "Carries a variable term value (the authored variable name, without a sigil) on a term-carrier: a single-term variable, bound by an enclosing quantifier or free. One of the four mutually exclusive term-value properties. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:termVariable only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Carries a variable terme valeur (the authored variable name, sans a sigil) sur a terme-carrier: a single-terme variable, bound par an enclosing quantifier ou free."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/thresholdLevel|rdfs:label"
msgid "threshold level"
msgstr "threshold niveau"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/thresholdLevel|skos:definition"
msgid "The minimum logic:AssessmentLevel an assessment on a row's logic:sourceDimension must reach — by the logic:levelAtOrAbove order — for the row's logic:projectsLadderEdge to be emitted. Range logic:AssessmentLevel (stated in prose). It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:thresholdLevel only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le minimum logic:AssessmentLevel an évaluation sur a row's logic:sourceDimension doit reach — par the logic:levelAtOrAbove order — pour the row's logic:projectsLadderEdge à be emitted."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/transactionStart|rdfs:label"
msgid "transaction start"
msgstr "transaction start"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/transactionStart|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:TransactionOutcome to the gmeow:State the program executed from — the start state of the executional-entailment run. Domain logic:TransactionOutcome, range gmeow:State (stated in prose). On failure the start state is left untouched (no successor is materialized); on success it is the first state of the logic:executedAlongPath path. The input side marks the executable program root with logic:transitionFromState; logic:transactionStart records, on the outcome, the start the verdict was computed from. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:transactionStart only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:TransactionOutcome à the gmeow:état the program executed de — the start état de the executional-implication run."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/transactionSucceeds|rdfs:label"
msgid "transaction succeeds"
msgstr "transaction succeeds"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/transactionSucceeds|skos:definition"
msgid "The boolean executional-entailment verdict of a logic:TransactionOutcome: true iff there exists a path from logic:transactionStart along which the program holds, false otherwise. Domain logic:TransactionOutcome, range xsd:boolean (stated in prose). Kept distinct from goal satisfaction (logic:satisfactionStatus over a logic:GoalEvaluation) and from plan success mode (logic:planSuccessMode): it is the bare 'a path exists from the start' reading of the transaction layer, and a false verdict is honest total failure rather than a weak or partial success."
msgstr "Le boolean executional-implication verdict de a logic:TransactionOutcome: true iff there exists a chemin de logic:transactionStart along qui the program holds, false otherwise."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/transactionTimestamp|rdfs:label"
msgid "transaction timestamp"
msgstr "transaction timestamp"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/transactionTimestamp|skos:definition"
msgid "The start-order timestamp assigned to a transaction (a concurrent-composition leg) under a timestamp-ordering protocol — the recorded event a logic:TimestampOrdering verification classifies the witnessed schedule against. Domain a transaction-program node (a logic:ConcurrentComposition leg), range xsd:integer (stated in prose); single-valued. Under logic:TimestampOrdering the schedule is well-formed iff every logic:precedes conflict edge runs from the earlier timestamp to the later one; a run declaring logic:TimestampOrdering that omits a leg's timestamp is a hard error. It is a recorded protocol EVENT — an input the classifier reads — not a derived verdict, and it is distinct from logic:temporallySucceeds, which orders the STATES of an executed path rather than the transactions of a schedule."
msgstr "Le start-order timestamp assigned à a transaction (a concurrent-composition leg) sous a timestamp-ordering protocol — the recorded event a logic:TimestampOrdering verification classifies the witnessed schedule against."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/transitionFromState|rdfs:label"
msgid "transition from state"
msgstr "transition from état"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/transitionFromState|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates an elementary update or transaction-path step to the predecessor state snapshot from which it starts. States are WorldStore named-graph snapshots; this relation records the path edge's source state without mutating that state. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:transitionFromState only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates an elementary update ou transaction-chemin step à the predecessor état snapshot de qui it starts."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/transitionToState|rdfs:label"
msgid "transition to state"
msgstr "transition to état"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/transitionToState|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates an elementary update or transaction-path step to the successor state snapshot it materializes. The successor is a new named graph produced by the transition oracle from the predecessor plus the effective `ins`/`del` updates. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:transitionToState only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates an elementary update ou transaction-chemin step à the successor état snapshot it materializes."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/transitiveProperty|rdfs:label"
msgid "transitive property"
msgstr "transitive propriété"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/transitiveProperty|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic: property-characteristic marker for transitivity: a property P such that P(a,b) ∧ P(b,c) entails P(a,c). The logic: analogue of owl:TransitiveProperty, minted standalone so logic: can combine it with logic:asymmetricProperty — a combination OWL 2 DL forbids globally (criticism 7) but logic: reasons over fully. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:transitiveProperty only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le logic: propriété-characteristic marker pour transitivity: a propriété P such qui P(a,b) ∧ P(b,c) entails P(a,c)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/trigger|rdfs:label"
msgid "trigger"
msgstr "trigger"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/trigger|skos:definition"
msgid "The trigger predicate of a logic:GuardedImplicationConstraint: the antecedent condition (optionally pinned to a logic:triggerValue) that, together with the target class, guards the required companion. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:trigger only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le trigger prédicat de a logic:GuardedImplicationConstraint: the antecedent condition (optionally pinned à a logic:triggerValue) that, together avec the target class, guards the obligatoire companion."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/triggerValue|rdfs:label"
msgid "trigger value"
msgstr "trigger valeur"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/triggerValue|skos:definition"
msgid "An optional fixed object value that pins a logic:GuardedImplicationConstraint's trigger to trigger(this, value) rather than the mere presence of the trigger predicate. An IRI or a literal."
msgstr "Un facultatif fixed object valeur qui pins a logic:GuardedImplicationConstraint's trigger à trigger(this, valeur) plutôt que the mere presence de the trigger prédicat."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/trueQuantity|rdfs:label"
msgid "true quantity"
msgstr "true quantity"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/trueQuantity|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a measurement to its frame-independent magnitude: the quantity that exists independent of any unit or frame — the pressure itself, prior to its expression in mmHg or kPa. The frame-independent leg of the true-quantity/measured-value seam (Principle 11): logic:trueQuantity carries the unit-independent magnitude while logic:measuredValue and logic:referenceFrame carry the frame-relative value, so the same true quantity round-trips across unit systems without re-identifying the magnitude. The domain property gmeow:trueQuantity grounds onto this, pointing at a gmeow:Magnitude. Stated in prose, matching the module's domain/range convention. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:trueQuantity only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a measurement à its frame-independent magnitude: the quantity qui exists independent de tout unit ou frame — the pressure itself, prior à its expression dans mmHg ou kPa."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/truthAlgebra|rdfs:label"
msgid "truth algebra"
msgstr "vérité algebra"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/truthAlgebra|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to the logic:TruthAlgebra it selects — the lattice of truth values over which valuations range. Single-valued on the contract. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:TruthAlgebra (stated in prose, matching the module's convention). One of the three independent truth-facet components, selected separately from logic:admissibleValuation and logic:designatedValues. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:truthAlgebra only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract à the logic:TruthAlgebra it selects — the lattice de vérité values sur qui valuations plage."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/uncertaintyMeasure|rdfs:label"
msgid "uncertainty measure"
msgstr "uncertainty measure"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/uncertaintyMeasure|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract to a logic:UncertaintyMeasure it carries — how graded belief is recorded. Set-valued on the contract: probabilistic, weighted/ranking, and fuzzy measures may coexist on the same result, so this records the set of measures in force, not one. Domain logic:ReasoningContract, range logic:UncertaintyMeasure (stated in prose, matching the module's convention)."
msgstr "Relates a logic:ReasoningContract à a logic:UncertaintyMeasure it porte — how graded belief est recorded."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/underMereologyProfile|rdfs:label"
msgid "under mereology profile"
msgstr "under mereology profil"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/underMereologyProfile|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a whole to the logic:MereologyProfile it is declared under — the scope within which the strong mereological axioms (weak supplementation) hold for it. A whole carries no logic:WeakSupplementation obligation unless declared under a profile via this relation; parthood is profiled, not universal (design/LOGIC-FOUNDATION.md, the typed-and-contextual-mereology-and-holons section)."
msgstr "Relates a whole à the logic:MereologyProfile it est declared sous — the scope within qui the strong mereological axioms (weak supplementation) hold pour it."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/unit|rdfs:label"
msgid "unit"
msgstr "unit"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/unit|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a measurement to the unit its logic:measuredValue is expressed in — a QUDT unit by reference (Principle 5), held on the measurement rather than on the frame-independent magnitude. The unit leg of the true-quantity/measured-value seam (Principle 11): the unit belongs to the measurement, not the quantity, so the same logic:trueQuantity round-trips across unit systems. Because the foundation chase is all-IRI, logic:unit is the IRI-valued witness that a framed value exists, and is the predicate the logic:MeasurementFrameMissing constraint keys on — a value expressed in a unit but lacking its logic:referenceFrame is the violation. The domain property gmeow:unit grounds onto this by sub-property. Domain a measurement, range a unit (stated in prose, matching the module's convention)."
msgstr "Relates a measurement à the unit its logic:measuredValue est expressed dans — a QUDT unit par reference (Principle 5), held sur the measurement plutôt que sur the frame-independent magnitude."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/unsupportedConstruct|rdfs:label"
msgid "unsupported construct"
msgstr "unsupported construct"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/unsupportedConstruct|skos:definition"
msgid "Names a construct the lowering could not carry at all, carried on a logic:ReasoningResult's preservation field — MULTI-valued. A query whose constructs intersect this set is loss-affected (a derived diagnostic, never a stored field). Domain logic:ReasoningResult (stated in prose)."
msgstr "Names a construct the lowering could not carry at tous, carried sur a logic:ReasoningResult's preservation field — MULTI-valued."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/utility|rdfs:label"
msgid "utility"
msgstr "utility"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/utility|skos:definition"
msgid "The preference quantity carried on a logic:GoalEvaluation — how desirable an outcome is. The ONE preference term: utility and preference are one concept here, so no separate preference property is minted. Domain logic:GoalEvaluation (stated in prose). The range is intentionally left open (no rdfs:range), matching the module's quantitative axes. DISTINCT from the uncertainty measures (logic:confidence, logic:probability, logic:weight, logic:evidenceStrength) and from logic:satisfactionDegree and logic:objectiveValue — desirability is never sureness, never how much of the goal is met, and never the measure an optimization goal extremizes; none substitutes for another."
msgstr "Le preference quantity carried sur a logic:GoalEvaluation — how desirable an résultat is."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/validUntilState|rdfs:label"
msgid "valid until state"
msgstr "valid until état"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/validUntilState|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a support/reified assertion to the successor state at which it stops holding as an active support. It is the path-state counterpart of temporal valid-until metadata: a `del` records the state boundary where the support is retired, while the historical support remains retained. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:validUntilState only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a support/reified assertion à the successor état at qui it stops holding as an active support."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/valueClass|rdfs:label"
msgid "value class"
msgstr "valeur class"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/valueClass|skos:definition"
msgid "The required value class of a logic:PathValueTypeConstraint: the class every value on logic:valuePath must belong to. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:valueClass only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le obligatoire valeur class de a logic:PathValueTypeConstraint: the class chaque valeur sur logic:valuePath doit belong to."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/valueObject|rdfs:label"
msgid "value object"
msgstr "valeur object"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/valueObject|skos:definition"
msgid "The fixed object of a logic:PathValueTypeConstraint's fixed-value variant: the required object (an IRI or a literal) of logic:valuePredicate on every value reached by logic:valuePath."
msgstr "Le fixed object de a logic:PathValueTypeConstraint's fixed-valeur variant: the obligatoire object (an IRI ou a literal) de logic:valuePredicate sur chaque valeur reached par logic:valuePath."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/valuePath|rdfs:label"
msgid "value path"
msgstr "valeur chemin"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/valuePath|skos:definition"
msgid "The path predicate of a logic:PathValueTypeConstraint: every value the focus carries on this predicate must be an instance of logic:valueClass. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:valuePath only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le chemin prédicat de a logic:PathValueTypeConstraint: chaque valeur the focus porte sur this prédicat doit be an instance de logic:valueClass."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/valuePredicate|rdfs:label"
msgid "value predicate"
msgstr "valeur prédicat"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/valuePredicate|skos:definition"
msgid "The fixed check predicate of a logic:PathValueTypeConstraint's fixed-value variant: every value the focus carries on logic:valuePath must itself carry this predicate with object logic:valueObject (Q(v, o)), rather than being an instance of a logic:valueClass. Paired with logic:valueObject; mutually exclusive with logic:valueClass."
msgstr "Le fixed vérification prédicat de a logic:PathValueTypeConstraint's fixed-valeur variant: chaque valeur the focus porte sur logic:valuePath doit itself carry this prédicat avec object logic:valueObject (Q(v, o)), plutôt que being an instance de a logic:valueClass."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/verdictProvenance|rdfs:label"
msgid "verdict provenance"
msgstr "verdict provenance"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/verdictProvenance|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:Conjecture to the logic:VerdictProvenanceKind recording whether its cases were engine-produced or reviewer-asserted — the one genuinely-new axis the conjecture library adds over the candidate spine. Single-valued and REQUIRED. Domain logic:Conjecture, range logic:VerdictProvenanceKind. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:verdictProvenance only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Relates a logic:conjecture à the logic:VerdictProvenanceKind recording whether its cases were engine-produced ou reviewer-asserted — the one genuinely-new axis the conjecture library adds sur the candidat spine."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/versionOfFunctionality|rdfs:label"
msgid "versionOf is functional"
msgstr "versionOf is functional"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/versionOfFunctionality|skos:definition"
msgid "Asserts on the canonical carrier that gmeow:versionOf is functional: a version belongs to exactly one lineage, as its skos:definition states. Functionality is enforced by gmeow:versionOf's owl:FunctionalProperty declaration through native DL consistency; this records the characteristic on the canonical carrier."
msgstr "Asserts sur the canonique carrier qui gmeow:versionOf est functional: a version belongs à exactement un lineage, as its skos:définition states."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/violatedCriterion|rdfs:label"
msgid "violated criterion"
msgstr "violated criterion"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/violatedCriterion|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates a logic:SerializationAnomaly finding to the logic:SerializabilityCriterion it violates — the criterion (logic:ConflictSerializability or logic:ViewSerializability) under which the history admits no equivalent serial execution. Domain logic:SerializationAnomaly, range logic:SerializabilityCriterion (stated in prose). It names WHICH history property the anomaly breaches; it does not assert a logical contradiction (the schedule's final state may be perfectly consistent), keeping the finding a property of the history rather than of any state."
msgstr "Relates a logic:SerializationAnomaly finding à the logic:SerializabilityCriterion it violates — the criterion (logic:ConflictSerializability ou logic:ViewSerializability) sous qui the historique admits no equivalent sériel exécution."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/violation|rdfs:label"
msgid "violation"
msgstr "violation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/violation|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates an offending entity to the constraint it violates — a logic:Discipline (an OntoUML structural anti-pattern), a logic:MereologyConstraint (a profiled-mereology axiom such as logic:WeakSupplementation), a logic:OccurrentConstraint (an occurrent well-formedness axiom such as logic:OccurrentChangeAsymmetry), or a logic:QualityConstraint (a quality/quantity well-formedness axiom such as logic:MeasurementFrameMissing): the derived diagnostic the foundation lowering materializes, the logic: analogue of a reasoning_lint message. A logic:violation fact is never asserted by hand; it is entailed by the lowering rules over the stereotype, subsumption, mediation and parthood facts, so its presence is a machine-checkable proof that the entity breaks the named constraint."
msgstr "Relates an offending entity à the contrainte it violates — a logic:Discipline (an OntoUML structurel anti-pattern), a logic:MereologyConstraint (a profiled-mereology axiom such as logic:WeakSupplementation), a logic:OccurrentConstraint (an occurrent bien forméness axiom such as logic:OccurrentChangeAsymmetry), ou a logic:QualityConstraint (a qualité/quantity bien forméness axiom such as logic:MeasurementFrameMissing): the dérivé diagnostic the foundation lowering materializes, the logic: analogue de a reasoning_lint message."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/weight|rdfs:label"
msgid "weight"
msgstr "weight"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/weight|skos:definition"
msgid "A solver or ranking weight — a numeric preference used to order or score derivations — not necessarily probabilistic and not an epistemic confidence. Normatively distinct from logic:probability, logic:confidence, and logic:evidenceStrength: a ranking weight carries no calibrated probabilistic or evidential meaning unless one is separately and explicitly declared."
msgstr "Un solver ou ranking weight — a numeric preference used à order ou score derivations — not necessarily probabilistic et not an épistémique confidence."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/wellFoundedMaterializerPlan|rdfs:label"
msgid "well-founded materializer plan"
msgstr "well-founded materializer plan"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/wellFoundedMaterializerPlan|skos:definition"
msgid "The AUTHORED MODEL of the intra-engine phase sequence the native well-founded-semantics evaluator runs per world (crates/logic/src/wellfounded.rs materialize()): the canonical process model applied one scale down from the build pipeline (gmeow:pipeline-build) — an intra-engine pass sequence rather than an inter-stage DAG. Its logic:planBody is the root combinator logic:wfPhaseSequence, whose left-first walk yields the three phases materialize (logic:wfMaterializeEdb) ; resolve* (the logic:Iteration logic:wfResolveLoop over logic:wfResolveFixpoint, gated by logic:wfFixpointNotReached) ; construct (logic:wfConstructModel) — matching gmeow_logic::WELL_FOUNDED_PHASES. Because the middle phase is a logic:Iteration (a loop), this plan is OUTSIDE the certified acyclic DAG fragment by construction; that is correct and expected, so it does NOT run logic:executedUnderContract logic:DagWorkflowContract. Principle 12 BOUNDARY: this plan is authored SOURCE the parity gate crates/pipeline/tests/wellfounded_plan_parity.rs checks the Rust runtime against — the reasoner NEVER parses this RDF at scheduling or runtime; the native loop is the runtime, the plan is its declared twin. As a logic:Plan it asserts its own gmeow:SocialObject sort directly, the prose grounding of logic:Plan licensing no DL inference of it."
msgstr "Le AUTHORED modèle de the intra-engine phase sequence the native well-founded-sémantique evaluator runs per monde (crates/logic/src/wellfounded.rs materialize()): the canonique process modèle applied one scale down de the build pipeline (gmeow:pipeline-build) — an intra-engine pass sequence plutôt que an inter-stage DAG."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/wfConstructModel|rdfs:label"
msgid "well-founded construct model"
msgstr "well-founded construct modèle"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/wfConstructModel|skos:definition"
msgid "Phase 3 of the well-founded materializer (crates/logic/src/wellfounded.rs materialize()): the final reduct against the converged well-founded model W — least_model_of_reduct(reference = W), a HARD FAIL if the result's fact-key set differs from W (an undefined/partial model, unsupported in v1), then emit the derived non-EDB rows stamped with the world graph. The last elementary phase transition of the intra-engine plan."
msgstr "Phase 3 de the well-founded materializer (crates/logic/src/wellfounded.rs materialize()): the final reduct contre the converged well-founded modèle W — least_model_of_reduct(reference = W), a HARD FAIL si the résultat's fact-key set differs de W (an undefined/partial modèle, unsupported dans v1), then emit the dérivé non-EDB rows stamped avec the monde graphe."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/wfFixpointNotReached|rdfs:label"
msgid "well-founded fixpoint not reached"
msgstr "well-founded fixpoint not reached"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/wfFixpointNotReached|skos:definition"
msgid "The loop-guard situation of the alternating-fixpoint phase: the double-reduct step has not yet converged — the new under-estimate K2 differs from the previous K by fact-key set (K2.key_set() != K.key_set() in crates/logic/src/wellfounded.rs). The logic:iterationCondition of logic:wfResolveLoop: the loop body re-runs while this obtains, and the iteration terminates when it ceases (K2 == K), at which point W = K is the well-founded model's set of true atoms."
msgstr "Le loop-guard situation de the alternating-fixpoint phase: the double-reduct step possède not yet converged — the new under-estimate K2 differs de the previous K par fact-key set (K2.key_set() != K.key_set() dans crates/logic/src/wellfounded.rs)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/wfMaterializeEdb|rdfs:label"
msgid "well-founded materialize EDB"
msgstr "well-founded materialize EDB"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/wfMaterializeEdb|skos:definition"
msgid "Phase 1 of the well-founded materializer (crates/logic/src/wellfounded.rs materialize()): seed the per-world EDB — collect world_edb_facts, echo the asserted rows, and load them (sorted-key order) into the seed FactStore that the alternating fixpoint starts from. The first elementary phase transition of the intra-engine plan; its successor is the alternating-fixpoint resolution."
msgstr "Phase 1 de the well-founded materializer (crates/logic/src/wellfounded.rs materialize()): seed the per-monde EDB — collect world_edb_facts, echo the asserted rows, et load them (sorted-key order) dans the seed FactStore qui the alternating fixpoint starts from."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/wfPhaseSequence|rdfs:label"
msgid "well-founded phase sequence"
msgstr "well-founded phase sequence"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/wfPhaseSequence|skos:definition"
msgid "The ROOT logic:SerialConjunction of the well-founded materializer's phase plan: do the EDB-seeding phase (logic:leftOperand logic:wfMaterializeEdb), THEN the resolve-then-build suffix (logic:rightOperand logic:wfResolveThenBuild). Walked left-first, the combinator tree yields the execution order materialize ; resolve* ; construct — the program twin of crates/logic/src/wellfounded.rs materialize() and of gmeow_logic::WELL_FOUNDED_PHASES. The program root logic:wellFoundedMaterializerPlan reaches it through logic:planBody."
msgstr "Le ROOT logic:SerialConjunction de the well-founded materializer's phase plan: do the EDB-seeding phase (logic:leftOperand logic:wfMaterializeEdb), THEN the resolve-then-build suffix (logic:rightOperand logic:wfResolveThenBuild)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/wfReductEngineCapability|rdfs:label"
msgid "well-founded reduct-engine capability"
msgstr "well-founded reduct-engine capability"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/wfReductEngineCapability|skos:definition"
msgid "The executional precondition on the actor the well-founded materializer's phase action schemas carry as their logic:capability: the least-model-of-reduct engine (crate::rule_ir::least_model_of_reduct) is available to evaluate a reduct against a reference fact set. The generic ability the native engine must hold to run any of the three phases — distinct from logic:wfWorldSeeded, which is a precondition on the world state, not on the engine."
msgstr "Le executional précondition sur the actor the well-founded materializer's phase action schemas carry as their logic:capability: the least-modèle-of-reduct engine (crate::rule_ir::least_model_of_reduct) est available à evaluate a reduct contre a reference fact set."


msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/wfResolveFixpoint|rdfs:label"
msgid "well-founded resolve fixpoint"
msgstr "well-founded resolve fixpoint"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/wfResolveFixpoint|skos:definition"
msgid "Phase 2 of the well-founded materializer (crates/logic/src/wellfounded.rs materialize()): the alternating fixpoint of van Gelder — the double-reduct step U = least_model_of_reduct(reference = K) then K2 = least_model_of_reduct(reference = U), repeated until K2 and K have the same fact-key set. The body of the logic:Iteration logic:wfResolveLoop; the loop runs while logic:wfFixpointNotReached obtains and converges on W = K, the well-founded model's set of true atoms. The single ITERATED phase of the plan — why the plan is outside the acyclic DAG fragment."
msgstr "Phase 2 de the well-founded materializer (crates/logic/src/wellfounded.rs materialize()): the alternating fixpoint de van Gelder — the double-reduct step U = least_model_of_reduct(reference = K) then K2 = least_model_of_reduct(reference = U), repeated until K2 et K possèdent the same fact-key set."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/wfResolveLoop|rdfs:label"
msgid "well-founded resolve loop"
msgstr "well-founded resolve loop"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/wfResolveLoop|skos:definition"
msgid "The logic:Iteration combinator wrapping the alternating-fixpoint phase of the well-founded materializer: its logic:iterationBody is logic:wfResolveFixpoint (the double-reduct step) and its logic:iterationCondition is logic:wfFixpointNotReached (K2 != K). The loop is the program-level twin of the `loop { … break when K2.key_set() == K.key_set() }` of crates/logic/src/wellfounded.rs — the back-edge that places logic:wellFoundedMaterializerPlan outside the certified acyclic DAG fragment."
msgstr "Le logic:itération combinator wrapping the alternating-fixpoint phase de the well-founded materializer: its logic:iterationBody est logic:wfResolveFixpoint (the double-reduct step) et its logic:iterationCondition est logic:wfFixpointNotReached (K2 != K)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/wfResolveThenBuild|rdfs:label"
msgid "well-founded resolve then build"
msgstr "well-founded resolve then build"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/wfResolveThenBuild|skos:definition"
msgid "The inner logic:SerialConjunction of the well-founded materializer's phase plan: do the alternating-fixpoint loop (logic:leftOperand logic:wfResolveLoop), THEN construct the final model (logic:rightOperand logic:wfConstructModel). The suffix program of the plan's outer serial conjunction."
msgstr "Le inner logic:SerialConjunction de the well-founded materializer's phase plan: do the alternating-fixpoint loop (logic:leftOperand logic:wfResolveLoop), THEN construct the final modèle (logic:rightOperand logic:wfConstructModel)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/wfWorldSeeded|rdfs:label"
msgid "well-founded world seeded"
msgstr "well-founded monde seeded"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/wfWorldSeeded|skos:definition"
msgid "The situation gate the well-founded materializer's phase action schemas ground on: the per-world store is selected and its asserted EDB facts are reachable (the sorted worlds list of crates/logic/src/wellfounded.rs materialize()). The shared logic:precondition of the three intra-engine phase schemas — the elementary phase transition applies only once a world is in scope."
msgstr "Le situation gate the well-founded materializer's phase action schemas ground on: the per-monde store est selected et its asserted EDB facts sont reachable (the sorted worlds list de crates/logic/src/wellfounded.rs materialize())."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/witnessIndividual|rdfs:label"
msgid "witness individual"
msgstr "témoin individu"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/witnessIndividual|skos:definition"
msgid "The individual a logic:ContradictionWitness records as forced to owl:Nothing — the entity whose type became unsatisfiable under the conjectured formula, identifying exactly where the contradiction bit. Single-valued, xsd:string (the individual's IRI as a string). Domain logic:ContradictionWitness. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:witnessIndividual only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Le individu a logic:ContradictionWitness enregistre as forced à owl:Nothing — the entity dont type became unsatisfiable sous the conjectured formule, identifying exactly où the contradiction bit."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/witnessPremise|rdfs:label"
msgid "witness premise"
msgstr "témoin premise"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/witnessPremise|skos:definition"
msgid "A premise that participated in the contradiction a logic:ContradictionWitness records — one serialized triple (subject predicate object) per value, MULTI-valued because a refutation typically rests on several jointly-inconsistent facts. Together the premises are the minimal derivation the reader can replay to see why the formula is refuted from the standpoint. Multi-valued, xsd:string. Domain logic:ContradictionWitness. It is not an interchangeable alias for a broader, narrower, or merely related construct; use logic:witnessPremise only under the stated identity and validation conditions."
msgstr "Un premise qui participated dans the contradiction a logic:ContradictionWitness enregistre — one serialized triple (subject prédicat object) per valeur, MULTI-valued parce que a réfutation typically rests sur several jointly-incohérent facts."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/witnessRequiredViolation|rdfs:label"
msgid "witness required violation"
msgstr "témoin obligatoire violation"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/witnessRequiredViolation|skos:definition"
msgid "Relates an individual to an anti-rigid type it instantiates with no materialized counter-world to witness the anti-rigidity: the instance-level diagnostic the anti-rigidity lowering emits under the strict witness-required policy (LOGIC-SEMANTICS.md §Anti-rigidity needs a witness policy). For an individual x typed by an anti-rigid Role or Phase T in a world, if there is no other materialized world in which x exists but is NOT typed T, a logic:witnessRequiredViolation fact is entailed in the typing world; a counter-world that witnesses x existing untyped by T discharges the obligation and no violation is emitted. Unlike the default witness-obligation policy (which emits logic:dischargeObligation, an obligation rather than a violation) this policy treats a missing counter-world as a hard failure; the construction of the witness world itself happens on demand. It is never asserted by hand; its presence is a machine-checkable proof that an anti-rigid instantiation lacks the world of existence its anti-rigidity requires."
msgstr "Relates an individu à an anti-rigid type it instantiates avec no materialized counter-monde à témoin the anti-rigidity: the instance-niveau diagnostic the anti-rigidity lowering emits sous the strict témoin-obligatoire politique (LOGIC-sémantique.md §Anti-rigidity needs a témoin politique)."

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/witnessWorld|rdfs:label"
msgid "witness world"
msgstr "témoin monde"

msgctxt "https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/witnessWorld|skos:definition"
msgid "The world IRI the logic:ContradictionWitness was found in — the modal/context world within the conjecture's standpoint where the contradiction was realized, so the refutation stays world-scoped rather than asserted across all worlds. Single-valued, xsd:string (the world IRI as a string). Domain logic:ContradictionWitness."
msgstr "Le monde IRI the logic:ContradictionWitness was found dans — the modal/contexte monde within the conjecture's point de vue où the contradiction was realized, so the réfutation stays monde-scoped plutôt que asserted across tous worlds."

# END TRANSLATIONS
